window.FWN_KEYBOARD_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_KEYBOARD_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2601,"title":"Chapter 2601: Chapter 2553: The Fisherman Profiting Off the Brawling Fishes","paragraphs":["With a wave of her sleeves, the Goddess of Wu Mountain vanished, causing Nuba’s attack to fall empty.","Nuba looked at the surrounding fog and sneered, “Yaoji, do you think I won’t be able to suppress you just because you morphed into a fog? That might be true for others, but that doesn’t include me!”","Her robe flared outward as her unkempt hair fluttered furiously. A visible heat wave began spreading from her, causing earth to crack and spirit springs to dry up. The lush trees on the mountain swiftly withered.","It looked as if the vibrant Wu Mountain had turned barren in an instant. Even the fog shrouding the mountain slowly dissipated, and not a single cloud was left.","Xingtian and Kuafu couldn’t help but speak up. “Madam, this matter...”","“Shut up! This has nothing to do with you, so don’t do anything unnecessary and side with outsiders!” Nuba roared.","Xingtian and Kuafu exchanged awkward looks. Nuba was the wife of an Ancestral Shaman, so they didn’t dare to offend her. That put them in a tough spot.","Yumen Beiqing roared, “We were the ones who informed the Goddess of Wu Mountain about Gu’s murder of Bao Jiang. You’re wronging her!”","Zu An was taken aback. He had indeed planned to stand up for the Goddess of Wu Mountain, but he hadn’t expected Yumen Beiqing to beat him to it. Didn’t she get jealous the last time I spoke with the goddess? What an abrupt change of mind!","“It’s you!” Nuba suddenly turned around. Her black fingernails grew longer as she swiped them at Yumen Beiqing, resembling spears.","Yumen Beiqing reacted fast. She activated the Emperor’s Suppression Talisman and swiftly conjured a golden-armored warrior. The warrior brandished its weapon to stop the black fingernails.","“A mere celestial warrior dares to stop me?” Nuba sneered.","Her black fingernails sunk into the warrior, afflicting it with a black aura that suppressed its energy. A second later, the golden-armored soldier disintegrated.","However, Nuba’s attack didn’t stop there. Her black fingernails continued surging toward Yumen Beiqing’s forehead.","Yumen Beiqing’s gaze turned cold, but she stood completely still as if she wouldn’t react to the attack at all.","Just then, Zu An appeared in front of Yumen Beiqing and deflected the black fingernails with his sword. At the same time, a fog enveloped Yumen Beiqing and transported her a hundred meters away.","The fog slowly morphed into the Goddess of Wu Mountain. Noticing Zu An’s glance, she nodded back at him in acknowledgment.","Nuba didn’t continue her attack. She looked at Zu An in confusion and murmured, “A human? How can there be such a strong human in the world?”","This world was dominated by the fiends and the shamans. The humans were a lesser race stuck between the two. Weak and foolish, the only thing they were good for was their reproductive prowess.","Zu An sneered, “Gu was the one who murdered Celestial Bao Jiang in cold blood. The Celestial Emperor has already resolved this issue, so why are you coming after us for an explanation?”","Nuba laughed miserably. “I am no match for Zhuanxu, and he has already lost a grandson. It wouldn’t do for me to go after him. But I haven’t settled the score with you yet.”","Zu An was speechless. This madwoman can’t be reasoned with!","The Goddess of Wu Mountain frowned. “Why are you acting like a crazy shrew? You’re the Yellow Emperor’s daughter.”","“Yellow Emperor... Hahaha!” Nuba looked as if she had suddenly lost her mind. “I sacrificed so much for the war back then, but what did I get in return? Nothing. Nothing at all!","“You, the Flame Emperor’s daughter, are adored by the masses despite doing nothing. What about me? Not only did I lose my divine powers and become incapable of returning to the Celestial Court, I was even reduced to this state! Others shun me wherever I go! I was lucky to have Gu as a child, but now I have nothing left. You stole everything from me!”","A thought surfaced in Zu An’s mind. He had heard about the Yellow Emperor’s life-and-death battle with Chiyou.","Chiyou, with the aid of Fengbo and Yushi, had claimed the upper hand over the Yellow Emperor’s army and even cornered them. Nuba had intervened and curbed Fengbo and Yushi, allowing the Yellow Emperor to turn the tables.","But I didn’t expect the Goddess of Wu Mountain to be the Flame Emperor’s daughter. Hold on, Big Manman is also skilled at controlling flames. Could she be related to the Flame Emperor?","The Goddess of Wu Mountain remained calm. “After the war between the Flame Emperor and the Yellow Emperor, the Celestial Court is now dominated by the Yellow Emperor’s lineage. What you have just said is of little concern to me, and it is meaningless to argue with me about all these things.”","Zu An and the Mermaid Queen exchanged astonished looks. They felt as if they had just stumbled upon piping hot tea. The Goddess of Wu Mountain had just revealed extremely important information.","It turned out that the Flame Emperor and the Yellow Emperor weren’t as close as they had previously thought them to be. It looked as if at one point, they were even enemies, and the Flame Emperor was the one who had fallen in defeat, resulting in the Yellow Emperor’s lineage taking power.","“What carefree words! I bet you've been harboring a grudge against me because you were dissatisfied with the Flame Emperor’s defeat, so you used this opportunity to kill my only son!” Nuba screeched. One of her eyes appeared through her unkempt hair, and it was so widened, bloodshot, and turbid that it felt as if she had gone utterly insane.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain shook her head. “You have already gone berserk.”","“I don’t care! I’ll kill anyone responsible for my son’s death!” Nuba unleashed a screeching sonic boom.","Yumen Beiqing nodded empathetically. She was the only one who understood how Nuba felt.","Nuba morphed into a ray of green light that charged at the Goddess of Wu Mountain. This time, the latter didn’t transform into a fog, and instead fought with Nuba in her current form. The two figures moved extremely swiftly; all that could be seen were a green light and a white light intersecting with each other.","Kuafu lightly bumped Xingtian’s arm and asked, “Who do you think is more likely to win?”","Xingtian analyzed the situation as he grimly replied, “Even though Nuba lost her divine powers, the Goddess of Wu Mountain doesn’t specialize in battle. Furthermore, Nuba’s power happens to suppress her. Things don’t look good for the Goddess of Wu Mountain.”","Zu An had come to the same conclusion too. He had already spotted a few close calls for the Goddess of Wu Mountain. At this rate, she’ll only last at most an hour before falling in defeat.","Just then, he heard Yumen Beiqing’s whisper, “Why don’t we take this chance to attack the madwoman together and kill her? Otherwise, she could come after us once the Goddess of Wu Mountain falls in defeat. We may not be a match for her then.”","It would be much easier for them to defeat Nuba with the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s help.","Zu An shook his head. “She’s still grieving over her son. Despite our conflict, it isn’t to the point where we should take her life.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain suddenly exclaimed. She had been sent flying by a strike on the shoulder, and Nuba made use of this opportunity to charge at her. She was intending to take the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s life!","Zu An couldn’t help but worry for the Goddess of Wu Mountain because of her extreme resemblance to Pei Mianman. Without any hesitation, he dashed in front of the Goddess of Wu Mountain and gently pushed her behind him.","Nuba screeched in anger, “You’re courting death!”","She gathered a destructive surge of energy that emanated terrifying heat waves between her hands.","“Be careful!” the Mermaid Queen cried. She could sense the pressure coming from the energy.","Yumen Beiqing narrowed her eyes as she secretly clenched her fists. It’d be best if they injure each other so I can make use of this chance to claim their lives."]},{"number":2602,"title":"Chapter 2602: Chapter 2554: Mastermind","paragraphs":["Concern appeared in the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s usually cold eyes. She intended to step forward to help Zu An when a sudden flash of seven-colored light caused the furious Nuba to vanish into thin air.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s mouth opened so wide that one could fit a chicken egg into it. Thinking that Nuba had hidden herself using a special movement skill, she quickly scanned the surroundings with her ki, but Nuba was truly nowhere to be found.","Even the heat and dryness were beginning to recede. Nuba had truly vanished.","Xingtian and Kuafu exchanged relieved looks. Whew, we aren’t the only ones who fell for that.","Yumen Beiqing was shocked and intimidated. His Seven-Colored Divine Halo is capable of subjugating Nuba too! I must only make a move when I’m confident of victory, or else there won’t be a second chance.","He’s just a normal human. Other than being taller, more handsome, and more muscular than average, there are hardly any strengths to him. How did he obtain such a ridiculously overpowered ability?","Another seven-colored light flickered around Zu An, and a disoriented Nuba fell to the ground. Zu An looked at her and said, “It was the Celestial Emperor who sentenced Gu to death based on the celestial laws. If you agree to not go after the goddess and the others, I’ll spare your life in light of the fact that you're still grieving over your son.”","Nuba coldly spat, “What if I refuse?”","“Then I’ll kill you right now,” Zu An calmly replied, as if it was something insignificant. He had weathered many storms and had been in a position of authority for a long time, so he naturally exuded an air of intimidation.","Nuba fell silent. She sensed that it wasn’t an empty bluff. She was ill-tempered, but she was no fool. The other party’s Seven-Colored Divine Halo was incredible. If she obstinately marched down this path, only death awaited her, but she needed to stay alive to avenge her son.","“I promise you.” She harrumphed before taking her leave.","Xingtian and Kuafu bowed to Zu An. “Thank you for showing mercy to Madam.”","As fellow shamans, they wouldn’t be able to turn a blind eye if Zu An made a move.","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief too. Nuba was the Yellow Emperor’s daughter and an Ancestral Shaman’s wife. It was hard to predict what would happen if he took her life.","“Thank you for your help,” a voice said as a faint fragrance drifted into Zu An’s nose. The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s gaze had mellowed considerably compared to before.","“Pardon me for my unnecessary intervention, goddess.” Looking at the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s snowy skin close up, Zu An couldn’t help but think that she was carved out of the same mold as Pei Mianman.","“You need not be so courteous. Nuba’s power happens to suppress mine. I’d have been in danger if not for your intervention.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain suddenly noticed his gaze, but Zu An's expression didn’t carry any lust; just yearning and tenderness. That shook her heart. “Are you yearning for your lover again?”","Zu An snapped out of his daze and awkwardly bowed. “My apologies.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled. Do I look identical to Miss Pei? It doesn’t seem as if he’s lying, and... Her eyes fell on the Mermaid Queen.","His two companions aren’t ordinary women. Since they backed up his words, it should be safe to assume that Miss Pei does exist. But how could there be two completely identical people in the world? Unless...","The conclusion she arrived at alarmed her. It prompted her to assess Zu An once more.","Meanwhile, Zu An was scanning his surroundings. He turned to the Mermaid Queen and asked, “Did you see little sister Ling’er?”","The Mermaid Queen turned to her side and was taken aback. “Hm? The Saintess was still there a moment ago. Where did she go?”","...","Meanwhile, Yumen Beiqing was discreetly following Nuba. Under normal circumstances, she wouldn’t do something like this, as her identity could be easily revealed. But now that her plan had fallen into shambles, she no longer cared as much whether Zu An learned about her true identity or not.","This is my final chance. I have to kill Nuba now so she won’t be scorched to death by the Golden Crows’ Ten Suns, thus preventing the series of subsequent events...","Such as Kuafu dying of exhaustion while trying to avenge Nuba, completely igniting the Shaman races’ fury. That was what later caused Hou Yi’s shooting of the suns. As long as I kill Nuba, there will be no reason for those events to happen. I might be able to change the fate of the Ten Suns!","She trailed behind Nuba, awaiting the perfect chance to make her move. Nuba was a formidable adversary, but Yumen Beiqing happened to be impervious to her power. Thus, she believed that if she utilized the element of surprise well, it wouldn’t be difficult for her to kill Nuba.","After stalking Nuba for some time, she finally found a chance to make a move. She was about to strike when she suddenly noticed a strange movement and hurriedly hid in a nearby tree.","“Who is it?!” Nuba was alarmed, but she looked in another direction instead of where Yumen Beiqing was hiding.","Crisp applause filled the air. A woman walked out and said, “As expected of a renowned expert. You found me so quickly.”","“It’s her?” Yumen Beiqing recognized the woman. It was Salamay.","They had parted ways with the Lord of Slaughter’s party after entering this world, and there had been no news from the latter in the meantime. She hadn’t expected to stumble upon Salamay here.","I wonder if Mojard told her anything. Probably not, since the Time Scribe wasn’t the real Mojard.","While Yumen Beiqing was still in thought, Salamay had already arrived in front of Nuba.","Nuba frowned. “A slave?”","Salamay was speechless. Her smile immediately froze. Can’t we have a pleasant chat? I used to be the princess of a powerful world, you know! Why does everyone in this world treat us like slaves and pets?","She felt uneasy. The legends passed down through the generations are likely false, meaning we didn’t descend from a lofty bloodline. The truth would plunge the entire Monster World into despair.","Recalling her mission, she took a deep breath and suppressed her feelings. “My master tasked me to relay a message to you.”","“I have no interest in what your master has to say. Scram!” Nuba was in a terrible mood after having suffered a defeat. She released a powerful heat wave that pushed Salamay a hundred meters away before the latter finally regained her balance.","Seeing that Nuba was going to leave without even sparing her a glance, Salamay anxiously shouted, “Are you not curious to know the true culprit behind your son’s death?”","Nuba instantly reappeared in front of Salamay, who was raised into the air as if an invisible pair of hands was holding her up by the neck.","Nuba’s hair fluttered wildly as she looked at Salamay with a twisted expression. “Who is it?”","“Someone goaded Gu into stealing the immortal medicine, convincing him to see it as an opportunity to eliminate his two older brothers... Cough cough. Release me! I... can’t breathe...” Salamay struggled desperately as she instinctively clawed at her neck, but it was to no avail.","“Give me a name!” Nuba roared as she finally dropped Salamay to the ground.","Salamay gasped for air, sounding like a broken bellows. For a moment there, she had almost tasted death! This world is too dangerous!","“My master says that this clue should be enough to lead you to the mastermind,” she quickly replied, fearing that Nuba would resort to violence once more.","Nuba frowned. A while later, she turned away and left without saying a word.","Salamay breathed a sigh of relief. She spat, “That madwoman.” She tidied up her clothes and patted her chest, muttering, “When my master refused to tell me the mastermind’s name, I thought that woman would hound me to no end. To think that she would leave just like that. Master has it all figured out!”","She glanced fearfully in the direction Nuba had departed in before heading back to report the matter to her master.","It was only after Salamay left that Yumen Beiqing finally emerged from her hiding spot with a darkened expression. Looking at the two directions where Nuba and Salamay had gone respectively, she hesitated for a second before deciding to follow Salamay."]},{"number":2603,"title":"Chapter 2603: Chapter 2555: Showing Ones Hand","paragraphs":["Yumen Beiqing figured that she could kill Nuba at any time. The latter was a renowned figure, and it was an easy feat to find her. So, she decided to prioritize following Salamay and figuring out who the latter's master was.","Someone else is pulling the strings here. I might have overlooked something important. Perhaps I just have to find that important thing to change the ending.","That greatly lifted her spirits. She carefully followed Salamay, fearing that the latter would discover her.","Salamay was very vigilant. She took remote paths, and sometimes even took detours to confuse anyone following her. She also frequently surveyrf her surroundings to ensure that no one was following her.","But with her strength, there was no way she could find the Sun Goddess when the latter was intentionally hiding from her.","Soon, Salamay arrived at a cliff. She knocked on the cliff wall, and a ray of light shone down. She took out a jade piece and placed it into the ligh; the jade glowed and reflected the light onto the cliff.","All of a sudden, a cavern appeared on the cliff face.","With a sweet smile, she walked in and bowed to the person seated inside. “Master, I have completed the mission you entrusted to me.”","The black-robed man impassively said, “Tell me how it went.”","Salamay recounted the details surrounding her encounter with Nuba. The black-robed man nodded in satisfaction. “Good. You didn’t do anything unnecessary.”","Seeing that the black-robed man was in a good mood, Salamay took this chance to ask, “Master, why didn’t you tell her the name directly? Why are you divulging information to her in this roundabout manner instead?”","The black-robed man laughed. “Be it shaman or fiend, mortal or deity, they share the same peculiar frame of mind. They are wary of information offered for free, but they don’t doubt the information that they personally uncover. That’s why it’s better to let her investigate the matter. She’s the Yellow Emperor’s daughter, an Ancestral Shaman’s wife. Her means and connections are not to be underestimated. It won’t be difficult for her to uncover the truth.”","Salamay was awed. “Master is truly sagacious! I am humbled by your ingenuity.”","The Lord of Slaughter secretly gave his daughter a thumbs up. He had been in a lofty position for a long time and was used to being bootlicked more than having to be the one bootlicking. It was hard for him to suddenly change his ways. Good thing my daughter is formidable. If she wins master’s favor, we can gather more intelligence. Who knows? Master might even bestow us the method to activate our ancient bloodline power...","All of a sudden, his expression stiffened. Huh? Why am I calling him master even in my thoughts? Where has my sense of shame gone? Where has my dignity gone?!","While he was doubting himself, the black-robed man’s voice suddenly turned cold. “You trash. You brought the enemy here with you.”","The gleeful Salamay was stunned. “Master, I didn’t...” The pressure exuded by the black-robed man in a fit of rage shook her very soul.","The black-robed man ignored Salamay and instead looked up at the entrance. “Why not come in for a chat when you’re already here?”","Yumen Beiqing slowly entered the cavern while coldly eyeing the black-robed man.","“The Fiend races’ Saintess?” How could the Lord of Slaughter not recognize the one person who had impeded the Monster World’s invasion of the Cultivation World for so many years? He sneered, “Hmph! You concealed yourself so well that I was never able to find you. To think that you would appear before me on your own accord!”","He swiped his claw at Yumen Beiqing, hoping to take her down to quell his master’s anger lest the latter blame Salamay for this lapse.","The black-robed man spat, “Idiot!”","The Lord of Slaughter was confused. Why does master value a mere Fiend races’ Saintess from a weak world so much?","The truth was soon apparent. A brilliant light suddenly shone in front of him. For a moment there, he thought he was looking at the rising sun. Terrifying heat and flames gushed at him, charring his resilient skin black. For an instant, he thought he was going to die.","He hurriedly unleashed all his protective methods, knowing that this wasn’t the time for him to withhold any of his aces. As the ruler of the Monster World, he had many invaluable treasures with him. Brilliant lights pulsated from his body, helping him fend off the terrifying flames. However, judging from the swift rate at which his defensive artifacts were being depleted and destroyed, he knew that it wouldn’t take long before he was reduced to ashes.","Salamay was horrified, but she was nowhere strong enough to intervene in this battle. She could only turn to the black-robed man with pleading eyes. “Master...”","Looking at the Lord of Slaughter’s artifacts, the black-robed man thought to himself that his slave had some value after all, and that it would be a waste for him to die here. So, he waved his cloak, and it swiftly enlarged into a humongous black cloth that enveloped the brilliant sun, causing the cavern to turn dark once more.","Salamay finally got a look at the black-robed man’s true appearance and was shocked. Contrary to her expectations, the black-robed man wasn't an unkempt old man or a twisted mutant. Instead, he was tall and dashing. He’s not as good-looking as that Zu guy, but he’s not bad either.","A force dragged the Lord of Slaughter backward, pulling him to safety. He quickly bowed and said, “Thank... you, master...” He was also surprised to see that the black-robed man was a young man.","Yumen Beiqing glared at the black-robed man in a mix of shock and realization. “It’s you!”","The black-robed man smiled. “I didn’t expect you to find me here. I’d expect no less from the Sun Goddess.”","Yumen Beiqing’s expression turned cold. “That explains why everything progressed in the worst direction no matter what I tried. You were pulling the strings. It’s a good thing I found the root of the problem now. It’s not too late to resolve the situation now.”","“You’re awfully confident about defeating me, mother,” the black-robed man replied with a relaxed laugh.","Salamay was treating the Lord of Slaughter’s injuries when they heard those words and immediately looked over. They assessed the two others with slackened lower jaws that nearly fell to the ground.","They are mother and son? How did a Fiend races’ Saintess from a weak world suddenly become master’s mother? And she looks so young that I would have thought that she was younger than master. What’s going on?","“Shut up. You have no right to call me that.” Yumen Beiqing glared at the black-robed man with wrathful eyes.","Salamay and the Lord of Slaughter slowly grasped the situation. It doesn’t seem like they're truly mother and son... but why does master call her mother then?","The black-robed man’s expression turned livid. “You people still look down on me. Of course, you’re the lofty Sun Goddess. Someone with a bloodline as noble as yours is more than qualified to look down on others. Little do you know that your arrogance will become your downfall!”","“I shall capture and hand you over to your father. You can reason with him instead.” Yumen Beiqing attacked the black-robed man.","“Hahaha! You’re too arrogant. Very well. I shall show you my true strength!” The black-robed man’s clothes puffed up as he transformed into a void in response to Yumen Beiqing’s attack.","...","Meanwhile, Zu An was still searching for Yumen Beiqing.","Seeing how anxious he was, the Goddess of Wu Mountain hesitantly opened and closed her mouth several times before finally speaking up. “You don’t need to be too worried about her. She’ll be fine.”","“Goddess, what makes you say so?” Zu An looked at her with sharp eyes. “Do you know something that I’m unaware of?”"]},{"number":2604,"title":"Chapter 2604: Chapter 2556: Search","paragraphs":["The Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled. “Not really. I merely sensed a formidable power hidden inside her body. She should have no problem protecting herself.”","“A formidable power?” The Mermaid Queen was stunned. The Fiend races’ Saintess’ cultivation should be beneath mine, but the knowledge and composure she displayed...","Zu An remained calm, as if he had already known that.","He hadn’t doubted Yumen Beiqing at the start. The way she hadn’t hesitated to sever ties with the Fiend races for him greatly resembled Xie Daoyun. But as he spent more time with her, he'd noticed so many anomalies that it was clear something was amiss. If he was that dense, he wouldn’t have survived skirting around death for so many years.","For instance, he had followed Yumen Beiqing’s information to locate Pei Mianman’s whereabouts, but the latter was nowhere to be found, as if she had never appeared in those places. After he thought about it, there was only one possibility: The information he'd received from that town was off.","He'd initially suspected that Xie Daoyun was misleading him out of jealousy, but he quickly rejected that conjecture. Having known Xie Daoyun for years, he knew better than anyone else that she was an educated, sensible, and gentle young miss. She wouldn’t do something like that.","Subsequently, more and more details popped up that further convinced him that she wasn’t the real Xie Daoyun.","For instance, while the two of them were getting steamy, he'd tried using some secrets that only he and Xie Daoyun knew to test her. Despite Yumen Beiqing’s best attempts to impersonate Xie Daoyun, she clearly didn’t know about these secrets. That had also made him realize how even when the two of them were getting passionate, Yumen Beiqing still exuded inexplicable coldness and even hatred toward him.","He couldn’t understand why a woman would submit to a man if she hated him. And if she truly hated him, why did the system not pick up on her rage? Sometimes, he'd wondered if he was reading too much into it.","However, more details surfaced when they arrived in this world, and they confirmed his conjecture that Yumen Beiqing was concealing many secrets from him. He tried to test her many times, but she'd never shown any openings.","But then, he'd secretly probed her body while they were getting some action, and it was then that he detected a formidable sealed power inside her. However, he hadn’t dared to probe the sealed power too deeply out of fear that she would notice his intrusion.","The act they'd put on together felt like a harmonious orchestra at first. It was only recently that Yumen Beiqing started looking distracted. It felt as if she was no longer interested in maintaining the act.","Even so, Zu An had had no choice but to continue the act because he needed her to find Pei Mianman and the real Xie Daoyun. Yumen Beiqing had to have come into contact with Xie Daoyun at some point to gather so much information about them.","He'd been planning to find a good time to have a show of hands with Yumen Beiqing when the latter suddenly went missing. There was a chance that Yumen Beiqing was leaving for good, so he had to find her, whether it was for Pei Mianman or Xie Daoyun.","Thus, he bowed to the Goddess of Wu Mountain and said, “Thank you for your advice, but I still have to find her, or I’ll feel uneasy.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain hesitated for a second before gently replying, “I am the cause of this matter. I’ll accompany you in your search.”","Zu An looked at her in astonishment. Her offer was at odds with her cold nature, but it would indeed be helpful to have the aid of someone from this world. It was also a pleasure to travel with someone who looked so much like Pei Mianman. “Thank you, goddess.”","The Mermaid Queen shot vigilant looks at the Goddess of Wu Mountain. Is she interested in big brother Zu too?","The thought that the other party resembled the woman Zu An loved deeply left her feeling profoundly helpless.","Xingtian and Kuafu walked over and clasped their fists at them. “We won’t be able to accompany you anymore, as we have to return to report the incident here.”","So many things had just happened at Zhong Mountain. All the powers in the world were in an uproar now. They had to return to their tribe to decide on their next move.","“See you!” There were many questions Zu An wanted to ask them, but his priority at hand was to find Yumen Beiqing. He didn’t dare to delay this matter.","After parting ways, Zu An began searching for Yumen Beiqing’s trail. He had been too focused on dealing with Nuba earlier, so he hadn’t noticed her sneaking away.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain pointed in a direction. “I know every blade of grass and tree on Wu Mountain. I sensed her heading in that direction. However, Wu Mountain is nothing more than a peak on Spirit Mountain. It won’t be easy to find a single person here.”","Zu An knew she was right. The Spirit Mountain of this world was tens of thousands of times larger than the mountain ranges in his previous world. Even the mountain peaks easily reached tens of thousands of meters in height. There were countless venomous creatures and ferocious beasts in the region. Powerful cultivators also established their caves here, and they constructed dangerous beguilement formations to protect their caves. Even a grandmaster from the Cultivation World would fare no better wandering the Spirit Mountain region and trying to survive in the wilderness; the odds of survival were zero. Finding a person here was harder than finding a needle in the ocean.","“It’s fine. At least we have a direction to work with now. Thank you, goddess.” Zu An began making his way in the direction pointed out by the Goddess of Wu Mountain. From time to time, he took detours, heading left at one moment and right in the next. It was as if someone was pointing out the directions for him.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain noticed his lack of hesitation in navigating and asked, “Did you plant a location talisman on that lady?”","Zu An shook his head. He had considered that, but he also knew that Yumen Beiqing wasn't as simple as she appeared. Such a move would reveal that he was suspicious of her, so he had to give up on that idea. “I can communicate with small animals. They're the ones pointing out the directions for me.”","He was relying on the jade badge’s ability to commune with living beings to find Yumen Beiqing. The latter had moved carefully, but she wouldn’t go to the extent of guarding against worms, birds, and small animals.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was awed. “You must have a pure and kind heart to be able to commune with animals.”","She had heard that only the noblest souls would inherit such powers. Even the Mermaid Queen’s eyes glowed wondrously as she looked at Zu An. I've chosen the right person!","Zu An’s face heated up. With the misunderstandings they were having, it was tough for him to break their bubble and tell them that it was an artifact’s ability.","Fortunately, he noticed a trail and soon arrived at the cliff face. He concluded, “She came here and entered that spot.\"","“There seems to be a concealment formation here.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain quickly noticed something amiss and waved her sleeves. A fog shrouded the cliff face, revealing the formation’s details. “It’s a complex formation. It won’t be easy to decipher it.”","“It’s not that hard.” Zu An whipped out his Tai’e Sword and plunged it into three locations. The formation on the cliff face scattered, revealing a black cavern.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain widened her eyes in shock. Absolute strength and a deep understanding of the formation’s weaknesses were required to dispel a formation in such a manner. This fellow is an enigmatic one.","The Mermaid Queen took out a Night Illumination Pearl to gently light the cavern. Intense heat pulsated from within. There was no oxygen in it at all. If not for their high cultivation levels, the immense pressure difference would have blown their bodies to bits as soon as they stepped into the cavern.","It was a mess inside the cavern. There had been a huge battle here."]},{"number":2605,"title":"Chapter 2605: Chapter 2557: Cause of Suspicion","paragraphs":["“Such extreme heat! Could this be where Nuba dwells?” The Mermaid Queen, being from the Ocean races, was extremely sensitive to dry and hot environments.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain frowned. “That shouldn’t be the case. Nuba didn’t leave in this direction, and her dwelling is some distance away from here.”","Zu An traced his finger across the cavern wall to inspect its molten glass-like quality. “Even though they both specialize in flames, there is a vast difference between Nuba’s power and this. Nuba’s heat is purely destructive and deathly, whereas this heat also contains vibrant life force within it, despite its potential for destruction.”","Most people wouldn’t have been able to tell the difference, but Zu An’s grasp of different powers had reached a higher level than before.","“Could the Saintess have come here to challenge the master of the cavern? This power should belong to the cavern’s master, right?” the Mermaid Queen deduced.","Zu An neither affirmed nor denied her guess. For the battle to have become this intense, both parties had to have been on the same level. A guess was beginning to surface in his mind.","He suddenly spotted something in his peripheral vision. He flew over and picked up a metal fragment. It looked like copper but wasn’t copper; it seemed to have broken off from a massive cauldron. Strange runes were inscribed on the metal fragment, but it was hard to decipher them, as most of them were destroyed.","“Ah!” the Mermaid Queen suddenly exclaimed in shock.","A human face was inscribed on the metal fragment. It was carved so exquisitely that it resembled a living being, but the face was warped in extreme pain. Just the sight of it was enough to make one uncomfortable.","“I wonder who carved something like that. With such skills, they should carve something better than this,” the Mermaid Queen grumbled.","“You’re right. This wasn’t carved onto the metal piece.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain took the metal fragment and gently touched the face on it. Her expression turned grim. “It is a living soul.”","The Mermaid Queen was stunned.","Zu An had also noticed something amiss with the human face, and he hurriedly asked what was going on.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain solemnly replied, “In this world, there are malevolent arts capable of extracting a living being’s soul and trapping them in special containers to achieve unspeakable goals. These runes serve to suppress the soul.”","Zu An grimly murmured, “Could Yumen Beiqing have come here for some reason, only to stumble upon the cavern’s master utilizing some sort of malevolent art, upon which the two of them came to blows?”","That would mean that Yumen Beiqing might be in danger. She was undoubtedly powerful, but someone who dabbled in such arts would be anything but a pushover.","“Look here!” the Mermaid Queen exclaimed. She had been trying to distance herself from that eerie mask when she inadvertently stumbled upon another discovery","Zu An and the Goddess of Wu Mountain looked over and saw that a corner of the cavern wall had crumbled. The extreme heat in the cavern had likely caused the walls to expand unevenly, resulting in the collapse.","Zu An gently pushed the wall. It collapsed, revealing a secret chamber. He first scanned the interior with his divine sense before leading the way in.","The Mermaid Queen followed him. Even though she was creeped out by this place, Zu An’s figure gave her inexplicable peace of mind.","Zu An walked straight toward the innermost stone wall. His earlier scan told him that there could be something here. He took the Night Illumination Pearl from the Mermaid Queen, and the content of the stone wall was revealed.","There were many rough lines inscribed onto the stone wall, depicting warped humanoid figures as well as all sorts of blood-red runes. A long wooden pole towered above them, and planted on it was a pitch-black banner. The patterns on the banner felt eerie, even though they had become blurred.","This resembles the Soul Summoning Banner I obtained from the monsters, which can induce instability in one’s soul just by waving it. But compared to the banner depicted on this mural, it’s almost like a baby standing before a giant.","“Myriad Souls Banner!” The Goddess of Wu Mountain spat out three icy-cold words.","“Goddess, do you know this item?” The Mermaid Queen could tell that it was nothing good from the name.","“There are malevolent beings who collect living souls and fuse them into banners. The more souls there are inside a banner, the greater its prowess. Banners with over ten thousand souls are called Myriad Souls Banners, and they wield terrifying prowess. One would have to commit many atrocities to forge something like that.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain looked at the lines on the walls with a frosty gaze. “Most parts of the mural have been erased, but it likely contains the forging method of a Myriad Souls Banner. For even a simple draft to induce such eeriness; its terror far surpasses any of the Myriad Souls Banners known to the world.","“Of course, stringent conditions have to be met to forge such a terrifyingly powerful banner.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain stared at the mural for a long time before adding, “I heard from my father that a Myriad Souls Banner of this caliber requires not just countless souls, but also the aid of someone who possesses the innate Cruel Poison Constitution to fuse lethal poison into it to maximize its killing prowess.”","Zu An was taken aback.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was the Flame Emperor’s daughter, though it was unknown which generation of Flame Emperor her father was. Regardless, the Flame Emperors were from Shennong’s lineage and were medical experts. This gave great credibility to her words.","The forging of this Myriad Souls Banner likely required someone with the Cruel Poison Constitution, and the only person Zu An knew who possessed the Cruel Poison Constitution was Ji Xiaoxi. He was extremely relieved that she hadn’t come to this world.","But the fact that the Mermaid Queen had been transported into this world and that he had been unable to find or contact Ji Xiaoxi in the previous spacetime fragment left him with an ominous feeling.","“Goddess, are there any rumors about a Myriad Souls Banner of this caliber appearing in the world recently?” Zu An asked.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain shook her head. “No, and that’s what makes it frightening. The other party must be hatching a massive scheme.”","“You mentioned earlier that the forging of a Myriad Souls Banner requires the collection of living souls.” The Mermaid Queen’s face suddenly paled, and her voice quivered. “Could this Myriad Souls Banner be behind the abrupt deaths of the Chang clansmen?”","Zu An and the Goddess of Wu Mountain were horrified to hear that. Now that Zu An thought about it, he hadn’t sensed their souls when he inspected their bodies. He'd thought that was because the underworld hadn’t been built in this world yet, so their souls naturally wandered around the world.","But looking back on it, it was more likely that their souls had been siphoned away by the Myriad Souls Banner. Only something as malevolent at that was capable of quietly massacring so many experts.","Why did the Myriad Souls Banner spare me and the Mermaid Queen? And why did Houtu not mention this when Xingtian reported this matter to her?"]},{"number":2606,"title":"Chapter 2606: Chapter 2558: Traces","paragraphs":["Could Houtu be the mastermind behind all this... This random thought that surfaced in Zu An’s mind astounded him.","There were indeed many dubious details surrounding this matter. For instance, he had only entered this world to help the future Houtu collect the Six Paths’ power insignias, and she had also transported the Mermaid Queen into this world. Houtu had to have known that the Myriad Souls Banner was responsible for the Chang clan’s massacre, but she'd chosen not to mention a thing and even told them not to get involved. If she wasn't the culprit, what reason did she have to withhold this information?","Cold sweat began raining down from Zu An’s head.","The Mermaid Queen noticed his pale face and asked in concern, “What’s wrong?”","“It’s nothing. I just thought of something bad,” Zu An replied with a strained smile. I hope I’m reading too much into it. Someone as powerful as Houtu has no reason to do something like this.","He turned to the Goddess of Wu Mountain and asked, “Goddess, can you report this matter to the Celestial Court and have them investigate this issue?”","He wasn't some hero character from some big action flick. There were official departments to deal with such vile situations, so there was no need for a lone ranger like him to worry about it.","He didn’t think that the Celestial Court was behind this. At the very least, they needed to maintain a righteous front, lest they lose the faith of the masses. It was unlikely they would do something that would shake their foundation.","Schemers chose to scheme because they couldn’t do certain things openly. Once the powerhouses of the Celestial Court got involved, it likely wouldn’t be too difficult to resolve this matter.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain nodded. She began writing in mid-air with her slender finger, just like what she'd done when she informed the Celestial Court of Bao Jiang’s death.","After she was done writing the message, she tried to send it upward, but the words flickered feebly before abruptly going out.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s expression darkened. “The world laws are in disarray due to the separation of heaven and earth. We might not be able to come into contact with the Celestial Court any time soon.”","Zu An hadn’t expected there to be such an implication. “Looks like we’ll have to investigate this matter by ourselves. I’m afraid that I’m still unfamiliar with this world. Goddess, is there anything you can deduce from these clues?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain stared at him, unsure of what he meant by ‘still unfamiliar with this world’. However, she didn’t dwell on it and replied, “I spend most of my time in isolation on Wu Mountain, so I don’t know much either.”","Zu An was stunned. Turns out she’s a hermit! This makes things troublesome.","“But we can ask someone.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s eyes lit up.","“Who?”","“The Kaiming Six Shamans!”","Zu An suddenly remembered how her attitude toward him had improved upon learning that he was a friend of the Kaiming Six Shamans. She was likely on good terms with them.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain brought Zu An and the Mermaid Queen back to Wu Mountain. “You can rest at my place first.”","Outsiders would have been shocked to hear that, as there had never been a precedent of her inviting others into her cave as guests.","The Mermaid Queen was confused. “Aren’t we going to meet the Kaiming Six Shamans?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled as she gestured toward the fog. “The fog will relay the news on my behalf.”","Zu An was awed. She must have a high affinity with the fog. No wonder there was a saying in his previous world—'the cloud and rain of Wu Mountain'.","The Mermaid Queen was mesmerized by the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s earlier smile. The latter had a seductive face but a cold disposition, but somehow, these two contrasting qualities came together in harmony for her. Even a woman like me is hopelessly charmed by her. Which man can possibly resist her advance?","At the same time, the Goddess of Wu Mountain was also sizing her up. It's been a while since I last saw such a beautiful woman. I heard she’s the Chang clan’s Saintess, which means that she’s a shaman. When did the Shaman races’ ladies become so beautiful? Even the renowned fairies in the sky can’t hold a candle to her.","Before they knew it, they had arrived at the foot of the Goddess Peak. With a wave of her sleeves, the Goddess of Wu Mountain summoned a cloud before inviting the duo onto it. Zu An and the Mermaid Queen stepped onto the cloud and found that it wasn't as fragile as they thought it would be, even though it was as soft as cotton.","The cloud carried the three of them up the mountain.","This was Zu An’s first time admiring the Goddess Peak up close. Compared to the other mountains in the vicinity, it looked slender, almost like a fair lady’s waist. A waterfall flowed down the peak, and the splashing water turned into the fog that constantly shrouded the peak.","The Mermaid Queen, being from the Ocean races, was extremely sensitive to water. She realized that the water flowing down the waterfall wasn't ordinary water, but condensed ki.","Having studied ‘One Drop of Heaven’s Essence’, Zu An had a deeper understanding of the waterfall. The ki waterfall was like a dragon vein that complemented Wu Mountain, forming a unique protective energy. Intruders risked being struck by lightning. Others wouldn’t be able to enter this place without the goddess’ invitation.","The mountain peak was filled with wondrous flowers and mysterious grasses. It was a scene as beautiful as the two women beside Zu An. The fog was much thicker on the mountain peak, forming a sea of clouds that matched the sea of flowers. It was already nearing sunset, and the golden sun rays shone through the clouds and basked the flowers in its brilliance. It was a splendid sight to behold.","Zu An was awed. “I can see why the goddess prefers to stay here. It’d be hard to leave a place as beautiful as this.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled. “You can stay here longer if you like...”","Halfway through, she realized that her words were inappropriate. The golden rays shining on her face concealed her blushing cheeks. It was only when she turned around that the golden rays finally flowed down her neck.","Zu An was mesmerized. The Goddess of Wu Mountain was usually extremely cold, which contrasted sharply with Pei Mianman, but her shy expression was identical to the latter's.","The Mermaid Queen was a little jealous. I’m still here. Can you not act like this in front of me?","Fortunately, the Kaiming Six Shamans arrived just in time to alleviate the awkwardness.","Upon hearing the Kaiming Six Shamans’ voices, the Goddess of Wu Mountain waved her hand to form a screen in midair with her fog. It resembled a video call.","The Kaiming SIx Shamans were surprised to see Zu An and the Mermaid Queen standing next to the Goddess of Wu Mountain. For so many years, the goddess has never allowed anyone to step foot on her peak.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain summarized what they'd discovered in the cavern. The Kaiming Six Shamans were shocked.","“To think that there’s such a deranged madman!”","“We have to root him out!”","“Such a person should be killed a thousand times over!”","“It’s a pity that the world's laws are in disarray. We aren’t able to contact Lady Houtu at the moment.”","...","While the Kaiming Six Shamans were outraged, a cloud brought the metal fragment they had found in the cavern before the fog screen. “Are you able to tell anything from this?”","The Kaiming Six Shamans gathered their attention to analyze the metal fragment. Soon, they reached their conclusion. “It’s no ordinary metal. It seems to be... No, it has to be from Genesis Mountain. Only that place has such unique copper!”"]},{"number":2607,"title":"Chapter 2607: Chapter 2559: The Celestial Court’s Secrets","paragraphs":["The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s eyebrows shot up. “The Yellow Emperor once mined Genesis Mountain’s copper to forge a copper cauldron at the foot of Thorn Mountain.”","Wu Peng nodded in approval. “The goddess has a good memory. The Yellow Emperor once harvested Genesis Mountain’s copper and forged a cauldron from it. The shamans residing there are known for forging artifacts. Many approach them to ask for a weapon.”","Zu An widened his eyes. “If this metal fragment was from Genesis Mountain, the shamans there must have clues about its maker.”","The trail of clues on Yumen Beiqing had ended at the cavern. Zu An had tried using the jade badge to ask nearby little animals about Yumen Beiqing, but none of them had any other information about her. Right now, their only choice was to head to Genesis Mountain.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain pondered for a moment before turning to Zu An. “You seem unfamiliar with the world’s terrain. I’ll accompany you to Genesis Mountain.”","Zu An was overjoyed. “Thank you, goddess!”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled. “Since Miss Yumen went missing at my place, I also have a responsibility to uphold.”","The Kaiming Six Shamans exchanged confused looks. The Goddess of Wu Mountain rarely leaves her mountain, yet she's been taking trips more frequently than ever. But when they thought about Zu An, it all made sense.","Looking at the Kaiming Six Shaman’s knowing smiles on the screen, the Goddess of Wu Mountain felt embarrassed. She coughed softly and said, “I’ll trouble you to inform the other powers about the situation. Let’s investigate this matter together and root out the mastermind.”","The Kaiming Six Shamans’ faces turned solemn. “Of course. Other than informing the other shamans, we will also do our best to get in touch with Lady Houtu. We’ll keep you informed if there’s any update.”","“I’ll be troubling you.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain nodded.","Seeing her reverting to her usual cold expression, the Kaiming Six Shamans ‘tactfully’ clasped their fists and took their leave.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain turned to Zu An and the Mermaid Queen and said, “I doubt you’re in the mood to rest. Shall we begin making our way to Genesis Mountain?”","“Thank you, goddess.” Zu An was moved. Who’s the one who said the Goddess of Wu Mountain is cold-hearted? Look, isn’t she caring and meticulous?","The Mermaid Queen had the weirdest look on her face. I bet the Goddess of Wu Mountain hasn’t noticed her change in demeanor yet.","The three of them got onto a cloud and headed off. There wasn’t much space on the cloud, so the three of them stood in close proximity to one another. Zu An could smell their unique fragrances.","The Mermaid Queen’s fragrance felt like the ocean breeze gently caressing his skin, and it evoked thoughts about the beautiful yet enigmatic ocean. Meanwhile, he Goddess of Wu Mountain’s fragrance was like a translucent veil, light yet blurry. It was cold, yet it held irresistible allure.","Zu An had to quickly pull himself together and divert his attention elsewhere by starting a conversation. “Goddess, you’re the Flame Emperor’s daughter, so why do you live on Wu Mountain instead of at the Celestial Court? Pardon me if this question offends you. You don’t have to answer it if that’s the case.”","He had always been curious about this world. He'd asked the Goddess of Wu Mountain a similar question before, but the latter snubbed him. He thought it was worth asking the question a second time now that they had gotten closer. He knew this question could pique her displeasure, but he needed as much information as possible to make a reasonable deduction about what was going on. It wasn’t the time to be worried about offending others anymore.","As expected, the Goddess of Wu Mountain fell silent for so long that the Mermaid Queen thought that Zu An could have offended her. But in the end, she spoke up. “It has been many years since the Flame Emperor’s lineage lost control of the throne.”","Seeing that she was willing to speak, Zu An decided to continue probing. “Is it because of the defeat against the Yellow Emperor?”","“You can say so.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain sighed. “The first Celestial Emperor was the Green Emperor. There are many legends surrounding him, so much so that I can’t tell which ones are true.”","“The second Celestial Emperor was Shennong, who was revered by the masses as the Flame Emperor. From him, the title of ‘Flame Emperor’ was passed down for nine generations, but the Celestial Court collectively refers to these Flame Emperors as the second Celestial Emperor.”","The Mermaid Queen never thought that she would hear these secrets. I’d have never encountered all these things if not for big brother Zu. I have to say that he’s truly like an incubus; women just fall in love with him no matter which world he’s in.","Thinking about how she'd been ensnared by him at first sight, the Mermaid Queen’s fair skin turned red like a blossoming tundra rose.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain continued. “The title of ‘Flame Emperor’ was passed down through the generations, but each successor was weaker than the previous. By the ninth generation, a man from the Xuanyuan clan rose through the ranks, and he later became known as the Yellow Emperor.","“The balance of power began tipping. There were multiple wars between the Flame Emperor and the Yellow Emperor, and the Yellow Emperor eventually emerged victorious. With that, the Flame Emperor’s lineage completely lost power in the Celestial Court.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain briefly paused before adding, “I am the youngest daughter of the final Flame Emperor.”","She hadn't explained it explicitly, but Zu An and the Mermaid Queen could already understand why she had taken up permanent residence in Wu Mountain. A new clan had taken over the Celestial Court. It was benevolent of the new rulers to spare her life, so how could they allow her to remain in the Celestial Court?","Zu An suddenly remembered what he had heard before and asked, “You mentioned that when they feel that their term is up, each Celestial Emperor passes down the position to their successor so that they can go into seclusion and pursue the great dao. Did the previous Flame Emperors turn a blind eye to this matter?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain shook her head. “Entities like them view the pursuit of the great dao to be their ultimate goal. Their descendants’ affairs are fleeting clouds to them. Besides, the Green Emperor was the founder of the Yellow Emperor’s lineage. The position has merely switched to the other side; the previous Celestial Emperors would not bother themselves with that.”","Zu An nodded. I wonder what the great dao that all these Celestial Emperors are pursuing is.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain continued, “The subsequent Celestial Emperors came from the Yellow Emperor’s lineage. After the Yellow Emperor was White Emperor Shaohao, followed by the incumbent Celestial Emperor Zhuanxu, who is also Shaohao’s nephew and is known as the Black Emperor.”","Zu An was surprised. “Why did Shaohao pass the position to his nephew instead of his son?”","“There are many speculations.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain took a moment to construe her thoughts before continuing, “Most people believe that the White Emperor’s sons failed to achieve anything significant compared to Zhuanxu. While the Celestial Emperor’s position can be passed from father to son, the successor must also prove himself worthy of the position.”","Doubt surfaced in Zu An’s mind. “What’s the situation with Emperor Jun then?”","“Jun is White Emperor Shaohao’s offspring. Many celestials support his ascension as the next Celestial Emperor, but Black Emperor Zhuanxu had a grandson named Zhongli who was highly talented too. There was intense competition between both sides. Jun claimed the upper hand and won the position of the official successor, but many still had a high opinion of Zhongli’s future.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain suddenly sighed. “But who could have thought Zhongli would sacrifice himself for world peace? We all underestimated him.”","These bits of information helped Zu An to clear up his thoughts, guiding him toward an answer.","At this point, the Goddess of Wu Mountain hesitantly spoke up. “The White Emperor’s lineage and the Black Emperor’s lineage are not on good terms. It would be best for you to steer clear of their fight.”","“All this over the Celestial Emperor’s position?” the Mermaid Queen remarked.","“That’s not all. The White Emperor’s lineage worships the phoenix, whereas the Black Emperor’s lineage worships the dragon. Even though both are from the Green Emperor’s lineage, they come from different maternal races. The White Emperor’s maternal race is the Phoenix race, whereas the Black Emperor’s maternal race has inherited the dragon’s bloodline.","“The Dragons and the Phoenixes were the world’s powerhouses before the Fiends and the Shamans came to power, and they were mortal enemies in that era. The enmity was passed down through the generations. That’s why you mustn’t get involved in the fight between those two factions, or else the only fate awaiting you is death,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain said.","Zu An was stunned. A famous daoist work in his previous life known as ‘The Cloud Bookcase with the Seven Labels: Records of Spirit Treasures’ once mentioned—’There was a calamity named Longhan[1]. After Longhan, the world transformed and entered the era of Yankang.’","Many webnovels in his previous life had built on that setting to talk about the war between the dragons and the phoenixes. Could I have inadvertently stumbled upon the truth here?","1. Longhan refers to an era of calamity, when the world is dominated by the Ancestral Dragons, the Origin Phoenixes, and the Genesis Qilins, and they fought one another for supremacy. ☜"]},{"number":2608,"title":"Chapter 2608: Chapter 2560: Aura of Death","paragraphs":["As a transmigrator, Zu An had read plenty of legends and webnovel settings in his previous life, so what the Goddess of Wu Mountain shared felt extremely familiar to him.","“Could I be in a fantasy world...” He shook his head and dispelled those miscellaneous thoughts.","He focused his attention on the issues before him. He'd been misled by his previous life’s impression, thinking that all the so-called emperors were humans. From the looks of it now, the emperors and even the celestials were all fiends. But that raised the question—where were the humans?","Upon hearing Zu An ask about that, the Goddess of Wu Mountain replied, “Lady Nuwa created the humans based on the traits of both the fiends and shamans, but humans turned out to be too weak. They don’t have the formidable power that shamans and fiends harness in their bloodlines. They have some prosperous tribes, but compared to the fiends and the shamans, they aren’t even worth a mention.”","She eyed Zu An with a frown. “On that note, I have never seen a human as strong as you.”","“I guess I’m just lucky,” Zu An replied in self-derision. I guess human civilization is still in its elementary phase.","“Where’s Lady Nuwa now?” Zu An wanted to gather more information.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain shook her head. “It has been a long time since she last showed herself. Some say she was conferred sainthood for her merit in creating humans, but there are also those who claim she has already passed away. There is no way to tell which is true.”","“Sainthood...” Zu An fell into contemplation. “Sainthood is the level that the Celestial Emperors are seeking to attain, right?”","Zu An had also asked her this question back then, but she hadn’t answered. This time, she briefly hesitated before sharing, “Yes, they are pursuing the legendary sainthood.”","“What saints are there in the world?” Seeing that she was willing to answer his question, Zu An was determined to squeeze out as much information as he could.","“Sainthood is an elusive level. The only ones said to have reached that level are the Green Emperor and Lady Nuwa. I can’t say for sure who else is a saint,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain explained. “Sainthood cannot be reached through rote cultivation. One has to find the dao suited for them and make it resonate with the great dao. Ever since ancient times, there have been many powerful entities, but many of them hit a bottleneck. They were only half a step away from achieving sainthood, yet they were unable to bridge the gap no matter what they do.”","Zu An mulled over those words. “Earlier, you mentioned that Lady Nuwa achieved sainthood from the merit of creating humans? Why is creating humans a significant feat? Aren’t the rulers of the world the Shaman races and the Fiend races?”","“Many are perplexed by that too. Humans are a weak race who are only decent in terms of reproductive prowess and learning ability.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain frowned in confusion. “In terms of reproduction, they can’t compete with beasts. In terms of learning, no matter how they learn, there’s no way they can compete with the Shaman races and Fiend races’ powerful bloodlines.”","At this point, she turned to Zu An with an apologetic look. “I don’t mean to insult you. In fact, your appearance made me realize that human potential could be unlimited. You were able to grasp the Fiend races’ cultivation skills and learn the Shaman races’ bloodline ability.”","Zu An knew she was referring to the shaman blood essence he had received from Houtu. “Goddess, please be assured that I’m not bothered by those words. I think I have a rough idea how Lady Nuwa reached sainthood. Humans must have prospered in the future, and this huge merit went back to her.”","“What makes you so certain that humans will prosper in the future?” The Goddess of Wu Mountain looked at Zu An with her beautiful eyes.","“I saw it in a dream.” Zu An couldn’t tell her that he had transmigrated here from the future. This world had deities and the Celestial Court; he was worried that the revelation that he was from the future could lead to unexpected dangers.","The Mermaid Queen looked at the Goddess of Wu Mountain with a conflicted expression. I got ahead of myself. I felt jealous seeing her chatting along so well with big brother Zu, so I forgot that we aren’t from the same era. On that note, I’m also not from the same era as big brother Zu.","She felt disappointed, and she looked at the Goddess of Wu Mountain with empathetic eyes.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain chuckled. “Don’t put yourself down. Cultivators beyond a certain level may see revelations in their dreams. Your dream may come true in the future, and you could become an important figure for the humans.” The moonlight shone on her face, causing her fair skin to glow with mesmerizing radiance.","Zu An was taken aback. I didn’t know I could use such an explanation too.","The Mermaid Queen’s interest was piqued. “Goddess, what are the different cultivation levels in this world? What’s the Celestial Emperor’s cultivation level?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain had refused to answer this question before, but there was no reason for her to withhold the information now. “Mortals, be it through cultivation or fortuitous encounters, can ascend to immortality and reach the level of Sky Immortal. Above Sky Immortals are True Immortals, followed by High Immortals. High Immortal is the limit for most people.","“Above High Immortals are the Golden Immortals. If there’s an insurmountable gap between mortals and Sky Immortals, the same gap lies between Golden Immortals and other immortals. Most Celestial Emperors are at that level.”","Zu An wondered what cultivation level he was at. I only ascended not long ago, but I have a feeling that I’m stronger than most Sky Immortals. I’m nowhere on par with the Celestial Emperors, so I guess I should be at the level of a True Immortal or a High Immortal.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain continued her explanation, “Above the Golden Immortals are the Overarching Golden Immortals. Such entities are a mere half step away from sainthood. Most retired Celestial Emperors are able to reach the level of Overarching Golden Immortals, but whether they reach sainthood or not depends on their fate. That is the level closest to sainthood that I’m aware of...”","That’s pretty similar to the novel settings I saw in my previous life. How cliche, though I guess that makes it easy to remember. Zu An wondered if this similarity was just a coincidence, or if there was something more to it.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain pointed toward the distance and said, “That’s Genesis Mountain. The shamans residing there are known for their ability to forge artifacts, and many renowned weapons are created there. It’s rumored that the sound of their hammering can be heard even from fifty kilometers away...”","The Mermaid Queen was perplexed. “Why is it so quiet?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain frowned. She could tell that something was amiss too.","Zu An’s expression darkened. “I sense the aura of death.”"]},{"number":2609,"title":"Chapter 2609: Chapter 2561: Bizarre Prayer","paragraphs":["Due to being the master of the underworld, Zu An had a heightened sensitivity toward death, even though it hadn’t been established in this world yet.","The mountain was well-lit, but it was so quiet that it felt eerie under the darkness of the night.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain grimly warned, “Be careful.”","She commanded the cloud beneath them to accelerate. However, as they approached Genesis Mountain, a wave of heat surged at them. Even the cloud they were riding on started slowly dissipating.","Zu An frowned. It felt as if nothing ever good happened whenever he encountered such intense heat.","With a wave of her sleeves, the Goddess of Wu Mountain released water vapor, causing the cloud to become more condensed. “Genesis Mountain is a giant volcano. The shamans turned the volcano into a massive furnace that could be used to forge the strongest weapons in the world.” She gestured to the nearby mountains and continued, “The earth flame from the main peak is drawn to the surrounding 72 peaks to form smaller furnaces.”","By then, Zu An and the Mermaid Queen could already see Genesis Mountain’s main peak, which had a circular opening. A crimson light shone from the opening, dyeing the surrounding sky the color of blood. The other 72 peaks were positioned in a formation around the main peak. Zu An could sense light-blue ancient runes inscribed on the mountains. They resonated with Genesis Mountain’s main peak to form a massive formation that allowed earth flames to flow safely and smoothly.","There was a strong, stinging smell in the air—it was the smell of metal, precious material, and sulfur. Who knew how many overpowered weapons had been born here?","As they got closer, the Goddess of Wu Mountain was no longer able to maintain her cloud, so they had no choice but to stop on a nearby mountain peak.","Zu An looked at the formations flickering in the sky and said, “The protection formation is still functioning. It would have attacked us if we continued flying straight in.”","“That’s weird. How did something happen when the protection formation is still functioning normally?” The Mermaid Queen surveyed their surroundings. It had been some time since they arrived in Genesis Mountain’s vicinity, but they hadn’t seen a single shaman.","“It is bizarre. There should have been battle marks if it was an invasion.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain mulled it over. “The Genesis Shamans amassed a sea of wealth from forging weapons, and that drew unwanted attention upon them. However, the Genesis Shamans have powerful weapons and defensive formations that are also strong enough to deter most troublemakers. Several renowned experts invaded Genesis Mountain, only to suffer tragic deaths. Since then, no one has dared to target this place.” She couldn’t make sense of the situation either.","“Let’s head in to take a look.” Among the trio, Zu An had the best grasp of the situation. The death aura inside Genesis Mountain was extremely dense.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain nodded. She led the way, as she had been here before.","The surrounding 72 mountain peaks were connected to the main peak via suspension bridges. Red rivers flowed beneath the bridges, but on second glance, they were made of flowing lava. Smoke lingered in the air. The suspension bridges were made out of black metal and wooden panels. Walking on them seared one’s legs; it was a wonder that the bridges hadn’t burned up yet.","While Zu An was wondering how the Genesis Shamans ensured the suspension bridges’ safety, he noticed the Goddess of Wu Mountain suddenly stopping. He asked, “What’s wrong?”","“It’s nothing.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain continued walking while casually fanning herself and wiping off her sweat. Her clothes were a bit more open than usual, revealing her snowy skin.","“Big brother Zu, why are you so dense? I’m from the Ocean races, and her Wu Mountain is manifested from a fog. We don’t do well in such hot environments,” the Mermaid Queen tugged Zu An’s sleeve and secretly reminded him.","Zu An looked at the Mermaid Queen. A hair strand was sticking to her face, and her cheeks were flushed red. Realization finally dawned on him. He secretly used the Snow Phoenix’s ability to cool down the surrounding air. Snowflakes even began drifting down.","“How beautiful.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain instinctively reached out to touch a snowflake, only to realize right after that Zu An was caring for her. She turned to him and said, “Thank you.”","“You've helped me a lot along the way. This is nothing compared to that.” Zu An smiled.","His smile was so warm that the Goddess of Wu Mountain didn’t dare to look him in the eye. She averted her gaze as she remarked, “It’s very rare for someone to be able to control multiple kinds of elemental ki like you.”","Zu An was surprised. “Is it the norm to only be able to use one element?”","Most cultivators in the future also specialized in a single element. Could it be the same for the more powerful ancient era too?","“Not exactly. Most shamans and fiends have powerful bloodline powers, so they often specialize in a single field and develop it to its maximum potential. It’s rare for someone to simultaneously cultivate multiple elemental abilities without suffering any setbacks... Is this due to humans’ learning ability too?” the Goddess of Wu Mountain wondered.","By this point, they had already reached the main peak.","Genesis Mountain had been modified into a nine-leveled forging platform. Nine was the number of extremity, which was why many world structures tended to involve the number nine. Each level consisted of a vast space filled with forging stands, a market, and residences, resembling a miniature city. The space became smaller the higher up one went, but there were also improvements in the scale of the forging stands and the extravagance of the residences. Going up the forging platform meant an increase in standing.","The suspension bridge led them to the fifth level, but there wasn't a single person to be seen. The massive city felt like a ghost town.","They made their way up to the highest level before coming to a halt. The ninth level was much smaller than the levels below, but it was still a vast area. At its center was a massive copper sculpture that was over three hundred meters tall, depicting a shaman holding a hammer.","Had Zu An and the others seen this sculpture under normal circumstances, they would have been awed by its craftsmanship. However, their attention was instead drawn to the ground.","Countless people were kneeling before the sculpture. Their clothes suggested that they were the Genesis Shamans. It looked as if they were praying to the copper sculpture with faint smiles. And yet, this seemingly heart-warming sight felt sinister, because all of them were dead.","The Mermaid Queen leaned toward Zu An and murmured, “Big brother Zu, their plight resembles that of the Chang clan.”"]},{"number":2610,"title":"Chapter 2610: Chapter 2562: A Friend","paragraphs":["The many Genesis Shamans gathered around the sculpture looked calm; there were even faint smiles on their faces. It felt unnerving.","Zu An squatted down to inspect the nearest Genesis Shaman’s body. “He's been dead for 12 to 16 hours.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was taken aback. “How do you know?”","Zu An replied, “His body has turned cold and stiffened. You can see marks that don’t disappear under pressure all over his body. These are signs that appear on those who have been dead for around twelve hours. Beyond that, the body will start loosening up.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was awed. “You’re well-educated, to know such information.”","“It’s all the wisdom of the predecessors.” Zu An smiled. There had been so many detective shows in his previous life; it wasn't that difficult to pick up bits and pieces of information. Besides, he had also picked up some things during his time as an Embroidered Envoy.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain murmured contemplatively, “I have underestimated the humans’ ability to learn.”","Sensing the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s amazed gaze, the Mermaid Queen puffed her chest up in pride, but she soon felt troubled once more. It’s a good thing that my lover is outstanding, but it’s also troublesome because he’s too outstanding, so he naturally draws in other women.","Zu An walked to the center of the crowd, where there was a Genesis Shaman who was standing instead of kneeling like the others. It looked as if he was about to bow down and pay his respects. This shaman was old, but he was more muscular than the others. His clothes were also visibly more opulent.","“He’s the Genesis Shaman race’s chieftain, Yanshan. I have met him before,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain explained with a pale face.","“The Genesis Shamans feel rather strong, as you mentioned.” Zu An could sense the valiance and strength of the Genesis Shamans even though they had already taken their last breaths.","“The experts of the Genesis Shaman race are all gathered here; this is a force to be reckoned with. What power could claim all their lives in an instant?” the Goddess of Wu Mountain wondered with a frown.","Zu An inspected the surroundings before rubbing his hands together. “Their souls are nowhere to be found. They must have died to that Myriad Souls Banner.”","“The forging of the Myriad Souls Banner must have been a success.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain turned increasingly paler. She understood what this all signified.","“Even the Myriad Souls Banner shouldn’t be able to kill so many experts without them fighting back. And you mentioned earlier that this place is guarded by a powerful protection formation!” the Mermaid Queen exclaimed.","“Indeed. The Myriad Souls Banner might be formidable, but it doesn’t have the power to quietly siphon so many souls at once. The Genesis Shamans should have had time to activate their protection formation to guard against the invader.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain contemplated. “Unless the culprit was an insider who attacked them while they were having a mass prayer.”","“Or the culprit is someone the Genesis Shamans weren’t guarded against,” Zu An added.","While they were speculating on the possibilities, a commotion suddenly echoed in the distance.","“Hm? All the Genesis Shamans are gathered here?”","“Their expressions look weird.”","“They seem to be all dead!”","The voices initially sounded confused, but they were quickly overtaken by shock.","Zu An and the others looked over.","A group had just entered the ninth level from another direction. Their leader was draped in a scarlet cloak, and his robe was embroidered with fiery auspicious clouds. A fiery-red crimson jade was fastened to his waist. He had defined facial features and deep, penetrating eyes. His eyebrows resembled flickering flames, and he wielded a copper flame axe. Flames seemed to quietly seethe around him, making him look so imposing that it was hard to look straight at him.","Zu An narrowed his eyes. He’s strong! I can feel immense pressure from him even when we’re this far away.","The group also noticed Zu An’s group. “There are survivors!”","“They aren’t Genesis Shamans.”","“Are they the culprits behind this massacre?”","...","Zu An’s eyes twitched. It was such a familiar scene. Kuafu and Xingtian also had the same misunderstanding the last time they were at the Chang residence. To avoid conflict, he quickly explained, “We just arrived here too and found them dead. May I know your names?”","Though it is a huge coincidence for them to appear here at the same time. Could they be the culprits trying to frame us?","“Empty words! We shall capture and interrogate you to get to the bottom of this!” The red-cloaked leader harrumphed. At his order, several golden-armored warriors rushed at Zu An.","Zu An was flabbergasted.","The Mermaid Queen was irked too. She began strumming her Deep Sea Harp, prompting the golden-armored warriors to fight among themselves.","Zu An was awed. These golden-armored warriors are nowhere weaker than her in terms of cultivation, so much so that she wouldn’t have been a match for them in a direct confrontation. Her powerful control and support skills make her more suited for chaotic battlefields.","The red-cloaked man’s eyebrows shot up, and he roared, “What a measly trick!”","His booming voice shook the golden-armored warriors out of their daze. The realization that someone had just made a fool out of them made the golden-armored warriors so angry that they charged at the Mermaid Queen.","“Halt!” With a wave of her sleeves, the Goddess of Wu Mountain summoned fog that stopped the golden-armored warriors. “How can you resort to violence without getting to the bottom of the matter? Are you planning to silence us because you’re the real culprits?”","“Audacious! How dare you speak to me, a celestial, like that!” The red-cloaked man was infuriated. He put down his copper axe and unleashed two waves of fire dragons toward her.","As beautiful as the Goddess of Wu Mountain was, he saw her as little more than a skeleton wearing makeup. He'd noticed that the two ladies controlled the water element, which made him the perfect match against them.","Even before the two fire dragons could reach the Goddess of Wu Mountain, the shirts and hair of the deceased Genesis Shamans began curling up.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was taken aback. His flames are formidable! Each fire dragon harnesses terrifying destructive prowess, not to mention that this environment is disadvantageous to me. I might not be able to take this attack.","Just then, Zu An appeared before her. He quickly formed a series of hand seals and unleashed a giant lotus against the two fire dragons. This terrain greatly boosts the prowess of fire ki; I can use fire to vanquish fire.","A loud explosion ensued. The two fire dragons and the lotus disappeared at the same time. The fog hindering the golden-armored warriors’ movements was vaporized, and some nearby Genesis Shaman corpses were burnt to a crisp.","Zu An and the other frowned.","“White Lotus Flame and Phoenix Flame... I see, you possess the phoenix bloodline. No wonder you’re so arrogant!” the red-cloaked man sneered. He began rising into the air as the flames seething around him grew increasingly tangible.","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. He suddenly recalled the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s warning. Considering how hostile he is toward phoenixes, could he be a descendant of the dragons?","Even so, this was no time to be thinking too hard. With the other party’s aura intensifying furiously, he knew he also had to go all out to survive this encounter.","Just then, a coy voice exclaimed, “Stop! He’s a friend!”"]},{"number":2611,"title":"Chapter 2611: Chapter 2563: Disappeared","paragraphs":["Zu An looked over in delight.","A white-robed woman had lifted her skirt and was frantically running over. Her black hair was casually twisted into a bun on her head. A couple of loose hair strands hung next to her ears, contrasting with her fair, slender neck. She had peach blossom eyes that would seem to be brimming with seductiveness even when looking at a dog, though the more palpable emotions that could be felt from them now were delight and excitement.","Her face was reddened from her sprinting. Perhaps due to her robe tightening around her waist, her chest bounced more than usual due to her movements. It added a tender touch to the harsh environment of Genesis Mountain.","“Yuqing!” Zu An was overjoyed. He hadn’t expected to meet her here. For a moment, he was worried that she was just a lookalike like the Goddess of Wu Mountain, but the familiar soft touch when she pounced into his arms made him realize that he hadn’t misidentified her.","“Big brother Zu...” Yun Yuqing buried her face in Zu An’s chest as she sobbed. She embraced Zu An with great force, as if fearing that he would disappear if she loosened her grip.","Zu An asked, “Yuqing, what are you doing here?”","He looked around, but Ji Xiaoxi and Jiang Luofu were nowhere to be found. This unnerved him. When they first arrived at the spacetime fragment, the three of them had decided to move together, but unfortunately, he'd been unable to find them afterward. He had entered this world where the Celestial Court existed via the Fiend races’ imperial tomb, so how had Yun Yuqing gotten here?","Many doubts surfaced in Zu An’s mind.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain glanced at the Mermaid Queen. Yet another gorgeous woman has leaped into her lover’s arms, but why is she not angry in the slightest?","The Mermaid Queen was conflicted. Zu An had told her about his companions before, so she was mentally prepared for this scenario. However, she hadn’t expected them to reunite under such circumstances.","This woman is truly beautiful, but again, a woman who catches big brother Zu’s eyes can’t possibly be ordinary. How should I introduce myself to her later? Should I say that I just got married to big brother Zu? Would that make me sound like a vixen?","“Miss Yun, who’s this guy?” The man shrouded in flames descended to their side. He glanced at Zu An with wary eyes, particularly since Yun Yuqing was embracing him.","“He’s my husband,” Yun Yuqing was embarrassed, but she still gathered up her courage to say so.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain lifted her eyebrows. She secretly glanced at the Mermaid Queen once more. Oyoy, that woman is proclaiming her dominance now. Hm? Why does it seem as if I can’t wait for them to fight each other?","The Mermaid Queen frowned. I was hesitating about whether to first assert my dominance, but she beat me to it.","Zu An was perplexed too. “Yuqing, who is this?”","The man took a courteous tone with Yun Yuqing, and it didn’t seem to be because he wanted to court her. Rather, his respect for her came from the bottom of his heart. This is weird, especially considering the huge difference in their strength. What’s their relationship?","“This is the Celestial Court’s Fire Celestial Lord Wuhui,” Yun Yuqing said. “He saved me when I was in danger.”","“Fire Celestial Wuhui? Celestial Court?” Zu An was taken aback. No wonder those golden-armored warriors look so familiar. They're celestial soldiers!","The Goddess of Wu Mountain sent a telepathic message to Zu An to explain, “The Celestial Court’s Fire Celestial governs the world’s flames. It is a highly respected position. Zhongli was the previous Fire Celestial, but he returned to the great dao while separating heaven from earth. The Celestial Court might have called Wuhui back to take the position.”","Zu An nodded. No wonder his flames are so formidable. So it turns out he’s the Fire Celestial.","Wuhui assessed Zu An and remarked approvingly, “Miss Yun, your husband is formidable.”","But Zu An was more concerned with what Yun Yuqing had just mentioned. “You said you met with danger. What happened? And how did you appear... here?”","Yun Yuqing bit her lips. “After we parted ways, big sister Jiang, little sister Xiaoxi, and I investigated the whereabouts of the Brilliant Pinflower. We soon learned that it could be located in the Fiend races’ imperial tomb, so we made our way over to take a look. However, the area was already occupied by the monsters, so we could only continue our search discreetly.","“We eventually found a chance to slip into the Fiend races’ imperial tomb, but we were suddenly struck by a white light that caused the surrounding space to be plunged into disarray. Before we knew it, we were already in this world.”","The white light likely refers to the opening of the dungeon. They must have been caught off guard and were swept in as well. But this is a good thing too. It would be disastrous if they were caught by the Monster Lord or the Lord of Slaughter.","“Where are Principal Jiang and Xiaoxi?”","Yun Yuqing’s eyes reddened. “Ever since we arrived in this world, we were treading carefully to understand what was going on, as well as looking for a way to return. But we stumbled upon a mysterious altar, and Xiaoxi’s Cruel Poison Constitution was suddenly triggered by a mysterious power...”","“What?!” Zu An was horrified. He knew how potent Ji Xiaoxi’s Cruel Poison Constitution was, and the Firecloud Cave’s master had just warned him that once the Cruel Poison Constitution flared up, the chances of survival were slim.","The absence of Ji Xiaoxi and Jiang Luofu caused his heart to lurch.","“We tried to suppress Ji Xiaoxi’s Cruel Poison Constitution, but to no avail. A mysterious man suddenly arrived then, and he said he was delighted that such a constitution existed in this world. He helped stabilize Ji Xiaoxi’s condition,” Yun Yuqing replied.","How strong must that person be to suppress the Cruel Poison Constitution?","“We were initially thankful to him, but it turns out that he merely coveted Xiaoxi’s unique constitution. He first kidnapped her before attempting to kill us.” Yun Yuqing’s face paled. The thought of what had happened then frightened her. “Fortunately, we were able to survive thanks to your protection artifacts, the Last Breath Talisman, and big sister Jiang’s scale artifact.”","Zu An’s expression darkened. That mysterious man was vicious enough to try to take their lives just like that.","“Where’s Principal Jiang?” he anxiously asked.","“When we woke up, we were in despair. That mysterious man was too powerful. We wouldn’t have been a match for him no matter how many more years we cultivated.” Yun Yuqing glanced at Zu An. “If only we'd known that you were in this world too back then.”","She continued, “Big sister Jiang sees Xiaoxi as her daughter. She mumbled that she would pay any price to save Xiaoxi. She told me a bunch of things, as if entrusting her final will to me. Then one day, by the time I woke up, she'd suddenly disappeared.”","“Disappeared?” Zu An widened his eyes."]},{"number":2612,"title":"Chapter 2612: Chapter 2564: Clearing the Fog","paragraphs":["“Yes, she disappeared.” Yun Yuqing was also confused when she recalled the situation.","“Try recalling the situation. Given your cultivation, even the slightest breeze shouldn’t have escaped your notice,” Zu An urged.","“I searched the area, but there were no traces of anyone else.” Yun Yuqing recalled the details of the situation. “If I have to point out anything peculiar, I think I heard big sister Jiang making a wish. I was too tired, and I thought she was wishing for Xiaoxi’s safety, so I didn’t pay it much heed and went to sleep. Later, I was jolted awake by a nearby flash of white light. By then, big sister Jiang was already gone. I don’t know if she had long disappeared by then, or if she disappeared along with the white light.”","“White light?” Zu An frowned. The problem probably lies with the white light.","“Can you describe the white light?” Fire Celestial Wuhui suddenly asked.","“I don’t know much because I was still in a groggy state. I merely saw a brilliant flash.” Yun Yuqing tried her best to jog her memory as she spoke. “The white light was bright, but not glaring. I felt small and insignificant, as if I was a speck of dirt in the universe. It was an odd feeling.”","“Oh?” Wuhui spent a moment in thought. “It sounds as if a celestial might have descended. You said you overheard her making a wish, right? Sometimes, when an entity makes a strong wish, it can draw the attention of a celestial.”","Yun Yuqing was overjoyed to hear that. “You’re the Fire Celestial, right? Can you help me investigate which celestial was summoned?”","Wuhui puffed up his chest. “Leave it to me. But due to the separation of heaven and earth, I’m unable to contact the Celestial Court for the time being, so I can only help you look into it when I return to the Celestial Court in the future.”","His willingness to help convinced Zu An to drop the grudge he had against Wuhui for recklessly attacking him. “Thank you, Lord Fire Celestial.”","Wuhui eyed Zu An with a confused frown. “How weird. You’re a human. When did someone as powerful as you appear among the humans?”","“It’s a coincidence.” Zu An couldn’t explain his background.","Yun Yuqing knew his background was a secret too, so she changed the topic. “Xiaoxi was captured, and big sister Jiang went missing, so I could only roam the world while searching for them. However, I was unable to do anything at all...”","Sensing her low spirits, Zu An gently grabbed her hand. She must have felt helpless, being transported into a foreign world filled with powerful entities while watching her companions disappear one after another. On top of that, she didn’t know I’m in this world too. She must have felt lonely.","Feeling the warmth of Zu An’s hand, Yun Yuqing calmed down a little. “Later, I chanced upon Lord Fire Celestial. He said that I have the purest Fiend races’ bloodline and helped me a lot along the way.”","“Fiend races?” Zu An was surprised. Isn’t she a demon?","Hold on, the Monster World’s True Demon race often bragged about being the descendants of the Celestial Court’s Fiend races. Could it be that Yun Yuqing’s Demon race are the true descendants of the Celestial Court’s Fiend races instead?","Sensing his confusion, Wuhui explained, “Miss Yun is the Green Emperor’s descendant. Her bloodline is so pure as to be rare even among Celestial Emperors. I was curious why there are no records of her in the Celestial Court, so I was planning to bring her to the Celestial Court and have the Celestial Emperor take a look at her.”","Noticing Zu An’s wary eyes, he added with a harrumph, “Calm down, there’s no faking her bloodline. This is a fortuitous encounter for her.”","“I understand. Thank you, Lord Fire Celestial.” Zu An bowed with a smile.","Wuhui’s complexion finally looked a little better.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain suddenly echoed in Zu An’s ears, “Wuhui only gave you half the picture. It is a huge fortuitous encounter for her, but the same cannot be said for you. Based on what I know, the Celestial Court forbids romance between celestials and humans. They wouldn’t allow someone or her pure bloodline to be sullied by a human.”","Zu An glanced at the Goddess of Wu Mountain, only to see that her lips were still, and she wasn’t even looking at him. She was secretly warning him of the pitfall. He chuckled softly and replied telepathically, “I’d only be happy for her if she could have such a fortuitous encounter...”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was surprised. Does he intend to give up on this relationship? That would be a gentleman’s way of doing things, but it feels regretful.","But Zu An quickly continued, “Even so, no one can get in the way of our relationship, not even the Celestial Court. If it comes to that, I’ll just turn everything upside down.”","“You mustn’t say such blasphemous words! If the Celestial Court learned about it... Putting all things aside, this Fire Celestial would fight you to the death!” The Goddess of Wu Mountain was horrified, and she quickly warned him. But at the same time, a faint smile formed on her lips. This man is indeed different from the others. There’s some kind of vibrancy and wildness to him that always catches others off guard.","“What are you doing here? How did these Genesis Shamans die?” Wuhui asked.","Yun Yuqing knew the man, and judging from their conversation, he had learned that one of the two ladies was the lofty Goddess of Wu Mountain. These made them unlikely to be the culprits. Though I heard the goddess usually holes herself up on Wu Mountain. What brings her here?","“We came here to investigate another case...” Zu An explained the situation to Wuhui.","“Myriad Souls Banner!” Wuhui’s flames suddenly flared up. “Who dares to commit such a vile and despicable deed?! I’ll make sure his soul burns for ten thousand years if I ever find him!”","“I’ll have to trouble the Celestial Court to look into this matter.” Zu An had been planning on handing this matter to the Celestial Court in the first place.","“We will take responsibility for this issue, but unfortunately, we are unable to reach the Celestial Court at the moment. For the time being, I’ll investigate it by myself,” Wuhui said. The separation of heaven and earth had caused great inconveniences for many issues.","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. He turned to Yun Yuqing and asked, “Speaking of which, what brings you here?”","“We were investigating the mysterious man who kidnapped Xiaoxi. We stumbled upon a clue and rushed here to see if we could find him. I didn’t expect to see you here.” Yun Yuqing was heartened. It was even more moving to reunite with her lover in a foreign land.","The Mermaid Queen suddenly spoke up. “Could the mysterious man who kidnapped Miss Ji be the same person who is forging the Myriad Souls Banner? The goddess previously mentioned that forging a powerful Myriad Souls Banner would require the concoction of special poisons.”"]},{"number":2613,"title":"Chapter 2613: Chapter 2565: All Clues Are Before Us","paragraphs":["Zu An’s expression darkened. He'd been so happy to be reunited with Yun Yuqing that he only thought about this possibility when the Mermaid Queen mentioned it. He turned to the Goddess of Wu Mountain and asked with a quivering voice, “What will happen to the person with the Cruel Poison Constitution during the forging of the Myriad Souls Banner?”","“Don’t worry. The person with the Cruel Poison Constitution will only be assimilated into the Myriad Souls Banner at the final step of the forging to maximize its prowess. The forging isn’t at its final step yet, so Miss Ji shouldn’t be in danger yet,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain consoled him, knowing what he was worried about.","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief.","Even though the Chang clan and the Genesis Shaman race had likely been wiped out by the Myriad Souls Banner, it was still considered a small-scale massacre compared to what it was truly capable of. There were legends that when a true Myriad Souls Banner appeared, the sky would darken and all lives would be assimilated.","Wuhui also said, “I have heard some rumors about the Myriad Souls Banner. Its flagpole is usually made of thousand-year-old yin wood from Scholar Trees or coffin wood. However, this Myriad Souls Banner is a special one. Its flagpole is made from yin wood that has been soaked with malevolent energies from ancient battlefields, or corpse ki, for at least ten thousand years.","“The banner normally has to be embroidered with human skin, but neither the Chang clansmen nor the Genesis Shamans have been skinned, so the culprit must have opted for another method. The other alternative is to use cloth stripped from powerful corpses overflowing with resentment.","“Other than that, the Myriad Souls Banner requires a core—a powerful vengeful spirit dripping with resentment to control other vengeful spirits. The mysterious man has likely chosen your friend as the main vengeful spirit. Your friend might be lacking in strength, but her unique poison constitution makes up for that. If the forging succeeds, the resulting Myriad Souls Banner will be far stronger than the world has ever seen. Wherever it appears, countless will die.”","“That means Xiaoxi is in danger!” Zu An was alarmed.","“It takes 81 days to forge the core. Miss Yun, how many days has it been since your companion was kidnapped?” Wuhui asked Yun Yuqing.","Yun Yuqing’s face turned pale. “It has been 63 days.”","“Then you still have 18 days to rescue your friend,” Wuhui said. “We can investigate based on the materials I have just mentioned.”","But Zu An wasn’t as optimistic. While it took 81 days to forge the banner core, each day that passed meant another day of suffering for Xiaoxi. Furthermore, the forging of the banner core was a malevolent process. There was no saying whether XIaoxi would still be alive near the end of the forging process.","“Yuqing, what abilities did the mysterious man use when he kidnapped Xiaoxi? Was there anything unusual?” Zu An knew Wuhui’s solution was unfeasible; Xiaoxi wouldn’t last that long.","Wuhui harrumphed. “Do you think I wouldn’t have asked that? The strength disparity between Miss Yun and the mysterious man is so great that there would have been no way for her to force the other party to reveal his specialization.”","Indeed, there was nothing useful in what Yun Yuqing described afterward. It was just like a human stomping on a roadside ant; how could the ant tell how much strength the human used and his posture when stomping down?","Zu An fell into deep thought to organize the information he had gathered thus far.","The Chang clan’s massacre. Yumen Beiqing’s disappearance. The Genesis Shaman race’s bizarre death. All of these were likely tied to the forging of the Myriad Souls Banner...","Hold on, I feel as if I've neglected something important.","He quickly racked his brains, and his eyes eventually fell on the Genesis Shamans. A thought popped into his mind. “I thought we had no more clues left, but the biggest clue is right before our eyes.”","“What do you mean?” The others were taken aback.","Zu An slowly explained, “We came here to investigate because of that metal cauldron fragment. The Genesis Shamans forged a unique cauldron for that mysterious man. What does he need the cauldron for when he already has the Myriad Souls Banner?”","“Cauldron?” Wuhui was confused. “What cauldron?”","Zu An took out the metal fragment. When he saw the human face imprinted on it, Wuhui’s complexion darkened. “It’s a living soul!”","“Indeed. That mysterious man not only forged a Myriad Souls Banner, but also requested the Genesis Shamans to forge a cauldron for collecting living souls for him,” Zu An said. “This means his ambitions are greater than what we have imagined.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was alarmed. “Just the Myriad Souls Banner is enough to lay waste to the world. What does he need such a cauldron for?”","Wuhui’s face turned livid. “I have heard about a legendary formation that requires these two items. However, that formation requires an entire world of living beings as tribute. Who has the gall and capability to pull off something like that?","“Furthermore, the Myriad Souls Banner required for that formation needs more than just someone with the Cruel Poison Constitution; it requires at least nine other powerful vengeful spirits too. But where can you find so many powerful individuals who harbor great resentment during their moment of death? The Celestial Court would have heard about it if such a thing happened.”","He kept talking as if he had thought of something terrifying, but wanted to refute his conjecture.","The golden-armored warriors paled upon hearing his words. Patrolling the mortal world usually gave them a sense of self-importance, as everyone else was a country bumpkin compared to them. But this case far surpassed their wildest imagination. It could even be beyond the capacity of the Fire Celestial to deal with.","Zu An walked up to the Genesis Shaman chieftain as he said, “We overlooked an important issue earlier. Why did the Genesis Shamans agree to forge the cauldron for that mysterious man?”","According to the Goddess of Wu Mountain, the Genesis Shaman race was decently powerful. Many years ago, someone could still be able to coerce them into forging an item for them, but that should no longer have been an issue.","The Mermaid Queen’s heart skipped a beat. “Are you saying that the Genesis Shamans did it willingly?”","“Indeed. It doesn’t look as if they were coerced into it.” Zu An nodded.","“That doesn’t make sense. A cauldron that captures living souls can only be used for malicious purposes. The Genesis Shaman race, on the whole, still belongs to the lawful camp. How could they have willingly forged something like that?” the Goddess of Wu Mountain exclaimed.","“There are two possibilities. One, they didn’t know the true purpose of the cauldron, which is unlikely given that they were master blacksmiths. This leaves the second possibility.” Zu An looked at the Genesis Shamans kneeling respectfully to the sculpture. “The mysterious man’s identity was significant enough to dispel the Genesis Shamans’ doubts, such that they were willing to forge a malevolent artifact for him.”"]},{"number":2614,"title":"Chapter 2614: Chapter 2566: Leaving a Hand","paragraphs":["Zu An walked into the center of a group of Genesis Shamans and copied their kneeling posture. “They aren’t kneeling to the sculpture to pray. No, they're kneeling to someone who is of a lofty standing.”","The others were astonished to hear that. They quickly tried kneeling alongside the Genesis Shamans and looking toward the sculpture too—their expressions slowly turned grim. Clearly, they agreed with his deduction.","“Only a handful of people can inspire such respect from the Genesis Shamans,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain said. Her respect for Zu An deepened a little.","They had been still completely clueless just a second ago, but he was able to gather so much crucial information from these minor details. She had always preferred to maintain serenity, but a little ripple of emotions spread through her heart that had remained still for many years.","“Could it be an influential celestial from the Celestial Court?” Zu An asked Wuhui, in hopes that the latter could help to brainstorm as to who fit the criteria.","Wuhui was infuriated. “Nonsense! The Celestial Court has no such conspirators! I bet the shamans are behind this! Only another shaman could command such worship from the Genesis Shaman race.”","You have successfully trolled Wuhui for +299... +299... +299...","The Mermaid Queen interjected, “The Shaman races have unbridled personalities and wouldn’t easily submit to others, especially their peers. Other than Lady Houtu and the other Ancestral Shamans, there is no shaman who can inspire such respect from the Genesis Shaman race. Do you really think they could be the masterminds?”","Even though she wasn’t a true shaman, she had spent a period of time in the Chang clan as their Saintess, which gave her some understanding of the Shaman races. She felt closer to the Shaman races, so she couldn’t help but speak up for them.","Wuhui’s flames flared, but he didn’t dare to reply yes despite his anger. He was the Fire Celestial, but he, too, could land in hot water if he recklessly accused those lofty entities of a crime.","Zu An’s mind churned into action. Could it be the Ancestral Shamans? Lady Houtu, for instance, is suspicious. She is the reason that the Mermaid Queen and I are here. Despite knowing the truth behind the Chang clan, she chose to withhold the truth.","There’s also Gonggong, who challenged the Celestial Emperor earlier at Zhong Mountain.","He couldn’t help but remember how he had witnessed the final generation Gonggong being sealed in the dungeon. In contrast, this generation’s Gonggong felt like a villain.","Of course, the Celestial Court was full of suspects too.","“We have narrowed down our suspects, but we’re still lacking a clue to further our investigation. Against entities of this level, an accusation without evidence is meaningless.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain looked at Zu An, wondering if the latter would bring them more surprises.","It was also then that Yun Yuqing finally recovered from her rollercoaster of emotions and began paying attention to the two women beside Zu An.","“Manman!” she exclaimed as she rushed to grab the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s hands.","She had already lost touch with two close sisters in this foreign world. Seeing yet another familiar face here brought her great solace. The other woman is also ridiculously beautiful. Why does Manman allow him to go around flirting with other women when she’s with him?","And why does he have to get involved with such beautiful women all the time? That heaps so much pressure on me!","Unaccustomed to Yun Yuqing’s cordiality, the Goddess of Wu Mountain pulled back her hands. He wasn’t lying. He does have a woman named Manman who looks like me. Even Miss Yun, whom he had just reunited with, mistook me for her.","“What’s wrong, Manman?” Yun Yuqing was taken aback by her distant attitude.","“She isn’t Manman. They just look alike. She is this world’s Goddess of Wu Mountain,” Zu An quickly clarified the situation. “Goddess, please don’t mind it...”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled. “I don’t mind it. Rather, I can tell that Miss Yun is on good terms with Miss Manman.”","She was curious why so many outstanding women were romantically involved with him, yet instead of harboring jealousy toward one another, they got along well like real sisters.","“Ah, so it’s the Goddess of Wu Mountain...” Yun Yuqing hurriedly apologized while assessing her. She sensed something amiss from how the other party looked at Zu An. Looks like I’m still underestimating big brother Zu.","“Why does this lady look so familiar? Miss Shang?” Yun Yuqing soon turned her attention to the Mermaid Queen. Even though the Mermaid Queen wore a veil, her features could still be made out when looking up close.","“She also only resembles Liuyu; she’s the Chang clan’s Saintess Chang’e,\" Zu An said. It would be tough to explain the Mermaid Queen’s true identity with outsiders around.","Wuhui and the golden-armored warriors were taken aback. This fellow is a player! How can he meet so many people who look like his lovers?","Even the Goddess of Wu Mountain couldn’t help but stare at Zu An. She would have never thought that even the Chang clan’s Saintess resembled his lover. This was starting to get a little ridiculous.","The glares from all sides made Zu An gulp. He quickly interjected, “I thought of a clue.”","“What is it?”","That immediately diverted everyone’s attention.","Zu An pointed to the chieftain of the Genesis Shaman race. “Do you know where his room is?”","“This...” The Goddess of Wu Mountain had been to Genesis Mountain before, but she had never visited the chieftain’s room.","Wuhui, however, replied with a harrumph, “That’s easy to figure out. The chieftain’s residence is bound to be grander than the others, and their race worships fire...”","The fire seething around him transformed into small fiery figures that scattered all over Genesis Mountain. There was no need to search the lower levels; there was no way the chieftain would live there.","Soon, the small fire figures returned and whispered into Wuhui’s ears.","“It’s over there,” Wuhui said as he began making his way over.","The group followed him and soon arrived at a house. The gate had two ferocious beast knobs, and they were both forged out of Genesis Mountain’s copper. However, the gate was opened wide, revealing the interior. In the room were nine pillars positioned in a specific formation, and each of these pillars was wrapped in the skin of a renowned beast. They seemed to be room decor elements to highlight the chieftain’s valiance.","At the center of the room was a furnace. This furnace was linked to Genesis Mountain’s earth flame, so its fire would never go out. All sorts of smithing tools were placed neatly by the side. Even the chieftain was constantly upgrading his skills, it seemed.","However, the room was a mess. It was as if someone had just burgled it.","Zu An walked up to the furnace and saw that it was full of ashes. There were several turtle shells inside too. The Shaman races used such things for divination. His heart sank. He'd thought that even if he chose to take the request to forge a malevolent artifact, the chieftain would have taken some precautions, so it would be possible to find clues in his room.","However, the mysterious culprit appeared to have shared the same thoughts as him.","Just then, a bizarre sound came from outside. The group looked up. A beast fang wind chime hanging on the roof outside was ringing despite the absence of wind. An earthquake suddenly ensued, as if something had come to life.","“Fire Celestial, look outside...” the golden-armored warriors exclaimed in horror."]},{"number":2615,"title":"Chapter 2615: Chapter 2567: The Ten Suns","paragraphs":["The group rushed out and saw that Genesis Mountain’s 72 peaks had lit up. Invisible waves rippled across the air as everything came to life. Totems carved with unique images lit up, forming a unique formation.","“Don’t worry, that isn’t an offensive formation.” Wuhui calmed down the crowd.","Zu An nodded. As expected of the Celestial Court’s Fire Celestial. He has a keen eye.","Suddenly, the sculptures on the 72 peaks each shot out two light beams from their eyes, and all the beams converged on the centermost volcano crater. Rumbles echoed, and the earth within a hundred-kilometer radius shook as if the volcano was about to erupt.","Wuhui looked at the crater and frowned. “The fire element ki has been triggered, but it’s not overly violent yet. It doesn’t look las if the volcano will erupt, though it won’t be a problem even if it erupts.”","Those words were spoken with a tinge of pride.","The golden-armored warriors breathed a sigh of relief. Indeed, it should be a walk in the park for the Fire Celestial who governs over flames to curb an eruption.","Lava suddenly spurted out from the crater. Everyone instinctively retreated, but the lava didn’t spill into the surroundings; instead, it morphed into a human silhouette.","“The Genesis Shaman chieftain!” the Goddess of Wu Mountain exclaimed. The forming lava silhouette was still blurry, but it wasn’t difficult to guess who he was based on his outline.","“He isn’t dead yet?” Yun Yuqing was confused.","“He is dead. This is merely a projection he made when he was alive.” Wuhui stared at the lava silhouette warily, not knowing what the Genesis Shaman chieftain was up to.","The lava silhouette spoke up. “I should be dead by the time you see me.”","The crowd was astonished. Only Zu An was composed, having expected this.","“I am the Genesis Shamans' chieftain. An esteemed guest came not long ago and requested us to forge something,” the lava silhouette murmured with a contemplative face. “It would be the utmost honor of our Genesis Shaman race to forge something for that lord, but... we soon became hesitant when we realized that he wanted to forge a Soul Destroying Cauldron capable of amassing countless souls.","“I didn’t understand why someone as lofty and radiant as that lord would forge something so vile. I voiced my doubt, and he answered my question. He said he was planning to use it against evil scum and make a warning out of them. The explanation made sense, and I didn’t think someone of his stature would lie about a matter like this.","“But a question slowly dawned upon me as we began to forge the Soul Destroying Cauldron. Was such a huge cauldron required to deal with all the evil beings in the world? The cauldron was big enough to store all souls in the world...”","Those words alarmed everyone present. What does it mean to store all souls in the world? Just what is that enigmatic man up to?!","“Just thinking about the possibilities filled me with deep fear, but I couldn’t fathom why someone of his stature would do something like that. Could I be overthinking it? I have been making divinations using tortoise shells in recent days, but the more I divine, the worse the results become. If my deduction is true, that lord will not allow this matter to leak out. We’ll likely be silenced for the part we play in this matter.","“So, I left this recording behind. I made sure to switch off this mechanism every day to ensure that this recording wouldn’t be played. If a day came when I failed to switch off the mechanism, this recording would automatically play. From the looks of it, I must have been silenced in the end.”","The lava silhouette looked melancholic, and it left the group with heavy hearts.","“If that lord has chosen to silence me, he will likely have destroyed all possible clues too. My room must be a mess now.”","Zu An couldn’t help but smile. The chieftain sure is open-minded to crack such a joke when leaving his will behind.","“But the things he destroyed were meaningless, as I have left the clues all over Genesis Mountain. Not even he can simply destroy all of Genesis Mountain, as that would catch the attention of the Celestial Court and the Shaman races. That’s the last thing he would want.”","Yun Yuqing panicked. “This fellow keeps prattling on, but he refuses to divulge the killer’s identity. How frustrating!”","Zu An patted her shoulder and said, “He must have his reason for doing so.”","At this point, the lava silhouette took a deep breath as if making up his mind. “I dare not reveal his name because that will draw his attention, and I don’t know if the person watching this recording has the power to deal with him. That would render all the preparations I have made meaningless. But if you’re smart enough, you should have already deciphered his identity, no?”","The lava silhouette blinked mischievously before vanishing.","Yun Yuqing was frustrated. “What’s with that? He ended up not saying anything at all!”","“No, he's already said it all,” Zu An, Wuhui, and the Goddess of Wu Mountain replied simultaneously with grim voices.","Wuhui and the Goddess of Wu Mountain glanced at Zu An. The two of them were of high standing, so it wasn't surprising for them to guess the culprit’s identity.","Zu An stared at the dissipating lava silhouette.","The latter had mentioned that the culprit was of exalted standing and emanated an inviolable light. That suggested he was a powerhouse of the Celestial Court. On top of that, the chieftain had spoken so fearfully as if he was afraid he had misunderstood the other party. It was only when he could no longer turn his eyes away from the truth that he'd prepared this recording. There weren’t many people in the Celestial Court who fit these criteria.","There was also a reason the chieftain had intentionally set this recording to play in the crater. When the lava silhouette first formed and later dissipated, it had vaguely formed the figure of a massive bird unfurling its wings. If one looked at it from a top-down angle, contrasted with the volcano’s crater, it resembled a divine bird amid the sun.","The only one who fit all these criteria was Emperor Jun!","The Genesis Shaman race’s chieftain wasn't the only one who couldn’t make sense of the situation. Even Zu An was baffled. Emperor Jun was already chosen as the next Celestial Emperor, so why was he doing all these things?","In truth, Zu An had already guessed that Emperor Jun was the culprit based on the crystallized ground and lingering fire element ki in the area where Yi died, but he couldn’t confirm the matter. Only now was he certain that Emperor Jun was behind all this.","Wuhui’s face darkened. “This is a huge matter. We must immediately inform the celestials.”","Since returning to the Celestial Court wasn’t an option right now, he could contact the more important celestials residing on earth.","Zu An wondered how he could save Xiaoxi and the others when he noticed something.","Everyone present looked up at the sky. For some reason, it was many times brighter than before, and the surrounding air became searing hot, too.","Ten suns had simultaneously appeared in the sky!"]},{"number":2616,"title":"Chapter 2616: Chapter 2568: Murdered","paragraphs":["“The Golden Crow Ten Princes!” Wuhui was both alarmed and infuriated. “How dare they! The Golden Crow Princes are supposed to come out in turn to serve as the world’s sun. There is a strict sequence to their appearances, so how can they appear together? Don’t they know that all lives will wither if they do this? This is against the celestial laws!”","Zu An was dazed. This wasn't his first time undergoing this event. Witnessing this scene once more felt unreal to him.","He couldn’t help but ask, “I know that the separation of heaven and earth has temporarily severed connections between the Celestial Court and earth, but why doesn’t the Celestial Court react when ten suns have already risen in the sky?”","Wuhui’s complexion looked awful. “A day in heaven is a year on earth. That’s the gap between deities and mortals. Countless lives will have died by the time the Celestial Court noticed the ten suns. This won’t do! I have to immediately inform the powerhouses on earth.”","Flames flared from Wuhui, and he was about to fly off when he noticed Yun Yuqing and called out, “Miss Yun, let’s go together.”","Knowing she would reject his offer, he added via telepathy, “Miss Yun, I know you can’t bear to part ways with your lover, but there’s no point staying by his side now. He has a goddess and a saintess with him now. Not only are they of a high stature, but they are also beauties who don’t pale in comparison to you. It’ll only make things awkward if you get in the middle of them now.”","Yun Yuqing was about to turn down Wuhui when she heard those words and hesitated.","Wuhui took this chance to press further. “All men have this bizarre mindset where the more noble a woman is, the more they subconsciously value them. I don’t doubt the deep bonds you share, but you’re at a disadvantage against those two women.”","Yun Yuqing lowered her gaze. Those words struck a chord in her heart.","“But you need not worry. Your bloodline is the noblest of them all; it's just that it hasn’t fully manifested. Come with us. I’ll restore your position. You shall become much nobler than them. You’ll be able to stand on equal terms with them by the time you return.” Knowing she was moved, Wuhui switched to a gentler tone and added, “We’re going to contact important celestials residing on earth right now. These connections may become invaluable in aiding your lover in the future.”","Yun Yuqing’s eyes lit up. She was finally convinced. “All right, but I’d like to have a private conversation with him first.”","Wuhui was in a good mood after convincing her. He had no reason to stop her, so he took his golden-armored warriors elsewhere to wait for her. Such a noble bloodline must not be sullied by a mere mortal.","Seeing that they were going to talk, the Goddess of Wu Mountain and the Mermaid Queen tactfully stepped aside to give them some private space.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain hesitantly glanced at the Mermaid Queen before asking, “Don’t you feel envious seeing your man getting close to other women?”","The Mermaid Queen shook her head. “I’m already satisfied to be able to be with big brother.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was taken aback. With her beauty and stature, she could have any man. I would never have expected someone this smart and rational to be so blind when it comes to love.","She didn’t understand it, but she was shaken. What sorcery does that man have to make such an outstanding woman fall head over heels for him?","The Mermaid Queen noticed her confusion, but didn’t explain it. She doesn’t understand the situation between me and big brother Zu. We’re from two different eras, so there is no future between us. All I can covet is a temporary reunion in this separate world.","She knew it would likely be an eternal farewell after departing from this world. That made their time together extremely precious. It was a waste to spend even a single second on jealousy.","Meanwhile, Yun Yuqing told Zu An what she had heard from Wuhui and smiled. “He underestimated our relationship. He thinks his words have moved me.”","Zu An was surprised. “But you're still choosing to go with them.”","Yun Yuqing put on a serious face and explained, “We have no comrades in this world. There are no disadvantages to forging friendly ties with the Celestial Court. We have to save Xiaoxi, so we will need all the help we can get.”","Zu An didn’t stand on ceremony. They needed all the help they could get to rescue Xiaoxi, and this was a fortuitous encounter for Yun Yuqing, too. He took out two talismans and handed them to her. “Keep this location talisman and alarm talisman. Activate the alarm talisman if you’re in danger. As long as you have the location talisman with you, I’ll soon be by your side.”","“Ah? Are you that formidable now?” Yun Yuqing was overjoyed. She held the two talismans close to her chest.","“I recently grasped a new skill.” Zu An smiled. As long as he had the other party’s coordinates, he could quickly get there with the skill he had grasped from combining the Shaman race’s secret art and Rainbow Morph.","As for the location talisman and alarm talisman, he had developed that with Xie Daoyun. The thought of her made his heart sink. He wondered where Yumen Beiqing and the real little sister Ling’er were.","“What’s wrong, big brother Zu?” Yu Yunqing asked out of concern.","“It’s nothing.” Zu An smiled. Yu Yunqing was already agitated because of Xiaoxi; there was no need to add to her troubles. “Be careful. I can see that Wuhui harbors goodwill toward you, but the Celestial Court might not have a favorable view of our ties.”","Yu Yunqing understood what he was getting at. “Don’t worry. You’re more important to me than anything else.”","She leaped into Zu An’s arms and kissed him. Then, she ran off with a furiously blushing face. Ah, I didn’t think too much earlier, but kissing big brother Zu in front of those two ladies felt like I was exerting my dominance over him in front of them. It seems a little bitchy.","The Mermaid Queen and the Goddess of Wu Mountain didn’t react much to the kiss, but Wuhui glared at Zu An with seething eyes. Miss Yun has fallen too deep in love. To preserve the purity of the Celestial Court’s bloodline, I mustn’t allow the two of them to meet!","You have successfully trolled Wuhui for +300... +300... +300...","He conjured a fire cloud with a wave of his hand before leaving with Yun Yuqing and his subordinates. Seeing Yun Yuqing look back at Zu An, he drove his fire cloud faster.","The fire cloud vanished astoundingly quickly. The Goddess of Wu Mountain walked to Zu An with a smile. “Looks like Wuhui is worried about Miss Yun changing her mind.”","“How can a pledge of eternal love unravel that easily?” Zu An looked at the Mermaid Queen, and the two of them exchanged smiles as they grabbed each other’s hands.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was speechless. Wow, how can there be such a seamless switch? It doesn’t feel off at all!","She quickly dispelled those miscellaneous thoughts and said, “All evidence points at that man. His high stature makes him difficult to deal with. Why don’t you follow me to Wu Mountain? I’ll request the Kaiming Six Shamans to rally other powers together against him.”","She had spent most of her life in isolation, so she didn’t have as many friends as the Kaiming Six Shamans.","“Thank you, goddess.” Zu An knew that Emperor Jun wasn't a foe he could oppose alone.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain conjured a white cloud and gestured for them to get on.","Zu An smiled and said, “I have a faster way to return to Wu Mountain.”","They'd had to manually travel to Genesis Mountain because he didn’t know its coordinates, but he still remembered Wu Mountain’s coordinates. He grabbed the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s arm and activated Rainbow Morph.","A rainbow shot across the sky. A second later, the three of them returned to Wu Mountain.","Despite having let go of their hands, the Goddess of Wu Mountain still felt warmth radiating from her arm. It made her blush a little. How could he grab a maiden’s hand without any warning?","It had been many years since she last had physical contact with anyone, let alone a man. However, she could tell from his clear eyes that he hadn’t intended to take advantage of her, so it seemed excessive to kick up a fuss over this.","Just then, the nervous Kaiming Six Shamans appeared in the vicinity. The Goddess of Wu Mountain anxiously asked them what had happened.","The Kaiming Six Shamans were overjoyed to see them, but their faces quickly turned bitter. “Something huge has happened! The Golden Crow Crown Prince has burned Nuba to death!”"]},{"number":2617,"title":"Chapter 2617: Chapter 2569: Destruction Upon the World","paragraphs":["“What?!” Even the usually composed Goddess of Wu Mountain was horrified.","On the one hand, she had just met Nuba not long ago. On the other hand, Nuba was not only the Yellow Emperor’s daughter, but also Ancestral Shaman Zhulong’s wife. Her death was bound to cause massive ripples.","Zu An, however, was calm. He was aware of how Nuba had met her end in history, though he hadn’t expected it to happen so quickly. It felt bizarre to be involved in such major historical incidents.","“We found it inconceivable too. We heard that she was looking for Emperor Jun but was unable to locate him, so she began insulting him to goad him into revealing himself,” Wu Yang explained.","“She must have gotten impatient.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain frowned. “Nuba has always had a bad temper.”","“That’s most likely the case,” Wu Peng agreed. “However, Emperor Jun was still nowhere to be seen despite her insults. It could be because he was no longer able to sense the happenings on earth after the separation of heaven and earth.”","“Emperor Jun could just be putting up with it. He is the next Celestial Emperor, and Nuba is an important figure. It wouldn’t be surprising if he decided to show some magnanimity to her taunts,” Wu Fan analyzed.","“But the Golden Crow Ten Princes couldn’t take it lying down. They rushed out upon hearing Nuba insult their father, and a conflict broke out. That culminated in the present situation,” Wu Di said with a sigh.","“Nuba should have been strong enough to stand her ground against the Golden Crow Ten Princes, but they happen to be able to suppress her ability. They made her powers go amok before killing her,” Wu Fu added.","...","The Kaiming Six Shamans quickly reconstructed the situation through their discussion.","The Mermaid Queen secretly tugged Zu An’s sleeve and whispered, “Could it be that Nuba dug up something related to that person too?”","“That’s possible,” Zu An replied. Thinking about it, Emperor Jun had arrived in the middle of Yi and Gu’s fight and killed Yi before erasing his trail. This suggested that Gu and Emperor Jun had been colluding.","If they further tugged on the thread, Emperor Jun could have been the one instigating Gu to kill Bao Jiang and steal the immortal medicine, and he could have had a part to play behind Er Fu’s murder of Yayu, too. If that was the conclusion Nuba came to, she was bound to want to avenge her son. That would explain why she'd harshly insulted Emperor Jun to goad the latter to confront her.","But what could Emperor Jun’s motive be behind all these things? What was he planning with the Myriad Souls Banner and the Soul Destruction Cauldron? He was already the next Celestial Emperor, so what was the point of doing all these?","“Look! The suns are quickly moving!” The Mermaid Queen pointed to the sky. It was so hot that her face was flushed, and a thin layer of sweat had formed on her forehead.","The group raised their heads and saw the ten suns in the sky quickly moving westward, causing the surrounding air to become cooler.","“Are the golden crows finally returning to Scalding Valley?” Wu Yang, who had opened up his robe to fan himself, asked in delight.","“It doesn’t look like it.” Zu An shook his head.","The ten suns’ movements were erratic; they would move quickly at one point only to suddenly stop right after, as if they were fooling around.","Wu Xiang’s ears suddenly enlarged until they were comparable to an elephant’s ears. He focused hard on the voices around him, and soon, his expression turned livid.","“Sixth Brother, what did you hear?” Wu Peng asked.","“The shamans are angry at Nuba’s death. Kuafu wants to settle the score with the Golden Crow Ten Princes, but they simply flew off. That angered Kuafu, so he’s chasing after them to demand an explanation,” Wu Xiang said.","“Kuafu chasing the suns!” Zu An exclaimed.","“What?” The others turned to look at Zu An in confusion.","Zu An had no way of explaining this historical event to them, so he said, “It’s too dangerous for Kuafu to pursue the Golden Crow Ten Princes alone.”","“Indeed. If they had the gall to kill Nuba, they wouldn’t show him mercy,” the Kaiming Six Shamans replied worriedly. Kuafu was powerful enough to stand his ground against several of the Golden Crow Ten Princes, but dealing with all ten of them at once was impossible.","“I’ll go take a look,” Zu An said grimly. It would be a stretch to say that Kuafu was a friend, but he did have a favorable impression of the other party’s candid personality.","Besides, Emperor Jun was likely involved in this matter. He wanted to get to the bottom of the issue and hopefully obtain news about Xiaoxi and Yumen Beiqing.","“I’ll go with you.” The Mermaid Queen tagged along, not wanting to part ways with him.","Zu An shook his head. “It’s too dangerous. You should stay here with the goddess.”","He clasped his fist toward the Goddess of Wu Mountain and said, “Goddess, I’ll be troubling you to take care of her.”","Confronting the Golden Crow Ten Princes was already dangerous, and they could even encounter Emperor Jun on top of that. Zu An could escape using Rainbow Morph, but he dared not bring the Mermaid Queen with him.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain nodded. “Don’t worry, we’ll protect her.”","The Mermaid Queen was reluctant to part ways with Zu An, but she understood the severity of the situation. She grabbed his hand and said, “You must stay safe.”","Despite the intense heat from the surroundings, she gave off an inexplicable coolness that calmed his heart.","Zu An was moved. A thought suddenly came to his mind, and he stuffed an item into her hand and secretly relayed some instructions to her.","The Mermaid Queen was taken aback. “But you need this more than me!”","“Don’t worry. I dare not say the same about the others, but I'm unparalleled in the art of fleeing.” Zu An had been skirting around death ever since transmigrating back then. Over time, he had honed the art of fleeing to a masterful degree.","Worried that the Mermaid Queen would continue turning down his gift, he bade her farewell before morphing into a rainbow to chase after the ten suns. He couldn’t move straight to where the Golden Crow Ten Princes and Kuafu were because he didn’t have their coordinates, so he could only manually chase after them.","But after crossing Spirit Mountain, his expression slowly turned cold. Spirit Mountain was an enigmatic mountain range where powerhouses and experts dwelled. While the sudden appearance of the ten suns had caused the temperature to reach unbearable levels, the powerhouses were able to protect even the flora and faunas using their formations.","But everything changed beyond that. The sky was constantly dyed a jarring dark red color. The trees beyond the Spirit Mountain swiftly withered. Their trunks cracked under the immense heat, and their sap swiftly evaporated. Lush forests were swiftly reduced to charred ground. It was hard to tell where the first spark of flame had started, but it hadn’t taken long for it to evolve into an inferno.","Many beast fled in a fluster. They were already the stronger ones, as the weaker ones had already been scorched to death. But escaping the protection of the forest meant direct exposure to the rays of the ten suns. Many of the beasts shrieked in misery as their bodies burst into flames. In the end, they were reduced to charred carcasses.","Zu An passed by a furiously bubbling river that was soaked in blood. Fishes and sea monsters tried leaping out from the water, but it was too late. Their flesh melted so quickly that only their bones were left before they could even leap out of the water.","Zu An noticed a human tribe next to the river and tried to rush over to save them. It was a decently-sized tribe. Its buildings were made by piling up simple stone blocks, but it was already nearing the scale of a city. Anyone could tell that it was a vibrant civilization.","But there wasn't a shadow to be seen...","No, it would be more accurate to say that there were shadows everywhere—the walls and the floors were covered in pitch-black carbonized silhouettes. Most people in this tribe had to have been mortals for them to not even leave corpses behind. The crude marks around were the only evidence of their existence in this world.","Zu An stopped before an underground cavern. It likely served as the tribe’s bunker in times of danger, but there was no one inside. There were only ‘wall murals’ to be seen. Some of these murals depicted a mother hugging her children tightly before their lives came to a halt.","Zu An had heard the word ‘carnage’ many times, but it was only now that its true meaning sank in for him. These people had just died, but he couldn’t sense their souls despite being the master of the underworld. He could only sense their resentment and fear.","Emotions gushed into his heart, leaving him suffocated. He looked at the sky. Those who have sinned must pay the price, even if they are gods!"]},{"number":2618,"title":"Chapter 2618: Chapter 2570: The Deafening Arrow That Shakes the Clouds","paragraphs":["Under the blazing sky, a giant reminiscent of a hill charged at the ten suns with a wooden staff. Every step he took easily traversed several mountains, yet he was still significantly slower than the ten suns. He had no idea how long he had been chasing the Golden Crow Ten Princes. It was so hot that his body was scorched red throughout, and a layer of dead white skin had formed around his lips.","He finally saw a raging river he remembered as the human tribes’ famed Yellow River. Under the ten suns, the river bubbled furiously, but he couldn’t care less. He squatted next to the river and began drinking its contents. He almost apepared to be enjoying it even though the water was boiling.","He drank so fast that it didn’t take long for him to gulp down the entire Yellow River. He regained his spirit and continued chasing after the ten suns with huge strides.","However, the suns seemed to be making fun of him. Instead of escaping while he was drinking water, they'd stopped to taunt him. It was only after he downed the river that they hurriedly sped off.","Under the extreme heat, Kuafu’s stamina was being quickly depleted. He soon started gasping for air, but luckily, he stumbled upon the Wei River. Like before, he drank up the entire Wei River before continuing to chase after the ten suns.","By this point, he had already realized that he was no match for the ten suns. Even if he caught up with them, he wouldn’t be able to exact vengeance for Nuba. However, he was fueled by indignation. He refused to submit to the ten suns just like that.","The Shaman races could be defeated, but their spirit could never be quelled!","The chase continued, but Kuafu quickly felt thirsty again despite having just drunk two rivers dry. He remembered that there was a huge lake ahead. Once he drank up that lake, he would have the energy to continue the chase.","It was a pity he didn’t last until reaching the lake. His legs felt increasingly heavy, and he soon struggled to keep his eyes open. He knew that he had reached his limit, though he couldn’t understand why. He wasn't be a match for the ten suns, but he should have been able to last longer.","He looked at the eerily smiling suns in the sky, and realization struck him.","“I see...”","The realization made him stop his chase. He used the last bit of life force he had left to toss his wooden staff. Where the staff landed, grass began to grow. Not even the ten suns’ heat could wither the vibrant life force sprouting out.","Peach blossoms flowered into peaches. The peaches fell to the ground and turned into new sprouts. From these new sprouts, new trees rose. Soon, an entire forest of peach trees emerged from the wooden staff.","Cries of misery suddenly echoed from the surroundings. They were wretched, yet there was a tinge of liberation in them.","“How dare you foil our plan!” a furious voice echoed.","A fireball fell from the sky and landed on Kuafu. However, Kuafu’s body was so strong that this meteorite-like attack didn’t smash his body to bits, but it charred huge swathes of his skin.","Even so, that wasn’t enough to vent the suns’ anger. They unleashed more fireballs to reduce him to ashes.","Just then, brilliant sword ki surged in from afar and sliced the fireballs into fireworks.","The ten Golden Crows looked over and saw a rainbow headed toward them. Before they knew it, Zu An had already landed next to Kuafu.","Seeing his charred body, Zu An’s expression darkened. “I arrived too late.”","Kuafu pointed at the sky. “Be careful of the vile...”","However, he breathed his last before he could finish his words. His eyes were wide with indignation, as if he regretted not being able to finish speaking.","The ten Golden Crows circled the sky. “Who are you? How dare you meddle in our business!”","Zu An ignored them. He glanced at the nearby peach forest, and it made him realize something. He gently closed Kuafu’s eyes as he murmured, “Rest assured, I know what you want to say.”","Others would think that the Golden Crow Ten Princes had come out for vengeance because Nuba insulted their father, and then continued roaming the world out of mischief. Their deeds had caused widespread destruction, but in light of their lofty standing, their punishments wouldn’t be too severe.","But Zu An knew things weren’t that simple. Based on the information he had gathered thus far, the sudden appearance of the ten suns was no coincidence. It was planned.","The Myriad Souls Banner, the Soul Destruction Cauldron...","The appearance of the ten suns has caused widespread deaths, but the souls of the deceased are nowhere to be found. Emperor Jun must be using the ten Golden Crows to complete the final step of sacrificing all living beings in the world to his formation.","Kuafu had to have figured that out, so he'd formed this peach forest with his staff to restrain the souls. That hindered the collection of the souls in the vicinity. No wonder the ten Golden Crows were so agitated.","“Brat, we’re talking to you! Are you mute?!” the Golden Crow Sixth Prince roared.","Zu An finally looked up at the ten suns. His eyes were sharp enough to make out the gleeful smiles on the ten Golden Crows. They couldn’t understand the weight of what they were doing. “You must have done all these things thinking that no one in the world could stop you.”","The ten Golden Crows were initially taken aback before bursting into laughter.","“Look at what you’re saying. A mere human like you intends to stop us?”","“Know your place, mortal ant!”","“We’re the Celestial Emperor’s sons! You don’t know how many blessings we've brought to the world over the years. So what if we have a little bit of fun now and then? Those weaklings only have themselves to blame for being unable to withstand our heat. That has nothing to do with us!”","“Why waste your breath on a mere ant? Ant, slice your detestable tongue and snap off your limbs right now; I’ll consider sparing your life.”","...","Zu An remained perfectly calm in the face of their gleeful laughter. If he's decided to send the ten suns out now, Emperor Jun’s preparations must be complete. It’s unlikely that Xiaoxi is safe.","He glanced at Kuafu’s charred body and remembered the doomsday scenarios he had seen along the way. Charred black human silhouettes filled the walls and the grounds of countless villages, as if trying to tell him something. He felt as if someone had set his blood on fire.","Just then, Mi Li exclaimed in agitation, “Calm down! Emperor Jun has spent a long time plotting this scheme. It’s not something you can deal with by yourself. The best you can do right now is to contact the Shaman races and have Wuhui report to the Celestial Court. There are plenty of powerhouses to deal with this incident. You mustn’t get involved in this massive karma.","“Don’t let your recklessness get ahead of yourself! This is one of the biggest incidents in the flow of time. You aren’t from this time. There’s no saying what will happen if you force your way into this matter. If you’re killed by Emperor Jun in this world, you won’t even get a chance to reincarnate!”","...","Mi Li had been keeping an eye on this matter. Upon sensing Zu An’s intentios, she had no choice but to wake up and advise him. She usually cherished her words as if they were gold, yet she'd suddenly spoken so much in a single breath. That reflected just how anxious she was.","A red bow appeared in Zu An’s hands, but he looked extremely calm. “Big sister empress, I know it would be wiser to heed your advice, but if a person cultivates so hard only to dare not make a move in the face of injustice, what has he been cultivating his entire life for?”","“You’ll die!”","“All beings eventually die.”","Zu An leaned backward as he drew his bow in an arc like a full moon. The surrounding ki furiously gushed toward his body. It didn’t feel as if he was pulling the bow alone, but as if billions of living beings were standing behind him.","A white light burst forth and pierced through a Golden Crow. Its blood flowed like a river."]},{"number":2619,"title":"Chapter 2619: Chapter 2571: Creeping Despair","paragraphs":["Crimson infernos unleashed by the ten suns; they crack the grounds and boil the oceans.","The Fusang branch burns to cinders, and countless souls bemoan heaven.","A bowstring is pulled in a perfect arc; its target heaven.","A thunderous snap that shakes the highest clouds!","The arrow pierces through a golden crow, causing blood to gush like a stream.","The descending celestial flames torch the plains.","...","The shot Golden Crow screamed in agony. His feathers scattered all over the ground as his blood spurted across the sky before he plummeted onto a western mountain, leaving a crater in his wake.","As time passed, a deep spring known as the Feather Spring would form there. That was also the place Zu An had seen when he first entered this place. Zu An had wondered why he didn’t see the Feather Spring when he entered this world this time; little could he have known that he was the one to inadvertently create it.","Countless despairing living beings on earth witnessed the downfall of a sun and cheered in delight. Tears of joy flowed down their faces. Even though it was just a single sun, it brought them hope and vented the anger they felt.","The more powerful entities thought further ahead. They wondered what would happen to the man who accomplished this feat. Emperor Jun and Xihe wouldn’t let someone who had killed their son live.","Those on Wu Mountain had a better grasp of what was going on. The Kaiming Six Shamans exclaimed in fear, “The one who shot that arrow can’t be that little brother, right?”","The Mermaid Queen naturally knew it was Zu An. She anxiously turned to the Goddess of Wu Mountain and asked, “Goddess, now that big brother has killed one of the Golden Crows, will the Celestial Court go after him for vengeance?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain looked grim. “The Golden Crows’ father and their mother will likely go after him. In particular, Sun Goddess Xihe is known to dote on her sons.”","At the same time, she was also awed. Zu An had to have known all this, but he'd still chosen to make a move. He felt like a valiant hero who stood steadfast to his principles.","“What should we do?” The Mermaid Queen panicked. She could still request help from her connections if this was her previous world, but she knew no one in this world. The inability to do anything left her feeling profoundly helpless.","“Wait for me here. Don’t go anywhere. I’ll contact those who can help.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain morphed into a fog and quickly left the area.","The Kaiming Six Shamans were taken aback. “The goddess has always been a lofty individual. She rarely speaks to others; it’s rare for her to proactively make a move. She must be seeking her elders for help.”","“Even the goddess is making a move. We can’t just sit still here.”","“Indeed. We have to get as many old friends to help out as possible, even if it means hurling out our pride!”","...","The Kaiming Six Shamans headed off as well, leaving the Mermaid Queen anxiously squeezing her sleeves while she observed the situation in the distance.","...","In the distant battlefield, the Golden Crows’ laughter halted. They were shocked and infuriated. “How dare you kill our Ninth Brother!”","You have successfully trolled the Golden Crow Princes for +888... +888... +888...","Zu An remained impassive despite the massive influx of Rage in his system. These Golden Crows are reacting so strongly just because they lost a brother. What about the massacred tribes I've seen along the way?","Not wanting to waste his breath arguing with the Golden Crows, Zu An drew his bowstring once more. Perhaps it was an illusion, but he didn’t feel as if he had expended any of his energy. On the contrary, he felt stronger than ever.","This didn't make sense. Perhaps he had significantly advanced his cultivation, but he didn’t have the aid of the Spirit Mountain’s Ten Shamans, Yun Jianyue, and Yan Xuehen this time. Even a single arrow should have expended his energy significantly. And yet, he felt more spirited than ever. This felt like neither the Kun Peng’s nor the Taotie’s Heaven-Devouring Sutra’s ability. Rather, this energy was something he had never felt before.","He suddenly recalled that the biggest difference between celestials and mortal cultivators was that celestials had divine personas capable of absorbing faith, wish energy, or other things along those lines. For a moment earlier, he'd felt as if he had received wish energy from billions of living beings. They strongly willed for vengeance against the ten suns and the conclusion of this apocalypse.","His deed had happened to grant hope to all living beings in the world, so they'd offered him their earnest blessings and prayers in hopes that he could accomplish this feat.","While he was pondering all these things, yet another white light harnessing the surrounding ki and the masses’ wish energy flew forth.","Yet another Golden Crow plummeted from the sky with a wretched shriek. The suns in the sky became much less glaring. Resounding cheers came from the surroundings.","The remaining eight Golden Crows didn’t dare to underestimate Zu An. They quickly spread apart and began their retaliation. Meteorites and flames fell from the sky and bombarded the ground where Zu An stood. Terrifying explosions followed; massive holes were left in the surrounding radius. Even the ground was turned into slowly flowing lava.","“That fellow must be dead now!” one of the Golden Crows hollered.","“He got off easy!”","“I think I saw a rainbow flash past.”","“You must be seeing things. How can there be a rainbow in such heat?”","...","They quickly realized that they weren’t seeing things. Yet another white light flashed past, and yet another Golden Crow screamed in misery and plummeted from the sky.","“What?!” The seven surviving Golden Crows were horrified.","They began taking evasive maneuvers while bombarding Zu An with even more attacks. With their sharp golden feathers, they formed a powerful sword formation that unleashed relentless attacks upon Zu An.","They had learned their lesson this time. The sword formation left no room for escape, and the seven Golden Crows even made sure to seal his aura off too. No matter where he dodged, the golden swords would chase him to the very end. An archer wouldn’t be able to pose a threat if he had no time to draw his bowstring.","They were determined to make him experience a fate worse than death!","Looking at the golden feather swords in the sky, Zu An suddenly felt small and insignificant. However, he didn’t panic. He knew his aura had been locked down on, and dodging would only result in him losing control over the momentum of battle.","Thus, he didn’t bother to dodge at all!","A Seven-Colored Divine Halo shone, and all the golden swords vanished into thin air.","The eyes of the Golden Crows nearly popped out from shock.","However, there was no time for them to think before three streaks of white light flew at them. Three Golden Crows screeched in misery as their blazing bodies plummeted from the sky.","“That is Zhuanxu’s bow, Suzeng! Why is it in his hands?”","The remaining four Golden Crows finally lost their courage. The first two deaths could still be passed off as carelessness, but despite them putting their strength together, their brothers were still falling one after another. By this point, it was clear to them that they were outclassed!","They desperately fled for their lives, morphing into four golden lights that fled in different directions. Each prayed desperately that the next victim would be one of their brothers, so they would have more time to make their getaway.","When the Golden Crow First Prince heard two screams of agony, he knew two more of his brothers had fallen. His expression warped in anger. Wait till I return from this ordeal. I’ll gather my men and tear that scoundrel into pieces!","He wasn’t worried in the slightest. He thought that there was no way Zu An could catch up with him after killing two of his brothers. The Golden Crow Radiant Flow was a top-notch movement skill. No other movement skill, other than the Heavenly Peng Stride and Rainbow Morph, could catch up with it.","Hold on! Rainbow Morph?","The sudden recollection of the rainbow they'd seen made the Golden Crow First Prince narrow his eyes.","Just then, he spotted a rainbow in his peripheral vision. Before he knew it, Zu An was already standing in front of him. He finally tasted the same despair experienced by the other living beings earlier."]},{"number":2620,"title":"Chapter 2620: Chapter 2572: Indignant? You Can Only Accept It","paragraphs":["As Zu An coldly stared at him with a giant red bow in hand, the Golden Crow First Prince felt so frightened that his feathers stood on end.","“Big brother, it’s a misunderstanding! It’s all a misunderstanding!” He squeezed out a smile.","“I prefer your earlier arrogance.” Zu An didn’t hesitate to draw his bowstring and manifest a white arrow.","“I was wrong, big brother. I know my mistake now. We shouldn’t have come out together in a moment of mischief, but I have at least worked hard to bring light to the world over the years. Please spare my life this once. I’ll do more good in the future to make up for my mistake.”","The Golden Crow First Prince had always been fawned on wherever he went; he had never been so subservient. I’ll slowly settle the score with him if I survive this ordeal. As formidable as he is, he's still nothing more than an unaffiliated cultivator. How can he compare to me, the noble son of a Celestial Emperor?","Zu An sighed. He remembered a classic line he had read in his previous life’s webnovels. “You don’t know your mistakes. You just know that you’re going to die.”","He released his bowstring, and the white light instantaneously appeared before the Golden Crow First Prince.","Just then, Zu An’s expression suddenly turned grim. The Golden Crow First Prince’s head didn’t explode as he had anticipated—some force had stopped his arrow. He looked closer and saw that a golden bell had manifested around the Golden Crow First Prince.","The golden bell was translucent and inscribed with obscure divine runes. It felt as if it was cloaked in a light, fluttery veil. Only those whose cultivation had reached a certain level could feel the dao flowing through it. Feeling the inviolable nature of the golden bell, Zu An suddenly felt as if his Tranquility Bell was a terrible bootleg.","A divine melody hummed as the space in front of Zu An slowly parted to reveal chaos within, before light suddenly burst forth. A figure slowly manifested amid the light. It was a man with long silver hair that cascaded like the Milky Way. The ends of his hair contained the sun’s flames, and they singed the area around them. He wore a black imperial robe with dark golden patterns that seemed to be forged out of the souls of countless primordial beasts. His very presence commanded heaven’s authority.","His eyes were gentle, but his gaze left Zu An feeling as if needles had stung him. This caused goosebumps to rise all over his body.","“How bizarre. A shaman’s aura mixed with a human’s bloodline...” The silver-haired man assessed Zu An, not understanding.","“Emperor Jun?” Zu An took a deep breath to loosen the tension in his muscles.","The silver-haired man shook his head. “Emperor Jun is my brother. People call me Taiyi.”","“Donghuang Taiyi!” Zu An’s eyes narrowed. That’s a supreme god whose standing in the legends equals Emperor Jun! The golden bell must be the legendary East Emperor Bell, renowned as the number one innate defensive artifact in the world. No wonder my arrow couldn’t pierce it!","Upon seeing Donghuang Taiyi, the Golden Crow First Prince straightened his hunched back and exclaimed, “Uncle, that scoundrel killed my other brothers! You must avenge us!”","This fellow is dead meat! Uncle has always doted on us! Now that uncle is here, no one can touch us anymore!","“Are the other Golden Crows dead?” Donghuang Taiyi was taken aback.","Sensing a powerful aura locking onto him, Zu An calmly replied, “I was only able to take down eight of them. The world can’t be without a sun, but two suns is still one too many. One will suffice.”","Donghuang Taiyi’s expression turned cold. “Hoh. You intend to continue your slaughter?”","The Golden Crow First Prince took this chance to hide behind Donghuang Taiyi as he looked at Zu An with a gloating expression. He’s asking for it. Where does he find the guts to continue running his mouth in my uncle’s presence? Does he take my uncle to be a pushover?","Zu An remained unfazed despite the immense pressure coming from Donghuang Taiyi. “The ten suns emerged simultaneously, causing countless lives to wither and die. They deserve to die for the sins they have committed. Do you, an esteemed personage in the Celestial Court, intend to violate the celestial laws?”","Donghuang Taiyi calmly replied, “They will be judged under the celestial laws; it’s not up to you to judge their crimes and punish them. Besides, they have diligently brought light to the masses over the years. How many living beings have prospered because of them? With the karma they have accrued, they don’t deserve death for such minor mistakes.”","“On the contrary, your crime of murdering the Celestial Court’s deities is much more grave. You ought to be sliced into bits.”","“Minor mistakes?” Zu An was first taken aback before abruptly bursting into laughter. “I thought you, with your exalted standing in the Celestial Court, would at least be capable of telling right from wrong. I didn’t expect you to have such double standards like anyone else.”","“Right from wrong?” Donghuang Taiyi scoffed. “The world simply observes its natural flow; it doesn’t exist to be right, and neither does it unravel over wrongs. All the talk about right and wrong is just self-deceiving, mortal babble. How hilarious it is for you to preach that to me with such seriousness.”","“Is it hilarious?” Zu An harrumphed. “You might think that humans are insignificant right now, and their values mean nothing to you. But one day, the concept of right and wrong will become mainstream in the world.”","Donghuang Taiyi’s face darkened. “How many years have you lived? How many years have I lived? Know your place! I am the stronger one here, and my standing is higher than yours. You’re just a mere unaffiliated cultivator. Even if I sentence you to death by a thousand cuts, you have no choice but to accept it, no matter how indignant you feel. This is the law of the world!”","He snapped his finger, and the air around Zu An suddenly turned turbulent. The gentle wind suddenly transformed into millions of incomparably sharp blades that covered every single inch of his skin.","“Uncle, don’t let him die an easy death!” the Golden Crow First Prince shouted excitedly.","The space around Zu An had been sealed off; he was unable to perform any defensive maneuvers. He couldn’t even use his instantaneous movement skills, let alone Rainbow Morph. No wonder he’s one of the top gods!","Without any hesitation, Zu An employed all his defensive methods. The Tranquility Bell manifested around him. After undergoing the heavenly tribulation, his Tranquility Bell had become many times stronger than before.","Even so, it was still instantly ripped through by the millions of air blades.","“How can that lousy bell of yours compare to my uncle’s...”","The Golden Crow First Prince was halfway through his sentence when his eyes nearly popped out. Another bell had appeared around Zu An, and it was the East Emperor Bell!","Living up to its reputation as the number one defensive artifact, it kept the countless terrifying air blades at bay.","Donghuang Taiyi was taken aback. “Rune Weapon Chart? How do you have that skill?”"]},{"number":2621,"title":"Chapter 2621: Chapter 2573: Forceful Murder","paragraphs":["Donghuang Taiyi eyed Zu An’s red bow and frowned. “The Dragon race’s bow, Suzeng, and the Dragon race’s skill. Are you a descendant of the true dragons?”","Zu An was stunned. He had heard that even though the Celestial Court’s Celestial Emperors viewed the Green Emperor as their founding ancestor, they were still divided into two factions. One was the Black Emperor’s faction, who viewed the Dragon race as their maternal race. The other was the White Emperor’s faction, who viewed the Phoenix race as their maternal race.","He had received the Rune Weapon Chart from Yu the Great back then. Looks like Yu the Great is a descendant of the Black Emperor.","He suddenly realized that this didn’t bode well for him. For various reasons, the Dragon race and the Phoenix race were on bad terms with each other, resulting in tension between the two factions. Donghuang Taiyi’s maternal race was the Phoenixes. That immediately deepened the grudge between them.","As expected, Donghuang Taiyi’s expression turned cold. “I was wondering how such a huge mistake could have happened. Turns out you have someone backing you. Do you think that your fake East Emperor Bell can stop my attack?”","The wind blades around Zu An became even more violent. The East Emperor Bell manifested by the Rune Weapon Chart was soon covered in cracks, looking as if it would shatter any time now.","The Golden Crow First Prince smirked. “Do you regret your actions now, scoundrel? If you kneel and kowtow to me right now, I’ll consider pleading for mercy on your behalf with my uncle.”","Heh, I won’t beg my uncle even if you kowtow and beg me right now.","He knew that most people looked tough on the surface, but once death became certain, they wouldn’t hesitate to grovel and do anything to survive, especially if they saw a ray of hope, no matter how unlikely it was. He wanted to see this detestable fellow kneel and break down in front of him. Only then would he be cleansed of the humiliation he had suffered at the other party’s hands.","Just remembering how he had lowered his head and begged Zu An for mercy earlier left him with a stinging sensation in his cheeks. I wonder if uncle saw that. How embarrassing!","Zu An glared at the Golden Crow First Prince. “I’ll kill you.”","The Golden Crow First Prince was stunned before he bent over and guffawed. “Hahaha! You’re already a dead man yourself, and you still want to kill me? Uncle, he thinks that he can kill me in your presence! Hahaha! I have never heard a greater joke in my life!”","A tinge of contempt flashed across Donghuang Taiyi’s face. “Young man, I concede that it is outstanding for someone of your age to reach your level of cultivation, but you’re still too weak compared to me.”","He waved his hand, and the East Emperor Bell around Zu An shattered. The wind blades exploited this opening to rush at Zu An. He made sure to control the wind blades precisely to each cut off a thin slice of flesh the width of a cicada’s wing, so that Zu An wouldn’t die too quickly.","Donghuang Taiyi smiled as if he was ready to marvel at his masterpiece.","However, the space around Zu An suddenly distorted. As if he had turned into a black hole, all the wind blades that approached him were absorbed.","Donghuang Taiyi's eyes widened in shock. “Taotie? The power of void?”","Zu An suddenly vanished into thin air, and in his place appeared a horrified Golden Crow First Prince. Uncle, I was waiting to admire that scoundrel’s miserable plight. How could you slip up here?","The Golden Crow First Prince looked at the terrifying wind blades rushing at him and paled. How can I withstand my uncle’s wind blades?!","Donghuang Taiyi was startled. The Taotie’s devouring ability had distorted the space around Zu An, which loosened his grip on the latter. He must have used that opening to escape, but how did he exchange positions with the Golden Crow First Prince?","With Donghuang Taiyi’s cultivation, he naturally sensed Zu An behind him. Knowing the red bow, Suzeng, posed a threat to him too, he instinctively summoned the East Emperor Bell to protect himself.","Even though he is much weaker than me, he possesses a lot of methods.","At the same time, he opened his palm to divert the wind blades rushing at the Golden Crow First Prince. If he accidentally killed his own nephew here, he would become the laughingstock of the world!","A white light divided the world into two. As soon as the wind blades scattered, the white light pierced through the Golden Crow First Prince’s body.","Pah!","The Golden Crow First Prince exploded like an inflated balloon. His feathers mixed with fresh blood scattered down, leaving a sinister, abstract painting in the sky.","It went without saying that the arrow had been shot by Zu An. He had made use of that brief opening to swap places with the Golden Crow First Prince using the position exchange skill.","He'd then pretended to attack Donghuang Taiyi despite knowing that the attack wouldn’t work even if he caught the latter by surprise, but it was all a feint. As he had expected, Donghuang Taiyi instinctively brought out the East Emperor Bell to protect himself. While ensuring his own safety, he also sought to rescue the Golden Crow First Prince from his wind blades.","Zu An had then made use of this opening to release his killer shot. Due to all the actions he had taken, Donghuang Taiyi couldn’t react in time.","Donghuang Taiyi was infuriated. “You’re courting death!”","You have trolled Donghuang Taiyi for +444... +444... +444...","How dare this ant kill my nephew before my eyes?","Not only would he be unable to face his big brother, Emperor Jun, and his sister-in-law, Xihe, but it would also sully his reputation if it became known that he, Donghuang Taiyi, couldn’t ensure the safety of a junior under his protection. How could he face others in the future?","He raised his arm and sent a palm backward. His palm encompassed an area of over twenty kilometers. Knowing that Zu An had an instantaneous movement skill, he widened the area of his attack so that Zu An would have nowhere to escape to!","This palm strike reduced the meandering mountain range behind him to bits. The ten suns had already turned the surroundings into a desert, and the palm further transformed the desert into a sea of lava. Smoke gushed into the sky.","Donghuang Taiyi’s expression suddenly turned cold. “Rainbow Morph!”","He sensed that he had failed to kill Zu An. The latter had escaped by morphing into a rainbow. Due to the Taotie’s devouring ability distorting the surrounding space, he could no longer lock down on Zu An’s aura as he did before.","“How many abilities does that fellow have?” Donghuang Taiyi was baffled.","His cultivation is at most that of a True Immortal, but his fighting prowess is comparable to a High Immortal...","No, in my presence, even a High Immortal is no more than an ant. I could easily kill a High Immortal, but that fellow’s abilities are proving to be an issue for me.","“Trying to escape? Do you think you can slip away from me?” Donghuang Taiyi morphed into a golden surge of light and pursued the rainbow.","There are too many secrets surrounding him. I can’t see through his background and karma. I have to capture him and get his secrets out of him."]},{"number":2622,"title":"Chapter 2622: Chapter 2574: You Have Guts","paragraphs":["Zu An’s Rainbow Morph was formidable, but Donghuang Taiyi was at least 30% faster than him. It didn’t take long before he was blocking Zu An’s path.","Zu An emerged from his Rainbow Morph to confront Donghuang Taiyi.","“You might have angered me, but you have also caught my attention.” Donghuang Taiyi examined Zu An from head to toe to figure out his background.","“That’s the stereotypical domineering CEO’s declaration. What a pity I’m not the female lead of a romance drama.” Despite Zu An’s casual words, his expression remained grim. His brain was furiously churning to find a way out of this.","Donghuang Taiyi wasn't particularly large, but his presence was so overwhelming to Zu An that it felt like there was nothing else except for him. In spite of Zu An’s many near-death experiences and his recent massive breakthrough, every cell in his body was furiously screaming danger at him.","Donghuang Taiyi frowned. He couldn’t understand Zu An’s statement about domineering CEOs and romance dramas. Experts of his caliber naturally abhorred the unknown. He harrumphed and said, “Forget it. I’ll first cripple your limbs before slowly interrogating you.\"","He was about to continue making a move when an anxious voice echoed, “Hold on!”","A cloud rushed over and morphed into a beautiful silhouette. It was none other than the Goddess of Wu Mountain. She was accompanied by the Kaiming Six Shamans and Xingtian.","Seeing that she was alone, Zu An was about to ask a question when she meticulously replied, “Miss Chang’e is still on Wu Mountain. You don’t have to worry about her.”","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. “What brings you here?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain assessed him with gleaming eyes. “We can’t turn a blind eye when you’re causing a huge ruckus here.”","Her words were filled with awe. Zu An had just shot down nine Golden Crows, after all. This was a feat beyond normal people, and those capable of subduing the Golden Crows would hold back because of their standing.","Zu An had done something else that no one dared to because of his righteous heart. He was courageous enough to stand up for the countless lives who had suffered under the Golden Crows’ tyranny.","This made her harden her expression. I’ll protect him no matter what it takes.","“Goddess?” Donghuang Taiyi frowned at the sight of her. “This has nothing to do with you, so stay away!”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain stood forward and raised her hands to protect Zu An. “The Golden Crows deserve to be executed for their sins. He’s merely enacting justice on behalf of heaven. What fault does he have?”","“Enacting justice on behalf of heaven?” Donghuang Taiyi scoffed. “Heaven has its own will. How can the likes of him be worthy of representing heaven?”","“If he’s unworthy, the same can be said about you lofty gods who turn a blind eye to your juniors massacring the masses!” The Goddess of Wu Mountain raised her slender neck as she berated Donghuang Taiyi. Her firm attitude was at odds with her usual nonchalant self.","The Kaiming Six Shamans were startled. They had never seen the goddess acting like this. Ever since Zu An arrived, they had seen many unknown sides to the goddess.","Her words made Donghuang Taiyi’s expression darken. “Yaoji, I am showing you respect on account of the Flame Emperor. Don’t overstep your boundaries.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was unfazed. “I am merely speaking up for what’s right. You celestials are the ones who betrayed the faith of the masses.”","“Audacious!” Donghuang Taiyi roared. An ancient bell chimed out of nowhere.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain moaned and spat out blood.","The Kaiming Six Shamans had their guard up, but the East Emperor Bell’s chime rang straight from their souls, rendering their defensive methods useless. It shook up their ki and caused them to ceaselessly vomit blood.","The chime also left Zu An’s head groggy, but Hundredwarble’s automatic counterattack and the Taotie’s devouring ability minimized the prowess of the chime. Seeing the goddess plummeting from the sky after sustaining severe injuries, he quickly flew over to catch her. He pumped his ki into her body as he asked, “Are you all right?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain gradually recovered from the blow. She belatedly noticed Zu An holding her by her waist, and that made her blush furiously. However, she wasn’t averse to it. “I’m fine. Thank you.”","The Kaiming Six Shamans, who had plummeted to the ground, rolled their eyes. We fell to the ground as well, so shouldn’t you at least help us up? Tsk, hoes over bros indeed!","“Donghuang, you’re too much!” Xingtian roared. He brandished his massive axe against Donghuang Taiyi. The sky shook as if the world was being severed into two.","Zu An was stunned. Xingtian was holding back back then. His axe is strong enough to even split the Golden Crow Princes in two.","“Know your place!” Donghuang Taiyi didn’t move in the least. He stood on the spot with his hands behind his back, his golden-embroidered black robe fluttering with the wind. He looked like a lofty immortal.","Dong!","A deep chime echoed. The East Emperor Bell had reappeared around Donghuang Taiyi. Xingtian’s powerful axe hack didn’t leave the slightest mark on the bell.","Instead, the rebound knocked Xingtian back by a kilometer before he regained his balance. He lowered his head and saw that his hands were bleeding profusely. Even so, he didn’t display the slightest fear. He even burst into laughter as his fighting spirit heightened. “Again!”","His muscles bulged, causing his physique to grow visibly. It didn’t take long for him to grow into a three-thousand-meter giant. He raised his humongous shield and charged at Donghuang Taiyi once more. The ground shook.","Zu An was awed. The Shamans are indeed born warriors. Their bloodline harnesses a berserk factor that makes them stronger the longer the battle drags out for.","Pah!","Despite the protection of the East Emperor Bell, Donghuang Taiyi was still knocked a hundred meters away under the sheer force of Xingtian’s charge.","“You’re courting death!” Donghuang Taiyi was infuriated. Despite not receiving any damage due to the East Emperor Bell’s protection, being knocked back in front of so many people pricked his pride. He waved his hand, and a surge of golden light sliced toward Xingtian’s neck.","“Be careful!” Zu An was taken aback. In the legends, Xingtian’s head was lopped off. Could this be the cause of that?","Xingtian narrowed his eyes. The East Emperor Bell was so sturdy that the rebound caused his reactions to be delayed. He tried to raise his shield to guard his neck, but he was a step too late. He wasn’t going to make it in time.","Just as he was about to be decapitated, a water dragon suddenly surged forth and collided with the golden light.","Boom!","The water dragon and the golden light neutralized each other.","“Taiyi, don’t you feel ashamed bullying the juniors?” A snake-bodied, human-headed man arrived at the battlefield riding on a wave. His fluttering red hair was particularly eye-catching.","When the waves scattered, the cracked earth regained its vibrancy. Even the desert that Donghuang Taiyi had reduced into a lava pool was extinguished and transformed into a lake.","Donghuang Taiyi’s face darkened. “Gonggong!”","Gonggong ignored him. He turned to Zu An and shot him a thumbs up. “You did great, lad. You have guts!”","Zu An felt conflicted. The final boss of his previous trip here had been none other than Gonggong, though the Gonggong was from another generation. Nevertheless, it still felt bizarre to receive the approval of the ‘antagonist’.","Donghuang Taiyi scoffed, “Gonggong, have you forgotten the agreement between the Ancestral Shamans and the Celestial Court? That brat killed my nine nephews. Do you intend to break the promise between our races for that murderer?”","Gonggong cackled. “You Celestials have been an eyesore for a long time now. If even a junior dares to stand up against you people, why should I, an Ancestral Shaman, cower?”"]},{"number":2623,"title":"Chapter 2623: Chapter 2575: Saving Her","paragraphs":["Zu An burst into laughter. He'd thought that Gonggong would claim the moral high ground and lambast Donghuang Taiyi until the latter could no longer raise his head. Who could have thought that Gonggong wasn’t interested in reason at all?","He'd outright declared his determination to mess with them. How could anyone rebut that?","Donghuang Taiyi’s eyelids twitched. “I can give you a fight if you want one, but I have other matters to settle today. I’ll fight you another day.”","Gonggong scoffed, “Do you take me for a fool? Who wants to fight you another day? I’ll fight you right now.”","The waves beneath Gonggong diverged into countless streams to simultaneously attack Donghuang Taiyi from multiple directions.","Donghuang Taiyi scoffed. A massive giant bell that harmonized with the dao manifested around him and blocked all the incoming water arrows. “How do you intend to fight me when you can’t even breach my defense?”","“We’ll have to fight to find out.” Gonggong laughed. A staff appeared in his hand, and he charged at Donghuang Taiyi.","The staff shone with a golden light. Zu An couldn’t help but stare at it. Why does it look so familiar? Could that be the future Sun Wukong’s Golden-hooped Staff?","Gonggong and the golden staff’s afterimages appeared all around Donghuang Taiyi, attacking the latter from different directions at an astounding speed. A deafening chime would sound with each strike, shaking up the spectators’ blood. Only by retreating fifty kilometers away did the impact of their clashes become more bearable.","“I am feeling better now...” the Goddess of Wu Mountain meekly told Zu An with a reddened face.","Zu An belatedly realized that he was still holding her in his arms. Alarmed, he quickly put her down and said, “My apologies. I was too focused on the battle...”","The sensation of her body lingered on his palm. Her body is so soft.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s heartbeat quickened as well, and she didn’t dare to look at him. She could only try to change the topic. “Who do you think will win?”","Zu An studied the two entities clashing in the sky. “Gonggong has been testing the East Emperor Bell’s defense from different angles for an opening, but he hasn’t found a breakthrough yet. The East Emperor Bell lives up to its reputation as the number one defensive artifact. It’s unlikely that Gonggong can defeat Donghuang Taiyi. At best, he can only push for a draw.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain said, “Gonggong is an Ancestral Shaman. His abilities can’t be underestimated. There’s a chance he can turn things around.”","Meanwhile, the battle was moving on to the next stage.","Even though Donghuang Taiyi remained unharmed despite Gonggong’s barrage of attacks, those who didn’t know better could think he had been overwhelmed and couldn’t counterattack. How could he, the great East Emperor, leave behind such a dark spot on his record?","Flames blazed from Donghuang Taiyi. He transformed into a massive phoenix and rushed toward Gonggong, burning the sky wherever he crossed. Gonggong’s afterimages were instantly devoured by the phoenix, but Donghuang Taiyi didn’t look satisfied with his counterattack. Instead, he looked at the ground with a grim expression.","A massive snake boasting a length of over thirty thousand meters suddenly rose from the ground. Despite its realistic appearance, it wasn't made out of blood and flesh, but water ki. This was Gonggong’s transformation.","The snake lurched at the phoenix. In response, the phoenix screeched and fought back. It was an intense fight where all sorts of laws and daos clashed, causing the world to shake.","But Gonggong soon found himself at a disadvantage. The East Emperor Bell continued to protect the phoenix, allowing it to claim the upper hand each time they clashed.","“Lord Gonggong, I’ll help you!” Xingtian noticed this subtle detail and charged into the fray with his massive axe and shield.","“Scram! This is my business with him!” Gonggong roared in anger.","He was already annoyed at failing to claim the upper hand, and this tactless junior still wanted to join the battle. If I fight him two on one, it won’t look good on me even if I win the battle!","That remark left Xingtian in an awkward position.","Zu An flew to Xingtian’s side and said, “Don’t mind it. He needs to uphold his pride too. Leave it to me instead.”","Zu An drew his Sun Slaying Bow and aimed it at the phoenix in the sky.","Xingtian anxiously exclaimed, “The Ancestral Shaman will reprimand you for this too!”","“I’m not a shaman; I don’t obey your Ancestral Shaman,” Zu An coldly spat. This was a rare opportunity to take down Donghuang Taiyi for good. He would be in trouble if Donghuang Taiyi got away, as there wouldn't necessarily be a Gonggong and a Xingtian to help him the next time.","“Brat, what are you doing?” Gonggong noticed Zu An’s actions and hissed.","“I’m just stretching my body. Don’t think too much of it.” Zu An fully drew his bowstring but didn’t fire the arrow.","Gonggong didn’t continue harping on it, since Zu An didn’t release his arrow. Besides, he had to focus on dealing with Donghuang Taiyi’s barrage of attacks.","Zu An’s gesture, however, made Donghuang Taiyi extremely uncomfortable. Under normal circumstances, he wouldn’t fear Zu An’s arrow since he had the protection of his East Emperor Bell. But Zu An’s refusal to shoot meant that he had to constantly keep an eye out for Zu An and guard against the other party’s attack. Zu An’s red bow, Suzeng, was a deity-grade artifact. If he let his guard down, the tables could be turned quickly.","But being distracted in a fight against Gonggong put him at a huge disadvantage. In the first place, Gonggong’s strength rivaled his. His biggest advantage over Gonggong was the East Emperor Bell. But now that his East Emperor Bell needed to be ready to block the Sun Slaying Bow’s attack at any moment, he had to think twice before deploying it for Gonggong.","This caused the tides of the battle to change. Donghuang Taiyi even had a few close calls, leaving him angry and frustrated. He wanted to charge over and kill Zu An first, but Gonggong wouldn’t give him the chance to do so.","You have trolled Donghuang Taiyi for +888... +888... +888...","The Goddess of Wu Mountain chuckled. She looked at Zu An with gleaming eyes. Indeed, there’s nothing more threatening than an unshot arrow. To think that he would come up with such a solution.","Perhaps Zu An’s actions looked lackadaisical, but in truth, he was focused on finding Donghuang Taiyi’s opening to unleash a fatal blow on him.","Suddenly, his hair stood on end. There were two exclamations from the side. “Be careful!”","A golden light flashed across the sky. He had never seen such a fast attack before. He'd have been able to dodge the attack under normal circumstances, but he was so focused on dealing with Donghuang Taiyi that he couldn’t react in time.","Fortunately, Xingtian was right beside him. With a furious roar, the mountain-like Xingtian stood in front of Zu An and raised his shield, but much to everyone’s horror, the golden light sliced through the shield and continued surging forth.","Blood splattered as Xingtian’s massive head was lopped off and flew into the air.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain transformed into a fog and enveloped Zu An to pull him to safety, but she, too, was scraped by the golden light. A moan escaped from her lips as she reverted to her human form.","Sensing that she was about to fall, Zu An quickly grabbed her. Her face was ghastly pale. Blood seeped from the corners of her lips. The golden light had inflicted severe injuries on her even though it was just a scrape. Zu An quickly turned toward the culprit.","The golden light slowly morphed into a middle-aged man, who wore a crown with twelve dangling jade pieces. His body was wrapped in the sun’s flames. A celestial chart revolved behind him. A golden fire flower bloomed with each step he took in the air. He had a dashing appearance, but his cold eyes and sharp eagle nose made him look cold.","“What a pity. You escaped from that attack,” a cold voice echoed. He eyed Zu An from the sky as if the latter was no more than an ant, though his cold eyes were filled with hatred.","Zu An’s heart sank. The middle-aged man’s imperial gown, and the solar flames that resembled Donghuang Taiyi’s and the Golden Crow Ten Princes’ made his identity apparent.","He was the next Celestial Emperor, Emperor Jun!"]},{"number":2624,"title":"Chapter 2624: Chapter 2576: His Life Is Mine","paragraphs":["Zu An had no spare energy to reply to Emperor Jun. He rushed to Xingtian’s side with the Goddess of Wu Mountain in his arms to see if he could save Xingtian.","To his surprise, Xingtian’s headless body suddenly brandished his axe and shield as he roared, “I have not been defeated yet! Let’s continue the battle!” Shockwaves rippled from his weapons. Having his head lopped off made him so furious that his attacks were filled with murderous intent. It was impossible to approach him like that.","Zu An had no choice but to back away along with the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","“How can he still speak?” The Goddess of Wu Mountain gasped in astonishment.","Zu An pointed to Xingtian’s belly button. “His voice seems to be coming from there.”","He had naturally heard the story about the headless Xingtian brandishing his axe and shield, but he could never have imagined that Xingtian’s head would be lopped off while saving him. His blood raced at that thought.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain took a closer look. Xingtian’s belly button was indeed opening and closing like a mouth. “Let’s find his head. He might be able to put himself back together.”","Stitching one’s head back onto their body wasn't difficult for cultivators of their caliber.","Zu An nodded in agreement. He flashed toward Xingtian’s falling head. As he was about to grab the head, however, a ray of flames shot through it and reduced it to ashes.","Zu An and the Goddess of Wu Mountain were shocked and infuriated. They looked back at the culprit.","Emperor Jun looked back at them with cold eyes. “Am I invisible to you?”","Xingtian howled chillingly. He clutched the severed stump of his neck as if his head were still there. Despite his head already being separated from his body, having it reduced to ashes still inflicted unbearable pain upon him.","Two blood streams flowed down from his nipples. All of a sudden, they opened to reveal his new eyes. He glared at Emperor Jun with bloody tears in his eyes.","“Die!” Xingtian roared from his belly button as he brandished his axe at Emperor Jun. A huge gorge was left on the ground wherever his axe crossed.","Emperor Jun morphed into a golden light to dodge the attacks.","However, light could be seen distorting in the wake of Xingtian’s attacks, indicating that they were strong enough to distort even space. That made Emperor Jun’s expression darken. He hadn’t expected Xingtian to become even stronger after having his head destroyed.","Hmph, the Shaman races’ berserk bloodline is abominable!","The headless Xingtian leaped over to Emperor Jun’s side and unleashed dozens of cuts.","Emperor Jun parried the attacks with his hand, but the attacks were so relentless that he began to lose his patience. “You’re courting death!”","Flames suddenly surged around Emperor Jun and rushed at Xingtian.","Just then, however, a powerful wave gushed over and stopped the flames.","Emperor Jun was startled. He raised his head to look at Gonggong. Isn’t he fighting Donghuang Taiyi? How can he have the energy to interfere with my fight? Did something happen to Taiyi?","But Gonggong and Donghuang Taiyi were still clashing intensely with each other.","Gonggong noticed the situation as well and was surprised. “That lad can control water?”","Indeed, Zu An had used the Hundredwarble and Crown of the Ocean Deity’s abilities to borrow Gonggong’s water and extinguish Emperor Jun’s flames.","Donghuang Taiyi shouted out a warning.","Emperor Jun’s eyes fell on Zu An once more. Hatred flared in his eyes. “It’s you!”","You have successfully trolled Emperor Jun for +444... +444... +444...","Two grand wings unfurled behind Emperor Jun. Each feather on his wings was comparable to a deity-grade artifact, and they shrouded Zu An with their sharp sword ki.","Having fought the Fiend Emperor and the Golden Crows in the Cultivation World, Zu An was familiar with this move. But it was Emperor Jun executing it this time, so it was more than a thousand times stronger. After sensing its terrifying destructive prowess, Zu An didn’t dare let his guard down. He quickly sent the Goddess of Wu Mountain to safety with a gentle force before drawing his Tai’e Sword to confront the sword ki.","In a matter of moments, Zu An was already inflicted with many sword wounds. Fresh blood oozed from his injuries. Even his manifested East Emperor Bell was instantly destroyed by the sword ki. He had only survived because of his Heaven-Devouring Sutra, but even so, he was still unable to neutralize most of the ki.","Emperor Jun was as shocked by Zu An as he hadn’t held back in his attacks. The latter had killed his nine sons and ruined his plans. He hated Zu An so much that he wanted nothing more than to grind the other party’s bones into ashes.","His first attack had been blocked by Xingtian’s head, but he hadn’t expected Zu An to take his second attack head-on and survive!","How can someone of his cultivation withstand my attack?","Emperor Jun gritted his teeth. He was about to charge at Zu An when the headless Xingtian roared and charged at him once more. His expression turned cold as he directed his sword ki toward Xingtian.","Xingtian raised his shield to protect himself while brandishing his axe to cut down the golden sword feathers. It didn’t take long before he was bleeding profusely, but that further invoked his bloodline power, causing his attacks to become more ferocious, like a war god.","Worried that Xingtian could slip up, Zu An quickly attacked Emperor Jun to share Xingtian’s burden.","“You despicable rats!” Emperor Jun spat through gritted teeth.","He could have easily defeated either of them individually. Xingtian was strong, but he specialized in physical confrontations. Any skills hurled at him would have put him in a fluster. But Zu An, despite his lower cultivation, happened to have all kinds of random methods. The sheer number of abilities he had shocked even Emperor Jun.","Their coordination covered each other’s flaws, making it difficult for Emperor Jun to take them down quickly. Of course, that didn’t mean he couldn’t defeat them; it would just take him longer than anticipated.","But what he lacked the most now was time. The ten suns in the sky had caused such a huge commotion that it was bound to catch the attention of all kinds of powerhouses. Gonggong was merely the first to arrive. Things could get messy if the other Ancestral Shamans or Zhuanxu came too.","He suddenly noticed the worried Goddess of Wu Mountain in his peripheral vision, and a thought surfaced in his mind. He feigned an attack before thrusting his palm at the distant Goddess of Wu Mountain.","A golden palmprint instantly appeared before the Goddess of Wu Mountain. Space compressed wherever the palmprint crossed, as if gravity had been amplified ten thousand times. If this attack landed, the goddess would immediately go splat.","The Kaiming Six Shamans wanted to save her, but they were too far away to make it in time.","Zu An was horrified. He performed an instantaneous movement to get to the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s side, but there was no time for him to escape with her. He could only embrace her and take on the attack with his back.","Pu!","Despite Zu An’s countless defense skills and the protection of the Heaven-Devouring Sutra’s devouring power, he was still unable to neutralize the palm strike and spat large mouthfuls of blood. Even pieces of his innards were visible amid the blood.","“Are you all right?!” the usually cold Goddess of Wu Mountain exclaimed in a fluster. She hurriedly cast her recovery spells to treat his injuries.","Zu An didn’t answer. With his current regenerative prowess, he could make a full recovery even if someone blasted half his body into bits, but it went without saying that Emperor Jun wouldn’t give him the time to recover.","Xingtian tried to stall Emperor Jun, but the latter had already anticipated this situation. While dealing with Xingtian’s attacks, Emperor Jun thrust his palm once more. If this palm strike landed, both Zu An and the Goddess of Wu Mountain would be reduced to a bloody mist.","Gonggong wanted to help, but Donghuang Taiyi wouldn’t give him the chance.","Just then, another sun suddenly appeared and blocked that devastating palm strike.","“What are you doing?!” Emperor Jun was shocked and infuriated.","The sun slowly morphed into a beautiful woman. “His life is mine. I shall end him personally!”"]},{"number":2625,"title":"Chapter 2625: Chapter 2577: Pain","paragraphs":["A searing crack appeared in the sky. A ravishing, mature lady emerged from billowing golden clouds. She was dressed in a fluttering, long skirt embroidered with 360 days of constellation patterns. Her hair resembled a golden waterfall, and her body was cloaked in a faint purple mist. It was as if sunset and twilight were in harmony on her impeccable face. She had a divine and lofty air.","She stared at Zu An coldly, looking as if she would tear him into pieces.","Emperor Jun nodded. “All right, I’ll hand him to you.” He then charged at Xingtian, hoping to use this opportunity to end the latter sooner.","Alarmed, the Goddess of Wu Mountain telepathically urged the Kaiming Six Shamans to aid Xingtian.","Two intense battles raged on the battlefield, but somehow, Zu An’s side had quieted down instead.","Looking at the woman, Zu An bitterly remarked, “Sun Goddess Xihe!”","The last time he was here, he'd followed Yi’s heroic path and shot down the nine suns, prompting the Sun Goddess Xihe to emerge and exact vengeance on him. Back then, he'd been too weak to survive Xihe’s rampage, so he had no choice but to use the Golden Phoenix’s ability to make her fall in love with him. Thanks to that, he escaped with his life. There was no way he would forget her face.","However, he had gone farther back in time now. He was likely thousands or even tens of thousands of years behind in terms of the timeline compared to the last time he was here. She might not be affected by the Golden Phoenix yet.","“We meet again. Last time, I told you that I’d kill you.” Xihe glared at him with hatred.","Zu An’s mind jolted. I’m not surprised that she knows me, but how does she remember the conversation we had the last time we were here? I’m now tens of thousands of years back in time; she shouldn’t know something that hasn’t happened yet.","For a moment, he even doubted time itself.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain shouted, “Sun Goddess, you should know about the deaths caused by the emergence of the ten suns. They would have been sentenced to death either way. He was merely exacting punishment on behalf of heaven!”","“Shut your mouth!” The Sun Goddess coldly waved her hand, and her jade bracelets clanged resoundingly against one another.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain felt as if the stars were shifting around her. She was sent flying and spat a mouthful of blood.","The Sun Goddess coldly eyed the Goddess of Wu Mountain. “They are my sons.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain understood where the Sun Goddess was coming from. The Golden Crows might have committed grievous sins, but they are still her children. There’s no way she can spare the man who murdered her children.","Zu An rushed to the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s side and inspected her body. The latter had already been severely injured before, and this blow pushed her further into death’s embrace. He took out a bunch of spirit medicine and fed it to her while addressing the Sun Goddess. “I’m the one you’re after. Don’t implicate the innocent.”","“Oh? Does your heart bleed to see her injured?” the Sun Goddess sneered. “I remember seeing more beautiful women by your side the last time we met, but she wasn’t one of them.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was baffled. Why does her tone sound so off? It’s almost as if... she’s envious. Hold on, I also sensed something unusual from that woman before. Could it be...","Just then, Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. “It hasn’t been long since we last met. It’s not as if you haven’t met Yaoji.”","Upon hearing him call her by her name, the Goddess of Wu Mountain blushed.","The Sun Goddess narrowed her eyes. “I don’t know what you’re talking about.”","“You don’t?” Zu An settled the Goddess of Wu Mountain down on a nearby peak before facing the Sun Goddess. “Should I call you the Sun Goddess... or Yumen Beiqing?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain widened her eyes. Just as I thought!","The Sun Goddess was taken aback. She was silent for a long time before asking, “When did you find out?”","Zu An felt stifled by her admittance. He explained, “When you provided me with a clue to Manman’s whereabouts, but no one saw her except for those in the first town we visited. It struck me that there could be something wrong with the intel. However, I didn’t think you had a reason to deceive me then. Little sister Ling’er wouldn’t do that out of envy.”","“When did you realize I wasn’t your little sister Ling’er?”","“I didn’t doubt you initially. The Fiend races were hostile toward me, but you unconditionally sided with me and even...”","At this point, Zu An and the Sun Goddess’ faces reddened as their hearts skipped a beat. They unceremoniously recalled what had happened in the shadows of the night...","The Sun Goddess took a deep breath. “Stop beating around the bush and get to the point.”","Zu An reined himself in and continued, “You led me to the imperial tomb using the Brilliant Pinflower as bait, but it wasn’t there. Later, I realized that you were trying to lure me to this world.","“When we arrived in this world, there was a mysterious power outburst near our cavern’s vicinity. I thought something had happened to you and rushed out, only to see you returning. Your reason made sense, but it was still too coincidental. Especially because I sensed the Sun Goddess’ power there.”","The Sun Goddess scoffed, “It’s all the Time Scribe’s fault. You wouldn’t have noticed it so quickly if not for him.”","“So you were the one who killed the Time Scribe.” Zu An nodded in realization. He had been feeling uneasy, as the Time Scribe had disappeared. “Indeed, you wouldn’t have been able to kill him without using your true powers.","“There were many lapses in your disguise afterward. I wouldn’t have doubted you based on those, but with my suspicion already piqued, these giveaways were conspicuous.” Zu An was perplexed. “The only thing I don’t get is why you've been doing all these things.”","“Someone as smart as you should be able to fathom a guess,” the Sun Goddess sneered.","Zu An thought about the time they had spent together. “You were trying to change history, or more specifically, the fate of the Golden Crows.”","The Sun Goddess lowered her gaze in despair. “I tried everything. I tried to save Yayu. I tried to protect Bao Jiang... But nothing worked. I even tried to kill Yi in advance, but fate pulled a prank on me—you became the new Yi. I realized that the hands of fate are correcting my actions. I can’t change anything no matter how I struggle.”","Zu An fell silent. The Golden Crows deserved death, but she’s a noble mother. She did all these things to save her children, but she was unable to outmaneuver fate.","“Where are Manman and Xie Daoyun?” As much as he sympathized with her, there were some things that he needed to get to the bottom of.","“I killed them,” the Sun Goddess sneered.","“What?!” Zu An was shocked and infuriated. He was so shaken that he struggled to maintain his balance.","His reaction brought glee to the Sun Goddess’ face. “Do you finally understand the pain of losing a loved one now? Don’t worry, you can join them in death!”","With that, she morphed into thousands of rays of golden light that charged toward Zu An."]},{"number":2626,"title":"Chapter 2626: Chapter 2578: Shocking Gossip","paragraphs":["“Be careful!” the Goddess of Wu Mountain exclaimed.","Zu An was still feeling downtrodden, but the Sun Goddess had already begun her onslaught. Unfortunately, the Goddess of Wu Mountain was too severely injured to help him even if she wanted to.","Her voice was nowhere as fast as the Sun Goddess, who was already before Zu An. As if vanquished, everything else vanished in the presence of her light.","Emperor Jun nodded in approval. He'd been dissatisfied when he saw how Xihe was having a pleasant chat with Zu An instead of killing the latter. Just as he was about to rush her, she'd finally made a move and gone all out. That put his mind at ease.","“Be careful! Despite that fellow’s low cultivation, he possesses many bizarre skills. He isn’t that easy of an enemy to deal with!” Emperor Jun warned when he sensed how Zu An was still alive despite Xihe’s attack.","Xihe coldly looked toward the ground. Zu An was standing there, gasping for air.","“You’re really after my life!” Zu An sweated profusely when he thought about the earlier situation. If not for his position swap ability, that attack would have taken his life. He had felt that aura before. It was similar to the attack that the mysterious Time Scribe had died to. Looks like Xihe really wants me dead.","Xihe scoffed, “Did you think I would swear loyalty to you just because I went to bed with you?”","She darted toward Zu An while unleashing rays of golden light. Her light vanquished everything in its path, even severing mountains apart. Zu An didn’t dare to let his guard down. He mustered his attention to deal with her onslaught.","Meanwhile, the Goddess of Wu Mountain widened her eyes in shock. Even though the two of them had previously behaved like a couple, considering Xihe’s true identity, she hadn't thought they would be involved in a physical relationship. Learning that the two of them had reached that level of intimacy was a shock.","Even the warring Donghuang Taiyi and Gonggong paused out of sheer astonishment.","Donghuang Taiyi looked at Zu An and Xihe in utmost shock. Xihe, as one of the loftiest goddesses of the Celestial Court, had plenty of suitors, and Donghuang Taiyi had been one of them too. But fate had other plans, and she'd eventually become his sister-in-law.","Nevertheless, he'd still harbored special feelings for his beautiful sister-in-law, which was why he doted on her ten sons a lot. Others had even jokingly remarked that the Golden Crows were his sons. He would sternly warn them not to run their mouths, but he still felt warm inside.","That was partly why he'd been so angry when he learned that Zu An had killed the Golden Crows.","However, because of his brotherly ties with Emperor Jun, he had never overstepped the line. He also respected Xihe for her upright character as well, so he'd never harbored inappropriate thoughts toward her. He'd thought that it was sufficient bliss to admire her and wish her happiness.","And yet, the goddess of his heart had rolled in the sheets with another man? And that man was a human, at that!","No, she must be saying that to deceive me!","He tried convincing himself of that, but deep down, he knew the truth. Many images flashed through his mind—the lofty goddess whom he didn’t dare to touch had been thoroughly sullied by a far lesser man of lowly bloodline! This made his anger flare. He was on the verge of exploding.","You have successfully trolled Donghuang Taiyi for +999... +999... +999...","In contrast to the infuriated Donghuang Taiyi, Gonggong shot a thumbs up at Zu An and burst into laughter. “You’re a completely different breed!”","He was already in awe of Zu An for daring to kill the Golden Crows—that was a feat that even the powerhouses dared not do—but to think that there was something more explosive than that!","He had been long displeased with the lofty celestials, but he had to admit that they were getting increasingly formidable. The world was slowly becoming accustomed to the rule of the Celestial Court. And yet, the next Celestial Emperor’s wife had been bedded by a mortal! This would become a stain on Emperor Jun's and the Celestial Court’s reputation!","I've never seen such a huge drama before! It was worth making the trip here!","He had already decided to spread this news even if everyone else kept it a secret. He would even dispatch his subordinates to plaster posters and advertise this matter. Thinking about the mess it would cause made him grin widely.","The Kaiming Six Shamans, already injured from the fighting, silently retreated in the face of Emperor Jun’s terrifying outburst of energy. It was clear to see that Emperor Jun was on the verge of going on a rampage. Only someone tired of living would trifle with him now.","They couldn’t help but sneak glances at Zu An. When they first saw the latter, they hadn’t thought there was anything special about him other than his looks, his height, and his ability to charm women. They would never have expected him to pull off something this insane.","Why is even the legendary Sun Goddess interested in him?","The Kaiming Six Shamans couldn’t make sense of the situation.","Emperor Jun had been confident that everything was in his grasp when he suddenly heard this explosive news. Xihe had mentioned something along this line the last time they met, but he'd thought that she was uttering nonsense in a fit of anger and shrugged it off. He was the lofty Celestial Emperor, whereas Zu An was an insignificant mortal. Any woman with eyes would know who to side with, right?","But Xihe’s words and that brat’s reaction hinted that it was real. The thought of his wife being under another man’s body made him so angry that he could pop a vein!","Is Xihe doing this to exact vengeance on me? Why? Why?!","He roared, “You scoundrel! I’ll tear your tendons and crush your bones! I’ll burn your soul with the sun’s true flames for a hundred thousand years!”","You have successfully trolled Emperor Jun for +1024... +1024... +1024...","He was about to charge at Zu An when a figure blocked his path.","It was Xingtian, who still had blood tears flowing down his nipples. “Your opponent is me!”","“Scram!” Emperor Jun roared in anger, but he couldn’t shake off Xingtian no matter how he tried. Xingtian was so sturdy that he firmly stood his ground no matter how battered his body was. Instead, his bloodline’s war god prowess made him more valiant the more he fought.","Seeing this, the Kaiming Six Shamans had no choice but to muster their courage to help Xingtian. Damn it! He’s having fun while the rest of us are suffering.","Zu An sneezed. Looking at the insane influx of Rage points in his system, he couldn’t help but wonder why Xihe had chosen to reveal this matter in public. Despite being enemies now, he had never thought of blackmailing her with it.","So why did she choose to reveal it on her own accord? She has nothing to gain out of this!","While he was perplexed, he suddenly received a telepathic message."]},{"number":2627,"title":"Chapter 2627: Chapter 2579: Gamble With My Life","paragraphs":["Zu An was taken aback to hear the content of the message, though he didn’t let anything show on his face.","Xihe’s attack was becoming fiercer. As the Sun Goddess, she commanded the sun’s brilliance. The sun could be gentle and warm, but it could also be wild and destructive. Mountains were crushed wherever they passed.","Zu An faced several close shaves. He would have long been torn into shreds if not for his rich combat experience and arsenal of mystical abilities.","Watching as Zu An was continuously pushed in his direction, Emperor Jun snarled. He finally found a chance to knock Xingtian back and charge out of the Kaiming Six Shamans’ encirclement to hurl a palm strike at Zu An’s back.","It was beneath his standing to attack a human, let alone such an assault. However, not a single person frowned on his action. If anything, they thought that he was too late to make a move.","Xihe radiated a brilliant golden light to seal off the surrounding space, giving Zu An no chance to slip away.","Emperor Jun nodded in glee. She’s my wife, after all. Despite being estranged in recent years, our coordination remains impeccable.","“Be careful!”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain anxiously unleashed the skill she had been channeling. A massive fog suddenly enveloped Emperor Jun in an attempt to stop his attack.","However, the flames around Emperor Jun flared, and the fog was instantly vaporized. The Goddess of Wu Mountain coughed from the backlash and nearly fainted. She was unable to help Zu An despite having depleted the final sliver of her energy.","But the split second she'd bought for Zu An turned out to be invaluable. Zu An was able to pull himself together to flash twenty meters away and dodge Emperor Jun’s palm strike.","But Emperor Jun wasn't that easy to deal with. Like a maggot suckling on a bone, he relentlessly pursued Zu An and unleashed yet another strike. This fellow is slippery like a loach. It’s hard for me to kill him alone, but now that Xihe is cooperating with me, it’ll be much easier.","Suddenly, Emperor Jun’s eyes widened. He abandoned his pursuit of Zu An and instead morphed into a golden light to dodge sideward. However, in his fluster, he forgot that Xihe had already sealed off the surrounding space with her golden light, rendering any teleportation abilities useless.","Excruciating pain assaulted his lower back. Without any hesitation, he thrust his palm to knock away Xihe, who had just assaulted him.","At the same moment, however, Zu An suddenly appeared beside him to plunge a pitch-black dagger at his ribcage. The ominous runes on the dagger alarmed Emperor Jun. Despite his strength and standing, he still felt threatened by the weapon. Golden light flared from his body as he quickly activated all his defensive methods.","But Zu An and Xihe’s cooperation was so impeccable that Emperor Jun couldn’t completely avoid the attack despite unleashing his full strength. He managed to avoid being struck in his vitals, but the pitch-black dagger still cut into his arm.","Emperor Jun used his artifacts to block further attacks from Zu An and Xihe so that he could retreat and catch a breather. He stared at his arm in horror, looking nowhere as relaxed as before. A black aura containing bizarre runes was slowly creeping up his arm.","In retaliation, the divine marks on his arm flickered, and a golden light shone to cleanse away the black runes, but for some reason, it wasn’t working. Instead, the black aura was gradually forcing back his golden light.","Emperor Jun was one of the supreme gods of the Celestial Court. His body was in harmony with the dao, granting him formidable recovery and cleansing abilities. Malevolent energies shouldn’t have been able to breach his defenses!","“What’s wrong with that dagger?!” Horrified, Emperor Jun unhesitatingly sliced off his injured arm.","The black aura devoured his arm as soon as it was severed from his body. It withered at a visible pace and turned into white bones.","Emperor Jun’s eyelids twitched. With his cultivation, his corpse wasn't supposed to wither for a million years after his death. His divine bones should also have been as pristine as the finest jade, emanating a faint divine light and pressure. And yet, his severed arm was already decomposing.","Meanwhile, Zu An and Xihe broke free from Emperor Jun’s defensive artifacts to flank him. What a pity! That was such a good chance to kil l Emperor Jun ! As expected of the Celestial Emperor. He survived despite being struck by the Poisonous Prick.","Earlier, Xihe had sent him a telepathic message suggesting that the two of them put on a show to deal with Emperor Jun. Since there was no reason for her to turn against Emperor Jun, Zu An couldn’t tell if Xihe was trying to entrap him. If this was her ploy, Zu An could find himself cornered by the celestial couple.","But when he looked into her eyes and remembered the time they had spent together, he'd still decided to trust her once more. It wasn't entirely a reckless decision, but rather, reflecting on the time they had spent together had left him with a guess.","Besides, there was no need for Xihe to resort to such trickery. The combined prowess of the celestial couple was more than enough to corner him. There was no need to do something this superfluous.","So, he'd decided to gamble with his life.","Xihe was surprised at first when Zu An agreed to go along with her, but in the end, they'd succeeded in injuring Emperor Jun.","A divine light shone from Emperor Jun’s severed right arm, and it didn’t take long for a new arm to sprout out. As a Golden Immortal, even if his body and Primordial Spirit were destroyed, he could make a full recovery as long as he had a single droplet of blood essence or soul fragment left; healing an arm was nothing in comparison.","Of course, that came at a price. If he were to sustain such grievous damage, it was unlikely that he would ever reach Sainthood.","This minor injury wouldn’t hinder him from reaching Sainthood, but the effects of that bizarre dagger left him at least 10% weaker than when he was at his peak. His complexion darkened. How could I, the Celestial Emperor, be pushed so far by a mere ant?","Of course, what angered him the most was still his wife’s betrayal. How dare that slut collude with that scoundrel to assassinate me? Turns out I was the laughingstock all along!","The knowledge that Zu An had not only conquered his wife’s body, but also her heart, made Emperor Jun seethe with anger.","You have successfully trolled Emperor Jun for +1024... +1024... +1024...","“Why?!” Emperor Jun glared at his wife. He couldn’t understand why she would do this.","They had been estranged for many years now, but they were still a couple on the surface. On top of that, Zu An had just killed nine of her sons. He couldn’t understand why she would side with Zu An to assassinate him.","Are Zu An’s techniques so great that she can overlook his crimes of killing her sons?","The images that popped into Emperor Jun’s mind made his face darken further.","You have successfully trolled Emperor Jun for +999... +999... +999...","Xihe glared back at Emperor Jun. “You know what you have done better than anyone else!”","“What did I do?” Emperor Jun was so furious that he began laughing manically. “That fellow killed our nine sons! I am trying to avenge our sons now! Instead of helping me, you collude with him to deal with me. You are unworthy of being a mother!”","“Shut your mouth!” Xihe’s mouth trembled. “You know who killed our sons better than anyone!”"]},{"number":2628,"title":"Chapter 2628: Chapter 2580: The Truth","paragraphs":["Even Zu An was dumbstruck, let alone the others. Huh? Wasn’t I the one who shot down the nine Golden Crows?","The Goddess of Wu Mountain stared at Xihe weirdly.","Could she have fallen in love with Zu An, so she’s subconsciously trying to find an excuse to absolve him of blame?","Emperor Jun was probably the one who instigated the simultaneous appearance of the ten suns to activate his vile formations, so it wouldn’t be a stretch to say that he’s played a part in the ten suns’ deaths.","Still, should I say that Xihe is blinded by love, or that Zu An is too charming? To think that she would overlook even her sons’ murderer...","Emperor Jun was infuriated. While glaring at Xihe, he pointed at Zu An and roared, “Xihe, are you out of your mind? Anyone with eyes can tell that he killed our sons! Are you so infatuated with him that you would go this far to defend him?”","You have successfully trolled Emperor Jun for +811... +811... +811...","Those words pricked Emperor Jun’s heart as well. Even though he was a philanderer, and the women around him often expressed dissatisfaction about it, he would console them by saying that he was just fulfilling his physical needs, and that his heart was still with them.","He hadn't realized it would hurt this much when he was on the receiving side.","Donghuang Taiyi interjected, “Indeed, sister-in-law. Your misunderstandings with my big brother can be resolved in private. It isn’t appropriate to thrash them out in front of outsiders.”","He couldn’t understand why Xihe was siding with that man. Did he thoroughly conquer her?","That thought made his complexion turn awful.","You have successfully trolled Donghuang Taiyi for +911... +911... +911...","Gonggong looked at Zu An with eyes of admiration, wondering how the latter pulled it off. Moments ago, he had still been viewing Zu An as a junior, but now, he was thinking that he should call him ‘senior’ instead.","Xihe glared at Emperor Jun with eyes brimming with hatred and tears. “I’m defending him? Isn’t it because you have long since killed my sons?”","“What?!” Everyone was stunned to hear that.","Most people thought Xihe had gone crazy, but some fell into contemplation.","Emperor Jun frowned. “You woman! How can you slander me with such nonsense to defend your lover?”","Xihe glared at him. “You thought you had fooled everyone, but your Ten Suns Apocalypse Formation requires the ten Golden Crows’ powerful souls as formation cores. To keep others from realizing what you have done, you severed fragments of your soul and possessed their bodies. You had them travel around to create a false impression that they were still alive.”","“Ten Suns Apocalypse Formation!” Gonggong was startled.","Zu An and the Goddess of Wu Mountain exchanged looks and saw the shock in each other’s eyes. This was aligned with the intel they had gathered thus far.","Emperor Jun’s face darkened. “I don’t know where you heard these rumors from, but they are utterly ridiculous! I am the Celestial Emperor; all living beings are my subjects. What reason do I have to do this?”","The Kaiming Six Shamans nodded. Despite being enemies, they couldn’t understand Emperor Jun’s motive for doing this.","“You’re seeking to eradicate the Shaman races so that the Fiend races will be the sole ruler of the world. You hope that this accomplishment can prop you up to Sainthood,” Xihe replied coldly, her words echoing loudly in the world.","Gonggong cursed in anger, “I’ve always thought this fellow was a dirtbag, but he’s worse than I thought!”","Emperor Jun’s cheeks twitched. He could already sense several unique divine senses paying attention to the situation here. He took a deep breath and replied, “What a load of nonsense! I am the Celestial Emperor, and I am a mere step away from Sainthood. I have no need to take such a risk to do something this depraved.","“Besides, the Shaman races are no weaker than our Fiend races. I would have to be out of my mind to oppose them single-handedly! Not to mention that I would lose my place in the Celestial Court too.”","His explanation had many powerhouses nodding in agreement. The logic behind Xihe’s accusations didn’t check out. Is she saying this because she fell in love with another man?","Zu An spoke up as well. “It goes without saying that you couldn’t deal with the Shaman races alone, so you had to incite conflict between the races to spark a war.”","Emperor Jun’s eyes widened. “I haven’t settled the score with you yet. How dare you make such slanderous remarks about me?”","He was about to make a move when he was interrupted by a water arrow from the side. It was Gonggong. “Let him speak his piece.”","Donghuang Taiyi’s eyebrows shot up. The drama had been so exciting that their fight stalled to a halt. That gave Gonggong the opportunity to interfere with the situation on that side.","Zu An took this opportunity to speak up. “You exploited Gu’s swelling ambitions and had him goad Er Fu into killing Yayu. The Celestial Court was bound to punish Er Fu after he committed such a grievous crime. All you had to do then was to stoke public opinion. If the Celestial Court sentenced Er Fu to death, Zhulong and the Shaman races would resent the incumbent Celestial Emperor. With that, the seeds of hatred would be planted.","“Given Zhulong’s standing, there was a good chance he could obtain an immortal medicine to revive Yayu. That would create a chance for Gu to obtain the immortal medicine. But as long as Gu killed Celestial Bao Jiang, whether out of his greed or your incitement, the Celestial Court would have to sentence him to death as an example to the others.","“No matter how things went, Ancestral Shaman Zhulong would lose at least two of his sons. That's not a grudge that could be overlooked that easily. Even though Zhulong chose to stay put, Gu’s mother, Nuba, challenged the Celestial Court’s authority. There were also several individuals stirring the Shaman races’ emotions to rile them up. I bet you planted those people on Zhong Mountain beforehand to control the narrative.”","Emperor Jun coldly harrumphed. “A load of nonsense!”","Zu An didn’t bother arguing with him and continued, “But you didn’t expect the incumbent Celestial Emperor to resolve this conflict by severing heaven from earth. The sacrifice of his most talented grandson appeased the Shaman races.","“Of course, you wouldn’t give up just like that. You intentionally leaked the news that you were responsible for her son’s death to Nuba, prompting her to go around cursing you out. It wasn’t convenient for you to confront her, so you had the Golden Crow Princes deal with her instead. Even if the Golden Crow Princes went overboard, the Celestial Court would show them leniency on the grounds that they were doing it out of filial piety. Some in the Celestial Court might be disgruntled, but they wouldn’t be able to say anything about it.","“But the Shaman races wouldn’t take it lying down. Renowned shamans like Kuafu and Xingtian confronted the Golden Crow Princes for an explanation, but the former was burned to death, whereas the latter had his head lopped off by you.” Zu An briefly paused as he wondered whether to mention that Emperor Jun had killed Yi too, but he held back since he had now become Yi.","“I just exacted vengeance for Kuafu by killing nine of the Golden Crows. That gave you the perfect excuse to step forward and kill me.”","“The Shaman races are hot-tempered. Given the conflicts between the races over the years, and the recent deaths of so many important shamans, the Shaman races were bound to come after you for vengeance. Gonggong is an example of that.”","Gonggong puffed up his chest. That was indeed something he would do.","Zu An sharply eyed Emperor Jun. “The Celestial Court wouldn’t know that you were behind this, so they wouldn’t sit still as the Shaman races sought to kill their next Celestial Emperor. An all-out war would ensue, and both sides would fight to the bitter end. When the fight heated up, you could bring out the Apocalypse Formation to massacre the Shaman races. Not only would the Celestial Court not blame you for it, they would even be thankful to you for your ample preparations. With that, you would have secured yourself a huge accomplishment. Am I right, future Celestial Emperor?”"]},{"number":2629,"title":"Chapter 2629: Chapter 2581: Show of Hands","paragraphs":["Zu An had previously harbored many doubts about the situation, but the clues swiftly connected when Xihe told him that Emperor Jun had already possessed the ten Golden Crows and stolen their souls to fuel the Apocalypse Formation.","Gonggong was horrified and enraged. “What a vicious man you are, Emperor Jun! I underestimated you!”","Emperor Jun’s face darkened. “Hah! How naive must you be to trust that brat’s far-fetched conjecture?”","“Am I to trust a deceitful scumbag like you over him?” Gonggong scoffed.","Emperor Jun was rendered speechless.","“What did you do to Xiaoxi?” Zu An asked aloud. He was feeling increasingly uneasy. Someone who could stoop to murdering his sons wouldn’t hold back against Xiaoxi.","“So it was for her.” Emperor Jun was at the peak of his anger. “Why don’t I send you to her side if you miss her so much?”","As he fully unleashed his aura as the next Celestial Emperor, two massive wings sprouted from Emperor Jun’s back. He jolted Xingtian backward with a powerful shockwave before morphing into a golden light that moved faster than the eye could follow.","“Careful!” Xihe anxiously shoved Zu An aside before transforming into a sun to confront Emperor Jun.","However, the golden light was so formidable that the sun was immediately split in two.","Horrified, Zu An hurriedly charged forward. The sun’s avatar faded, revealing Xihe’s plummeting figure.","Zu An swiftly caught her, only to see a deep laceration that exposed her bones across her chest. Her beautiful face had turned ghastly pale. He was relieved that Xihe was strong enough to withstand the attack, or else it would have split her in two.","Seeing how naturally Xihe snuggled into Zu An’s arms, Emperor Jun’s eyelids twitched. “Very well. You adulterous couple dare to flaunt your love in front of me! I’ll make you suffer a fate worse than death!”","You have successfully trolled Emperor Jun for +999... +999... +999...","He unfurled his wings. As he morphed into a golden light and charged at the duo, his feathers transformed into sharp weapons.","He was truly enraged. This was the third time the golden light had appeared on this battlefield. The first time, it had severed Xingtian’s shield and head. The second time, it had severely wounded Xihe. This time, he was planning to kill Zu An and Xihe together.","Gonggong tried to rush over to rescue Zu An, only to be blocked by Donghuang Taiyi. “Your opponent is me.”","Unable to bypass Donghuang Taiyi, Gonggong could only watch as everything unfolded. Deep down, he knew that Zu An and Xihe were no match for the enraged Emperor Jun, especially now that Xihe had been incapacitated.","A seven-colored light suddenly shone. The golden light that was going to slice Zu An and Xihe apart vanished.","Gonggong was speechless, while Donghuang Taiyi was shocked. They couldn’t even sense Emperor Jun’s aura anymore, as if he had been erased from the world.","The Kaiming Six Shamans were dumbfounded. Only the Goddess of Wu Mountain realized what had happened. He’s finally used that ability, but is it enough to trap a Celestial Emperor?","Xihe stared at the man holding her in his arms. She had hated him so much that she wanted nothing more than to tear him apart, but perhaps due to the time they had spent together and the effects of the other party’s Golden Phoenix ability, she realized that she had unknowingly fallen in love with him.","She'd had many chances to kill him, but still hesitated and eventually held herself back. Even so, at the same time, she couldn’t forgive him for killing her sons. This contradiction had tortured her.","Later, when she learned that the culprit behind her sons’ deaths wasn't him but Emperor Jun, she'd felt as if a weight had been lifted from her heart. She was relieved.","There were so many words she wanted to tell him, but it all condensed into a single sentence. “Be careful. He isn’t that easy to deal with.”","Zu An knew that too.","In the Seven-Colored Divine Halo’s world, Emperor Jun transformed into a thirty-thousand-meter-wide Golden Crow. His wings were so vast that they covered the sky. Countless artifacts floated in his vicinity, emanating ancient auras. Golden lights pulsated from Emperor Jun’s body, causing the Seven-Colored Divine Halo’s world to shake intensely as if it would shatter at any moment. A piercing, majestic bird call echoed.","Emperor Jun finally broke free from the Seven-Colored Divine Halo’s world and circled the sky as he gazed down on Zu An in astonishment. A mere mortal actually can imprison me! Wouldn’t I have been in danger if he were any stronger?","His eyes turned cold. I can’t let someone like that roam free even if I have no grudge against him. Otherwise, there is a chance that he might become a threat to me.","He flapped his wings, and the world trembled.","Zu An embraced Xihe tightly and activated his position swap skill. But to his horror, he appeared right in front of Emperor Jun instead. He must have changed the world laws here to make me teleport in front of him!","“An ant like you can’t begin to comprehend what beings like us are capable of.”","Emperor Jun didn’t even make a move—he simply looked at Zu An—and Zu An’s body began disintegrating as if eroding to the wind. No matter how he channeled his cultivation techniques, he could only slow the rate of disintegration.","“It’s futile. He has the power to modify world laws. I never thought I’d end up dying with you,” Xihe said with a conflicted expression. Even she had no idea if she was sad or heartbroken.","But Zu An refused to submit to fate. His only option was to use the power of Keyboard Come, but if he used it in his current state, he would likely die. Even so, he was determined to kill Emperor Jun even if it spelled his death!","He was about to speak when ancient runes suddenly enveloped him. Thesey shone with peculiar lights that protected him and Xihe.","“The Shaman races’ ancient runes!” Zu An had seen similar characters when he used the Shaman races’ secret art.","His body’s disintegration halted, and he even began to recover. He took this opportunity to channel the Primordial Origin Sutra to heal his own and Xihe’s wounds. The ki around him pulsated, and before he knew, they were already some distance away from Emperor Jun.","Emperor Jun’s massive avatar didn’t pursue them. Instead, he looked warily in their direction.","Sensing something, Zu An turned around to take a look. What he saw caused him to freeze up. Behind him was a snake of inestimable size. Even the largest dragon he had seen was nothing but a lizard compared to it. The snake had brilliant eyes—one was reminiscent of the sun while the other resembled the cold moonlight.","Xihe immediately recognized the snake. “Ancestral Shaman Zhulong!”","Zhulong’s standing and strength was top-notch even among the Ancestral Shamans. Past generations of Celestial Emperors had treated him with utmost respect. It had been ten thousand years since he last made an appearance, which led to rumors that he had passed away and returned to the dao.","Zu An was shocked. He had encountered many huge things that triggered his fear, but those paled in comparison to the humongous entity right before him. The pressure emanated by Zhulong was overwhelming. His only source of relief was that Zhulong wasn’t an enemy. In fact, it was thanks to Zhulong’s intervention that he and Xihe had survived Emperor Jun’s attack.","Gonggong burst into laughter. “You’re finally here!”","Zhulong ignored him. He turned his humongous head toward Emperor Jun and sneered, “Emperor Jun, you must think that I’m dead to pull so many stunts.”","Emperor Jun quickly reined in his earlier arrogance and said, “Zhulong, you mustn’t listen to that brat’s nonsense. I have nothing to do with what happened to Nuba and your sons.”","“Do you think I’d believe your words?” Zhulong glared at Emperor Jun with wrathful eyes.","He had been in seclusion for a long time, but this time, he awoke to find his wife and two sons dead. On top of that, his only remaining son had committed a grievous mistake and would soon be punished under the celestial laws. How could he not be angry?","Emperor Jun’s expression darkened. “What do you want?”","“A blood debt must be repaid with blood!” A humongous snake body was vaguely visible amid the clouds, encircling the surroundings.","Emperor Jun suddenly let out a frenzied laugh. “Hah! Do you think I fear you people?”","With a wave of his hand, a massive cauldron appeared on the ground. An ominous wind blew, and the clear sky suddenly darkened."]},{"number":2630,"title":"Chapter 2630: Chapter 2582: Hellscape","paragraphs":["A blood-colored light enveloped the sky. Some of it reflected off the clouds and cast a sinister glow on the crowd beneath. Jarring noises resembling crunching bone echoed from the ground. Nearby mountains began to collapse.","Alarmed, Zu An quickly flitted to the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s side and brought her to safety.","Shortly after they departed, the mountain they had previously been standing on collapsed. What came surging out of it wasn't searing lava, but an army of deceased spirits that emanated dim green light. Their faces were warped with resentment, as if they would pull any living beings they could get their hands on down to hell with them, so that they would suffer the same pain.","Zu An was startled. These deceased spirits resembled the vengeful spirits he had seen in the Oblivion River. He hadn’t expected to see something similar here. He anxiously warned the people present, “Don’t let those vengeful spirits touch you. They can corrode your soul.”","Those present here understood the severity of the situation. They either avoided the vengeful spirits or exorcised them.","However, the other living beings further away weren’t as lucky. Many of them found themselves grabbed by the vengeful spirits. They tried to fight back, but they quickly lost their strength and were dragged into the vengeful spirit horde. They began turning into vengeful spirits themselves before joining the others in hunting down more victims.","Noticing Zu An’s worry, the Goddess of Wu Mountain consoled him. “Don’t worry, the Crimson Emperor personally refined Wu Mountain. Chang’e will be safe there.”","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. No wonder Wu Mountain felt so mystical—it was constructed by the Crimson Emperor.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain glanced at Xihe, only to find herself meeting the latter’s eyes. Both of them felt awkward.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was only friends with Zu An, yet here she was in his arms. Xihe and Zu An had an intimate relationship, but she was Emperor Jun’s wife.","While the two women were feeling awkward, a loud buzzing sound echoed. Gigantic pillars slowly rose from the ground and towered over everyone else. Every pillar was made out of squirming, blood-red flesh, and it looked as if some kind of enigmatic, ancient being was about to come back to life.","Zu An did a quick count—there were 108 pillars in total. Their positions also aligned with the Great Constellation Formation.","Zhulong roared in shock and anger, “Emperor Jun, you massacred so many living beings to forge such vile pillars of flesh and blood!”","Emperor Jun remained calm. “It’s their fate. I’m merely fulfilling their destiny.”","“How can you, the Celestial Emperor, commit such a vile deed and proclaim it as fate? How shameless can you get?!” Gonggong berated him while clashing with Donghuang Taiyi. “Taiyi, have you lost your mind as well to side with him?”","Donghuang Taiyi didn’t answer. Instead, his attacks only became fiercer.","Millions of flesh tendrils that resembled blood serpents suddenly extended from the pillars. They were monsters manifested from grudges. The tendrils grabbed every living being in sight and furiously devoured them. As far as Zu An’s divine sense could reach, the world had been plunged into a hellscape.","Brilliant lights shone from Zhulong’s eyes. Wherever the lights reached, the flesh tendrils were reduced to ashes.","Gonggong unleashed water dragons to rip apart the flesh tendrils. The others also began their counterattack. However, there were too many tendrils, and ten more sprouted out in the time it took them to destroy one. There was no way to destroy all the tendrils.","Just then, many small cracks appeared across the ground. Shrill laughter that induced goosebumps echoed. Dense congregations of specters emerged from the cracks and began ripping off the flesh of the living with their sharp teeth.","The Kaiming Six Shamans’ Wu Yang was so severely injured in his battle with Emperor Jun that he failed to dodge the specters’ onslaught. In the blink of an eye, he was sucked dry until only his skin was left. The other five shamans were in agony, but they were unable to save him.","With even Wu Yang falling prey to these specters, there was no way mere mortals would stand a chance against them. It didn’t take long for them to be sucked dry into thin pieces of skin. These skins fluttered into the air and morphed into specters as well. They screamed “Just like me, just like me” as they searched for new victims.","At the same time, fireballs fell from the sky. Upon closer examination, these fireballs were the skulls of those who had died to the ten suns.","The water in the distant rivers defied gravity and flowed into the sky. The beings residing in therivers were quickly reduced to bones.","Massacres were happening no matter where one looked.","The blood clouds in the sky began revolving to form ten vortices. These vortices slowly transformed into a sun each, recreating the phenomenon of the ten suns. However, these suns actually resembled eyes.","The screams and wails of countless beings filled the world.","“We need to destroy those eyes! Otherwise, all living beings will die once the Ten Suns Apocalypse Formation is completed!” Xihe exclaimed.","Zhulong and Gonggong had already gotten to action, charging straight at the eyes in the sky. However, a massive bell blocked their attacks.","Zhulong roared in anger, “Taiyi, are you still siding with Emperor Jun despite the terrible sins he has committed?”","Donghuang Taiyi smiled. “My big brother’s methods might be extreme, but since he’s doing it for our Fiend races, it’s understandable.” He was blatantly siding with Emperor Jun.","Gonggong cursed out of anger, but Zhulong understood the underlying meaning behind those words. “You’re also seeking to destroy our Shaman races.”","“The world may be big, but there’s only enough room for our Fiend races,” As he gazed down on the living beings below, Donghuang Taiyi floated in midair.","Zhulong burst into laughter. “Do you think that you two can destroy our Shaman races?”","Right after those words were spoken, translucent figures began appearing out of thin air. Wherever those figures appeared, the surrounding vengeful spirits wailed in agony before disintegrating into dust.","“What powerful auras!” Zu An was shocked.","“They are Ancestral Shamans,” Xihe explained. “They have only projected their avatars here, but their strength is still not to be underestimated.”","“With this, Emperor Jun and Taiyi should be dead meat, right?” Zu An’s heart was put at ease. This is the power of a strong backing!","Emperor Jun and Taiyi were powerful, but their strength was only comparable to a single Ancestral Shaman each. Now that the other Ancestral Shamans were here, it was time for the tides to be turned on them.","Zu An and Xihe were interacting naturally when it suddenly struck them that they were no longer a couple. The atmosphere between them turned awkward.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain sensed the change in the atmosphere and interjected to alleviate the awkwardness, “That’s not necessarily the case. Emperor Jun looks confident.”","That was indeed the case, as Emperor Jun didn’t look surprised in the slightest. He opened his arms wide and said, “Do you think we’re the only ones who wish to eradicate the Shamans? This is the collective wish of most fiends in the Celestial Court!”","The celestial gate opened, and countless celestial soldiers appeared behind him."]},{"number":2631,"title":"Chapter 2631: Chapter 2583: The Path to Heaven","paragraphs":["Looking at the sky full of celestial guards and feeling the pressure they exerted, Zu An finally understood how Sun Wukong in the myth must have felt when he stood against the Celestial Court.","Gonggong bellowed in fury, “Do you think you’re the only one with troops?”","He took out a seashell-shaped artifact and blew a melancholic note. Countless shaman warriors charged in from all directions, and there was no lack of renowned shamans among them. In terms of aura, they didn’t pale against the celestial guards.","Zhulong, on the other hand, wasn’t as reckless as Gonggong. He looked at the celestials in the sky and sneered, “Does Zhuanxu know about this?”","Emperor Jun calmly replied, “There wouldn’t be so many of us if he didn't know about it.”","The Shamans were infuriated. Some of them even cursed loudly. How could they not be angry when the Celestial Court’s Fiend races had been scheming to eradicate them for such a long time? Even the Ancestral Shamans were enraged.","It was unknown who made the first move, but a full-blown battle soon broke out. Terrifying lights filled the battlefield. Powerful shamans and celestials began dying right from the get-go.","Zu An wanted to join the battle, but Xihe stopped him. “Let’s leave this place first.”","Zu An frowned. “I have to settle the score with Emperor Jun and force him to divulge Xiaoxi’s whereabouts.”","“I have a rough idea of where she is,” Xihe replied.","“You do?” Zu An was surprised.","“Let’s leave this place first.” Xihe clutched her chest as she spoke. Her face was pale from the severe injuries she had sustained. “If we continue dawdling here, we won’t be able to get away.”","Zu An knew she was right. There were many experts stronger than him here. While he could temporarily stand his ground with his Sun Slaying Bow and his arsenal of skills, it was only a matter of time before he was worn down and killed. To make things worse, both Xihe and the Goddess of Wu Mountain were severely injured. It was impractical of him to take care of them while dealing with the chaotic battlefield.","On top of that, Zu An sensed that the surrounding ki was flowing peculiarly—a formation was being constructed. Not daring to hesitate anymore, he held the Goddess of Wu Mountain and Xihe in each of his hands, morphed into a rainbow, and fled the battlefield.","Emperor Jun noticed his movement and attempted to claw at the rainbow. His hatred for Zu An had reached a breaking point; there was no way he would let the latter escape under his watch.","However, a humongous head suddenly appeared in front of him. It was Zhulong, who said, “Emperor Jun, it’s time to settle our score.”","Zhulong was grateful to Zu An for uncovering the truth behind his wife and sons’ deaths, so he'd decided to step in and ensure the latter’s safe departure.","Wary of Zhulong’s strength, Emperor Jun could only watch as Zu An left.","Zu An traveled for a long time before finally releasing his Rainbow Morph. Even when he was so far from the battlefield, he could still sense terrifying shockwaves rippling through the air. The fight between the Shamans and the Fiend was getting heated up.","“This is weird. If Zhuanxu supports the crusade against the Shamans, why would he sacrifice his cherished grandson to sever heaven from earth...” the Goddess of Wu Mountain murmured in confusion.","If Zhuanxu had known that a war would break out nevertheless, he wouldn’t have sacrificed his grandson to appease the Shamans in the first place.","“Zhuanxu and Emperor Jun have never been on good terms. There’s no way Zhuanxu would support him,” Xihe said. “I’m guessing that Zhuanxu might be incarcerated somewhere.”","Zu An was taken aback. “He’s the Celestial Emperor! Who could incarcerate him?”","“You lack understanding of the Celestial Court. Many in the Celestial Court view themselves as superior beings and are reluctant to share the world with the Shaman races. It also doesn’t help that the Shamans are bad-tempered, which gave rise to many conflicts between both sides over the years. The situation has reached a blowing point,” Xihe explained. “You saw the celestial guards Emperor Jun summoned. I don’t think they are reluctant participants in this war. Chances are that they have been wanting to deal with the Shaman races for a long time now.”","“Aren't the Shaman races in danger then?” Zu An was worried. The world was big, but if the Shaman races fell in defeat here, it was only a matter of time before Emperor Jun found him.","“Not necessarily. The Ten Ancestral Shamans are born from Pangu’s blood essence. They are incredibly powerful entities, each having unique abilities. The Shamans are also born warriors. It’s too early to tell who will emerge victorious,” Xihe consoled him. “These are beyond our influence. The outcome will not change with or without us.”","Zu An fell silent. He had only gotten a glimpse of the battlefield between the Fiends and the Shamans, but he had already witnessed the deaths of many experts whose strength didn’t pale to his. It was indeed beyond him to influence the outcome of the battle.","“Where do you think Xiaoxi is?” he asked.","“The Celestial Court,\" Xihe answered.","Zu An was taken aback.","“Jun’s plan should have been flawless, but your appearance...” Xihe paused briefly before continuing, “Your appearance messed up his plan. The battle between the Shamans and the Fiends broke out prematurely. He didn’t use the Myriad Souls Banner earlier, likely because it hasn’t been fully refined yet.","“The earth is under the Shaman races’ jurisdiction. It’s unlikely he would risk placing something as important as the Myriad Souls Banner here. It’s more likely for him to have placed it in the Celestial Court, especially since he has the support of most celestials. There is no place safer than that.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain harrumphed. “How many people have died for those bastards’ greed? How dare they call themselves celestials?” The realization that most celestials were aware of the events that were transpiring on earth made her angry despite her usual coldness.","“Survival of the fittest. If they win this battle, history will be theirs to write.” Xihe remarked impassively. Being in a lofty position, she had already seen through all these things. “Let’s quickly make our way to the Celestial Court.”","“Heaven has been severed from earth. How can we get to the Celestial Court?” Zu An was worried.","“There’s another road to heaven on Kunlun Mountain.” Xihe looked westward.","Zu An nodded. He grabbed the two women and rainbow morphed toward Kunlun Mountain. Halfway into the journey, he belatedly remembered that the Goddess of Wu Mountain was severely injured and felt apologetic for dragging her along.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled at him. “Don’t worry. I have recovered after taking your pills. I am, after all, the Crimson Emperor’s daughter. I won’t die that easily.” For some reason, she just wanted to spend more time with him.","It was too late for Zu An to escort her back to Wu Mountain, so it would be safer to bring her along with him. Silence loomed among the three of them for the remaining part of the journey.","“I’m sorry,” Zu An suddenly said. He had shot down nine of the Golden Crows despite not knowing that they were already possessed by Emperor Jun.","Xihe understood what he was getting at. There was a moment of silence before she suddenly remarked, “I had planned to kill you.”","“But you didn’t.”","“I didn’t know why either... Someone I thought was my enemy turned out to not be an enemy, and the true enemy turned out to be the person I was the closest to.” Xihe thought about how history had remained the same despite her efforts, but she'd ended up uncovering such a truth instead. She could only be awed by how powerful the forces dictating fate were.","Zu An tightly grabbed her hand and said, “I’ll exact vengeance for you!” There was no chance of reconciliation between him and Emperor Jun anymore.","Xihe wanted to withdraw her hand, but he was so strong that after several tries, she gave up and let him be. There was no lust in her, only bottomless sorrow.","Following the two women’s guidance, Zu An finally arrived at Kunlun’s peak and stopped before a massive tree. This tree had no branches; it rose straight toward the sky. Its trunk emanated a purple light as if it were shrouded in a veil. At its top were nine sprouts with green leaves and black flowers.","“Is this Jianmu, the sacred tree connecting heaven and earth?” Zu An murmured. This tree was huge, but it wasn’t so big as to cover the sky.","Xihe nodded. She walked up to the tree and placed her hand on it.","A golden light shrouded them. Zu An felt himself being transported inside Jianmu, and he swiftly moved upward, as if riding on an elevator.","Suddenly, their surroundings shook intensely. It felt as if the tree was going to collapse."]},{"number":2632,"title":"Chapter 2632: Chapter 2584: Meeting Xiaoxi Once More","paragraphs":["“What’s going on?” Zu An looked downward and saw giants swinging their axes against the sacred tree. They appeared to be shaman warriors, and they were likely intending to cut down the sacred tree to stop the Celestial Court from dispatching further reinforcements.","“Don’t worry. Jianmu was born alongside heaven and earth; it can’t be cut down that easily. You should be worried about them instead,” Xihe sneered.","Profound ancient runes lit up around the sacred tree. These weren’t divine runes, but something superior. These characters were born alongside heaven and earth, and they harnessed the dao of the world. The giants didn’t even have any time to scream before they were reduced to ashes.","Zu An was taken aback. Those runes are incredible. What a pity I can’t remember and copy them. It must be because my cultivation isn’t high enough.","A light suddenly appeared in front of Zu An. Before they knew it, they had already emerged from the other end of the sacred tree. The first thing he noticed was that they were standing on top of clouds. He was initially worried about falling through the clouds, but he soon realized that it was no different from walking on the ground, except for it being softer. It must be a huge formation to sustain this effect throughout the Celestial Court. I wouldn’t be able to do thiswith my current abilities.","He raised his head and saw a towering celestial gate with curved eaves and interlocking wooden brackets. It looked narrow, but he knew that was just a visual effect. Even the largest being in this world could pass through it easily. Behind the celestial gate was a bunch of palaces built amid foggy mountains. Immortal birds flew freely in the clouds, making the place look ethereal.","“Is this the Celestial Court?”","This was Zu An’s first time visiting the legendary Celestial Court, but he wasn't in the mood to enjoy the scenery. He'd thought that given the huge number of celestial guards that descended earlier to clash with the Shaman races, there wouldn’t be many celestials left in the Celestial Court. And yet, there was still a platoon of celestial guards guarding the celestial gate.","Their leader was a giant built like a metal tower. He held a massive axe while vigilantly eyeing the surroundings. He would have noticed Zu An and the others if they hadn’t concealed themselves beforehand.","“That is General Zhao Lingguan of the South Celestial Gate. He’s known as the number one slaughterer of the South Celestial Gate. I didn’t expect him to not participate in the battle and instead remain here. This complicates things,” Xihe said worriedly.","“Is he powerful?” Zu An asked.","“Very. I’m not sure I could defeat him even if I weren’t injured,” Xihe replied grimly. “But if we wish to enter the Celestial Court, there is no way to circumvent this gate.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain suggested, “I’ll distract him so you can slip through in the meantime. I am the Crimson Emperor’s daughter, after all. He won’t make things difficult for me even if I’m captured.” Now that she couldn’t fight anymore, this was all she could do for Zu An.","Zu An chuckled. “There’s no need for that. Is Zhao Lingguan Emperor Jun’s subordinate?”","“Yes, he is Jun’s close aide. Jun wouldn’t have placed him here otherwise.” Xihe nodded.","“That makes things easy,” Zu An said. Zhuanxu is a failure of a Celestial Emperor. How could he let his successor usurp his power to such an extent when he hasn’t even stepped down yet?","Zu An suddenly transformed into Emperor Jun. Xihe and the Goddess of Wu Mountain instinctively darted aside, as if scalded by hot water.","“Don’t worry, it’s me,” Zu An said in his original voice.","The two goddesses remained in disbelief. Zu An could only tell them about the Lord of Myriad Transformations, and the two of them finally breathed a sigh of relief.","“This ability of yours can’t be used for anything good,” Xihe remarked.","Before Zu An could explain anything, Zhao Lingguan sensed their presence and shouted, “Who’s there?” The metal tower-like figure instantly appeared before them.","Zu An naturally held Xihe in his arms. Xihe’s face reddened, but she didn’t struggle because she knew that he was doing this to convince Zhao Lingguan of his disguise.","Zhao Lingguan was taken aback to see Zu An. “Emperor Jun, what are you doing here?”","“Xihe is injured. I’m sending her back so that she can be healed,” Zu An calmly replied.","Zhao Lingguan was perplexed, knowing that Emperor Jun and Xihe had been estranged for many years now. Have they patched things up?","Zu An wasn’t about to give him time to think. “How are things on Zhuanxu’s side?”","That drew Zhao Lingguan’s attention elsewhere. “Rest assured, Emperor Jun. Zhuanxu has been suppressed by the Great Constellation Formation. He won’t be able to do anything.”","Zu An was shocked, but he didn’t let it show. “Good. Continue guarding this place well; don’t allow anyone to enter or leave the Celestial Court. The future of our Fiend races depends on this.”","Zhao Lingguan was about to ask Emperor Jun if his departure from the battlefield would affect their plans when he heard those words. He solemnly replied, “Rest assured, Emperor Jun. No one will cross the South Celestial Gate as long as I’m here!”","Zu An nodded in approval.","Zhao Lingguan could hardly suppress his grin. This contribution should at least raise my position by three ranks, right?","Just like that, Zu An strutted into the Celestial Court with Xihe and the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","Xihe and the Goddess of Wu Mountain glanced at Zhao Lingguan, who was waving goodbye with a smile. They couldn’t believe that a hurdle they had thought to be impossible would be overcome so easily.","This man is unbelievable.","Zu An looked at a brilliant congregation of stars and planets in the distance. That must be where Zhuanxu is imprisoned.","The most effective way to change the tide of the battlefield would be to rescue Zhuanxu, but Zu An didn’t hesitate to make his way to Emperor Jun’s residence. To him, the outcome of the war between the Shamans and the Fiends was nowhere as important as saving Xiaoxi.","Under Xihe’s guidance, the three of them soon arrived at Emperor Jun’s residence. The place was protected by countless defensive formations, but Xihe breached them easily.","As soon as they entered his main hall, they felt like they had been transported into another world. The world outside looked ethereal, and a faint fragrance lingered in the air. However, the world inside the main hall was eerie and sinister.","A pitch-black Myriad Souls Banner floated in the middle of the hall. Tortured screams and miserable cries emanated from the banner. Just listening to those voices could shake one’s psyche. Countless warped specters flew forth from the banner, but no matter how far they flew, they were unable to break free of the Myriad Souls Banner’s restraint.","A fragile woman lay atop an altar in the middle of the hall. She was unconscious, and her skin was so pale that it looked transparent. It felt as if she could vanish at any moment.","“Xiaoxi!” Zu An was horrified. Emperor Jun was indeed using her to forge the Myriad Souls Banner!","Xiaoxi’s eyelids fluttered, but she didn’t regain consciousness. A tear flowed down the corner of her eye. As soon as the tear fell on the ground, it transformed into a black aura and was absorbed by the Myriad Souls Banner."]},{"number":2633,"title":"Chapter 2633: Chapter 2585: Five Directions Demon Suppression Formation","paragraphs":["The Goddess of Wu Mountain exclaimed, “Her soul is being siphoned away! She might only be left with the final sliver of her soul, which is why she looks nearly transparent.” As the Crimson Emperor’s daughter, she was highly knowledgeable.","Zu An panicked. “Is there a way to save her?”","“We have to destroy the Myriad Souls Banner and find a way to bring her soul back to her body...”","Before the Goddess of Wu Mountain could finish speaking, Zu An charged forward with his Tai’e Sword and unleashed a radiant burst of sword ki.","But the black aura surrounding the Myriad Souls Banner was almost tangible. As it approached the Myriad Souls Banner, the sword ki swiftly lost its radiance. In the end, it weakly struck the banner before vanishing into thin air.","Zu An was stunned. The black aura surrounding the Myriad Souls Banner was so corrosive that it could even affect his sword ki!","Unwilling to give up, he drew the Sun Slaying Bow and shot at the Myriad Souls Banner. A white light reminiscent of a comet violently slammed into the banner.","This attack wielded the power to bring down a sun, yet it merely shook the banner.","Zu An was dumbstruck.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain explained, “Your arrow absorbs surrounding ki to amplify its destructive prowess, but all the natural ki in here has been eroded by the Myriad Souls Banner’s demonic ki. That’s why your arrow was unable to destroy it.”","Xihe surveyed the hall’s layout. “There’s a convoluted formation in this hall that resonates with the Myriad Souls Banner. In essence, you're not just attacking the banner, but the entire palace along with it. Not even the Celestial Emperor can destroy the banner like that.”","This palace had been around for a long time. It had been reinforced by countless celestials, such that one could call it a top-notch defensive artifact. Zu An’s attack was bound to fall short against it.","Zu An frowned. He tried stowing away the Myriad Souls Baner with his Seven-Colored Divine Halo, but it refused to budge. The Myriad Souls Banner was one with the palace, and Zu An didn’t have the means to stow away the entire palace.","Xihe looked at the woman on the altar and said, “If we can’t destroy the Myriad Souls Banner, we’ll have to kill her. If he forges the Myriad Souls Banner, no one will be able to stop Jun. The whole world will be plunged into destruction.”","“Absolutely not!” Zu An knew this was the rational decision to make, but how could he abandon Xiaoxi?","Xihe looked at him before falling silent.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain opened her mouth, but she decided against saying anything.","Zu An surveyed the surroundings while raking up everything he knew about formations in his head. A rough idea popped in his mind. “Emperor Jun is formidable to have linked the Myriad Souls Banner with his palace, but this method comes with a downside. The Myriad Souls Banner is a malevolent yin artifact, whereas this palace represents light. Those are two opposing forces.","“Emperor Jun must have found a way to temporarily suppress the conflict. All we have to do is to undo that, and the palace will help us to suppress the Myriad Souls Banner.”","Xihe and the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s eyes lit up. They thought that it was a feasible plan. “How should we go about it?”","“I know a Five Directions Demon Suppression Formation that can achieve that effect. However, it requires cleansing ki to be simultaneously channeled from five directions, but even with my instantaneous movement, I can only cover three directions.” Zu An racked his brain for a solution.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain said, “Have you forgotten that Xihe and I are here too? Even though I’m weak against fire, I’m still the Crimson Emperor’s descendant. I can channel the fire element in my bloodline to cleanse the surrounding demonic ki. Xihe, as the Sun Goddess, is the nemesis of all malevolent forces. She should have no trouble taking a direction too.”","Xihe nodded. “Indeed, but are you sure you’re up to the task? You were severely injured earlier.”","“Don’t worry, I am a goddess too,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain replied with a confident smile.","Knowing Xiaoxi didn’t have much time to spare, Zu An quickly explained the crux of the formation to the two women. Then, he took out a formation compass from his Brilliant Glass Bead and planted formation flags all around the hall. The Goddess of Wu Mountain and Xihe made their way to the southeast and southwest directions as planned.","Xihe took her position and sat down. Her body radiated a searing light reminiscent of the sun. In the face of her cleansing ki, the surrounding black aura swiftly disintegrated.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain nicked her palm with her fingernail before forming a hand seal to invoke the Crimson Emperor’s bloodline. Flames suddenly blazed around her. Shockingly, it was on par with Xihe’s power.","Zu An was finally able to put his heart at ease. Without any hesitation, he began flitting between three directions, channeling the Primordial Origin Sutra in the north direction, the Phoenix Flame in the northwest, and the White Lotus Flame in the northeast. He alternated among the three directions so fast that outsiders would have thought that there were three Zu Ans.","Needless to say, this was a highly exhausting feat, and he swiftly felt his limit approaching despite his cultivation and resilient body. However, he gritted his teeth and held on for Xiaoxi’s sake.","The five streams of cleansing ki suffused the room like five stars lighting up the dark sky. As the formation flags lit up one after another, the Five Directions Demon Suppression Formation eventually fully activated.","The black aura in the hall swiftly thinned. Sensing danger, the Myriad Souls Banner unleashed a thick black aura that swiftly enveloped the five sources of brilliance.","“This is bad!”","The trio found themselves plunged into darkness. The lights they released gradually dimmed like candle flames before a wind, on the verge of being extinguished.","Zu An began to feel flustered. He continued to move between the three locations based on his memory while searching for a solution out of this quandary.","He could still hold on because his cultivation skill had the power to purge evil beings, and as the Netherworld’s master, demonic aura born from souls could hardly hurt him. However, Xihe and the Goddess of Wu Mountain were already injured. It would be terrible if they were to be inflicted with the demonic aura.","All of a sudden, his vision blurred. The demonic aura around him suddenly morphed into the universe, and several eyes slowly opened. Each of these eyes was on the scale of a planet, and they had lights and runes shimmering around them.","Zu An could hardly describe the appearance of the eyes with words, but there was a feeling that was particularly strong in him. He felt a sense of divinity. It was higher than the deities of the Celestial Court, as if it represented the celestial beings at the very core of the universe.","Coming into contact with these eyes felt bizarre and conflicting. It felt as if he was going to fall into an eye, be killed by another eye, and fuse into yet another eye.","...","Meanwhile, unlike the bizarre situation Zu An had found himself in, the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s face had gone completely red. She found herself placed in the position of a bride in a marriage ceremony, and the groom was none other than Zu An!"]},{"number":2634,"title":"Chapter 2634: Chapter 2586: Dream Butterfly","paragraphs":["The Goddess of Wu Mountain fell into a daze. Hm, what was I doing earlier?","Something felt amiss, but her mind refused to process what was going on. It was as if the logical part of her brain had shut down, rendering her incapable of recognizing the bizarre situation she was in.","Her attention was quickly drawn to the scene before her. She was in a huge room, seemingly a palace. It looked simplistic and humble, a far stretch from the glorious celestial palaces and her cavern on Wu Mountain. She vaguely heard the maids outside addressing someone as king.","Judging from the surrounding ki, this seems to be a human country’s palace?","She thought that it was a decent palace by human standards, especially since her impression of humanity was still one of primitive tribes.","She was sitting on a huge bed. It was so soft that it made her heartbeat hasten. The bed was covered in celebratory red drapes, and the word ‘囍 (Bliss in Marriage)’ was plastered everywhere. All this left her wondering: When did I get married?","If her groom wasn’t Zu An, she would have immediately grown vigilant, but somehow, everything seemed to make sense when she looked at his familiar face and faint smile. I actually married him! And it looks like we’re on the consummation stage of our marriage.","“How beautiful.” Under the illumination of the flickering candlelight, Zu An examined her up close. Wonderment was reflected in his eyes.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain shyly averted her gaze, not daring to meet his eyes. Despite the lack of a mirror in the room, she knew that her face had to be bright red. Even though she could sense the admiration in his eyes all along, it was her first time being directly complimented by him. He has a way with words... Is he not worried about angering the other ladies around him?","She suddenly fell into another daze. What are the names of the ladies around him? Why can’t I remember them? She even became uncertain whether there were other ladies around him or not.","In her daze, she felt hot, soft lips pressing against her cheeks. Zu An had kissed her. What’s he doing? Why is he suddenly so proactive?","Shocked, the demure Goddess of Wu Mountain instinctively tried to push him away. However, his hands held her body in place like metal bars.","“You...” She was about to say something when Zu An’s face suddenly became magnified in front of her, and before she knew it, her lips were sealed.","Her eyes widened as her mind completely went blank. He kissed me? Has he always been this wild...","What further flustered her was that she should have gotten angry, but she felt no anger at all.","She had heard fairies chatting about love before, but the concept of love had always eluded her. It was only at this moment that she realized that their descriptions were apt—she could hear her heart beating loudly.","Zu An’s movements were so skillful that she swooned right away and instinctively closed her eyes. Is my response too promiscuous? Should I push him away lest he think I am a casual woman? But he’s so good at it...","Sensing Zu An going further and further, the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s eyes suddenly shot open. She finally pushed him away and said, “No, we can’t do this anymore.”","Zu An was perplexed. “Why are you so shy when we’re already an old couple? Ah, I get it now. How could I be so dense? What a frisky one you are.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was stunned.","Come again, who’s frisky? And what do you mean by old couple?","While she was confused, Zu An wrapped his arm around her waist once more and pushed her down. This familiar yet foreign sensation prompted the Goddess of Wu Mountain to instinctively embrace him.","“AH!”","“It’s getting more and more realistic. Manman, it’s a waste you didn’t pursue an acting career.”","...","Tears brimmed in the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s eyes as she lay in a daze. Why was I so proactive earlier? How could I have given my body to him just like that? But our movements were so smooth that it really felt like we were an old couple.","...","Many doubts surfaced in her mind, but it was quickly interrupted by another dominant thought. I didn’t know this could feel so... No no no, I shouldn’t think about it now!","...","Before her mind shut down, she suddenly became cognizant of a crucial detail. Wait, why did he call me Manman?","She looked at the copper mirror by the side. It was indeed her, but her reddened face and moist eyes looked feminine and seductive. It was unlike her usual cold demeanor.","She belatedly remembered how Zu An had excitedly called her Manman on their first meeting and embraced her. He has a lover who looks exactly like me. This must be his marriage night with that Miss Manman, and they are the king and queen of some human country.","She shyly pushed Zu An away. “I’m not your Manman!”","Looking at Zu An’s shocked eyes, the scenery before her shattered to reveal a pitch-black fog suffused with eerie demonic ki. She finally remembered what she'd been doing earlier. The many souls inside the Myriad Souls Banner must have shaken my mind and stirred up hidden desires that even I was unaware about.","But why did I see such an embarrassing illusion?","Thinking back to the moment their bodies and souls became one, the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s face turned scarlet. It had felt so realistic that it made her wonder if it was truly just an illusion.","Just then, Zu An suddenly reappeared beside her. She shouted in a mix of frustration and embarrassment, “I won’t let you bully me anymore!”","She warned herself that it was only an illusion, and she was even ready to shatter this embarrassing illusion once more.","Zu An awkwardly dodged her attack as he asked, “What’s wrong, goddess?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was startled. Ah, it’s the real Zu An. Her face reddened. “It’s nothing. I was in an illusion earlier, but I have woken up now.”","Zu An was perplexed. What does she mean by bullying?","“Did you and Miss Manman reside in a palace, where you're the king and she’s the queen?” Something prompted the Goddess of Wu Mountain to ask this question which, even she found hilarious. How could he know what happened in my illusion?","Zu An was taken aback. “How did you know?”","He and Manman had spent decades as a couple in Yinxu. The time they'd spent together was so beautiful that he nearly couldn’t extricate himself from it.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s face reddened. Hold on, was that not my hallucination?","But Zu An wasn’t in any state of mind to probe deeper. He flashed away after confirming her safety, saying, “Take care! I’ll check on Xihe.”"]},{"number":2635,"title":"Chapter 2635: Chapter 2587: Revealing Himself","paragraphs":["The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s face turned hot. Even now, she still remembered Zu An’s scent and burning passion. Based on his earlier words, what I just experienced might be what he and Miss Manman went through. But why would I have such an illusion when I am completely unaware of it?","She suddenly remembered Zu An mentioning that she looked identical to Miss Manman, and she had seen her reflection in the illusion too—they were identical. They only diverged in their disposition and expressions. With her vast knowledge, she suddenly wondered: Could Miss Manman be my reincarnation?","When this thought emerged, her heart suddenly raced. Hold on, this is unbelievable. Could I still be in an illusion? Given that I was plunged into an illusion, the same should have happened to Zu An too. Is he able to escape that quickly?","She looked in the direction where Zu An disappeared with uncertain eyes.","Zu An had indeed been in an illusion earlier. He'd gone through an endless cycle of being devoured and restored by the eyes, undergoing countless destructions and rebirths, before he finally woke up from it.","Years of treading around death had tempered his resilience. It would take more to bring him down. It was also a good thing that not all the eyes had wanted to destroy him. The balance between destruction and rebirth had given him the chance to regain consciousness.","He had no idea what those eyes were, and he couldn’t help but notice how Mi Li hadn’t intervened in the entire process. Even now that he was out of the illusion, he still retained a vivid memory of those eyes.","Are these the universal deities that Mi Li and the Time Scribe previously mentioned?","Just then, he arrived at Xihe’s position. Xihe’s light was flickering, and she was smiling bizarrely. It was an eerie sight.","“Xihe! Xihe!” Zu An hurriedly cleansed the black fog around her and infused a surge of warm primordial ki into her body.","In the first place, Xihe's position as the Sun Goddess granted her strong immunity against demons. With Zu An’s help, it didn’t take long for her to regain consciousness. The first thing she did upon opening her eyes and seeing Zu An was to embrace him.","Zu An was stunned, saying, \"I still have to maintain the other three directions.”","While the softness pressing against him was tempting, he could only leave his posts to check on them using his flames and ki temporarily. He needed to be ready to return to the other three directions at any moment to replenish the energies, so the formation wouldn’t collapse.","Xihe belatedly realized this wasn’t a dream and anxiously retracted her hand.","There were a thousand things Zu An wanted to ask her, but he had no choice but to return to his position and maintain the formation.","Xihe’s cheeks reddened. Was it all an illusion?","In the illusion, she'd lived a blissful life with Zu An. The ten Golden Crows were still alive, and she'd made them call Zu An 'father'... Recalling the scene made Xihe’s toes curl up so hard that they nearly dug into the ground.","However, when she remembered that the ten Golden Crows were dead, her expression quickly sank. Her previously reddened face became pale once more.","Given her capability, she had already subconsciously realized that it was all a lie in the illusion, but she'd wanted the happiness to last for just a moment longer. She'd even considered never waking up again. It was only when Zu An woke her up that she could no longer find reasons to stay in there.","With the three of them regaining consciousness, the Five Directions Demon Suppressing Formation finally whirred back to life. Under the influence of the formation, the palace glowed as other demon suppression formations began to activate.","The pitch-black demonic ki inside the hall gradually thinned as many souls were freed from the Myriad Souls Banner’s control. Transparent faces that were previously marred with anger and ferocity regained their peace, and their souls dissipated into starlight.","The remaining demonic ki gathered within a three meter radius of the Myriad Souls Banner. The banner buzzed eerily as it tried to make a final stand against the celestial palace’s cleansing powers.","But these formations had been constructed and refined by countless Celestial Emperors and deities; it would be an understatement to say that they were powerful. On top of that, they were aided by Zu An’s Five Directions Demon Suppression Formation.","The Myriad Souls Banner was fighting a losing battle. The radius of the demonic ki grew smaller and smaller.","Just then, a dashing youth dressed in a black robe with golden embroidery suddenly appeared in the palace. Xihe shuddered at the sight of the youth.","The youth turned to Xihe. He pointed a finger at Zu An and said, “Mother, that fellow killed my nine older brothers. Are you really going to work with the enemy?”","He was the only Golden Crow who had escaped.","“No, that’s not how it is...” Xihe’s voice quivered.","“That is how it is! He shot us down with his bow, Suzeng. I saw my nine older brothers die before my eyes. He would have killed me too, if not for uncle arriving in time. Mother, you have to avenge my big brothers!”","Xihe’s face turned pale. “You have misunderstood. The culprit is Jun. He...”","The Golden Crow interjected before she could finish her piece, “Mother, there’s no way our father would hurt us! Who fooled you? Is it that gigolo? You mustn’t be fooled by him!”","“It’s not him...” Xihe thought about the mysterious man she'd met and hesitated.","Now that I think about it, it was a one-sided claim on his part, saying that Emperor Jun killed the Ten Suns and was planning to construct the Apocalypse Formation. Why did I believe him so easily? Could I have been subconsciously hoping for that to be the case because I don’t want Zu An to be the enemy?","“Mother, I don’t blame you for being fooled by that gigolo. If you aren’t going to avenge my big brothers, I’ll do it alone!” the youth roared angrily. He spread his wings and unleashed a barrage of sword ki against Zu An.","Zu An was already struggling to maintain three directions. The Goddess of Wu Mountain exclaimed in astonishment, “Be careful!”","However, she was so severely injured that just maintaining the formation sapped all her strength. She couldn’t help him.","Zu An had to admit that this last Golden Crow had chosen a good time to attack them. His hands were indeed full at the moment... but sometimes, hands weren't required to suppress someone.","A Seven-Colored Divine Halo shone, and the Golden Crow charging toward him vanished.","“Spare him!” Xihe exclaimed.","Zu An replied, “Don’t worry, my divine halo only imprisons people. He'll be safe. Besides, I doubt I can hold him in.”","Xihe was taken aback. Why won’t you be able to hold him in? My tenth son is the youngest and weakest among his brothers. There’s no way he can struggle free of your divine halo.","A golden light shone through the Seven-Colored Divine Halo, and the Golden Crow youth broke free from his incarceration. However, his eyes now looked much older and more vicious.","“Emperor Jun, you can’t keep hiding it,” Zu An remarked with a sigh."]},{"number":2636,"title":"Chapter 2636: Chapter 2588: Focusing on the Weakest Link","paragraphs":["The familiar coldness coming from her tenth son made Xihe’s heart sink. Her rational self had known that the youth before her was likely to be a fake, but she still harbored a sliver of hope. There was no need to go very far to deceive someone who had lost everything like her—all one had to do was to show her a glimmer of hope, and she would fool herself.","The youth glared at Zu An coldly. “I spent countless years meticulously setting up my grand plan, but it was all nearly ruined because of you. You should take pride in that.”","“Grand plan my ass! It’s just your greed. In order to construct this vile formation, you even killed your own sons, yet you have the cheek to appear self-righteous,” Zu An spat in disdain.","“A mere ant like you would never understand!” Emperor Jun sneered. “For the sake of eliminating the vile Shamans, sacrifices are inevitable. Once the Shamans have been vanquished, we will have a new world. They will exist eternally in a new form in that new world. Isn’t that much better?”","“You lunatic! You're out of your mind!” Xihe cursed.","“Xihe, you are a disappointment. You are the Sun Goddess, the wife of the next Celestial Emperor. How could you hook up with a mere mortal human? Your lack of shame is appalling!” Emperor Jun coldly glared at her. “However, I’ll magnanimously grant you another chance. Return to my side, and I won’t pursue this matter.”","Xihe seethed with anger. “Do you think it’s possible for anything to remain between us after you killed my sons?”","“They are only dead now,” Emperor Jun calmly replied. “Once I achieve Sainthood, it’ll be a walk in the park to revive them. There’s no need to fuss over the temporary.”","“You can revive them?” Xihe’s eyes lit up. She had schemed for many years, even going as far as to return to the past, all to rescue her sons from their miserable fate. If Emperor Jun could revive the Golden Crows after achieving Sainthood, his proposal would be worth considering.","“Of course. Do you think a saint wouldn’t be capable of that?” Emperor Jun replied proudly.","“I don’t think you’d be capable of that,” Zu An suddenly interjected.","Emperor Jun narrowed his eyes. “A summer worm will never know of winter. What does an ant like you know about the capabilities of a saint?”","“There is a good example from not long ago. When Zhulong’s son, Yayu, died, Celestial Emperor Zhuanxu immediately bestowed him with an immortal medicine to revive him. However, upon revival, Yayu turned into a witless monster. Does that count as bringing someone back to life?” Zu An had figured things out, allowing him to speak in a composed but confident manner.","“Hmph! Zhuanxu has yet to reach Sainthood. Just because he can’t do it doesn’t mean I can’t do it after reaching Sainthood,” Emperor Jun impatiently replied.","“Immortal medicines are naturally-formed resources harnessing the universe’s origin dao. Zhuanxu and Zhulong were unable to revive Yayu even when using such a medicine; I doubt you’d be able to do it as a saint,” Zu An sneered. “The crux to reviving the Golden Crows doesn’t lie in Sainthood, but something else.”","“What is it?” Xihe was both taken aback and elated. Zu An seemed to be suggesting that he had a way to save her sons.","“How can you trust that gigolo’s words?” Emperor Jun scoffed. “This is a feat that even Zhuanxu failed at. Even I’d have to reach Sainthood to perform this miracle, but that ant claims he can do it?”","It was as if a bucket of cold water was poured over Xihe. He’s right. Zu An isn't weak by any means, but there are stronger experts in the Celestial Court. If even the Celestial Court’s deities could only rescue a walking corpse, what can he possibly do?","“The immortal medicine failed to properly revive Yayu because this world doesn’t have the netherworld and the Six Paths of Reincarnation. The souls of the deceased are prone to dissipating into the void. Zhuanxu and Zhulong only managed to rescue Yayu’s body and not his soul.” Zu An turned to Emperor Jun and continued, “Even if you reach Sainthood, the most you can do is to reforge the Golden Crows’ bodies. You won’t be able to do a thing about their souls.”","“Netherworld, Six Paths of Reincarnation...” Emperor Jun frowned. “What nonsense is that?”","Xihe, however, had heard about the Six Paths of Reincarnation in the future. Looking at Zu An, she solemnly asked, “Will you be able to save my sons?”","“I can give it a try, but I can’t guarantee it.” Zu An didn’t want to deceive her.","But his hesitant answer brought a relieved smile to Xihe’s face. “I trust you. I’m grateful to you for helping me. I have mentally prepared for failure.”","Emperor Jun was infuriated. “Xihe, you used to be a smart woman. How can you fall for that gigolo’s nonsense?! Have you truly fallen in love with that human?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s gaze swiftly alternated among Emperor Jun, Zu An, and Xihe; she was making full use of her front row seat to relish in this drama.","Xihe’s ears flushed in anger. “He might only be a mortal human, but he’s a hundred times better than a beast who murders his sons!”","Zu An interjected, “Xihe, don’t let him sway your feelings. He’s only saying so much to buy time.” He turned to Emperor Jun and continued, “I bet your main body is busy fighting the Shamans. This body only contains a sliver of your soul, so you aren’t confident you can deal with us. That’s why you’re saying so much to secure Xihe’s aid.”","Emperor Jun’s eyes narrowed. “I should have killed you a long time ago, bastard!”","You have successfully troll ed Emperor Jun for +444... +444... +444...","“It’s high time we settle our score!” Zu An stood up. Now that the Five Directions Demon Suppression Formation had activated the celestial palace’s cleansing power, there was no need for them to continue maintaining it.","“You’re courting death!” Now that his ploy was exposed, Emperor Jun couldn’t hold himself back anymore. He unfurled his wings and unleashed his feathers as a barrage of golden arrows at Xihe, Zu An, and the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","Zu An opened his arms wide and manifested a massive black hole to swallow the barrage of golden arrows. Despite stopping the attack, he narrowed his eyes as he realized that he had lost track of Emperor Jun.","The next moment, he sensed Emperor Jun standing right next to the Goddess of Wu Mountain, brandishing a whip of golden light to sever her neck. Alarmed, Zu An quickly used his position swap to take her position.","Emperor Jun smirked. He had anticipated Zu An’s reaction. Golden light gushed forth from his hands, instantly transforming into a cage to imprison Zu An. At the same time, he shot two beams of golden light from his eyes at Zu An.","Emperor Jun had long since realized that the Goddess of Wu Mountain was the weakest link of the trio. Whenever he attacked her, Zu An would have no choice but to rush to her rescue. This created chances for him to lay traps for Zu An. This was the same move that would have taken Zu An’s life earlier if not for Zhulong’s timely intervention. But Zhulong wasn't here to save him this time.","Just then, a figure appeared in front of him to take Emperor Jun’s two beams of golden light.","Xihe spurted a mouthful of fresh blood. It was fortunate that she, as the Sun Goddess, had an exceptionally resilient constitution and the Celestial Court’s divine jurisdiction. It also helped that Emperor Jun hesitated at the sight of her and held back a little. Otherwise, she could have been reduced to ashes. Still, suffering another blow in her already weakened state pushed her to the verge of death.","Emperor Jun was infuriated. How could his wife sacrifice herself for another man?!","You have successfully trolle d Emperor Jun for +999... +999... +999...","The silver lining to Xihe’s incapacitation was that she could no longer aid Zu An. There was no need for him to hold back anymore. As long as he exploited these two women well, it would be a walk in the park for him to kill Zu An.","As he once again charged at the Goddess of Wu Mountain, viciousness flashed through his eyes.","Zu An understood what Emperor Jun was up to. Such a battle was too disadvantageous to him, so he decided to use his ‘Fragrant Barf’ ability to draw Emperor Jun’s aggro. The latter immediately halted his attack and glared at him with raging eyes.","“Let’s have a proper duel as men instead. It’s pathetic seeing a future Celestial Emperor desperately attacking women over and over again,” Zu An sneered.","“I’ll kill you!” Emperor Jun knew that Zu An was taunting him, but for some reason, he couldn’t control his emotions at all. The only thought he had in mind was to kill Zu An right away.","Fearing that the shockwaves from their clashes would injure the two ladies, Zu An morphed into a rainbow and departed from the celestial palace. Emperor Jun followed him as a surge of golden light."]},{"number":2637,"title":"Chapter 2637: Chapter 2589: Counterattack","paragraphs":["The rainbow and golden light intertwined now and then, only for the chase to resume shortly after. It didn’t take long for Zu An to incur injuries.","Emperor Jun was the future Celestial Emperor, after all. Even with just a sliver of his soul in a Golden Crow Prince’s body, he was still not an opponent Zu An could deal with. His only concern earlier had been that Xihe and Zu An would join forces against him, but in a 1-on-1, Zu An had no chance of turning the tables on him at all.","“Don’t worry, I won’t let you die so easily. I’ll rip off your flesh bit by bit, and your soul shall eternally suffer in the Myriad Souls Banner!” Emperor Jun spat threats through clenched jaws while chasing after Zu An. He wanted to see Zu An suffer a mental breakdown.","But Zu An didn’t show the slightest fear. Instead, he calmly replied, “You said such words earlier too, but I’m still prancing around here. As a Celestial Emperor, you need to do more than running your mouth.”","Emperor Jun’s cheeks twitched. He'd wanted to erode Zu An’s willpower, but the latter had turned the tables on him.","You have successfully trolle d Emperor Jun for +600... +600... +600...","He had no idea why he easily lost control of his emotions whenever he was dealing with Zu An. Someone of his level of cultivation was supposed to have far greater control over their emotions.","However, a smile soon formed on his face. Zu An was fleeing toward the South Celestial Gate. Despite his calm exterior, he must be panicking inside to flee to the South Celestial Gate of all places. Did Xihe not tell him that Zhao Lingguan and the celestial soldiers stationed there are all my people?","He couldn’t wait to see the look on Zu An’s face.","However, when he saw Zu An’s appearance changing into that of his original body, his smile suddenly stiffened up. “What is that bastard up to? Who does he think he's fooling with such cheap tricks?”","In the meantime, the two of them reached the South Celestial Gate. Zhao Lingguan and the celestial soldiers had long noticed the commotion and rushed over.","Emperor Jun was just about to order Zhao Lingguan to take down Zu An when the latter beat him to it. “Zhao Lingguan, take down that unfilial son of mine right now!”","Emperor Jun’s heart skipped a beat. He finally understood where the problem lay. He was currently taking the identity of the Golden Crow’s Tenth Prince. Very few people in the Celestial Court knew about him possessing the Golden Crow Ten Princes, and Zhao Lingguan clearly wasn’t one of them.","“Your Majesty, what happened?” Zhao Lingguan and the other celestial guards were baffled. The Golden Crow Tenth Prince is trying to kill Emperor Jun ? Did the sun rise from the wrong direction today?","Putting aside how the father and son came to blows in the first place, shouldn’t Emperor Jun be one-sidedly teaching his son a lesson? How did Emperor Jun end up on the losing side against his son?","Having guessed their thoughts, Zu An quickly replied, “He has gone berserk under someone’s influence. He assaulted me and Xihe in an attempt to refine us.”","He tried to explain how ‘Emperor Jun’ was being put in a disadvantageous position against his son with a generic cover story. He didn’t dare to go into detail, as he didn’t know whether Zhao Lingguan knew about the Myriad Souls Banner or not.","Emperor Jun was stunned. How can this bastard be so shameless? “Don’t listen to him, Zhao Lingguan! I am the real Emperor Jun!”","Zhao Lingguan stared at the arguing duo in bewilderment. He couldn’t believe such a ridiculous thing could happen in the Celestial Court, especially with Emperor Jun. This Emperor Jun looks and feels like the real Emperor Jun , but for some reason, the Golden Crow Tenth Prince’s manner of speech feels inexplicably familiar.","“Quickly send some men to my chamber to rescue Xihe. After being attacked by that unfilial son, she’s on the verge of death.” Zu An said.","Through this ‘unwitting’ reminder, Zhao Lingguan suddenly remembered that Emperor Jun had carried Xihe into the Celestial Court via the South Celestial Gate earlier. That proved this Emperor Jun was the real one. This is my chance to prove myself.","With a heart quivering with glee, he turned to the real Emperor Jun and roared, “Tenth Prince, how can you commit such an atrocious deed? You should surrender right away!”","I must hold back against the Tenth Prince later. They are still father and son, after all. If they mend their relationship afterward, I’ll become the sinner instead. What I should do is capture the Tenth Prince alive and hand him over to Emperor Jun to mete out punishment.","Emperor Jun was rendered speechless. “Zhao Lingguan, how can you be this dumb?”","Zhao Lingguan was infuriated. “I shall apprehend you on His Majesty’s behalf!”","He raised his axe, which instantaneously expanded to three thousand meters in length, and hacked it down on Emperor Jun. Even the Celestial Court’s sea of clouds was split into two before the overwhelming might of his axe.","But this attack landed on empty air. Emperor Jun surged over to Zhao Lingguan’s side as a surge of golden light and spat, “Scram!” He sent Zhao Lingguan flying with a kick.","Zhao Lingguan was speechless. I thought this would be an easy battle. When did the Tenth Prince become so powerful?","However, he wasn’t about to be humiliated in front of his subordinates. With a furious roar, he charged at Emperor Jun with his massive axe. “Where do you think you’re going?!”","Emperor Jun was rendered speechless. Zu An had already been in his grasp, only for this fellow to appear out of nowhere and tie him down. What made things even more frustrating was that he couldn’t tell Zhao Lingguan the truth! It was shocking news for a Celestial Emperor to possess his son’s body. Revealing the truth could solve the problem at hand, but there could be severe repercussions in the future.","Left with no choice, Emperor Jun had to devote his attention to shaking off Zhao Lingguan. By the time he succeeded, Zu An was nowhere to be seen.","“Where did he go? Did he return to the celestial palace?” Emperor Jun was about to head back when he suddenly felt a rush of anger. His gut feeling was telling him that Zu An was in another direction.","So, he followed his gut feeling and eventually saw Zu An rushing down the sacred tree Jianmu. He burst into laughter. “I should have let Xihe witness your cowardice. Who could have thought you would abandon them and escape by yourself?”","After everything that had happened, he didn’t want to waste any more time. He just wanted to kill Zu An and get this over with. Golden light beams erupted from his eyes. No matter how fast Zu An was, he couldn’t be faster than light.","Much to Emperor Jun’s surprise, Zu An made no attempt to dodge the attack. Instead, he took out a formation plate and created a spatial rift in front of him. The golden light shot through the spatial rift and was diverted onto the sacred tree Jianmu.","Emperor Jun was horrified. It finally dawned on him that Zu An wasn’t banking on Zhao Lingguan to defeat him. Zu An had merely been buying time to construct a teleportation formation here in order to use Jianmu’s divine runes against him! He would have nothing to fear if he was in his peak condition, but he only had a sliver of his soul here. In his current state, Jianmu’s divine runes were more than enough to pose a threat to him.","Still, he wasn’t the Celestial Emperor for no reason. With a wave of his sleeves, he swiftly formed another spatial rift around Jianmu to divert his beams of golden light elsewhere.","Zu An sighed. He hadn’t expected Emperor Jun to react so quickly.","Emperor Jun secretly wiped away cold sweat before glaring at Zu An with cold eyes. “You are a scheming one. I nearly fell for your trick. There won’t be a second time.”","The same trick wouldn’t work twice.","Zu An was aware of that, but he chuckled nevertheless. “I know that you won’t attack Jianmu on your own accord anymore... but I can!”","He emulated the Golden Crow’s sword ki using the Rune Weapon Chart and attacked Jianmu. At the same time, he used his position swap to exchange places with Emperor Jun.","Emperor Jun sneered, “What’s the use of swapping positions? The divine runes don’t recognize the aggressor by their position, but...”","His expression suddenly warped. He noticed that Zu An had reverted to his original form, which made him realize that Zu An had struck Jianmu in his appearance using his methods.","He had no idea how Zu An’s disguise worked, but even Zhao Lingguan had been fooled by it. In other words, there was a chance that the divine runes could perceive him as the aggressor!","“NO!”","He was about to dodge when the divine runes lit up and devoured him with their terrifying light."]},{"number":2638,"title":"Chapter 2638: Chapter 2590: Rescue","paragraphs":["In his normal condition, Emperor Jun wouldn’t fear these divine runes. He had plenty of ways to deal with such situations. But this was only a sliver of his soul, and it was possessing the Golden Crow Prince’s body. This was considered an evil, unorthodox method.","Furthermore, Jianmu’s divine runes had the power to dispel evil!","Zu An had attacked Jianmu using Emperor Jun's face and aura to trigger the divine runes, and to make things worse, he'd even swapped their positions! The divine runes didn’t have intelligence and were incapable of telling people apart, so they could only identify the aggressor through their aura. Meanwhile, Zu An’s earlier attack had harnessed the auras of the Golden Crow Prince and Emperor Jun’s soul sliver.","Emperor Jun was instantly devoured by the divine runes’ light.","Cold sweat dripped down Zu An’s forehead. He had been taking on a huge risk there. If the divine runes had somehow identified him as the aggressor, he would have been the one suffering that fate. Fortunately, he had played plenty of games in the past and was skilled at finding loopholes to exploit.","His bet had paid off!","With a scream of agony, Emperor Jun plummeted from the sky like a sandbag.","The divine runes reined in their light and reverted to normal.","Zu An carefully caught the Golden Crow Tenth Prince’s body and confirmed that there was no longer any soul pulsing in it. That meant Emperor Jun’s soul sliver had been vanquished! He had no idea why the divine runes had only obliterated Emperor Jun’s soul sliver, but hadn’t harmed the Tenth Prince’s body; but this wasn’t the time to be thinking about that. He quickly brought the prince’s body back to the celestial palace.","On the battlefield between the Fiends and the Shamans, Emperor Jun, who had been imposingly massacring his enemies, suddenly clutched his head and let out a miserable cry. The nearby Ancestral Shamans took this chance to counterattack. If not for Donghuang Taiyi protecting him with the East Emperor Bell, he could have lost his life there and then.","“What happened?” Donghuang Taiyi asked, concerned.","Emperor Jun didn’t answer, but he stared intently in the celestial palace’s direction. The soul sliver he had left there as a precaution had been killed! The backlash of that dealt a heavy blow to him. To make things worse, this hinted that something had gone awry in the celestial palace, and the Myriad Souls Banner wouldn't necessarily be safe anymore...","Knowing that he couldn’t leave things be, he said, “I’ll leave things here to you. I need to make a quick trip back to the Celestial Court.”","He was about to leave when his surroundings were suddenly sealed off. It was Zhulong’s doing.","“I’m your opponent, Emperor Jun. You won’t get away that easily,” Zhulong said as he angrily charged at Emperor Jun.","Emperor Jun had no choice. These Ancestral Shamans were so strong that he could only barely fend against them with his cultivation. There was no way he could escape when they were doing all they could to tie him down.","...","At the Celestial Court, Zhao Lingguan was delighted to see Zu An. “You’re back, Your Majesty!”","He saw the Golden Crow Tenth Prince in Zu An’s hand and was awed. As expected of His Majesty. He still subdued the Tenth Prince in the end. He probably struggled earlier because he didn't want to go too far dealing with his own son.","Hm, why does the Tenth Prince look dead?","“Mm. Continue guarding the South Celestial Gate well. I’ll bring him to apologize to his mother,” Zu An said as he entered the Celestial Court with the Tenth Prince.","Zhao Lingguan nodded. Disobedient brats ought to be beaten up by their parents.","The shame he felt from being outmaneuvered by the Tenth Prince disappeared. He puffed up his chest as he regained his usual liveliness.","Zu An soon returned to the celestial palace, where he found Xihe and the Goddess of Wu Mountain pacing around the hall anxiously. When they saw him, their eyes lit up in delight. They were about to rush forward to welcome him back when they each remembered that there were other women present and held themselves back.","Xihe’s gaze soon fell on the Golden Crow Tenth Prince. “He...”","“Emperor Jun’s soul sliver died. I brought the Tenth Prince’s body back,” Zu An replied.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was astonished. To think that he could kill Emperor Jun ’s soul sliver? That’s practically a miracle!","Unable to hold herself back anymore, Xihe rushed forward to grab her son’s corpse and began sobbing pitifully.","Zu An gently patted her shoulder. He knew that at times like this, no words could help.","He then turned his gaze to the Myriad Souls Banner, which no longer looked as imposing as before. Under the suppression of the celestial palace and the Five Directions Demon Suppression Formation, its demonic ki had completely receded into it.","Thus, he drew the Tai’e Sword and unleashed a brilliant sword ki strike at it.","The Myriad Souls Banner could no longer absorb such powerful ki. With a loud crack, it shattered into pieces. Countless souls gushed out from the banner and fled in all directions, delighted that they had finally regained their freedom. Even though they would soon dissipate into thin air, they would rather disappear than suffer eternally in the banner.","However, some vile souls noticed Ji Xiaoxi’s body lying on the altar and charged at her, hoping to occupy her body and come back to life.","“Scram!” Zu An roared. The combined prowess of his primordial ki and his authority as the Netherworld’s master easily crush those vile souls. No other soul dared approach Ji Xiaoxi’s body, fearing they would suffer the same fate.","As the netherworld’s master, Zu An had exceptional sensitivity when it came to souls. It took a while, but he eventually found a faint silhouette amid the countless souls. This silhouette looked timid, but no other souls dared to approach her as if she were an incarnation of horror.","As expected of the Cruel Poison Constitution . Emperor Jun used her as the Myriad Souls Banner’s core for a reason. Even her soul is laced with lethal poison that intimidates other souls.","Ji Xiaoxi’s soul had been split into many fragments to dampen the effects of the Cruel Poison Constitution, lest she poison the other souls inside the Myriad Souls Banner to death. It was thanks to that she'd lasted long enough for him to rescue her.","Still, it hurt Zu An to see how fragmented her soul had become. She must have suffered a lot.","Not daring to hesitate, he used a secret art inside the Netherworld Book of Life and Death to summon a couple of specters. These figures were initially frightened and tried to escape, but the sight of Zu An inspired inexplicable trust in them, prompting them to subconsciously fly toward him.","“Don’t be afraid, Xiaoxi. I’m here to save you,” Zu An spoke gently for fear that he would scare her.","It was hard to tell whether the specters understood his words or not, but they smiled and allowed him to do as he pleased. In the end, they returned into Ji Xiaoxi’s body.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain passed a jade bottle over to Zu An. “This is Wu Mountain’s Cloud Fog Essence. It helps to heal the soul.”","Zu An looked at her with grateful eyes. That was indeed what Xiaoxi needed right now.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled. She waved a hand, and a droplet of viscous liquid resembling honey flew from the bottle into Ji Xiaoxi’s mouth.","Zu An could feel the rich energy and life force contained within the droplet. This is much more potent than Milk of Purple Frost.","Ji Xiaoxi moaned as her complexion became visibly redder. However, her injuries were so severe that even with the Netherworld’s secret arts and the Cloud Fog Essence healing her soul, she wouldn’t regain consciousness so quickly.","So, Zu An entrusted the Goddess of Wu Mountain to take care of her before scanning the room. One by one, he found ten unique souls resembling little birds. He used his secret art to channel the souls toward the Golden Crow Tenth Prince’s body.","These little Golden Crows became more lively the closer they got to Xihe. Their wings fluttered as if they were cheering.","Xihe was both stunned and delighted to see this. With a quivering voice, she asked, “Is it still possible... to save them?”","She almost wanted to cover her ears, fearing that the answer would shatter her heart.","“Of course. This world must have a sun.” Whether for the greater good or his ties with Xihe, Zu An was inclined to help the Golden Crows. “However, they have been dead for too long, and on top of that, Emperor Jun used their souls to control the Myriad Souls Banner. That has resulted in the severe erosion of their souls.”","Xihe’s heart sank. Her hatred for Emperor Jun hit a boiling point.","“I’m incapable of saving them individually. What I can do now is to fuse their souls to form a complete soul. This soul will retain their individual memories and personalities. We can only nurture their souls in a body and try to find ways to heal them in the future.”","Xihe had thought that it was hopeless; she hadn’t expected there to be such a solution. She was so overjoyed that she cried tears of joy. “This is good enough! It’s good enough!”","Over the years, she had tried countless ways to change the trajectory of history, but she was unable to defy fate no matter what she did. She had already resigned herself to despair, so how could she not be excited upon learning that there was a chance to rescue her ten sons?"]},{"number":2639,"title":"Chapter 2639: Chapter 2591: The Celestial Emperor’s Repayment","paragraphs":["The Golden Crows were much stronger than Ji Xiaoxi in the first place. Shortly after their fragmented souls entered the Golden Crow Tenth Prince’s body, the Tenth Prince’s body slowly opened his eyes.","“Mother...” Seeing Xihe, the Tenth Prince burst into tears. He was about to get up when he suddenly clutched his head and exclaimed, “Ugh, it hurts!”","Xihe was overjoyed to hear the voice of her son, but she was horrified to see him in such pain. She anxiously turned to Zu An.","Zu An explained, “Their souls are incomplete. It’s only normal for them to suffer a headache.”","Soon, different voices echoed from the Tenth Prince’s mouth.","“Huh? What am I doing here?”","“Who are you?”","“Isn’t this tenth brother’s body?”","“Mother, what are you doing here?”","“I vaguely recall father killing me.”","...","The commotion caused by the different voices caused the Tenth Prince’s headache to worsen. Just then, the Goddess of Wu Mountain threw a jade bottle over and said, “This should make them feel better.”","Xihe directed a grateful nod at her before feeding a droplet of Cloud Fog Essence to the Tenth Prince. That eased the Tenth Prince’s pain, and he gradually calmed down. That gave Xihe the chance to explain the situation to them.","Zu An returned to Ji Xiaoxi’s side and gently held her hand, infusing ki into her body to aid her recovery. When he felt just how cold her hands were, his heart stung.","“Don’t worry, Miss Xiaoxi will be fine,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain consoled him.","But Zu An wasn’t that optimistic. Xiaoxi had been the ‘main ingredient’ in the Myriad Souls Banner, so her soul was bound to have suffered a lot of damage. Furthermore, it was unknown whether this incident would trigger her Cruel Poison Constitution.","Just then, Ji Xiaoxi’s eyelids fluttered. Overjoyed, Zu An called out for her.","A while later, Ji Xiaoxi finally opened her eyes. Delight and hesitation flickered in her eyes when she saw Zu An. “Big brother Zu, am I dreaming?”","Unable to hold himself back anymore, Zu An pulled her into his embrace. “No, it’s not a dream. It’s all right now. Big brother Zu will protect you.”","His warm embrace convinced Ji Xiaoxi that this was all real. She finally revealed a smile that came from the bottom of her heart as she said, “I was in a scary place earlier. My body felt light, and it was on the verge of being devoured by darkness. I was so afraid, until I heard big brother Zu’s voice in the distance. It was as if I finally found my pillar of support. It’s because of you that I didn’t lose myself to the darkness...”","Her words made Zu An feel even more sorry for her. “It’s all over now. I’ll be by your side from now onward.”","It was hard to tell what was in Ji Xiaoxi’s head, but upon hearing his words, her face turned red. She then happened to notice the Goddess of Wu Mountain, and that sent her into a fluster. She tried to push Zu An away but was too weak to succeed. In the end, she shyly smiled at the latter and said, “Big sister Pei is here too.”","“I’m not Miss Pei,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain replied. I must truly resemble Miss Pei for her to say that too. That made her even more curious about Zu An’s history with Pei Mianman.","“Ah?” Ji Xiaoxi blinked in confusion. Is big sister Pei angry at me?","Zu An quickly explained the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s identity to her. Ji Xiaoxi was fascinated. She hadn't thought there could be two people who resemble each other so much in the world.","Meanwhile, Xihe brought the Golden Crow Tenth Prince over to thank Zu An when a huge explosion suddenly echoed in the distance. The entire palace shook due to the explosion.","The group was startled. “What happened?”","“Something happened to the formation suppressing Zhuanxu.” Zu An recalled the Great Constellation Formation being in the direction of the explosion.","The group rushed to the window to ascertain the situation. There, they saw the stars in the sky plummeting one after another, a sign that the formation was unraveling.","Zu An grimly said, “Let’s quickly leave this place.”","There was no telling how Zhuanxu would react to them. Given their relationship with Emperor Jun, Zhuanxu’s ire could be drawn to Xihe and the Golden Crow Tenth Prince. At the same time, Zu An carried the shamans’ aura right now, and the shamans had bad blood with the fiends.","Besides, Zu An had a terrible impression of Zhuanxu. The latter had little control over the Celestial Court despite being the Celestial Emperor, and had simply watched as Emperor Jun caused so much trouble.","The others agreed with his suggestion.","Zu An picked Xiaoxi up.","The group was about to leave when a divine light suddenly surged from the distant formation. Zhuanxu had to have broken free of his restraint.","Alarmed, Zhao Lingguan rushed over with his subordinates. “Where do you think you're going?”","He charged at Zhuanxu with his massive axe.","The figure amid the divine light casually pressed downward, and a giant palm descended from the sky and smacked Zhao Lingguan and his subordinates down from the Celestial Court. The falling stars’ debris then fell on them, turning into mountains that buried them within.","Zu An was stunned. Has Zhao Lingguan always been this courageous?","Of course, Zhao Lingguan wasn’t so foolish as to think he could subdue a Celestial Emperor. He'd thought that Emperor Jun was nearby and all he had to do was buy some time for Emperor Jun to appear. He could have accrued merit that way. Little did he know the Emperor Jun he had just seen was Zu An.","The person in the divine light glanced in the direction of where Zu An and the others were before taking a step forward. Before Zu An and the others could react, he was already inside the celestial palace.","Zu An and the others froze in place. Damn it, we were still a step too late.","Zu An anxiously urged Xihe and the Goddess of Wu Mountain to be careful, only to realize that they weren’t responding, as if someone had frozen them in place.","“What did you do to them?” Zu An furiously glared at the man shrouded in divine light.","The man wore a resplendent coronet and a five-colored silk robe embroidered with gleaming jewels. His presence was so powerful that it made one overlook his appearance; all one would remember was his inviolable authority.","“Don’t worry, they are fine. I just want to talk to you,” Zhuanxu said.","Zu An fell silent. He must have used some kind of spatial domain-type skill. As expected of a Celestial Emperor. His methods are impressive.","But the thought of how Zhuanxu had done nothing all this while despite his incredible prowess, sitting idly as Emperor Jun messed around, made him even angrier.","“You seem to be blaming me.” Zhuanxu saw through Zu An’s thoughts.","“I wouldn’t dare. I’m merely perplexed as to why you haven’t done anything despite your formidable abilities. You were even imprisoned by your own people. I find it baffling,” Zu An replied sarcastically.","“It’s more complicated than you think. I’m not just up against Emperor Jun and Taiyi here...” Zhuanxu suddenly paused here, as he was reluctant to share more details with Zu An. “And how do you know I haven’t done anything at all?”","“Oh? Enlighten me, please,” Zu An replied. All you've done is to sever heaven and earth by sacrificing your most talented grandson.","“How could you have shot down the Golden Crows and foiled Emperor Jun’s plan if I hadn’t bestowed Suzeng to you?” Zhuanxu replied with a faint smile.","Zu An frowned. “You might not have been the one who gifted Suzeng to me. Besides, how could a future event resolve a past incident?”","Zhuanxu chuckled. “The past, the present, and the future; those are concepts thought up by mortals. To beings like us, there’s no difference among them. We can influence the timeline with a simple intervention at any temporal point. I might have gifted Suzeng to you in the future, but it came in handy here, no? It would be unnecessary to bestow it upon you a second time.”","Zu An’s head shook, as he felt as if he had heard the chime of truth. He vaguely felt something, but the moment passed, and he failed to fully grasp what exactly it was.","Zhuanxu wasn’t interested in speaking further on the matter. “You have done me a huge favor, so I’ll allow you to make a request. Is there anything you want?”"]},{"number":2640,"title":"Chapter 2640: Chapter 2592: Defying Spirit Tears","paragraphs":["Zu An’s eyes lit up. “Will any request do?”","Zhuanxu saw the gleam in Zu An’s eyes and chuckled. “It has to be within my means. I won’t be able to help you if you request to become a saint.”","Zu An replied, “I don’t need that much. I just want you to save my lovers, such as Chu Chuyan, Qiu Honglei, Ji Xiaoxi... I want them to recover from their afflictions.”","Zhuanxu’s smile froze up. “You’re a sly one. You’re making several requests of me at once.”","He did some calculations on his finger as if divining their conditions. A while later, he slowly replied, “Saving Miss Chu is your fate; I can’t intervene in that. As for Miss Qiu, you have saved her, and she should recover in due time. As for Miss Ji...”","Zhuanxu’s gaze fell on the lady in Zu An’s arms. A divine light shone on her. “Emperor Jun has triggered her Cruel Poison Constitution through the Myriad Souls Banner. I can only temporarily suppress it. You need to treat her in time, and I believe you already know the way to do so.”","Zu An was stunned. I still have to find those medicines in the end. But at least Xiaoxi’s Cruel Poison Constitution has stabilized for the time being.","“So there’s nothing you can help me with. Is this all you’re capable of as the Celestial Emperor?”","Zhuanxu’s eyelids twitched. “Fine, I’ll take that as a gift from me. You can make another request, but I suggest you think things through. You won’t be granted another chance.”","Zu An pondered hard, but in truth, he already knew what he needed. “You’ll fulfill my request as long as it’s within your means.”","“Of course. I, the Celestial Emperor, will not renege on my promise,” Zhuanxu replied in displeasure.","“I want the power insignias of the Celestial World and the Human World.” Zu An quickly added, “You said you wouldn’t renege on your promise.”","Zhuanxu was speechless.","It was a long time before he finally replied, “You... I might have obliterated you on the spot for your insolent request had I not known about the karmic effects beforehand.”","Zu An was stunned. He knows what I’m doing?","A golden light suddenly manifested in Zhuanxu’s hands. He gently flicked it into Zu An’s hands. “This is a sliver severed from the Celestial World’s power insignia. It should be enough for you.”","Zu An couldn’t help but ask, “Do you already know that I’m using the power insignias to forge the Six...”","Zhuanxu interrupted him before he could finish that statement. “Some things mustn’t be said out loud... The Human World’s power insignia isn’t with me, but you need not worry. It’s fated to fall into your hands very soon.”","Zu An was shocked. It felt as if Zhuanxu knew everything. For a moment there, he wondered if he was nothing but a piece on a chessboard.","He wanted to ask more questions, but Zhuanxu interjected, “Alright, I have to settle the war between the Shamans and the Fiends now. Farewell.”","His figure vanished right after.","Everything soon reverted to normal. Xihe and the Goddess of Wu Mountain anxiously said, “Let’s hurry up and leave. We’ll be in danger once Zhuanxu comes...”","Zu An replied, “He was already here.”","“He was here?” The two women were confused. They were unaware of the conversation that had just taken place.","Zu An was also awed by Zhuanxu’s abilities. He had no idea how the other party had achieved such a formidable feat.","It was then that Xihe suggested, “It’s too dangerous to get implicated in the war between the Shamans and the Fiends. Why don’t you come to Scalding Valley with me? It should serve as a safe refuge for the time being.”","Zu An hesitantly replied, “I might have to take a trip back to Wu Mountain. I feel uneasy for some reason, as if I've overlooked something.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain and Ji Xiaoxi had no objections to that.","Xihe said, “I have to bring the Golden Crows back to Scalding Valley as soon as possible to nourish their impaired body and souls. I won’t be able to accompany you for the time being.”","Saving the Golden Crows had always been her goal, so Zu An didn’t stop her. Silence loomed between the two of them. They vaguely realized that this could be farewell for them.","“I’m sorry for the things I've done in this time. Don’t worry, the lady named Xie Daoyun is fine. I’m only temporarily occupying her body. As for Miss Pei, she came to look for me, but I was worried that she would see through my impersonation, so I captured and imprisoned her in a formation. You just have to do this upon returning to rescue her...”","Xihe quickly shared the imprisonment location and the formation details. She then turned to the Goddess of Wu Mountain and remarked, “Miss Pei truly resembles Yaoji. If I’m not mistaken, Yaoji should be her former incarnation.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain had already guessed as much. Given their striking resemblance and inexplicable connection, there had to be some kind of link between them. Still, when she thought about the intimate relationship she would have with Zu An in the future, she couldn’t help but blush furiously.","“Xihe, I...” Zu An’s voice was hoarse. He wasn’t sure what to say in this situation.","He thought about their time together, including their intimate moments. They had been no different from a real couple. But at the same time, he had also shot down nine of the Golden Crows and used the Golden Phoenix ability against her. He had done her a great injustice.","Xihe placed her finger on his lips. There was no point in thinking so much about it now. The outcome was better than she'd expected, and the time she spent with him was enjoyable. She had never experienced such love before. Her marriage to Emperor Jun had always been a political one; there was no true love between them.","“Can I hug you one last time before we part ways?” Xihe looked at him carefully, worried that he would turn her down.","Zu An pulled her in for an embrace. The two of them hugged each other tightly. Words failed them at this moment.","The Golden Crow Tenth Prince stared dazedly at this scene as the ten souls in him broke into an uproar.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain tactfully walked away to give them some privacy.","Ji Xiaoxi wanted to walk away too, but she was in Zu An’s arms and was currently sandwiched tightly between the duo. Her face was flushed. I shouldn’t be here. No one can see me. Oof, big sister Xihe is too big. Crap, I’m running out of breath...","...","Xihe eventually left.","Yumen Beiqing’s body fell limply, and Zu An rushed forward to support her. He first checked her vitals and confirmed that there was nothing wrong. Xihe had warned him that she would require some time to recuperate before regaining consciousness.","Ji Xiaoxi suddenly exclaimed, “What’s that?”","Zu An looked in the direction she was pointing and noticed a droplet of golden fluid on his shoulder. It appeared to be a teardrop Xihe had left behind when embracing him earlier.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain walked over and took out a jade bottle to store the golden fluid. “You mentioned that you were looking for an ingredient called Defying Spirit Tears. I pride myself on being knowledgeable, but I have never heard of that before. However, I think I get it now.”","“Is this it?” Zu An was astounded. He would never have thought that what he was looking for had been by his side all along. And yet, he felt bitterness instead of joy.","“This is incomplete. It’s still lacking something,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain remarked with a glint in her eyes. Before Zu An could ask anything, she added, “It isn’t safe here. Let’s return to Wu Mountain first.”","Zu An nodded. He morphed into a rainbow and transported them out of the Celestial Court.","As they landed on Wu Mountain, the Goddess of Wu Mountain suddenly remarked with a frown. “Someone barged into my cavern.”","Zu An was shocked. He anxiously flashed into the cavern, but the Mermaid Queen was nowhere to be found."]},{"number":2641,"title":"Chapter 2641: Chapter 2593: Forlorn Heart","paragraphs":["In the meantime, Xie Daoyun gradually regained consciousness. She was temporarily dazed as she surveyed her foreign surroundings. Memories were surfacing in her mind, filling her in about what had happened while she was possessed. Despite stealing control over her body, Xihe hadn’t sealed off her senses, so Xie Daoyun recalled most things that had happened. In particular, when she thought about what Xihe had done with big brother Zu...","While she was berating Xihe for being shameless in her mind, she noticed that Zu An was looking for something. She asked, “What’s wrong?”","“Big sister Xie, you’re awake! The Mermaid Queen has gone missing, and big brother Zu is searching for her.” Ji Xiaoxi quickly explained the situation to her. The two were resting beneath a tree, looking after each other.","“The Mermaid Queen...” Xie Daoyun recalled the Ocean races’ renowned beauty and the intimate moments she'd shared with Zu An. Big brother Zu is a playboy! But the Mermaid Queen truly resembles Miss Shang...","Meanwhile, Zu An grabbed the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s arms and asked, “Didn’t you say she would be here? What happened?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain winced in pain. Zu An snapped out of his daze and quickly released her. “My apologies. I got too anxious.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain didn’t mind something this minor. She consoled him, saying, “Calm down. Let me see what happened first.”","Zu An was surprised to hear that. Is she able to peer into the past?","Sensing his confusion, the Goddess of Wu Mountain flung her sleeves as she explained, “All of the fog shrouding Wu Mountain is my eye.”","The surrounding fog converged into a screen that projected everything that had happened on Wu Mountain while they were away.","...","The Mermaid Queen nervously paced to and fro across Wu Mountain’s peak. The changing colors in the sky and the occasional deafening explosions made her so worried that every second was a torture to her. She was worried sick about Zu An. She wanted to help, but she had no idea where he was. With her current cultivation, a mere shockwave could cost her life if she got embroiled in the war between the Shamans and Fiends. If so, not only would she be of no use to Zu An, but she would also never meet him again.","She remembered the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s warnings before she left. Despite her anxiety, her rationality still prevailed. She wasn't on the main battlefield, but the shockwaves rippling from the distance were destructive enough to shatter mountains and crack earth. And yet, when they reached Wu Mountain, a mysterious light always neutralized the energy.","Just as she was feeling awed by Wu Mountain’s extraordinary qualities, she suddenly sensed something and turned around. A figure was flashing up the mountain. When she noticed that the figure was carrying a bow, she was initially happy —she thought that Zu An had returned. She was about to rush forward to welcome him back when she noticed that the figure was different and halted her footsteps.","That figure soon reached the mountain peak. It was indeed not her lover, but a man whom she had met once before, Feng Meng. He was the one who had previously led a platoon to capture her.","Feng Meng looked at her with admiring eyes. “As expected of the Chang clan’s renowned Saintess. You are gorgeous!”","Sensing he was up to something, the Mermaid Queen put up her guard. “What do you want?”","Feng Meng grabbed the bow he was carrying and gently stroked it. “The world sees Yi as the world’s number one archer. No matter how hard I work, I am still nothing more than second to the world. I refuse to accept that. Now, there is a way for me to prove my superiority over him. His fiancée is going to be my woman!”","The Mermaid Queen’s face darkened. She quickly formed a hand seal to unleash water arrows on the other party.","Feng Meng easily shot down her water arrows one after another. “You dare to use arrows against me? Arrogant!”","The Mermaid Queen didn’t answer. She continued unleashing skills on Feng Meng.","However, Feng Meng nocked and shot arrows so fast that it left afterimages in his wake. He dissipated the Mermaid Queen’s skills easily with an arrow each, leaving the latter with a lurching heart. She had crossed blows with Feng Meng when the latter pursued her, and she knew that his strength was far superior to hers.","While leisurely shooting down her water skills, Feng Meng chuckled, “I’ll spare your life if you hand the immortal medicine over to me.”","The Mermaid Queen was startled. “How do you know it’s with me?”","Zu An had secretly slipped her the immortal medicine as they parted ways. Outsiders shouldn’t have known about that.","“Heh! Your movements are all within my master’s...” Feng Meng noticed something halfway through and hurriedly stopped talking. “Hmph! Cut the crap and hand the immortal medicine over. I might consider sparing your life if you do so. Otherwise, I don’t mind taking both your body and the immortal medicine.”","Looking at his vile smile, the Mermaid Queen knew better than to trust his words. There was no way he would let her off the hook just because she handed over the immortal medicine. He was merely trying to grind down her desire to resist. As the Ocean races’ number one beauty, she had come into contact with countless people who harbored malicious intentions toward her. Her instincts about this were unmatched by others.","Thus, she'd chosen to engage Feng Meng while fighting him off to stall for time, hoping that the others would rush back in the meantime. Unfortunately, no one returned.","Feng Meng wasn’t a fool either. It didn’t take him long to figure out her intention.","The Mermaid Queen realized her time of reckoning had come. In this critical moment, she stuffed the immortal medicine into her mouth and jumped down Wu Mountain’s peak. Feng Meng wanted to grab her, only for her to shove him aside with a palm strike.","An expert of her caliber wouldn’t die even when jumping off a cliff, but it would be a different story if she dissipated her ki and unraveled her protection. Gazing into the distance, the Mermaid Queen left a tear droplet behind as she murmured, “Farewell, my lover...”","Looking at this sight, Zu An felt as if his blood had frozen in place. He had never felt such piercing pain in his chest before.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain grabbed him out of worry. “Don’t do anything silly. Watch to the end first; there might be more to the situation.”","Zu An mustered his courage to look at the screen in the sky. A white glow suddenly enveloped the Mermaid Queen, and her fall suddenly stopped. Instead, she began floating upward. Feng Meng was overjoyed. He flew over to capture her, only for the white light to jolt him away. An ethereal melody played from the sky as flower petals and divine light fell on the Mermaid Queen. That added an air of divinity to her already gorgeous self.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain exclaimed, “She’s ascending to immortality! And it looks like a high-tier ascension.”","“Ascending to immortality?” Zu An’s eyes reddened as he finally saw a sliver of hope.","“Indeed. There are other ways to achieve immortality aside from overcoming a heavenly tribulation, such as consuming potent world herbs. That immortal medicine was innately born, and it is without doubt one of the most potent herbs in the world. It helped her ascend straight to immortality.”","Zu An stared at the screen.","The Mermaid Queen continued ascending. Feng Meng, hindered by the laws of heaven, could only watch in frustration as she ascended. A moon suddenly appeared in the sky and welcomed the Mermaid Queen into it.","Zu An’s expression turned weird. He suddenly recalled the poem ‘Chang’e should regret stealing the spirit medicine, with her forlorn heart consoled only by blue sky and emerald sea.’","He hadn’t expected the Mermaid Queen to become the real Chang’e, and he wouldn’t have expected there to be such a background story to Chang’e stealing the spirit medicine and ascending to the moon."]},{"number":2642,"title":"Chapter 2642: Chapter 2594: Exchanging Hearts","paragraphs":["Zu An continued staring at the screen in the sky.","After the Mermaid Queen ascended, Feng Meng spent a while venting his anger before leaving in frustration. Wu Mountain reverted to normal, and nothing else happened afterward.","Zu An was infuriated. That Feng Meng deserves to die!","But now wasn’t the time to settle the score yet. He had to first look for the Mermaid Queen on the moon.","“Where’s the moon?” Zu An asked the Goddess of Wu Mountain. Unlike on Earth, the moon in this world wasn't a planetary body floating in the universe. Similar to how Xihe, the mother of the ten suns, lived in the Scalding Valley, the moon existed in a physical location too.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain spent a moment in thought before replying, “I remember there being a place called the Frost Palace at a remote location in the Celestial Court...”","Zu An nodded in comprehension. The Frost Palace was likely where the moon was, so he began to set off.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain advised him, “A war is raging right now, and there is currently unrest in the Celestial Court. It’ll be extremely risky to head over right now.”","Zu An replied, “I have to make the trip no matter how risky it is. I can’t let her stay there alone.”","He had already shot down the suns. What was there to fear from the moon?","Seeing that he had made up his mind, the Goddess of Wu Mountain said, “Give me a moment.”","She took out a jade bottle and pointed it at the sky. Shortly after, a droplet of moon-white fluid descended from the fog. Zu An widened his eyes at the familiar fluid. “That’s the teardrop from the Mermaid Queen!”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain nodded as she stowed the droplet into her jade bottle. This was the teardrop shed by the Mermaid Queen out of extreme sorrow when she thought that she would never meet Zu An ever again.","“So this is how the Defying Spirit Tear is formed.” Ji Xiaoxi, as a medical expert, swiftly noticed the extraordinariness of the teardrop. “But it’s lacking something.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain had a worried frown. “We’ll go with you.”","Zu An hesitated but didn’t turn her down. He was worried that if he left them here, another Feng Meng could appear to harm the ladies. So, he quickly made his way to the sacred tree Jianmu with the ladies.","After Zhuanxu severed heaven from earth, this was the only remaining road to the Celestial Court. If one were to simply fly upward, one would only reach outer space and not the Celestial Court.","It didn’t take long for them to return to Jianmu, only to find the passageway sealed. It turned out that after regaining control of the Celestial Court, Zhuanxu had decided to temporarily seal the tree's passage to safeguard against retaliation from Dijun’s subordinates.","Zu An’s heart sank. He hadn’t expected such a thing to happen. I shouldn’t have left the Celestial Court so quickly! But then again, he wouldn’t have known about the Mermaid Queen’s plight if he hadn’t returned to Wu Mountain.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain consoled Zu An, “You don’t need to be too worried. The Frost Palace should be far from the war between the Shamans and the Fiends, so Miss Chang’e is at least safe for the time being.”","Zu An knew that too; it was just that he felt terrible not knowing when the two of them could reunite. He said, “Since I can’t meet her for the time being, I’ll first settle my scores.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was worried. “There appears to have been someone behind Feng Meng. Feng Meng is already formidable as he is; his master is bound to be even more so.”","“I already have a rough idea who it is.” Zu An recalled the words Xihe had secretly told him while they were embracing. The doubts he had were slowly unraveling.","“Big brother Zu, I’ll go with you,” Xie Daoyun said. Now that she had made huge advancements in her cultivation, she was confident that she would be able to help.","“I’ll go too.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain was worried about leaving him be.","“I want to go too!” Ji Xiaoxi raised her hand.","Zu An burst into laughter. “You're severely injured, and your soul is impaired. How can you come with me when you’re already struggling as it is?”","Ji Xiaoxi stuck out her tongue and murmured wretchedly, “I’m so useless that I can’t help big brother Zu at all.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain argued, “It’s too dangerous for you to go alone.”","Zu An pondered briefly before nodding. “You’re right. Let’s return to Wu Mountain first. We need to make some preparations.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was hugely relieved to see that he was no longer planning to move recklessly. “All right.”","Xie Daoyun frowned at the sight. Zu An’s proposal to return to Wu Mountain was so smooth that it almost sounded as if that was his home. She had been watching the situation all along, so she was aware of how the two of them had become acquainted.","She still remembered how cold the Goddess of Wu Mountain was when they first met. When did they become so close?","...","The group made their way back to Wu Mountain. Due to her weak soul, Ji Xiaoxi soon fell asleep.","Xie Daoyun told Zu An about what happened after she was transported away by the Nature Jade Plate and unwittingly became the Fiend races’ Saintess Yumen Beiqing. Similarly, she also learned about what had happened recently from Zu An.","She wanted to continue chatting with Zu An, but her soul was also shaken from being possessed by Xihe. Before she knew it, she had also fallen asleep in her lover’s arms.","Zu An carried her to a room and placed her down. He considered lying down too, but he couldn’t sleep at all. Too many things had happened recently. He went out to the cliff where the Mermaid Queen had jumped down from. He looked at the bright moon in the sky. Gong Suyin must be feeling lonely there.","He felt bitter regret at how he had initially avoided her despite her determined advances.","“Are you thinking about Miss Chang’e?” the Goddess of Wu Mountain asked gently from behind.","Zu An turned around. Under the cold moonlight, the Goddess of Wu Mountain looked ravishing. “Goddess, you haven’t gone to sleep yet?”","“Don’t call me 'goddess'. Call me Yaoji instead.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain blinked. “We are friends, aren’t we?”","Zu An understood what she was getting at and replied, “My real name is Zu An.”","“I know.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain chuckled. She tidied up her skirt before sitting down beside him.","“You know?”","“The ladies around you have been calling you big brother Zu. I’m not a fool.”","Zu An felt apologetic. “I’m sorry. I didn’t mean to deceive you.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain wasn’t bothered by it. She looked at the moon in the sky and asked, “Miss Chang’e probably isn’t Chang’e either, right? I recall you all calling her the Mermaid Queen?”","“Indeed...” Zu An thought about how they had been through so many life-and-death situations, realizing that it would be heartless for him to continue putting distance between them. Thus, he decided to tell her the truth about their backgrounds.","“I see. You aren’t from this period in spacetime...” The Goddess of Wu Mountain lowered her head contemplatively. The anomalies she had noticed finally made sense, and it made her realize why a droplet was missing from the Defying Spirit Tear...","Zu An wanted to apologize again when the Goddess of Wu Mountain raised her head and looked at him with her beautiful, starry eyes. “Big brother Zu, can you tell me more about you and Miss Pei?”","Zu An was taken aback. He hadn’t expected her to make such a request. I guess she must be curious, given how much they resemble each other.","Thus, he told her how he first met Pei Mianman and everything that had happened afterward.","When she heard about the decades they had spent as a couple in the Yinxu dungeon, the Goddess of Wu Mountain blushed. It reminded her of what she had seen not long ago in an illusion.","Was that really an illusion..."]},{"number":2643,"title":"Chapter 2643: Chapter 2595: I’m the Kind to Exact Vengeance","paragraphs":["Zu An was perplexed by the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s particular interest in the Yinxu dungeon. He tried asking about it, but she refused to answer. She simply looked away with flushed cheeks and evasive eyes. Despite being confused, he still told her everything he knew. Of course, he wasn’t so tactless as to carelessly reveal insider details about the time he spent with Manman.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was extremely curious about that, but how was she supposed to ask about that? She could only ask details about the Yinxu dungeon to corroborate the illusion she'd seen back then.","A long time later, she remarked, “Xihe said that I could be Miss Pei’s previous incarnation. Do you believe that?”","Zu An chuckled. “Yes and no.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was confused. “Ah?”","“I believe it because the two of you are identical. That’s why I mistook you for her the first time we met. It would be too much of a coincidence to say that there's no connection between the two of you. However, I also don’t believe it because your personalities are drastically different. You’re cool and graceful, while Manman is as passionate as fire.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s eyes drooped. “You must find me too cold.”","“That’s not it. I have met women whose personalities resemble yours, such as Chu...” Zu An’s smile suddenly stiffened up. It didn’t seem like a wise idea to talk about other women in front of a woman.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain teased him. “You’re indeed a player.”","Zu An felt awkward. “It’s not what you think...” But he had no idea how he could explain it.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain didn’t harp on this topic. “Do you prefer ladies who are cooler or more passionate?”","Zu An was stunned. For a moment, he couldn’t tell whether she was asking him to compare between Chuyan and Manman or her and Manman... However, he reacted quickly. “Only children do multiple choice questions. Adults take it all.”","It wasn't a direct answer, but it still said it all.","“You’re so sly.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain regretted the question as soon as she blurted it. She had no idea what prompted her to ask such a question. Is it because he’s fated to leave this world?","His answer was just nice. It didn’t make her feel awkward or uncomfortable.","Just like that, they sat by the cliff shoulder beside shoulder and chatted for a long time...","After several days of rest and recuperation, the ladies made huge strides in their recovery. Even Ji Xiaoxi was much more spirited than before.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain asked, “Where do you intend to head next?”","“Taoqiu!”","“The human race’s capital?” The Goddess of Wu Mountain was taken aback. Zu An had been gathering information about the human race in recent days, but she didn’t expect that to be his next destination.","“I need the Human World’s power insignia, so I have to pay a visit to the human race.” Zu An didn’t explain any further. He had planned to leave the three ladies here, but now that they had recovered, they insisted on tagging along.","Zu An didn’t turn them away. He grabbed them and began making his way to Taoqiu. He had already figured out the directions there over the last few days. This world was massive, but with his Rainbow Morph, it didn’t take him long to reach Taoqiu. Unlike the humble tribes he had seen before, Taoqiu was already taking the shape of a city. It even had city walls.","In this era, most humans wore straw clothes and grass skirts. Some of them even just went around nude, except for some leaves covering their genitals. In contrast, Taoqiu’s populace was clothed, albeit in rough and crude clothes. Nevertheless, hints of the future prosperity of the human civilization could already be seen here.","“So this was how human civilization came to be.” Ji Xiaoxi was awed. As a human, she felt proud to see how this city was slowly becoming more prosperous.","Xie Daoyun also observed the city in excitement. This was a rare glimpse into history.","“What a pity we’re here as enemies,” Zu An remarked with a sigh.","Ji Xiaoxi and Xie Daoyun were stunned.","Even the Goddess of Wu Mountain was baffled. You’re a human too! Did you come here to massacre your ancestors?!","Zu An was not here to deal with the ordinary humans. Instead, he took a deep breath and roared, “Feng Meng, get out here!”","His voice boomed thunderously across the city.","The humans were horrified. Some warriors rushed out with their weapons.","“Who dares to cause trouble...” Some warriors rushed out with their weapons and glared at the group in animosity... although that lessened when they saw how ravishing Xie Daoyun, Ji Xiaoxi, and the Goddess of Wu Mountain were. “What do you want? Feng Meng is the hero of our human race!”","Zu An frowned. He roared once more, “Feng Meng, are you going to hole yourself up like a tortoise?”","The warriors were infuriated. They angrily criticized Zu An for his disrespect.","Zu An received a huge influx of Rage points, but his calm gaze remained fixed on a specific direction in the city.","There was a burst of white light, and an arrow appeared before him the next instant. It was so fast that the three women beside him didn’t even have time to warn him to be careful.","However, the arrow stopped in front of Zu An, unable to advance any further, as he'd caught it with two fingers.","The human warriors gasped. They hadn’t expected the intruder to catch Feng Meng’s divine arrow so easily. What’s his background?","Feng Meng appeared on the city wall. He was taken aback to see Zu An. “It’s you.”","Without any hesitation, Zu An drew the Sun Slaying Bow and shot an arrow at him.","Feng Meng was startled, but he quickly nocked his bow and retaliated with an arrow of his own.","His archery was indeed formidable; his arrow accurately struck the one Zu An shot. This brought a hint of glee to his lips. However, his smile soon froze in place when Zu An’s arrow split his arrow into halves before whizzing toward him. The arrow was moving so fast that he had no time to dodge.","Just then, a saber suddenly appeared out of nowhere and hacked down on the arrow, changing its trajectory.","Feng Meng snapped out of his daze and hurriedly dodged to the side, but the arrow still scraped his arm. There was a burst of bloody mist as the arrow’s sheer momentum ripped off his arm.","A woman beside him quickly fed him a pill. “Eat it!”","Feng Meng quickly popped down the pill. The stump of his ripped arm began wriggling as another arm swiftly sprouted out. However, his complexion remained awful. I didn’t expect a mere scrape to result in such a severe injury.","The brawny, saber-wielding man looked at Zu An in astonishment, too. “It hasn’t been long since we parted ways. How did you become so strong?”","“It has been a while, Lord of Slaughter, and...” Zu An’s gaze fell on Salamay."]},{"number":2644,"title":"Chapter 2644: Chapter 2596: Courting Death","paragraphs":["Salamay chuckled. “It has been a while, young master. You’re still as dashing as ever.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain, Ji Xiaoxi, and Xie Daoyun frowned upon hearing her laughter. Her way of speaking is so detestable.","Zu An looked around and noticed someone missing. “Where’s Princess Suolun?”","“Tsk tsk tsk. The princess will be moved to know that you’re so concerned about her.” Salamay shook her head. “But shouldn’t you show concern to me too, young master? How heartless!”","Zu An harrumphed. “It hasn’t been that long, but you have changed.”","“Changed? Am I more beautiful than before?” Salamay asked.","“You’ve become cheap.”","“...” Salamay’s smile froze on the spot.","You have successfully trolled Salamay for +444... +444... +444...","The smiles didn’t disappear. In this case, they merely moved from Salamay’s face to Ji Xiaoxi and the others.","Seeing his daughter getting humiliated, the Lord of Slaughter harrumphed in anger. “Brat, you’re courting death!”","He stomped his feet, causing the ground to shake. He leaped into the air and unleashed terrifying saber ki on Zu An.","The humans on the city wall, despite being a far distance away, couldn’t withstand the terrifying pressure and fell paralyzed on their butts. Their weapons scattered all over the ground.","Zu An drew the Sun Slaying Bow and shot an arrow. It pierced right through the Lord of Slaughter’s saber ki and accurately struck his saber.","Ding!","A piercing sound rang out, and the Lord of Slaughter was sent flying. His arm was numb, and he stared at his saber in shock. It was cracked.","This put him in a terrible mood. He had already returned to his peak, and several fortuitous encounters had further raised his fighting prowess. On top of that, Salamay had shared with him how Zu An defeated the Monster Lord back then, which gave him a good grasp of Zu An’s skills. Given that Zu An’s cultivation was beneath his, as long as he leveraged on his own strengths, he should have been able to pull off an easy victory against the latter. He hadn’t expected to suffer such a huge setback right from the get-go.","“Be careful of his bow. That’s Suzeng, a divine weapon that can even shoot down the suns in the sky,” Feng Meng warned.","The Lord of Slaughter was appalled. He had seen Zu An use this bow before, but never had it displayed might comparable to what shot the suns down earlier. He was glad Zu An had opted for rapid fire instead of going for a full power shot, or else that earlier arrow could have claimed his life.","“Don’t you pride yourself on being the number one archer? Why don’t we compete on those terms?” Zu An sneered as he shot another arrow at Feng Meng.","Feng Meng took in the earlier lesson and didn’t dare to let his guard down. He rapidly fired three arrows, each one accurately striking the heads of Zu An’s arrows to neutralize their force.","In the meantime, the Lord of Slaughter used the chance to charge at Zu An like a cannonball.","However, the Goddess of Wu Mountain gently moved her fingers, and layers of rippling water suddenly blocked his path. This caused the Lord of Slaughter’s movements to slow as if he was trapped in a bog.","In the meantime, Xie Daoyun channeled her talismans. Two massive golden-armored warriors descended from the sky. One held the Lord of Slaughter down, and the other swung his massive axe down on the latter’s head.","The Lord of Slaughter roared. He transformed into his true body, enlarging into a humongous dinosaur monster that towered over the others. He knocked down a golden-armored warrior with a kick, before brandishing his saber to slice the other one in half.","The golden-armored warrior who was knocked down tried to return to his feet, only for the Lord of Slaughter to raise his massive foot and stamp down on the former's head.","Pu!","The golden-armored warrior’s head burst like a watermelon, and his figure dissipated.","These kills drew out the Lord of Slaughter’s bloodthirst. He raised his neck upward and unleashed a terrifying roar.","The humans spectating the battle were so intimidated by the roar that some even pissed their pants. This was natural fear they felt toward their nemesis.","“Monster! He’s a monster!”","“He isn’t a human!”","“What kind of monstrosity is he?!”","...","A few human warriors had still been planning to aid the Lord of Slaughter, but the sight of his true form caused their feet to halt in place. Some even retreated out of fear.","The Lord of Slaughter’s eyes reddened. These lowly, reprehensible humans! Just wait till I subdue Zu An; I’ll surely capture some to have a taste! Fine, in light of that lord, I’ll just gobble up a thousand of you. He shouldn’t punish me if it’s only to this extent.","Many more hands suddenly sprouted out of Feng Meng’s body, and his bow seemed to clone itself as well. He began firing arrows at Zu An like a gatling gun, not giving the latter any time to rest while buying time for the Lord of Slaughter to approach him.","The Lord of Slaughter understood the intent and charged toward Zu An. The next moment, however, the sky abruptly darkened, and a purple sea of lightning instantly enveloped him.","It was the High Firmament Talisman!","Despite the Lord of Slaughter’s resilient body, the ferocious purple lightning still had him screaming in pain. As this world was rich in natural ki, the prowess of heavenly lightning was far stronger compared to other worlds.","“You lowly slut! How dare you!” Salamay roared as she charged at Xie Daoyun with a dagger.","Xie Daoyun was startled. She was too busy channeling the High Firmament Talisman to dodge.","“I won’t allow you to hurt big sister Xie!” Ji Xiaoxi suddenly cried out as she sprayed a black fog at the incoming Salamay.","Salamay’s plan was to endure the poison fog and first get rid of Xie Daoyun. Since Ji Xiaoxi's cultivation was only on the level of Taoqiu’s ordinary warriors, Salamay didn't think she was a threat. Furthermore, she always carried a couple of defensive artifacts with her.","It was only upon coming into contact with the black fog that she realized how grievous of a mistake she had made. Her protective artifacts enveloped her with protective light barriers, but all of them shattered as soon as they came into contact with the fog. She felt an excruciating pain assaulting her, and that prompted her to quickly retreat.","“GAHHH! MY FACE!” Salamay retreated while clawing at her face. It didn’t take long before her beautiful features were disfigured. To make things worse, the black fog was still seeping deeper into her body. It melted her flesh and blood, revealing her white bones beneath.","This made the Lord of Slaughter roar in anger.","The spectators were horrified as well. They couldn’t believe that the sweet-looking, frail lady would employ such a terrifying poison.","Ji Xiaoxi was stunned too. She quickly tossed a porcelain bottle over. “Here, hurry up and take the antidote.”","As a renowned physician, she had previously concocted medicine to suppress her body’s poison. At the same time, she also controlled the black fog to leave Salamay’s body.","Without any hesitation, Salamay grabbed the porcelain bottle and downed its contents. Her frenzy gradually receded as the medicine took effect. With her formidable recovery prowess, she swiftly regrew her flesh and skin. However, perhaps due to the poison seeping in too deeply, all kinds of warts and scars were left on her beautiful face, making her look hideous.","“You bitch! I’ll murder you!” Salamay glared at Ji Xiaoxi with venomous eyes. She had never expected to suffer such a setback in the latter’s hands.","“S-Sorry...” Ji Xiaoxi profusely apologized, not having expected Salamay to end up like that.","Zu An was speechless How can anyone be this kind? If the situation was reversed, there’s no way Salamay would spare her.","He turned toward the city and shouted, “You’re still holding out. Are you planning to watch as they march to their deaths here?”","After saying his piece, Zu An shot a gleaming arrow that easily dispersed Feng Meng’s exaggerated arrow rain. The arrow whizzed onward with unabated momentum to shatter Feng Meng’s bow before pinning him against the city wall."]},{"number":2645,"title":"Chapter 2645: Chapter 2597: Motive","paragraphs":["Feng Meng was flabbergasted. He had neutralized Zu An’s arrow with three arrows earlier, so he thought he could catch Zu An off guard by firing many arrows at once. He hadn't thought Zu An could unravel his arrow rain with just a single arrow!","Was he toying with me earlier?","The arrow forcefully pinned him to the city wall, and the excruciating pain nearly caused him to pass out. He tried raising his hand to pluck out the arrow, but he couldn’t muster the strength. He finally understood how the Golden Crows felt when being shot down.","It was a terrifying feat, considering how Zu An hadn’t taken his time to build up energy for this arrow, and the earlier arrow rain had weakened the arrow’s might by at least half. If not for that, it would have torn Feng Meng apart.","Salamay could no longer be counted on in this situation. She had just clawed her face apart and was now glaring at Ji Xiaoxi with venomous eyes.","As for the Lord of Slaughter, he had finally struggled free of the purple lightning storm, but he was in terrible shape. His body was charred black, and his red flesh could be seen through his cracked skin. Smoke was rising from his body. He smelled so delicious that a few people gulped.","That further angered the Lord of Slaughter. How dare these ants think of eating me?!","But he didn’t dare to charge in recklessly anymore. With Feng Meng incapacitated, it would be suicidal for him to continue the fight.","Zu An paid no heed to the Lord of Slaughter; his eyes were focused on the city. Seeing no one was coming out, he shot another arrow at Feng Meng. This is the culprit who caused the Mermaid Queen to ascend to the Frost Palace. I’ll exact vengeance for her.","Feeling the devastating energy harnessed in that arrow, Feng Meng’s every cell frenziedly screamed at him to dodge the attack. However, he was pinned to the city wall and was unable to move at all. He could only watch as death encroached on him. He cried, “Save me, master!”","A divine light descended and knocked away the arrow at the last moment.","Feng Meng felt his crotch turning wet, but he felt no shame at all; only relief. I’m glad that master intervened. I should be able to survive this ordeal now.","A figure emerged from the city’s skyline and leisurely approached Zu An a step at a time.","“Emperor Yao!” The humans in the city kneeled and kowtowed to the figure.","Zu An assessed the humans; there was no fear on their faces. They hadn't been coerced into worshipping him. Their respect for him came from the bottom of their hearts.","The figure landed on the city wall as he asked, “Isn’t it too much for you to come to Taoqiu to kill my people?”","He had a squarish face, thick eyebrows, and deep eyes. He naturally commanded authority when he spoke.","“Is he one of your people too?” Zu An glanced at the monstrous-looking Lord of Slaughter.","Emperor Yao’s expression stiffened. It took a while before he recovered and asked, “Why have you come to Taoqiu to cause trouble?”","“You’re asking why?” Zu An sneered. He pointed at Feng Meng and scoffed, “Not too long ago, that fellow went after my friend. You were the one who ordered him to do so, Emperor Yao, so why are you feigning ignorance?”","“I don’t know what you’re talking about.” Emperor Yao didn’t seem surprised that Zu An knew his identity. He gestured for the human warriors to seek refuge in the city.","The human warriors insisted on fighting alongside him, to which Emperor Yao replied with a chuckle, “They are very powerful. You’ll only lose your life in vain if you remain here. Besides, there might not necessarily be a fight between us.”","Upon hearing those words, the human warriors finally retreated into the city. There were no longer any humans in the city gates’ vicinity.","Zu An frowned. “Are you roleplaying a good ruler in front of me?”","“You’re overthinking it. Since they worship me as the Human Emperor, I am obliged to protect them well. It has nothing to do with you,” Emperor Yao replied calmly.","“You put on a righteous face in front of them, but do they know about your despicable deeds?” Zu An sneered.","“Despicable deeds? What do you mean?” Emperor Yao chuckled, unfazed by Zu An’s accusations.","“You orchestrated the war between the Fiends and the Shamans, didn’t you?” Zu An glared at Emperor Yao.","“Nonsense. Who doesn’t know that Emperor Jun is the mastermind behind the war between the Shamans and the Fiends? What does this have to do with me?” Emperor Yao shrugged. The faint smile on his lips hinted at his interest in this conversation.","“Yes, Emperor Jun’s ambitions played a huge part. He secretly forged the Myriad Souls Banner, collected souls from all over the world, and even killed and possessed the ten Golden Crows. However, you have also been actively pushing things along,” Zu An sneered.","“Take the events at Zhong Mountain, for instance; Zhuanxu sacrificed his grandson to sever heaven from earth. That should have suppressed the conflict between the Shamans and the Fiends, but shortly after, Nuba began publicly cursing Emperor Jun, demanding he reveal himself.","“Emperor Jun had carried out his plans covertly. Nuba wouldn’t have figured out the truth so quickly if someone hadn’t tipped her off. Due to Nuba’s relentless actions, Emperor Jun had no choice but to accelerate his plans and bring the ten suns out to devastate the world.”","Emperor Yao calmly replied, “It’s only normal for Nuba to seek vengeance for her son in a fit of anger. Besides, if not for my reminder, Emperor Jun wouldn’t have been forced to put his plans into motion in a rush. More people would have died if he had more time to prepare.” He turned to Ji Xiaoxi and added, “This lady would have also become a part of the Myriad Souls Banner if not for my reminder. You should be thanking me for that.”","Zu An was rendered speechless. Emperor Yao made so much sense that he couldn’t retort against that.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain asked, “Yao, isn’t Emperor Jun your father? I don’t understand why you did all this.”","“Emperor Jun is a womanizer. I am but one of his many sons. My mother was a rag to him—to be used and thrown away—and she died lamenting her fate. That made him pay even less attention to me.” Emperor Yao chuckled self-deprecatingly. “But I am thankful for that, or else I could have ended up in the same plight as the ten Golden Crows.”","“Did you foil his plan out of hatred?” The Goddess of Wu Mountain nodded in realization.","To her surprise, Emperor Yao harrumphed in disdain. “Don’t take me to be that shallow. Ultimately, his deeds were reprehensible. Anyone with a conscience would do everything they could to stop him.”","He spoke with an air of righteousness, which made him look bigger than before. Even the Goddess of Wu Mountain had a better impression of him.","But Zu An coldly pointed out, “You could have publicly exposed him if you wished to stop him, but you quietly supported his ploy instead. I was perplexed about your aim all along, but it finally made sense when I saw how much the human race respected you.","“Emperor Jun sought to obliterate the shamans so the fiends could monopolize the world. He attempted to attain Sainthood through accomplishing this unprecedented deed.","“And yet, your gaze was set further ahead. You wished to use the war between the shamans and the fiends to stage the downfall of the two races, so the human race could rise through the ranks and prosper. Your goal was to attain Sainthood through your merit as the Human Emperor.”"]},{"number":2646,"title":"Chapter 2646: Chapter 2598: Frenzy","paragraphs":["“Attain Sainthood?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain and the others widened their eyes in realization. Zu An’s words cleared up all their doubts.","Even the Lord of Slaughter and Feng Meng nodded in agreement. They had known all along that their master was plotting something, but they had no idea what his ultimate goal was.","Emperor Yao looked at Zu An with approving eyes. “You’re indeed smart to have guessed my motive. It’s no surprise you were able to foil Emperor Jun's scheme and even win his wife over in bed.”","He seemed to respect Zu An more because of the latter than the former. Perhaps due to his mother’s plight, Zu An and Xihe’s scandal made him feel vindicated.","The other ladies looked at Zu An with bizarre gazes.","Zu An said, “...Please don’t talk nonsense. Xihe and I have a clear conscience. Our relationship is nowhere as dirty as you put it out to be.”","Emperor Yao burst into laughter, but he couldn’t be bothered to argue. “Yes, my goal was to use the rise of the human race to attain Sainthood. Everyone has their way of attaining Sainthood; no path is superior to the other. If anything, you should be thankful to me.”","“I should be thankful to you?” Zu An snorted in contempt.","“Of course!” Emperor Yao replied proudly. “Look at the human race. They are weak, foolish, and backward. But you and your friends... You are charming and strong, despite being human too. This proves my path is right. The human race will prosper in the future. As someone who has benefited from my efforts, shouldn’t you be thankful to me?”","Zu An frowned. Emperor Yao’s words made sense. If not for Emperor Yao, the human race wouldn't have prospered, and Zu An and his friends could have never come into existence either. Still, he said, “That doesn’t change the fact that you killed so many beings to fulfill your greed.”","Emperor Yao shook his finger. “You have two things wrong. One, it was not I, but Emperor Jun who killed those beings. Two, my actions were not to fulfill my greed but for the greater good. More beings would have died in Emperor Jun's hands if not for my intervention.”","Zu An and the others exchanged looks. They knew that Emperor Yao was twisting the narrative, but there was some sense in his words, making it hard to refute his points.","“That’s why we aren’t enemies.” Emperor Yao chuckled upon seeing their faces. “I’m not afraid of you, but there is no reason for us to fight. Even if you defeat and kill me, that will affect the future. The basis of your existence might cease to be.”","Zu An took a deep breath. Considering all the records about Emperor Yao in human history, he knew it was unwise to make a move against the other party here.","Besides, given that this was a turning point in history, it was unlikely Zu An could touch Emperor Yao even if he gave it everything he had, similar to how Xihe couldn’t stop the simultaneous appearance of the ten suns and the subsequent downfall of the nine suns no matter how she tried.","So, Zu An pointed to Feng Meng and asked, “Why did you send him to harm Chang’e, if we aren’t enemies as you said?”","Emperor Yao frowned. “I only ordered him to retrieve the immortal medicine. I didn’t expect him to act on his own accord out of lust for Chang’e.”","Feng Meng panicked. “Master, I have served you with devotion over the years. You have to save me!”","Emperor Yao’s expression turned cold. “You should have known such a day would come when you used my name to commit such outrageous deeds. I have already saved you several times now. Who was the one who healed your soul when you were on the verge of death?”","Feng Meng knew he couldn’t count on Emperor Yao anymore, so he turned into countless black little pigs and escaped in all directions. This was his escape method; it was the tactic he'd used to escape last time. He would suffer a grievous loss that would take a long time to recover, but at least he would be alive.","The Lord of Slaughter was taken aback. Even Emperor Yao was surprised. He hadn't expected Feng Meng to be so decisive.","But Zu An reacted right away. His aura had always been locked onto the culprit who caused him and the Mermaid Queen to be ‘eternally separated’. He shot an arrow via the Sun Slaying Bow, and the arrow exploded mid-flight into a massive rain of golden arrows that covered everything within a radius of five kilometers.","Boom!","Countless black pigs squealed as they were killed by the arrow rain. A massive pit over fifty meters deep was left in the wake of the arrows. The nearby city wall also collapsed as a result. It was fortunate Emperor Yao had ordered his men to retreat into the city, or else they could have been implicated in this.","Sensing that Feng Meng’s soul had been thoroughly destroyed by this assault, the Lord of Slaughter gulped and reflexively retreated. The Sun Slaying Bow was too scary; he wasn’t confident he could deal with it. Sensing Zu An’s gaze falling on him, he hurriedly retreated to Emperor Yao’s side. “Master!”","It had previously filled him with shame and anger to call Emperor Yao ‘master’, but he was now saying it on his own volition. He knew that was the only way he could preserve his life.","Emperor Yao looked conflicted. He debated whether to protect the Lord of Slaughter or not.","Just then, Salamay shouted, “Hmph! Let us go right now, or else it’ll be the end of this lass!” She had slipped back into the city during the chaos and returned with Suolun Shi as a hostage.","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief when he saw that Suolun Shi was still alive. “It’s a relief that you’re fine.”","“Big brother Zu...” Suolun Shi was ashamed. Zu An had entrusted her to guard the prisoners, but she'd foolishly fallen for Salamay’s tricks and ended up becoming the prisoner herself.","“It’s up to you to decide whether she’ll escape unscathed or not.” Salamay pressed her knife tightly against Suolun Shi’s neck. “Do you know why she released us in the first place?”","“Why?” Zu An and the others were curious to know how Salamay and the others escaped.","“Don’t say it!” Suolun Shi exclaimed with a reddened face. She even attempted to charge forward to let the knife slit her neck.","But Salamay had been on guard against that. She stopped Suolun Shi by grabbing her vitals before continuing with a smirk, “It’s because she wants your love, but she knows she’s nothing compared to your lovers. With such an inner demon, it wasn't too difficult for us to convince her.”","Despair filled Suolun Shi’s eyes. She would rather die than confront this moment. She lowered her head, not daring to face Zu An.","Zu An gently spoke up. “Princess Suoluo is beautiful, kind, and has a powerful background. Which man wouldn’t like her? You merely took advantage of her lack of worldly experience.”","Light returned to Suolun Shi’s eyes. She could tell that Zu An didn’t truly like her, but his willingness to console and preserve her dignity was more than enough to move her.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain stared at Zu An. No wonder he has so many women by his side. With a mouth a sweet as his, which woman wouldn’t fall for him?","But those words greatly triggered Salamay. “Fine, fine. She lacks worldly experience, but I’m sly and scheming. Since that’s the case, you can regret it for the rest of your life!”","Her face distorted in frenzy. She knew that their only way out of this was to continue holding Suolun Shi as a hostage, but she couldn’t control her emotions at all. Anger and killing intent poured out from her heart. Let everything go to ruin then!","She unhesitatingly slit Suolun Shi’s neck.","“NO!” The Lord of Slaughter panicked, knowing they would be doomed if they lost the hostage. My daughter is usually smarter than this. What happened?","Zu An also hadn’t expected her to go berserk. It was already too late for him to stop her.","Just then, Salamay’s body stiffened. She gurgled, and fresh blood spurted out of her mouth.","She looked down and saw a spear conjured from flames piercing through her chest. She turned around with great difficulty and saw a man covered in flames."]},{"number":2647,"title":"Chapter 2647: Chapter 2599: The Final Power Insignia","paragraphs":["“Wuhui?” Salamay had been in this world for some time now. While serving Emperor Yao, she'd consciously tried to gather information about the powerhouses in this world. She needed to know who could and couldn't be trifled with. She'd even considered exploiting the conflicts between the powerhouses to free herself from Emperor Yao’s slavery.","Fire Celestial Wuhui was a renowned expert in this world, and he fell into the category that she couldn’t mess with. She couldn’t comprehend why Wuhui would suddenly attack her when there was no grudge between them.","Everything only clicked when she noticed Yun Yuqing standing behind Wuhui. Her eyes brimmed with indignation. Why can others always find such a strong and loyal backing? The Incestuous King was devoted to me but he was weak, wher eas Emperor Yao is strong but isn’t willing to stand up for me.","Why?! Why do others have such a good life when mine is so tough?!","She wanted to vent the seething anger from life’s injustices with a roar, but Wuhui’s fire spear had already claimed her life. Her body collapsed to the floor. Her eyes remained wide, but the light in them had been extinguished.","“My daughter!” The infuriated Lord of Slaughter charged over.","A glint flashed through Wuhui’s eyes. With a flick of his wrist, his fire spear transformed into a massive fire saber. He brought it down upon the Lord of Slaughter with unstoppable momentum.","The fire saber’s terrifying aura and killing intent shocked the Lord of Slaughter, but it was already too late to back down. He mustered his courage and swung his saber with all his might.","The physical saber and the flame saber clashed. However, the former caved in and exploded into countless fragments. The flame saber continued rushing forth with unabated momentum to slice through the Lord of Slaughter’s chest.","Pu!","A bloody mist splattered. The Lord of Slaughter’s massive body collapsed.","“Hm? He’s still alive even after taking a strike from me?” Wuhui was surprised too. He brandished his flame saber once more to kill the Lord of Slaughter for good.","Yun Yuqing took this chance to transport the terrified Suolun Shi to Zu An’s side.","Zu An was overjoyed to see Yun Yuqing. “What brings you here?”","“We happened to pass by. Wuhui is in the midst of contacting the experts of this world.” The sight of her lover made Yun Yuqing’s eyes curve into beautiful crescents.","Suolun Shi further lowered her head miserably. Big brother Zu’s lovers are so beautiful and competent, whereas I only cause trouble for him.","Just then, there was another twist on the battlefield. Emperor Yao flashed over to the Lord of Slaughter’s side. He made no particular movement, but a spherical light barrier that manifested around him blocked Wuhui’s flame saber.","“Are you going to stand in my way, Yao?” Wuhui coldly asked. He had a fiery temper to match his position as the Fire Celestial.","Emperor Yao smiled. “There isn’t a grudge between you two, and he isn’t fated to meet his end here.” The latter half of the sentence was directed at Zu An.","Zu An was stunned. He knows a fair bit. “Indeed, he’s fated to meet his end in the future.”","In the future, the Lord of Slaughter would break free of his seal and go on a massacre. Qiu Honglei would be forced to perform her mysterious ritual dance to summon an enigmatic entity to subdue him. Since Qiu Honglei was already out of danger, it would be unwise to tamper with the cause and effect of the world, or else the future could be thrown into disarray.","Seeing that, Wuhui retracted his flames. “Fine, I’ll spare him then.”","The Lord of Slaughter was shocked. Wuhui surprisingly respects Zu An’s opinion. Are the two of them acquainted?","But what shocked him more was their discussion. Salamay had told him what would happen in the future. In the first place, he had come to this world in hopes of obtaining an ancient legacy to rewrite his fate. He'd thought his encounter with Emperor Yao was a blessing, as the latter could help him awaken his ancient bloodline. Little did he know that the other party had thought of him and his daughter as disposable tools all along. Despite his struggles, his fate remained unchanged.","His daughter’s death and the realization that he was helpless to change fate lifted his reservations, and he roared at Emperor Yao, “Yao, how can you just throw us aside after we did so many dirty deeds for you?! I’ll haunt you even as a ghost!”","Emperor Yao laughed. “You won’t have a chance to become a ghost.”","He tapped the Lord of Slaughter’s forehead, sending a ray of golden light into the latter’s head. The Lord of Slaughter’s angry eyes slowly lost their light before gradually closing.","Zu An was startled. “What are you doing?”","“Calm down, I didn’t kill him. I’m merely erasing his memories. I don’t think he recalls anything that happened here when you encounter him again in the future, right?” Emperor Yao smiled.","Zu An looked at Emperor Yao wryly. I bet you’re just silencing him lest he reveal the dirty things he's done for you.","But he had to concede that Emperor Yao was right. He was also worried that if the Lord of Slaughter retained his memories about this world, the latter could assassinate him as soon as he broke free of his seal.","Zu An suddenly empathized with Xihe. Fate was so powerful that it felt as if they could only be helplessly swept away by it. Somehow, fate had a way of correcting its trajectory in unexpected ways, ensuring that history aligned with the future.","“What are you doing here, Wuhui?” Emperor Yao asked.","“I was rallying the experts on earth together to investigate Dijun’s forging of the Myriad Souls Banner, but that has little meaning now that the war between the shamans and the fiends has already commenced. So, I came here to propose an alliance with the human race to deal with the shamans,” Wuhui replied.","Emperor Yao chuckled. “When did the Celestial Court start thinking so highly of the human race as to extend a hand to them?”","Wuhui harrumphed. “The human race might be insignificant, but it’s only right for them to raise their arms and fight in this tumultuous period.”","Emperor Yao reined in his smile. “That may be true, but why does the human race have to fight for your people?”","Wuhui was appalled and enraged. “The Celestial Court protected the human race over the years, and the human race worships the deities of the Celestial Court too. You yourself are from the Celestial Court, and a descendant of the Celestial Emperor no less. How can you choose to fight for the enemy?”","“But the Sshamans have also protected the human race, and the humans worship some shamans as deities too. It doesn’t seem right to choose a side.” Emperor Yao paused as he glanced at the city. “I might be from the Celestial Court, but the human race now worships me as the Human Emperor too. I cannot let down their faith in me.”","Wuhui’s expression darkened. “Are you planning to help the shamans?!”","Emperor Yao shook his head. “The human race is too weak to be caught in the war between the shamans and the fiends. We shall help neither side.”","Wuhui exhaled in relief. “Fine. Just remember your own place and fulfill your promise!”","The worst-case scenario was for the human race to side with the shamans. Compared to that, the human race taking a neutral stance was an acceptable outcome.","Wuhui still needed to recruit the other powers and bring them under the Celestial Court, so he didn’t want to waste time here. He turned to Yun Yuqing.","Yun Yuqing shuffled to Zu An’s side and said, “I want to stay with him.”","Wuhui frowned. Were it in the past, he would have never allowed someone with such pure Celestial Emperor bloodline to stay with a mortal, lest their pure bloodline be sullied. However, with the war between the shamans and the fiends intensifying, Wuhui would soon have to join the battlefield too. It would be dangerous for him to continue taking Yun Yuqing with him. So, he made sure to warn Zu An before leaving on his fire cloud.","Emperor Yao turned to Zu An and smiled. “We’re the only ones left now. Would you like to fight or not?”","Zu An was speechless. This fellow is a master of psychological warfare. My hostility toward him has mostly faded after everything he said.","More importantly, Emperor Yao was key to the human race’s future prosperity. Unpredictable things could occur if something were to happen to Emperor Yao now. Perhaps Zu An and his lovers would even cease to exist in the future.","“You’re right. There’s no reason for us to fight.”","“It’s a pleasure to communicate with a smart man. Here, I have a gift for you. You’ll probably need it.” Emperor Yao casually tossed an item over.","Zu An caught the item and inspected it. It was a staff harnessing the Human Emperor’s aura. It was the Human World’s power insignia!"]},{"number":2648,"title":"Chapter 2648: Chapter 2600: The Frost Palace’s Curse","paragraphs":["Zu An remembered that the Lord of Slaughter was the one who had brought this staff to this world. He hadn’t expected it to fall into Emperor Yao’s hands.","He found it even more surprising how easily Emperor Yao was handing it to him, especially since it harnessed the power of the Human Emperor. Becoming the Human Emperor was no easy feat; one needed to be acknowledged by the vast majority of the human race. Only Emperor Yao had the means to pull it off in this era.","“Do you know what I’m going to do?” Zu An was intrigued.","“I have a rough idea. Didn’t Zhuanxu share a sliver of his Celestial Court’s power insignia with you as well? This is the best decision we can make for the future.” Emperor Yao looked toward the battlefield where the shamans and fiends clashed with a deep look.","Zu An suddenly felt a surge of respect for Emperor Yao. The latter wasn't just the shallow schemer he'd previously thought. Emperor Yao harbored great ambitions; it was just that their paths diverged.","“I’m apologetic about what happened to Chang’e. On second thought, I’ll give you another present as a token of my sincerity.” Emperor Yao waved his hand through the air, opening a spatial rift that quickly expanded into a warp portal. Starlight shimmered across the pitch-black portal.","“This...” Zu An was surprised to sense the Celestial Court’s aura inside the gate.","“It’s a trump card I prepared back then. This portal allows me to travel between earth and heaven without passing through the South Celestial Gate. However, the severance of heaven and earth has shaken this portal too. I can only maintain it for a day.” Emperor Yao smiled. “You should need it right now.”","Zu An had to concede that Emperor Yao understood human emotions well. “Thank you.”","Emperor Yao glanced at the Lord of Slaughter, saying, “I’ll leave this to you.”","With that, he turned around and returned to the city, where he was met with the human populace’s resounding cheers.","Zu An was awed by Emperor Yao’s popularity. He glanced at Salamay’s corpse and felt wistful. Who could have known that she would meet such an end?","Considering that they were at least acquainted, he dug a simple grave for her on a distant mountain. He considered erecting a tombstone for her, but he didn’t know what to inscribe on it. Looking at the mound before him, he thought about everything she had done and sighed. “You didn’t have to put yourself through all this.”","Yun Yuqing murmured, “Big brother Zu laments whenever a beauty dies.”","Ji Xiaoxi shook her head. “Big brother Zu has always been kind-hearted.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s eyes flickered, but it was hard to tell what she was thinking.","After burying Salamay, Zu An stowed the Lord of Slaughter in his Seven-Colored Divine Halo. Following that, he turned to Xie Daoyun and said, “You’ll have to seal him away when we return to Yumen Beiqing’s spacetime fragment to close this loop.”","Xie Daoyun nodded. She had already deciphered the sealing formation; it was just that she hadn’t found a way to subdue the Lord of Slaughter thus far.","He then turned to the group and said, “I’ll send you back to Wu Mountain first before making a trip to the Celestial Court.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain frowned. She looked at the portal with worried eyes. “Be careful. It might be a trap.”","“I can sense the Celestial Court’s aura coming from the other side of the portal, so there should be nothing wrong with the destination. I also have Wu Mountain’s coordinates, so I can return if things go awry.” Zu An was confident in his odds of survival given his current strength and grasp of space.","That eased the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s worries.","Yun Yuqing was perplexed. She had asked Wuhui about the Goddess of Wu Mountain after their previous encounter, and Wuhui had told him that the Goddess of Wu Mountain was a cold and reclusive person. And yet, the Goddess of Wu Mountain allowed Zu An to freely enter and leave Wu Mountain as if it were his home.","How far have the two of them progressed?!","Zu An gently lifted the ladies with a wave of his hand before flashing back to the Wu Mountain via Rainbow Morph.","“Be careful,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain warned him. It wouldn’t be convenient for her to tag along, since he was there to look for Chang’e. The other ladies thought the same too.","However, Zu An turned to Yun Yuqing and said, “Wuhui mentioned you have the purest Celestial Court’s Fiend Bloodline. You shouldn’t miss this fortuitous encounter. I’ll bring you with me.”","Yun Yuqing was taken aback, but she happily agreed to it. Zu An’s lovers were so outstanding that it heaped a lot of pressure on her. There was no way she would miss a chance to become stronger. This would allow her to better share some of Zu An’s burdens in the future.","But most important of all, this allowed her to have some private time with Zu An.","Zu An brought Yun Yuqing back to Taoqiu’s outskirts using Rainbiw Morph.","Yun Yuqing was amazed. “Big brother Zu, you’re formidable! To think that you can cover such a huge distance in the blink of an eye.” What she enjoyed more was monopolizing big brother Zu’s hands, however.","“I was only able to return so quickly because I recorded the coordinates to this place,” Zu An explained with a smile. He confirmed the safety of Emperor Yao’s portal once more before stepping in with Yun Yuqing.","The space around them distorted. As soon as Zu An stepped out of the portal, he was faced with the celestial palace. He breathed a sigh of relief, knowing that the portal had worked.","A divine light suddenly surged out of the celestial palace, and Zhuanxu’s silhouette appeared behind the two of them. The latter was surprised to see Zu An.","Zu An was surprised too. “I only just arrived, but you've already found me?”","“I closed all the passageways leading to the Celestial Court so that the battle wouldn’t reach here. Your portal would have been hard to detect under normal circumstances, but it is exceptionally conspicuous now.” Zhuanxu was perplexed too. “How did you get here?”","Zu An made no attempt to conceal the truth for Emperor Yao. The latter was too sly. It wouldn’t be that bad for the Celestial Emperor to keep an eye on him.","“No wonder I kept sensing the traces of another enigmatic entity. So he’s the one.” Zhuanxu chuckled. “But he has helped me a fair bit this time.”","Zu An was taken aback. Di d Emperor Yao open this portal for me as a message to Zhuanxu? Now that I think about it, they have a common ene my— Emperor Jun —and an enemy’s enemy is a friend.","It feels as i f Emperor Yao had everything calculated, but I bet he didn’t expect to be sealed away by Shun in the future, while Shun is none other than Zhuanxu’s descendant.","But that was a fight between the Celestial Emperor and the Human Emperor; Zu An couldn’t be bothered to get involved. He had more important things at hand, so he told Zhuanxu about what had happened to the Mermaid Queen.","Zhuanxu did a quick calculation with his fingers. “I see... I’m afraid you will be disappointed. You won’t be able to take her away with you.”","“Why?!” Zu An was stunned. “You are the Celestial Emperor. Can’t you at least do this much?”","Zhuanxu frowned. “The Celestial Emperor has to obey the rules of nature too. Chang’e’s ascension is inscribed in fate. The Frost Palace carries an ancient curse: anyone who moves into the Frost Palace is destined to be lonely. Now that Chang’e has become one with the Frost Palace, separating her from it would only bring about her destruction. But this isn’t necessarily a bad thing. She’ll cultivate faster than anyone else in the Frost Palace...”","Zu An interjected, “What’s the point of having unparalleled cultivation when the tradeoff is a life of loneliness? Is there no solution?”","Zhuanxu briefly paused before replying, “It might be possible to do something about the Frost Palace’s curse ten thousand years from now...”","“Ten thousand years...” The thought that the Mermaid Queen had to suffer ten thousand years of loneliness made his heart lurch.","“It might not be a short time, but it isn’t a long time for a deity either,” Zhuanxu consoled him.","“Is the ten thousand years counted by the Celestial Court’s time or mortal time?” Zu An asked.","“Of course, it’s calculated by the Celestial Court’s time.”","Zu An’s heart sank. A day in heaven was equivalent to a year on earth."]},{"number":2649,"title":"Chapter 2649: Chapter 2601: Fulfilling Her Wish","paragraphs":["Zhuanxu smiled. “You don’t have to be so pessimistic. She might not be able to leave the Frost Palace, but you can drop by often to visit her. Once the war settles down and order is re-stablished, it won’t be as difficult for you to enter the Celestial Court.”","Zu An fell silent. He knew that the war between the Shamans and the Fiends would cause both races to retreat into the shadows. On top of that, Zhuanxu wouldn't necessarily be the one calling the shots in the Celestial Court by then.","Besides that, he would eventually have to leave this world. There was another world waiting to be rescued, and he also needed to complete the Six Paths of Reincarnation.","Once he left this world, the Mermaid Queen would have to spend a long time alone. Who knew whether she could endure it until their reunion?","Just then, Zhuanxu turned to Yun Yuqing and remarked, “Ah, you must be the lady Wuhui mentioned. Indeed, you have the purest Celestial Emperor bloodline. It’s a pity that you have yet to awaken your bloodline power. Child, follow me. I’ll help you awaken your bloodline.”","Yun Yuqing glanced at Zu An.","Noticing their reservation, Zhuanxu smiled. “You can say that she’s my descendant in a way. I have no reason to harm her. Awakening her bloodline power requires the invocation of ancient rituals...”","Zu An finally nodded. “Yuqing, I’ll look for you later.”","At the same time, he shot her a glance. Yun Yuqing nodded. He had given her a teleportation talisman; she could use it if she felt that she was in danger, and he would rush over.","Zhuanxu lifted Yun Yuqing onto a cloud, and the two of them flew off into the distance.","Zu An quickly made his way toward the Frost Palace. The further he flew, the colder the resplendent immortal palaces became. Even the air was no longer as sweet; it was tinged with cold as well.","A forlorn palace floated in the distance, as if signaling the world’s edge. The words on the plaque, ‘Frost Palace’, made Zu An frown. Just looking at these characters made him feel empty and cold.","He gently pushed the door open. The courtyard was barren except for a withered, ancient tree, a stark contrast to the other vibrant immortal palaces that cultivated flowers and herbs.","Zu An was perplexed. Didn’t the Frost Palace in the legends have an osmanthus tree? Could this be the osmanthus tree? But it's already withered!","Creak!","The door in front of him suddenly opened. A beautiful figure stood in the doorway, staring at him in disbelief.","“Big brother Zu?”","“Suyin!”","Even though it hadn’t been that long since they parted ways, the Mermaid Queen looked much frailer. Her eyes were red and puffy. She had to have cried a lot over the last few days.","Zu An's familiar voice made her eyes light up with joy. Unable to hold herself back anymore, she leaped into Zu An’s arms and embraced him tightly. “It really is you. It really is you...”","Her arms were wrapped around him so tightly that it hurt a little, but that only made Zu An’s heart hurt more. She'd no doubt suffered much turmoil. Zu An said, “Don’t worry, I'm here now...”","Pearls fell to the ground with crisp clacks. Zu An felt the Mermaid Queen's tears drenching his chest. He gently patted her shoulder as he said, “I know what happened. Before coming here, I killed Feng Meng to avenge you.”","“I don’t want vengeance. I just want to be with you,” the Mermaid Queen whimpered.","Zu An had never seen her so frail. She was a strong-willed woman who had mesmerized an entire world’s experts. She was mature and graceful. And yet, she was now acting like a child. This incident had undoubtedly frightened her. He recalled what Zhuanxu said earlier, and that made him feel even more awful.","The Mermaid Queen cried for a long time before gradually drifting off to sleep. Looking at her sleeping visage, Zu An gently wiped her tears and tidied up her unkempt hair. She probably hasn’t slept a wink since coming here.","He carefully carried her into the nearby room, which only contained the bare necessities—a table, a chair, and a bed. He noticed that the bed was made out of ice and frowned. He couldn’t bear to lay her on it, so he sat on the bed himself and laid her down in his embrace.","This movement, albeit gentle, caused the Mermaid Queen to jolt awake. She anxiously clutched onto Zu An’s sleeves as she exclaimed, “Don’t leave me!”","Zu An’s heart ached. He patted her head and said, “I’m here, I’m here.”","The Mermaid Queen exhaled in relief. She took a few seconds to compose herself before replying, “I’m sorry. I made a fool of myself.” Even though she had only rested briefly, she was in a much better condition than before.","“I doubt I would have fared any better than you if I were placed in the same position,” Zu An replied with a bitter smile.","“Nonsense. You’re the most incredible person I know. You always overcome the hurdles standing in your way, no matter how tall they may be. I love how you remain composed no matter how hopeless the situation looks.” The Mermaid Queen hooked her hands around Zu An's neck. There were no more tears in her eyes; only tenderness remained.","“I'm not that incredible...” Zu An replied. Just like how I have no way of rescuing you from the Frost Palace now. Unwilling to resign himself to fate, he stood up and said, “I’ll take you out of here!”","He carried the Mermaid Queen up and flew her to the South Celestial Gate. He kept a close eye on her condition and was delighted to see her safe and sound. Who in the world said she can’t leave the Frost Palace?","The Mermaid Queen guessed his thoughts and bitterly explained, “It’s futile. I’ve tried it. I can leave the Frost Palace temporarily, but I’ll find myself suddenly reappearing there shortly after.”","She vanished right after saying that. Startled, Zu An rushed back to the Frost Palace and saw her standing by the doorway, waiting for him. When she saw him, her worry faded to joy.","“There’s something amiss about this Frost Palace.” Zu An drew his Tai’e Sword and slashed the palace door. With his current cultivation and the Tai’e Sword’s prowess, he could even slice a mountain, let alone a mere palace door.","Much to his astonishment, his slash failed to slice anything off the door. Not only that; divine runes also started lighting up around the Frost Palace and a terrifying aura began to build up.","Zu An was stunned. These divine runes resembled those he had seen from the sacred tree Jianmu.","The Mermaid Queen immediately stood in front of him and protected him with both hands. “Stand down! He’s my man!”","The divine runes slowly extinguished as if they understood her words.","Zu An blinked in confusion.","The Mermaid Queen explained with a bitter smile, “After it acknowledged me as its master, I have become one with the Frost Palace. I am now the Frost Palace, and the Frost Palace is me.”","Zu An had been wondering whether to draw his Sun Slaying Bow to give it another try, but after hearing her words, he had no choice but to give up on that plan.","“Big brother Zu, you don’t need to worry about me. I understood everything from the moment the Frost Palace acknowledged me as its master. There is no way for me to leave this place.” The Mermaid Queen grabbed his hand and consoled him.","Zu An fell silent. If she'd truly come to terms with her plight, she wouldn’t have cried earlier.","“Big brother Zu, I have an unfulfilled wish. Can you help me with that?” The Mermaid Queen looked at Zu An with glistening eyes reminiscent of the evening sky’s afterglow."]},{"number":2650,"title":"Chapter 2650: Chapter 2602: A Day In Heaven, A Year On Earth","paragraphs":["“What’s your wish?” Since he couldn’t save her right away, Zu An solemnly swore to fulfill her wish no matter what it was.","The Mermaid Queen blushed, but she determinedly raised her head and looked at him with her beautiful eyes. “We have gotten married in the Chang clan, but we didn’t finish the final step.”","Zu An’s heart quivered. They had gone through all the marriage formalities that day. The only step they had stopped short of was the consummation of their marriage. He was still wondering what kind of unfulfilled wish she had, but who could have thought this would be it?","The Mermaid Queen squirmed in embarrassment. “Big brother Zu, am I shameless for asking...”","Zu An sealed her lips before she could finish her words. Her body initially stiffened up, but it soon fell limp in her lover’s embrace.","It was a long time later before their lips parted. By then, her fair complexion had already become completely red.","With a wave of her hand, ‘Blissful Marriage (囍)’ papers were plastered on the walls and windows. Red lanterns hung on the doors of the Frost Palace. The icy-cold bed was covered in a thick couple quilt. Red drapes hung over the previously monotonous bed. The once-cold room suddenly looked merry.","Zu An was amazed. After becoming an immortal, he had learned how to conjure illusions like turning stones into gold, but he could sense that the changes around him weren’t just an illusion. These additions might have appeared out of nowhere, but they were real.","The Mermaid Queen shyly said, “I can now control everything inside the Frost Palace. Do you like the decorations I have put up?”","“I love it!” Zu An embraced her tightly. All these things showed how important this was to her. It was, after all, a woman’s most important day. How could it not be important to her?","He then took out all the jeweled accessories he had stashed away in his Brilliant Glass Bead and put them on her.","“Aiyo, that’s enough! I can hardly lift my head now,” the Mermaid Queen coyly exclaimed. Zu An’s haphazard actions had resulted in her head being covered in accessories.","Looking at the mess on her head, Zu An couldn’t help but laugh. “You’re already beautiful as it is. It feels as if I've done something extraneous.”","He removed the accessories he'd placed on the Mermaid Queen before taking out a red cloth and gently placing it over her head in their place.","The Mermaid Queen’s heart quivered. She felt inexplicably nervous. Having her eyes once again covered in red reminded her of the night of her marriage at the Chang clan. She had also nervously waited for him to arrive like that, only to be met with an unfortunate outcome.","Will the same thing happen this time too?","The sight before her suddenly lit up. The red cloth had been lifted.","Zu An was dazzled by the beauty before his eyes. The Mermaid Queen was already gorgeous normally, and the redness reflected on her snowy skin only further accentuated her charms. Zu An exclaimed, “Suyin, you’re truly beautiful!”","“Are you still calling me Suyin now...” The Mermaid Queen pouted.","“My wife!”","“Hubby~”","Her exclamation of ‘hubby’ was so sweet and tender that Zu An nearly melted. He quickly grabbed two wine cups and filled them to the brim. Noticing the Mermaid Queen’s confused gaze, he explained, “This is a human tradition—cross-cupped wine. Doing it on the night of consummation signifies two individuals coming together as one.”","“We have to do it then!” The Mermaid Queen’s eyes lit up. She grabbed a wine cup and crossed her hand with Zu An’s, her gaze expectant.","Her overflowing excitement made Zu An’s heart ache. He quickly did the same too.","After downing their cross-cupped wine, the Mermaid Queen asked with a reddened face, “What do we do next?”","Zu An chuckled. “It’s now time to get down to business.”","The sudden approach of Zu An’s face caused a mini explosion in the Mermaid Queen’s head. She felt as if she was heating up from head to toe.","...","Ji Xiaoxi marveled at the rare flowers and herbs growing on Wu Mountain’s peak and remarked, “Goddess, it’s so beautiful here!”","The usually cold Goddess of Wu Mountain revealed a faint smile at her adorable gestures. “Don’t call me goddess. Call me Yaoji instead.”","“All right, big sister Yaoji.” Because of her striking resemblance to Pei Mianman, Ji Xiaoxi instinctively felt close to the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","Just then, Xie Daoyun walked over with a vibrant flower. “Xiaoxi, this is the medicine you wanted from the cliff.”","“Thank you, big sister Xie.” Ji Xiaoxi took the flower with glowing eyes.","Xie Daoyun and the Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled.","“Miss Yaoji, it's already been a month. Why isn’t big brother Zu back yet? Is he in danger?” Xie Daoyun asked worriedly. “Didn’t that man say that the teleportation formation would only last for a day?”","“With his abilities, he should be able to deal with any danger that comes his way.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain looked at the sky. “Emperor Yao said the teleportation formation only lasts a day, but a day in heaven equals a year on earth. It’s only normal for him not to be back yet.”","“Ah?” Ji Xiaoxi and Xie Daoyun were astounded. While big brother Zu spends a day in heaven, we have to wait a year for him down here?","“It’ll be a year in no time. Years would pass in a flash when I admired the fog from the mountain peak,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain said, though she was surprised to find that time seemed to pass slower now, even though she should have already grown accustomed to it.","Ji Xiaoxi and Xie Daoyun exchanged looks and stuck out their tongues. Immortals have a scary sense of time.","As the Goddess of Wu Mountain fell into a melancholic mood, the surroundings seemed to become a little heavy. Xie Daoyun decided to break the mood, asking, “Xiaoxi, why were you looking for this flower?”","“This flower is called Beauty Blood. I've only seen it in books; I didn’t expect to find it on big sister Yaoji’s Wu Mountain,” Ji Xiaoxi explained as she tore out the flower’s bright-red petals one by one, revealing a pristine jade-like fruit within.","“How beautiful!” Xie Daoyun widened her eyes.","The fruit inside was at least three shades fairer than her, and it had a form reminiscent of a beauty.","“Is it called Beauty Blood because of the flower petals’ blood-red color?”","“Both its petals and fruit can be used as medicine, but its most valuable part is still this.” Ji Xiaoxi gently pressed her fingernail against the white fruit, and a blood-red fluid flowed out from within.","“How mysterious!” Xie Daoyun remarked, but right after, she suddenly thought about something that caused her face to redden. Tsk, this flower is so inappropriate!","When she looked at the innocent Ji Xiaoxi and unfazed Goddess of Wu Mountain, however, she suddenly realized that she was the only dirty-minded one. But again, I’m the only one who is experienced among the three of us. That brought a smile to her lips, and she felt a slight sense of superiority.","Just then, the Goddess of Wu Mountain said, “You can maximize Beauty Blood’s medicinal effect if you grind the petals and fruit together.”","“Big sister, thank you for your pointer.” Ji Xiaoxi brought out her mortar and pestle to grind the petals and fruit. However, the petals and fruits remained distinct even as her forehead became slick with sweat.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain flicked her finger. A fog condensed into a droplet of water, which fell into the mortar. The petals and fruit softened up, allowing them to be ground into a bright red paste."]},{"number":2651,"title":"Chapter 2651: Chapter 2603: The Solution to Saving Her","paragraphs":["Xie Daoyun wiped away Ji Xiaoxi’s sweat before looking at the celestial palace. “I wonder how big brother Zu is faring.”","“He and Miss Chang’e must be cherishing their final moments together.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain let out a melancholy sigh as she thought about Chang’e’s plight, and by extension, her relationship with Zu An as well.","In a way, I'm in the same position as her.","Xie Daoyun sighed as well. “I hope their last moments together are happy.”","Just a moment ago, she'd been feeling impatient about having to wait a year, but the realization that Zu An and Mermaid Queen only had a day with each other made her feel sorry for them.","“I wonder what they're doing.” Ji Xiaoxi continued grinding the medicine while looking at the sky with curious eyes.","...","The Mermaid Queen felt as if she was being battered by a heavy storm.","As a member of the Ocean races, she was no stranger to storms. She'd even enjoyed diving into storms and challenging rapid tides in her younger years. No matter how intense the storm was, she could always conquer it with ease.","It was only now that she realized she had gotten ahead of herself. It turned out that there were storms in the world that were beyond her means to handle. She felt like a lone leaf floating amid choppy waters, at risk of drowning at any moment.","Thinking back on how she'd maneuvered through rapid currents back then, she tried her best to relax her body as much as possible and move along with the storm instead of opposing it.","Fortunately, heaven seemed to have detected her fear, and the wild storm died down. The sun emerged through the clouds, and a refreshing drizzle ensued. Basking under the warm sunlight felt exceptionally comfortable.","Unable to curb her emotions anymore, she tightly embraced her lover and bit his ear. “I want a child...”","Those words were as good as a war horn on the battlefield, especially when coming from a top-tier beauty. Which man could resist such a passionate confession from a woman like her?","The swaying red lanterns outside the Frost Palace seemed to say it all. The withered tree in the courtyard suddenly sprouted to life. Green leaves grew from its barren branches, and beautiful flowers blossomed. The sweet fragrance of osmanthus flowers drifted through the Frost Palace, as if reflecting the cloying sentiments between the newlyweds.","...","Some time passed. The Mermaid Queen lay on Zu An’s chest with bright-red cheeks. She reflexively twirled her hair against his chest as she said, “Hubby, you seem unhappy.”","“Ah? Do I?” Zu An was taken aback. He hadn’t expected her to be so sharp as to sense that.","“Yes, something seems to be on your mind. Are you worried about me?” the Mermaid Queen asked as she adjusted into a more comfortable position in his arms.","Zu An didn’t know how to answer that question.","The Mermaid Queen smiled. “You don’t need to feel so conflicted. I know I can’t leave this place. After being able to spend this night with you, I have no other regrets. Who knows? I might even have your child now. If so, I'll have someone to accompany me here.”","She suddenly stiffened up and hurriedly corrected herself. “No, that would be too selfish. It would be unfair to keep our child here with me.”","Zu An held her even more tightly. “My wife, I’ll rescue you from here.”","The Mermaid Queen chuckled. “Hubby, you don’t need to feel pressured. I’ll be here anyway. You can visit me whenever you miss me.”","Zu An felt a sharp pain in his chest. They had to be at least more than ten thousand years away from the era he lived in. She would be all alone in the meantime.","“I’ll stay here with you,” he suddenly said. It would be too cruel to leave her here alone.","The Mermaid Queen was taken aback before bursting into laughter. She was laughing out of joy, though; she was so happy that tears flowed uncontrollably from her eyes. She pressed her cheek against Zu An's chest and said, “Hubby, I’m happy to hear those words. It makes me happy to know that you've thought about that. But I can't be that selfish. You're shouldering too many responsibilities, and there are many things you need to do. I can’t keep you here with me.”","Zu An opened his mouth. He usually had a glib tongue, yet his throat suddenly felt so dry.","“Don’t worry. I’ll wait. I’ll wait till the day you come for me, no matter how long it takes.” The Mermaid Queen suddenly straightened her posture. A lock of her hair fell on his cheek. “Hubby, let’s not discuss such unhappy things. Let’s talk about something more light-hearted. Why don’t you tell me about your experiences before our meeting? I want to learn more about you.”","Zu An wrapped his arms around her tightly and shared his history with her.","A day could sometimes be so long, yet it could also be so short.","The Mermaid Queen nudged Zu An. “Hubby, it’s almost time.”","She'd learned about the warp portal from what Zu An shared with her. She tried her best to maintain a smile, but her eyes couldn’t help but tear up. The thought of separating from Zu An filled her with misery.","Zu An suddenly thought about something and summoned Mo Xi. The Mermaid Queen was startled by the sudden appearance of a curvaceous woman dressed in skimpy clothes.","“She’s Mo Xi...” Zu An roughly shared Mo Xi’s background. “Her ability, ‘Farewell, Nanchao’, allows her to sever any contract in the world. Your relationship with the Frost Palace can be considered a contract, but the problem is that she can only sever contracts that are of her level.”","The Mermaid Queen was disappointed. The lady before her could only be considered a slightly stronger human; it was unlikely that Mo Xi could grow to her level anytime soon.","Zu An had also figured as much. The gap between the two ladies was so huge that it was unlikely that Mo Xi could catch up with the ascended Mermaid Queen even if she was given years to cultivate.","All of a sudden, however, an idea popped into his head. He asked Mo Xi if she could stay and cultivate with the Mermaid Queen. This would give her plenty of time to grow. This was an era rich with natural ki, and the countless powerful celestials and shamans meant that there could be fortuitous encounters at every corner. Staying here could greatly accelerate Mo Xi’s growth.","Mo Xi looked away in response, but that lifted Zu An’s mood. Judging from her response, he could tell that it was possible; it was just that she was reluctant to do so.","“What do I have to do to convince you? Do you want more Ki Fruits?” Zu An had accumulated 3,039,680 Rage points thus far, so he could redeem a lot of Ki Fruits.","Mo Xi shook her head. Zu An communed with her soul and sensed her intention, but that only made him frown in bewilderment. What she wanted wasn’t Ki Fruits, but something else, and it was an item that he could have never imagined.","She wanted a costume from his Rage System’s shop, one that provided no benefits whatsoever. It was the costume that had startled Zu An back then—the bikini!"]},{"number":2652,"title":"Chapter 2652: Chapter 2604: Mutation","paragraphs":["The Keyboard System’s shop did sell beautiful costumes, but they provided no combat benefits or special effects, and on top of that, the prices were exorbitant. Zu An remembered complaining that only someone out of their mind would spend so many Rage points to buy a bunch of rags.","He'd been moved by the bikini though. He'd thought that the price could be worth it if he could get a valkyrie to wear it. But that was merely a fleeting thought. The series of events that happened afterward resulted in him forgetting all about it.","He'd never thought that all of a sudden, Mo Xi would make this request!","He eyed the bikini’s price—2,999,999 Rage points.","Those damned capitalists are the same everywhere. It’s three million, but they still want to play mind games to make you think you're only going to spend two million-ish.","“Are you certain that’s what you want?” Zu An sought confirmation, as the situation felt nothing short of ridiculous.","Mo Xi nodded. A rare hint of desire shimmered in her eyes.","“You must work hard to raise your cultivation and sever her contract afterward,” Zu An added worriedly.","Mo Xi nodded impatiently in response. Not daring to dawdle any longer, Zu An quickly bought the bikini.","When she saw the little strips of cloth Zu An held in his hand, the Mermaid Queen blushed. The Ocean races were open when it came to clothing, with many opting for revealing swimming clothes. Even so, she had never seen such skimpy clothing before.","Overjoyed, Mo Xi snatched the bikini.","For a moment, Zu An was worried that Mo Xi would start changing her clothes on the spot. While that thought sparked his anticipation, the mood didn’t seem right for that.","In the end, however, Mo Xi merely turned on the spot, and her super short skirt was immediately swapped with the bikini.","Zu An’s nose almost spurted blood on the spot. This woman doesn’t even try to hide it at all! But he had to admit that her figure was out of this world. Her healthy brown skin tone gave her an air of primal wildness and vibrance.","Even the Mermaid Queen couldn’t help but remark, “Little sister Mo Xi has an incredible figure.”","Mo Xi turned to Zu An with expectant eyes.","Zu An understood her intention and complimented her. “It looks great, but you shouldn’t wear it outside. It’d feel as if other men were taking advantage of you if they saw you in it.”","His worried expression brought amusement to Mo Xi’s eyes, but she still accepted his suggestion. Her expression seemed to say, “Don’t worry, I’ll wear it for you alone.”","Zu An asked her to use ‘Farewell, Nanchao’ to sever her contract with him so she could stay with the Mermaid Queen, but she turned down his suggestion, saying that she could stay here without severing the contract.","Zu An was surprised. These valkyries are incredible, to be able to exist independently in a distant spacetime far away from their hosts. Have I underestimated their potential? Was I too focused on my growth, so I neglected them?","“Thank you, hubby.” The Mermaid Queen’s eyes regained their usual spirit.","Hope was always the most important thing in this world. Mo Xi was currently still weak, but her existence brought hope to the Mermaid Queen. Even if she couldn’t sever the contract in the end, her company would still make the days in the Frost Palace more bearable.","Zu An grabbed her hand and said, “I’ll be back.”","“Mm~” The Mermaid Queen leaped into his arms and embraced him tightly.","The two of them hugged for a while, cherishing their final moments together.","“Big brother Zu, it’s time to go,” Yun Yuqing’s voice suddenly echoed. She had flown over from the distant celestial palace. Her disposition felt sharper than before, as if she had gained greater confidence.","She quickly noticed the bikini-wearing Mo Xi and was taken aback. Hold on! What’s with this sexy woman wearing such bold clothes?","Zu An also sensed the flickering of the distant warp portal and understood that it was on the verge of disappearing, but he stared yearningly at the Mermaid Queen.","The Mermaid Queen walked them out to the Frost Palace’s entrance. Her hands were so tightly locked with Zu An’s that their palms turned pale. It was as if they were inscribing each other into their bodies.","Separation was usually signified by the setting sun, but why did the warm rising sun suddenly feel so sorrowful too? The Frost Palace was shrouded in a white fog that seemed to represent indissipable melancholy.","“Big brother Zu, we have to leave now, or else we won’t make it in time.” Yun Yuqing didn’t want to be the villain in this situation, but she had no choice but to remind him. The warp portal was flickering with increasing intensity, and its light was dimming. It looked as if it would vanish at any moment now.","The Mermaid Queen leaned in and passionately kissed Zu An. Unable to suppress her emotions anymore, her tears fell to the ground, making crisp sounds resembling pearls striking a jade plate. These sounds echoed endlessly in Zu An’s heart.","Yun Yuqing lifted her eyebrows. She felt as if she should be angry at this situation, but she could sympathize with the persistent melancholy lingering in the air.","Zu An opened his mouth, but the countless words in his mind were jammed in his throat. In the end, they manifested as a string of meaningless, quivering noises.","“Go on. I’ll keep waiting for you.” Suddenly, the Mermaid Queen gently but determinedly pushed Zu An toward the warp portal.","“I’ll be back for you!” Zu An was finally able to release some of the stifled feeling in his chest.","“Mm!” The Mermaid Queen tearfully waved Zu An goodbye. The wind tugging at her robe made her appear even more frail.","As her voice slowly grew more distant, Zu An finally came to understand what it meant for the ‘wind to sting his eyes’.","Yun Yuqing dragged him into the warp portal, and the two of them returned to Taoqiu’s outer perimeter. The portal vanished practically as soon as they stepped out of it. Had they been a second slower, they would have been trapped in the Celestial World for good.","The Fiends and the Shamans were the ruling races of heaven and earth. A clash between entities of their might would take a long time to conclude. This battle could easily last for tens of thousands of years. A war marking the end of an era was bound to be anything but simple.","“Big brother Zu...” Yun Yuqing didn’t know how to console Zu An. Words fell flat here.","Zu An rubbed his cheeks. By the time he stood up once more, he had already reverted to normal. “Don’t worry about me. At least there’s a sliver of hope. I’ll find her one day. On another note, have you awakened your bloodline?”","Yun Yuqing felt conflicted. She would have been less worried if he'd simply burst into tears and vented his emotions. If a day when he could no longer maintain his strong front ever came, he would only end up in greater pain.","But she couldn’t open his heart, so she could only reply, “Indeed. I seem to be Zhuanxu’s descendant. Our bloodline should have grown thinner with each generation, but it suddenly mutated when it came to me and became purer. My bloodline is closer to the founding Green Emperor than Zhuanxu’s.”"]},{"number":2653,"title":"Chapter 2653: Chapter 2605: Perplexed","paragraphs":["“That's wonderful news!” Zu An was happy for her. “But why isn’t there any exceptionally huge advancement in your cultivation?”","He had examined Yun Yuqing using his aura and confirmed that her cultivation had advanced from Grandmaster’s Ascension Mortal Form to Earth Immortal’s Heaven Soul. The feat of raising her cultivation by two stages in an instant would have caused a huge stir in their previous Cultivation World.","But this was the Celestial World. Yun Yuqing had the purest Celestial Emperor Bloodline, and she'd even had Celestial Emperor Zhuanxu personally helping her to awaken her bloodline. Considering these factors, her growth felt rather lackluster.","Yun Yuqing tidied up Zu An’s unkempt clothes as she answered, “Zhuanxu told me that my cultivation is too low, and if my cultivation suddenly advanced too much within a short time, my body wouldn’t be able to take it. So, he only awakened my bloodline. He told me to naturally raise my cultivation through training so I would have a stronger foundation.”","Zu An nodded in agreement. Zhuanxu’s explanation made sense. He asked, “What power does the Celestial Emperor bloodline hold?”","Yun Yuqing replied uncertainly, “I’m not sure either. Zhuanxu told me that once my cultivation reaches a certain level, the secrets of the world will naturally unravel. Right now, my bloodline allows me to cultivate a hundred times more efficiently compared to before.”","Zu An was stunned. Putting aside the Celestial Emperor bloodline’s other abilities, just the boost in Yun Yuqing’s cultivation speed was already out of this world. He asked, “How did you awaken your bloodline?”","That was what the True Demon race had craved back then, but their efforts ended in futility.","Zu An had learned from Emperor Yao that when the Lord of Slaughter and Salamay escaped, the elders of the True Demon race had escaped with them. The Lord of Slaughter had tried to recruit them, but the True Demon race’s elders valued the awakening of their bloodlines more. They'd agreed to serve the Lord of Slaughter, only to find an excuse to flee later so they could find a way to awaken their bloodlines.","By sheer coincidence, they'd then bumped into Emperor Jun. Emperor Jun could have helped them awaken their bloodlines, but back then, he needed living souls for the forging of his Myriad Souls Banner. A tragic fate had thus befallen the True Demon race’s elders as a result.","“Zhuanxu brought me to a garden in the Celestial Court. That appears to be a place where generations of Celestial Emperors are worshiped...” Yun Yuqing shared what she'd seen along the way. Even Zu An was awed.","Chatting like that, they arrived at Wu Mountain before they knew it. On the mountain peak, Ji Xiaoxi was grinding her medicine, Suolun Shi was practising her swordsmanship, and the Goddess of Wu Mountain was standing in a daze by the mountain cliff. Meanwhile, Xie Daoyun quietly drew the scene by the windowsill.","There were several people on the mountain peak, but only the mountain wind could be heard. Everything was stiflingly quiet.","Zu An was amazed. Other than the Goddess of Wu Mountain, the other ladies looked different from usual, both in their choice of clothes and make-up. On second thought, however, it wasn’t surprising for them to change their clothes and make-up every day.","Ji Xiaoxi spotted Zu An and shook her head. “Aiyo, I’m seeing things again.” It was as if she had seen this sight far too many times before.","“What do you mean, seeing things?” Zu An was perplexed.","Tok!","Ji Xiaoxi dropped her mortar, which shattered into several pieces. She looked up in disbelief. “Big brother Zu?”","The other women sensed the commotion and looked over. When they saw Zu An, they immediately rushed over.","Even the Goddess of Wu Mountain ran over, though she quickly remembered her usual demure self and hurriedly slowed her footsteps. Suolun Shi also slowed down, worried about her current appearance.","Xie Daoyun didn’t harbor that many reservations, however. She ran the fastest despite being the furthest away.","But Ji Xiaoxi still beat her to the punch. She leaped into Zu An’s arms and began sobbing.","Feeling her trembling body and seeing the tears brimming in the other ladies’ eyes, Zu An was taken aback. “It's only been a day. Why are you all so worked up?”","“What do you mean, a day? We've already spent a year waiting for you!” Ji Xiaoxi sobbed.","Realization suddenly dawned on Zu An. Ah, a day in heaven equals a year on earth!","He had heard that saying many times before, but his previous trips to the Celestial Court had been short ones, so the difference in time hadn’t registered strongly to him. This time, he'd only stayed in the Celestial Court for an entire day because he didn’t want to part ways with the Mermaid Queen. Only now did he realize that an entire year had passed on earth!","This left him feeling conscience-stricken. He turned to the ladies and said, “I’m sorry. I kept you waiting for so long.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled. “It’s fine. A year isn’t a long time to me, though the others might not be used to the time difference.”","She often spent her time standing in a daze on Wu Mountain. Even a decade or a century would feel nothing more than a snap of a finger to her.","Xie Daoyun reined in her feelings and said, “Big brother Zu, we were worried about Emperor Yao tampering with the warp portal. We might have confronted him by now if not for big sister goddess telling us that a day in heaven equals a year on earth.”","As the other ladies walked over, Ji Xiaoxi hurriedly stepped aside, feeling too embarrassed to continue staying in Zu An’s arms. However, a joyful smile had appeared on her tearful face.","“I failed to consider that and warn you beforehand.” Zu An couldn’t resist the urge to look at the sky. For there to be such an exaggerated time difference between heaven and earth, could the Celestial World be located in the vicinity of a black hole...","“You have only been to the Celestial Court twice. It’s normal for you to overlook that,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain consoled him. If the Kaiming Six Shamans were here, they would surely wonder when the cold goddess had become so understanding.","“Did you manage to see big sister Suyin?” Xie Daoyun looked around. “Why isn’t she with...”","Her words trailed off as she realized something, and she regretted blurting those words out.","“I met her.” Zu An’s expression darkened at the mention of the Mermaid Queen.","“What happened?” the Goddess of Wu Mountain asked.","“She has become the Frost Palace’s master and can no longer leave its premises,” Zu An replied grimly.","“AH?!” The other ladies were shocked.","Suolun Shi asked, “Is it impossible to save her, even with your abilities?”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain explained, “I have heard legends about the Frost Palace. Its existence predates even the Celestial Court. No one knows about its background, but it is a known fact that the Frost Palace has a terrifying curse...”","Upon hearing her explanation, the other ladies turned pale. They couldn’t help but wonder how much despair they would have been in if they were in the Mermaid Queen’s position. This made them extremely sympathetic to her plight.","“The divine marks on the Frost Palace are a testimony to its extraordinary nature.” Zu An told them about how he had tried to destroy the Frost Palace, only to be nearly killed by its backlash. His story stunned the other ladies.","“Little sister Chang’e is too pitiful. I’ll visit her frequently at the Frost Palace once the path between heaven and earth is reestablished,\" the Goddess of Wu Mountain said. Even she, despite being the Flame Emperor’s daughter, couldn't do anything about the enigmatic Frost Palace.","The other ladies exchanged looks as they realized that among them, only the Goddess of Wu Mountain could do that. The rest of them weren’t from this world and couldn’t stay here in the long term. Even if they remained behind, it was unlikely that they could survive the long years. Only the Goddess of Wu Mountain was impervious to the erosion of time.","“Thank you, goddess!” Zu An was overjoyed. With her company, the Mermaid Queen wouldn’t be so lonely. “There’s someone else accompanying Suyin in the Frost Palace right now...”","He told the ladies about Mo Xi.","The ladies were relieved to hear that. Just thinking about the Mermaid Queen’s plight made them feel suffocated with despair. They were glad to hear that there was a chance she could be freed from her plight.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was perplexed. “Farewell, Nanchao? Is there such a formidable ability in the world? Why have I never heard about it?”"]},{"number":2654,"title":"Chapter 2654: Chapter 2606: The Final Tear","paragraphs":["Zu An was stunned. He'd never considered that issue. Given its mysterious background, he'd always assumed that it was normal for the Keyboard System to have skills that others had never heard about. However, now that the Goddess of Wu Mountain had pointed out this issue, he couldn’t help but think deeper about it.","It wouldn’t be a stretch to say that this was the golden era of cultivation, with powerful shamans and celestials all over the world. Besides that, the Goddess of Wu Mountain was the Flame Emperor’s daughter. She wasn't as strong as the powerhouses of this era, but she had vast knowledge of the world.","For someone as knowledgeable as her to have never heard of this ability, there could only be two possibilities: One, the ability didn’t exist in this world. Two, the ability hadn’t been created in this era.","If it were the former, it would suggest that there were stronger worlds out there. Zu An was mentally prepared for that, but nevertheless, this was the legendary Celestial Court! The people he'd met thus far were mythological figures he had grown up hearing about. He couldn’t imagine what even more powerful entities would be like.","If it were the former, it would mean that ‘Farewell, Nanchao’ would be created someday in the future. This experience of transmigrating into the past gave Zu An a better grasp of spacetime and historical events. Thus, he knew this ability could have been created through a similar process.","Was I the one who created this skill in history?","He thought about it, and felt that he was the only one who would be motivated to create such an ability. That was a grim thought. To be honest, Zu An didn’t like the feeling of traversing into the past. The slightest misstep could spell disaster. If something similar to the Frost Palace scenario were to happen several more times, he didn’t know if his heart could take it.","“What’s wrong?” the Goddess of Wu Mountain asked worriedly.","“I had a few bad conjectures.” Zu An snapped out of his thoughts. “Yaoji, thank you for taking care of them.”","“You don’t need to thank me for this. I’m used to being alone. Their company soothed some of my loneliness.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled. Under the rays of the morning sun, she looked so beautiful that even the other ladies were mesmerized.","Xie Daoyun thought it was unfair. Pei Mianman is already gorgeous as she is. Not only does the Goddess of Wu Mountain look identical to her, she even has Chu Chuyan’s ethereal disposition. How can anyone compete with that?","Zu An was about to say something when he suddenly sensed something. He quickly took out a box. It was the Nature Jade Case that had brought them to this world. The box was shaking nonstop, and its top was emanating a white light. The surrounding spatial ki was whirring to life.","Xie Daoyun’s eyes lit up. “We can return now!”","There was no place like home!","The other ladies were excited too. After being away for so long, they couldn’t wait to return home. Only the Goddess of Wu Mountain was stunned. However, she was so used to concealing her emotions that the others didn’t notice her unusual mood.","“Oh no!” Ji Xiaoxi suddenly exclaimed. “We haven’t found my little aunt yet!”","Zu An replied, “I asked Celestial Emperor Zhuanxu. He isn’t sure who took big sister Jiang away, but that person appears to be of a high stature. She should be safe for the time being.”","He suddenly remembered the mysterious entity Qiu Honglei had summoned back then. I wonder if the person who took Jiang Luofu away is stronger than that.","The answer eased some of Ji Xiaoxi’s worry, but she remained in low spirits, as there was no way of knowing whether her little aunt was truly safe or not. It also dampened the other ladies’ mood. They had come here together, only to still have several people missing even now that they were about to return. On top of that, the Mermaid Queen was still trapped in the Frost Palace...","Zu An felt distressed. He didn’t want to return so quickly, as there were still many secrets in this world waiting to be uncovered. In particular, he wanted to pay a visit to the Houtu of this era, as there were many questions he wanted to ask her.","But the Nature Jade was already reacting. If he missed this chance, there was no telling when it would next react, or whether it would even react at all. He didn’t dare to make that gamble, especially not when he had his companions with him.","“But we haven’t completed Xiaoxi’s Defying Spirit Tears,” Xie Daoyun suddenly pointed out.","They had been helping Ji Xiaoxi collect all kinds of herbs in the past year, so they understood that the Defying Spirit Tears were still lacking something. Even Ji Xiaoxi, despite her medical prowess, had no idea how to complete them.","Zu An’s expression darkened. The ingredients to treat Ji Xiaoxi were extremely rare, and most of them could only be found in this world. If they left now, perhaps they could never gather all the ingredients.","They had everything else they needed; the only thing they were lacking was the Defying Spirit Tears. If they missed this chance, the regret would be unbearable.","“Don’t worry, I have found the missing part,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain said.","“Really?” Zu An was overjoyed.","The other ladies were skeptical. We spent a year together. Why has she never mentioned this to us before?","“Of course. I wouldn’t lie about this,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain replied with a smile. “May I talk to you in private?”","The other ladies tactfully excused themselves to give them some space.","Yun Yuqing whispered to the others, “Do you think they'll have a farewell kiss?”","“Farewell kiss?” Xie Daoyun was taken aback. “Surely not, right?”","She had come to understand the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s personality in the time they'd spent together. The latter was unlikely to do something that bold.","“Huh? Is big sister goddess in love with big brother Zu too?” Ji Xiaoxi asked in astonishment.","Yun Yuqing rolled her eyes. She couldn’t be bothered to answer the foolish lass’ unnecessary question. She turned to the others and asked, “Shall we make a bet?”","That piqued Xie Daoyun and Suolun Shi’s interest. They began gossiping among themselves.","However, Zu An and the Goddess of Wu Mountain were strong enough to overhear their words. Zu An awkwardly said, “Goddess, please pardon them. They don’t mean any ill will.”","“It’s fine. I have come to know them after spending a year with them,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain smiled. “And they aren’t wrong. I do fancy you.”","“Ah?” Zu An was shocked. The other party had used such a calm tone to relay such shocking news that his mind stalled to a halt for a brief moment.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain walked to the mountain cliff as she spoke with her usual cold voice, though it carried a slightly unusual tinge. “Before I got to know you, I used to spend my days standing here, feeling the mountain’s breeze, watching sunrise, sunset, and the billowing clouds. I was content with those days. But after coming to know you, everything changed.","“I came to know about joy and sorrow.” At this point, the Goddess of Wu Mountain turned around to reveal the tears flowing down her usual stoic face. “From the moment I saw Xihe’s and Chang’e’s tears, I knew that the final tear aly with me, but I couldn’t imagine what would lead up to that.”"]},{"number":2655,"title":"Chapter 2655: Chapter 2607: Return","paragraphs":["A glistening teardrop flowed down the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s cheeks. This one floated, unlike the others that had fallen to the ground. She raised her dainty hands and gently guided the teardrop into a jade bottle.","She passed the jade bottle to Zu An. “With this, you should be able to complete the Defying Spirit Tears and treat Xiaoxi.”","Seeing how she was still thinking on his behalf despite being in tears, Zu An couldn’t hold it back anymore and pulled her into his arms.","The previous him, like many other men, had thought that it would be best if all beautiful women in the world could be his. But now that he had many lovers, he realized that love could be hurtful at times.","He had been through far too many separations. After his separation from the Mermaid Queen at the Frost Palace, he'd thought that nothing else could hurt him anymore.","But now, he realized that he was extremely wrong. A heart could be hurt twice in succession, even if one time was more painful than the other.","The other ladies in the distance noticed them hugging and frowned, as if discussing their earlier bets. But when they noticed the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s tears and Zu An’s pained look, their excitement waned. Even from a distance away, they could feel the sorrowful air on Zu An’s side.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain trembled in Zu An’s arms. It was rare for her to even speak to others, let alone be embraced by a man. Being held by his sturdy arms left her shy, but she also couldn’t help but wonder how much longer she could enjoy this embrace.","Zu An racked his brain for a solution, not wanting a repeat of what happened with the Mermaid Queen. All of a sudden, his eyes lit up, and he reached out to wipe her tears as he asked, “Yaoji, why don’t you come with us if you don’t mind?”","The Nature Jade would likely have no problem taking another person with them. Unlike Chang’e, who was bound to the Frost Palace, the Goddess of Wu Mountain wasn’t tied down by anything.","To his surprise, the Goddess of Wu Mountain shook her head and replied, “I can’t go.”","Seeing the confusion in Zu An’s eyes, the Goddess of Wu Mountain slowly explained, “I have been on this mountain ever since I was conferred as the Goddess of Wu Mountain. I don’t know how long has passed, but I often unknowingly morph into Wu Mountain’s Goddess Peak. In a way, I have already become one with Wu Mountain. I’m in a similar situation to little sister Chang’e. She is cursed by the Frost Palace, whereas I’m tied down by Wu Mountain.”","Zu An felt as if his heart had been plunged into a glacier. He could take a person, but he couldn’t take an entire mountain away with him. He felt helpless. When he first transmigrated over, he'd been much weaker, but he had never felt as helpless as this. Despite having grown stronger, it felt like there were more things that he couldn’t resolve now.","“Don’t be upset about it. This is my fate. I’m glad I met you. Meeting you has opened my eyes, and I was able to experience many different emotions I never knew about before.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain turned around and consoled Zu An instead.","That only pained Zu An more, however.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain grabbed his hand and led him to the cliff. “Big brother Zu, you don’t have to be sad. Whenever you see this cloud and fog, it will be the same as me being by your side. If Wu Mountain still exists in the future, you can look for me there too. It’s just that I might have completely morphed into the Goddess Peak by then.”","Zu An’s eyes reddened, and his voice was deeper than usual. “I’m worried about you. I have other friends with me, but you’ll be staying here alone.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain laughed. “I’m not alone. The wind, the clouds, and the rain are my friends. Besides, little sister Chang’e is still around. I can visit her now and then for a chat.”","Zu An often heard that his mouth was as sweet as if it were smeared with honey, but why did everything just feel so bitter right now? He struggled to find the words to console her.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain wouldn’t have cried so hard if she were truly fine. Her composure was merely a front to lessen his worry, but her consideration only made him feel worse.","“I’d love to meet Miss Manman,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain suddenly remarked.","Her judgment aligned with Xihe’s—she was likely Pei Mianman’s previous incarnation. It was good news that the future Pei Mianman got together with Zu An, but her very existence meant that the Goddess of Wu Mountain had eventually passed away. She had no idea how she died and why she had chosen to reincarnate, but there must have been a compelling reason.","My love is fulfilled in the future, but this also means that I’m unlikely to meet him ever again in this life. That thought made her emotions go into turmoil again, and tears glistened in her eyes.","A drizzle began falling upon Wu Mountain, enveloping it in fog.","Zu An was about to say something when the Nature Jade suddenly emanated a brilliant light that enveloped him and the other ladies. The next second, they all vanished into thin air.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain tried to grab him, but it was too late.","For a long time, she was reluctant to lower her hand that had frozen in mid-air. The vibrant Wu Mountain suddenly felt unbearably empty. She initially hadn't been able to get used to the guests residing in Wu Mountain, finding them too noisy. However, she found herself reminiscing about their joyous laughter.","She walked to the cliff and looked at the distant sea of clouds. Her figure slowly blurred until she morphed into the Goddess Peak.","That day, Wu Mountain rained heavier than ever.","...","Before they knew it, Zu An and the others appeared inside a lake. He quickly pulled the others up to shore before falling silent.","“Where are we?” Ji Xiaoxi surveyed their surroundings, but it was so dark that if they weren’t cultivators, they couldn’t have seen a thing at all.","“It’s the Fiend race’s Imperial Tomb,” Xie Daoyun, who retained the memories of the time she'd been possessed by Xihe, said.","“Ah, we returned to that spacetime fragment!” Ji Xiaoxi was delighted. That meant they could soon return to their original era. However, she soon recalled something and apologetically pulled on Zu An’s arm. “Big brother Zu, are you still feeling awful?”","Before Zu An could answer, a gleeful laugh echoed in the distance. “Milord was right! You would eventually return here!”"]},{"number":2656,"title":"Chapter 2656: Chapter 2608: Vanished","paragraphs":["Monster soldiers swarmed in from the surroundings and encircled them. Several powerful monsters emerged from their ranks. Xie Daoyun, remembering them from her memories, recognized them to be the renowned Monster Generals!","They were none other than the Shadow Monster King, the War Priest, the Shadowhorror Devil, and the Doomsday Spirit!","The other Monster Generals had been either killed or severely injured by Zu An and the Lord of Slaughter in their previous showdown. It looks like the injured ones haven’t recovered yet.","Faced with so many ferocious monsters, Ji Xiaoxi fearfully leaned closer to Zu An. Xie Daoyun, Yun Yuqing, and Suolun Shi secretly prepared their hand, ready to attack at any moment.","Had it been before, they would have spiraled into a panic when faced with so many monsters. However, they'd met far too many powerful entities in the Celestial World, so much so that the enemies before them, despite being far stronger, didn’t look as intimidating anymore.","The ladies looked to Zu An for instructions, only to be shocked to see a mask on his face.","Zu An had to wear a mask to avoid affecting the future. Since he would come into contact with some of these Monster Generals in the future, there was no telling what would happen if they saw his true face here and recognized him when they met again in the future. That was a risk he couldn’t take.","The War Priest was perplexed by the absence of notable figures in the party. “Where are the Lord of Slaughter and the others?”","Zu An had been a difficult opponent for them back then, but after reviewing their battles, they realized that his strength was only on par with that of an average Monster General. It was just that he had all kinds of tricks that made him a troublesome foe. But now that they had a better grasp of those tricks and knew how to guard against them, it would be much easier to deal with him now. Not to mention they had come up with new skills and tricks for this rematch.","“Scram! I’m not in the mood to deal with you now.” Zu An was already in a terrible mood, and these sidekicks still wanted to annoy him at this juncture!","What further frustrated him was that he couldn’t kill them right now. He needed them alive so he could deal with them in the future. What a hassle!","The Shadow Monster King and the others were enraged. “You scum! How dare you blatantly disrespect us? I’ll rip off your skin and remove your tendons! You shall watch in despair as the ladies beside you suffer fates worse than death!”","You have successfully trolled the Shadow Monster King for +444... +444... +444","You have successfully trolled the War Priest...","...","The influx of Rage points didn’t lift Zu An’s mood; it only fanned his anger.","All of a sudden, there was a flash of seven-colored light. It swept away the Monster Generals before they could understand what was going on. They found themselves twirling all around a seven-colored world as if they were laundry inside a washing machine, causing their heads to spin.","Then, they were hurled out of the light and landed heavily on the ground.","The Monster Generals tried to leap to their feet to counterattack. How could they admit defeat when they hadn’t even used their artifacts and skills? But no matter how they flailed around with their hands and feet, they couldn’t get to their feet, as if the earlier fall had broken them for good. They felt so giddy that they could vomit.","The monster soldiers were dumbstruck. What’s going on? We came here to destroy these humans, right? How did the tables turn on us? How in the world were the almighty Monster Generals defeated in the blink of an eye?","The monster soldiers lost their fighting spirit. If not for their fear of the Monster Lord’s punishment, they would have thrown their weapons away and surrendered by now.","Zu An couldn’t be bothered to waste his time on the monster soldiers. He grabbed Ji Xiaoxi’s hand and led the other ladies out of the Imperial Tomb.","The monster soldiers instinctively opened a path for them to cross. They lowered their heads, not daring to meet Zu An’s eyes. However, despite the monsters’ attempt to steer clear of Zu An’s party, there were simply too many of them here, and the space in the Imperial Tomb was limited.","Ji Xiaoxi and the others could still smell the monsters’ repulsive aura. However, none of the monsters dared to step out of line. This peculiar experience left the ladies excited and awed. They would never have thought that the savage monsters could be this obedient.","They soon left the Imperial Tomb. The sight of the sun evoked a wistful feeling. It felt as if so many things had changed since.","A powerful aura came surging in from the distance. It was the Monster Lord and his aides. They had rushed over upon receiving news about Zu An’s return.","When he saw Zu An’s party, the Monster Lord frowned. “Where’s the Lord of Slaughter?”","There was a flash of seven-colored light, and the Lord of Slaughter’s massive body was hurled onto the ground. A huge commotion broke out.","The Lord of Slaughter had dominated the Monster World for so long that many monsters still viewed him as the strongest despite the Monster Lord’s usurpation of power. They thought that the Monster Lord had only come to power because of his schemes.","And yet, they were witnessing the strongest monster, the Lord of Slaughter, being hurled on the ground like a sandbag with their own eyes.","The Monster Lord’s eyes quivered. He had only usurped the throne from the Lord of Slaughter by developing a comprehensive plan and planting many chess pieces beforehand, and even so, it was a narrow victory.","To make things worse, the Lord of Slaughter had even grasped the secret behind the Fiend race’s Imperial Tomb and entered the legendary Celestial World!","All this while, the Monster Lord had been worried that the Lord of Slaughter would stumble upon a fortuitous encounter in the Celestial World and awaken his bloodline power. As a countermeasure, he'd prepared many slaughter formations and stationed the Monster Generals and their armies in the Imperial Tomb. He'd even developed new moves to catch the Lord of Slaughter by surprise.","To think that his strongest enemy would be defeated just like that!","The Monster Lord quickly snapped out of his daze and laughed. “So you have dealt with the Lord of Slaughter! The enemy of one's enemy is a friend. I will handsomely reward you for your merit!”","At the same time, he wondered what was going on with the Shadow Monster King, the War Priest, and the others. Why aren’t they making a move?","Those two Monster Generals were extremely powerful, and they were aided by the Shadowhorror Devil, the Doomsday Spirit, and the monster armies. Even the Monster Lord would struggle to deal with such a lineup.","He had rushed here as soon as he received the signal. Surely they can’t be dead yet?","“Who’s your friend? This is the human world. Scram from this world with your subordinates, and I’ll consider sparing your lives,” Zu An sneered coldly.","The Monster Lord’s smile stiffened. He first glanced at the unconscious Lord of Slaughter, followed by the eerily silent Imperial Mausoleum. There’s something amiss about this fellow. However, he soon burst into laughter and said, “You’re merely putting on a strong front. If you were truly that powerful, you wouldn’t have to demand our departure.”","However, a blade of sword ki suddenly appeared before his eyes. It was so fast that he didn’t have time to react. By the time he glanced at his right arm, it had already vanished from sight!"]},{"number":2657,"title":"Chapter 2657: Chapter 2609: Looking for Chang’e","paragraphs":["Even Xie Daoyun and the others were shocked.","Even though Zu An had attained immortality, the Monster Lord’s strength was at least on par with many deities. It would be one thing if he was caught off guard by Zu An’s seven-colored light, but how could the Monster Lord’s arm be lopped off so easily in a confrontation?","Only Yun Yuqing could fathom a guess as to what happened. Big brother Zu has fought too many powerful figures in the Celestial World, including Celestial Emperor-tier opponents. His will is far too strong for the Monster Lord to oppose.","The concept of one’s willpower influencing one’s fighting prowess was no secret. In a fight between two people of similar strength, the one with stronger willpower was likely to claim the upper hand. Yun Yuqing had seen plenty of such examples in her many years of cultivation.","But tempering one’s willpower was easier said than done. It had to be slowly built up by accruing victories against powerful opponents. Zu An had only fought the Celestial Emperors to a draw, but considering his far weaker cultivation, that was a formidable feat. If that couldn’t temper an invincible will, nothing would.","The Monster Lord, not knowing the true story, couldn’t understand how Zu An could have become this powerful when he had only left for a short time. In the end, he attributed it to a fortuitous encounter in the legendary Celestial Court. He glanced at the unconscious Lord of Slaughter, and he suddenly felt extreme fear.","This isn’t an opponent I can defeat! The thought of that made him lose all fighting spirit. Smoke swiftly enveloped him as he unleashed all his escape methods. By the time the smoke dissipated, he was already nowhere to be seen.","Zu An sensed a spatial disturbance, and judging from that, he deduced that the Monster Lord had used a teleportation artifact. However, he didn’t stop the Monster Lord, as the latter wasn’t meant to die in this era.","Instead, he cast a sweeping gaze across the monster army and bellowed, “I’ll give you ten days to scram from this world. I’ll purge every monster who’s still here after ten days.”","The invading monster army was so huge that Zu An couldn’t hope to defeat them single-handedly. Even if he could, the monster army’s desperate retaliation would only inflict greater damage on this world.","Ten days would be enough for most monsters to leave via large-scale teleportation formations, but they wouldn’t have enough time to bring their weapons and resources back with them. Those would serve as wartime reparations. Besides that, it was also unlikely that all the monsters could evacuate within ten days. The remaining ones would serve as fodder to quell the anger of this world’s races.","The monsters were flabbergasted. Cowardice had already been forming in their hearts when they saw the Lord of Slaughter being hurled out like a dead dog. The sight of the Monster Lord losing his arm and escaping further crushed their morale. Their formations collapsed, and the monsters fled frantically in all directions.","Xie Daoyun said worriedly, “Big brother Zu, the monsters have no principles. You might have intimidated them for the time being, but they might change their minds once they snap out of it.”","Her experience of dealing with the monsters as the Fiend races’ Saintess Yumen Beiqing made her opinion credible. After some thought, Zu An took out his Sun Slaying Bow. Now that the Monster Lord had escaped, he wasn't worried about the latter seeing it.","He nocked an arrow and shot it into the sky. It soon plummeted from the sky like a comet, falling directly on the monster army’s camp.","Boom!","That was, after all, an arrow that could shoot down a sun.","Zu An had to hold back because he wasn’t sure if this world could withstand his full-powered arrow, but even so, it smashed through the monster camp and annihilated it. A huge pit was left in the heart of the camp, and the ground turned into lava. Smoke filled the surrounding air. The monsters who were slow to escape were blown to bits; the survivors, scared out of their wits, fled with everything they had in desperation.","Meanwhile, a translucent bell around Zu An protected the ladies around him, keeping the terrifying shockwaves at bay.","Yun Yuqing, Suolun Shi, and the others wanted to pursue the escaping monsters; they held a deep grudge against the monsters, and wouldn’t miss the chance to massacre them.","Xie Daoyun stopped them. “There’s no point chasing them. We also need them to spread the news about what happened here for the other monsters to give up and return to their world.”","Yun Yuqing nodded in agreement. “As expected of the Fiend races’ Saintess! Little sister Xie is truly meticulous!”","Xie Daoyun blushed in embarrassment.","The sight of the burning monster camp left the ladies with many thoughts, especially Xie Daoyun. She had led the Fiend races in this world on a counterattack against the monsters. Even now, she could still remember how suffocated she felt whenever she thought about the monsters’ fearsome strength.","Who would have thought that Zu An could resolve this situation with such ease?","“Big brother Zu, let’s return to the Fiend races first and inform them about the monsters’ movements. We should also discuss the sealing of the Lord of Slaughter,” Xie Daoyun said.","Zu An replied, “You return to the Fiend races first. I’ll leave you to prepare for the Lord of Slaughter’s sealing. There’s another place I need to go to first.”","Xie Daoyun was talented in formations, and she knew how the Lord of Slaughter was sealed in the future. This task was within her means.","Sensing the sorrow in his eyes, Xie Daoyun’s heart quivered. She could guess where he was heading. The other ladies also exchanged looks, knowing better than to touch his wound.","After bidding the ladies farewell, Zu An stowed away the Lord of Slaughter with his Seven-Colored Divine Halo and flew into the sky.","Looking at his departing silhouette, Ji Xiaoxi asked, “Big sister, is big brother Zu heading to the Frost Palace to visit big sister Chang’e?”","“It seems so.”","“But it’s still day. The moon hasn’t come out yet.”","“Big brother Zu is very knowledgeable. He should have a way to find the moon... right?”","...","Zu An could naturally find the moon. He flew above the clouds and dashed out of the stratosphere, eventually entering the vastness of space. After attaining immortality, his body was tough enough to withstand the extreme conditions of space, though he wasn’t sure how far he could travel in the void.","He looked at the world behind him and saw a familiar blue planet. It is indeed Earth! It looks much larger than the planet I’m familiar with though. Could it be because it's rich in ki?","Zu An tossed aside his miscellaneous thoughts and soon found the moon. He quickly descended on it. Circular pits were visible on its dirt-cloaked surface. He couldn’t detect the slightest life on it.","His heart sank. He couldn’t find the Frost Palace, which meant Chang’e wasn’t here."]},{"number":2658,"title":"Chapter 2658: Chapter 2610: Everything Has Changed","paragraphs":["He had already expected as much when he emerged from the stratosphere, however. Flying upward should have led him into the Celestial Court, but it was nowhere to be found. All he encountered was boundless space.","Zu An fell silent. Did the Celestial Court disappear altogether? Or does it not exist in the sky, unlike what everyone thought, and that there is some kind of teleportation formation in the sky that transports you to the Celestial Court? What kind of place is the Celestial Court?","He suddenly recalled the Celestial Court’s peculiar flow of time. A day in heaven equaled a year on earth.","It’s probably located near a black hole. Is there no way to access the Celestial Court in this era?","Maybe Zhuanxu’s severing of heaven and earth and the felling of the sacred tree Jianmu resulted in the beings on Earth ceasing to worship the Celestial Court. It’s probably tough for those legendary gods to appear in our world now too.","Zu An felt frustrated. His inability to access the Celestial Court meant that he couldn’t reunite with the Mermaid Queen. He had marked some of the Celestial Court’s coordinates back then, but he couldn’t sense them anymore. It could be because he was too far away, or that a formation had blocked them.","In the end, he descended from the moon and returned to Earth.","This Earth was much larger than the one he was on before his transmigration. Did the later drying up of ki cause the planet to contract? He had several conjectures, but there was no way to confirm them.","While descending from the sky, Zu An suddenly turned to a mountain range. I might be unable to reach the Celestial Court now, but what about the surface? The Goddess of Wu Mountain is also waiting for me!","Countless years had passed since the era of the Celestial Court, so the world was bound to have changed in the meantime.","Zu An made his way to Wu Mountain based on the coordinates he remembered, but there was no mountain there when he arrived—in its place was a lake. He thoroughly searched the lake, but there wasn't the slightest trace of Wu Mountain.","“The coordinates must have changed due to the terraforming of the world,” he said to himself. He'd even constructed a teleportation formation on Wu Mountain, but so much time had passed that he could no longer sense it.","He searched based on his memories and grasp of space, and he also asked the locals about their regional myths and legends. Days later, he finally found Spirit Mountain.","This world’s Spirit Mountain was richer in ki than other places, but it was severely lacking compared to the Celestial World’s Spirit Mountain. No wonder people seemed to get weaker with each passing generation in the cultivation stories I read in my previous world. Turns out it’s because of the change in environment.","He enveloped Spirit Mountain with his divine sense—its topography roughly lined up with the Celestial World’s Spirit Mountain.","Soon, he arrived before a beautiful mountain peak. Everything was different from how he remembered it to be, but as he made his way over, he felt an inexplicable sense of intimacy. He flew up to the peak. The ki waterfall and flower fields were nowhere to be found; the place was covered in weeds instead. Even so, he could still see through the weeds to recognize the original mountain peak.","He made his way to the cliff. He tried opening the cave using the method he remembered, though he didn’t bear much hope. Too much time had passed, so he felt the cave would have eroded over time as well.","Much to his delight, however, the cliff opened to reveal a familiar cave!","Zu An trembled. Could Yaoji still be inside?","Yaoji, as the Goddess of Wu Mountain, was one with Wu Mountain. If Wu Mountain was still around, chances were that she was also around too.","“Yaoji?” Zu An gently called out. Despite his nervousness, his footsteps were slow. He was afraid that he would receive a disappointing answer.","The dark cave suddenly lit up, and a pleasant melody played. Flower petals fell from the sky. A beautiful figure slowly walked out, just as when they first met.","“Yaoji!” Overjoyed, Zu An rushed straight over to embrace her.","Little did he expect to pass right through her figure. His smile immediately froze in place. It turned out that was merely an illusion of the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","It should have been apparent to him, but he was so shaken up that he'd overlooked that.","“Big brother Zu, I have always been curious how you would react when you see me once more. Let me guess. You must have been very excited, only to be disappointed when you realized that I was an illusion.” The beautiful figure’s cold voice was tinged with a bit of mischief.","Her words slightly consoled Zu An’s heavy heart. He could tell this wasn’t a soul fragment but merely a recording, so conversation wasn’t possible between them.","“Actually, I have another guess—you might have tried to embrace me too.” She suddenly let out a sigh. “Maybe it’s one-sided, but I still remember our final embrace. It was so warm and comfortable, yet so sorrowful too.”","“Yaoji, I did try to embrace you earlier, and I'm still embracing you now.” Zu An walked up to the illusion and gently ‘held’ her despite knowing it was an illusion.","The illusion spoke yet again. “I don’t know whether the first thing you did was to embrace me or not, but I bet you are embracing me now after hearing my words.”","Zu An quietly looked at her face. She was identical to the Yaoji he remembered. He hadn’t expected a cold beauty like her to be so meticulous.","“I want to embrace you too, but I can’t.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain also took an embracing posture, as if lying against his chest.","“You are the only one other than me who knows how to open this cave. If someone tries to open it by force, everything in this cave will be destroyed,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain continued. “I promised to wait for you. I waited for a thousand years, ten thousand years... I don’t know how many tens of thousands of years I have waited. You know me. I don’t have a sense of time.”","Her gentle words shook Zu An's heart. To him, it had only been half a day since they parted ways, but to her, it had already been tens of thousands of years. He couldn’t imagine how sorrowful it must have been for her to wait for him day after day with an expectant heart, only to be disappointed again and again.","“Yaoji...” Zu An’s voice became hoarse. Words fell short in the face of the harshness of time.","Worry brimmed in the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s eyes. “I know you wouldn’t forget me, big brother Zu. You promised to look for me, but you didn’t come after so long. I was worried that something had happened to you, so I went to look for little sister Chang’e...”"]},{"number":2659,"title":"Chapter 2659: Chapter 2611: Reincarnation","paragraphs":["Zu An’s heart quivered. He had just gone to the moon to search for Chang’e, only to learn that the Celestial Court had vanished from the world. He'd been grieving over possibly never meeting the Mermaid Queen again when a clue suddenly popped up here.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain continued, “Little sister Chang’e knows you better. She feels it’s unlikely for any mishap to have befallen you given your wits and strength. There must be a compelling reason why you haven’t looked for us yet. She has been pondering that question, and we concluded that the most likely reason is time.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain lowered her head in sorrow. “If a day in heaven translates to a year on earth, there could be other temporal disparities in the world too. A spacetime traveler like you might have a different flow of time from us. Our ten thousand years might have been just a few years or even a few days for you.”","The Goddess of Wu Mountain couldn’t hold back her tears anymore.","Zu An felt his heart clench. He wanted to wipe off her tears, but his hands passed right through her projection. That made him feel worse.","“Let’s not talk about sad matters anymore. You must be concerned about little sister Chang’e. She’s famous in the Celestial Court, with many male deities seeing her as their dream lover.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain chuckled. “But little sister Chang’e never paid them any heed. She told them that her heart already belongs to someone else. The male deities were so angry that some declared they would teach that person a lesson. There were several extremely powerful individuals among them. Little did they know that their love rival wasn’t in this world.”","Her teasing words brought a smile to Zu An’s face, though it pained him to be unable to protect the Mermaid Queen from other people’s harassment.","As if sensing his worry, the Goddess of Wu Mountain quickly added, “But there’s nothing to worry. Little sister Chang’e is one with the Frost Palace. No one can hurt her in the Frost Palace, not even the Celestial Emperor.”","Zu An breathed a sigh of relief. At the same time, he became increasingly curious about the Frost Palace’s origin.","“I was worried that little sister Chang’e would feel lonely while I wasn't around, so I offered to bring her a pet to stave off her loneliness. I thought she would choose a cat or a dog, but she is surprisingly fond of rabbits. So, I caught a mutated jade rabbit in the wilderness for her. She was very fond of it,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain said gleefully. She was satisfied with her gift.","Zu An hadn’t expected the Goddess of Wu Mountain to be the one who gave Chang’e her Jade Rabbit. The Jade Rabbit was capable of cultivating, and she would later transform into a pretty woman and slip into the mortal world. Although, that was a thing for the future.","“Little sister Chang’e also introduced me to Miss Mo Xi. We have been looking for ways to hasten her cultivation. Miss Mo Xi isn’t fond of speaking, but she’s very talented and cultivates fast. However, she’s still unable to catch up with little sister Chang’e. We always seem to be slightly off the mark from meeting the requirements for ‘Farewell, Nanchao’.”","Zu An frowned. Mo Xi should have received an abundance of resources from the Goddess of Wu Mountain and the Mermaid Queen, yet she was still unable to surpass Chang’e. This made him even more curious about the Frost Palace’s origin.","Hold on, the Goddess of Wu Mountain said that Mo Xi isn’t fond of speaking. Did Mo Xi speak in front of them?","Zu An had many questions, but all he had now was a recording left behind by the Goddess of Wu Mountain. Conversation wasn’t possible, so he could only listen to her narration.","“I thought the Frost Palace could use some greenery and tried transplanting some plants and flowers there, but I haven’t succeeded yet. But I’ll continue trying to find a plant that can thrive in the Frost Palace.”","Zu An was moved. The Goddess of Wu Mountain was a reclusive individual who enjoyed her peace. It was completely unlike her to proactively help the Mermaid Queen. In other words, she had done all that for his sake.","“You must be curious about the outcome of the war between the Shamans and Fiends.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain wryly shook her head right after saying those words. “I nearly forgot. You’re from the future. You must already know the conclusion.”","“The war continued for a long time, and countless powerful Shamans and Celestials met their end. The final showdown even resulted in the deaths of most Ancestral Shamans, with only Houtu and a few other Ancestral Shamans surviving the ordeal. Emperor Jun and Donghuang Taiyi died in that battle too.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain looked a little shaken up when she spoke about that grand battle. It had to have been truly terrible.","“There was no victor in the war between the Shamans and the Fiends. Both sides receded into the shadows, opening room for the rise of humankind. Humans are hardworking and brave, and they are adept at learning the skills of both races. I’d expect no less from big brother Zu’s race,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain said, talking about the human race with a gentle gaze.","She didn’t continue elaborating on that, knowing Zu An had to be familiar with that history. Instead, she moved the topic on to something else, “Xihe often drops by the Frost Palace to chat with us. She also visits me at Wu Mountain from time to time. A lot of Miss Mo Xi’s cultivation resources came from her.”","Zu An harbored conflicting feelings about Xihe. Even though the latter had approached him with the intention of exacting vengeance for her sons, they had indeed spent a long time together as an intimate couple.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain was awed. “To think that you could make the renowned Sun Goddess, the ex-Celestial Empress, fall in love with you in such a short time. You’re impressive indeed...”","Faced with her cold eyes, Zu An’s face reddened despite knowing she was an illusion.","“I don’t like her presence at Wu Mountain. She’s too searing. Her presence dissipates the mountain fog and withers the plants.” The Goddess of Wu Mountain pouted. “But little sister Chang’e is fond of her. The Frost Palace feels much warmer whenever she’s around. As they often appear together in the Celestial Court, a legend has begun spreading among the humans, saying that the Sun Goddess and the Moon Goddess are close sisters.”","...","Hearing the events that had transpired over the years filled Zu An’s heart with warmth. If only I could have gone through these events with them.","“Xihe heard from little sister Chang’e that there is a Miss Shang in the future who greatly resembles her. She was envious that we had future incarnations, and she said that she wanted to be Chang’e’s big sister if she ever reincarnated,” the Goddess of Wu Mountain said with a smile.","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. Could Shang Hongyu be...","The Goddess of Wu Mountain’s voice suddenly sped up. “When I first heard about Miss Manman and Xihe’s talk about reincarnation, I initially didn’t get it. I know myself. I’d rather wait for you as myself than to undergo reincarnation. However, I’m starting to see why as of late.”","Zu An was startled. Her tone... Did something huge happen?"]},{"number":2660,"title":"Chapter 2660: Chapter 2612: Reunion","paragraphs":["However, the Goddess of Wu Mountain didn’t mention what happened. She hesitantly said, “There are many things I can’t tell you. Xihe and little sister Chang’e have told me that the past has both fixed and uncertain variables. Things may become fixed if I say them now, and that may lead to unexpected outcomes.”","Zu An could roughly understand her concerns.","Mi Li had also shared her understanding of spacetime with him. It would be more accurate to refer to recorded history as Schrodinger’s history. Major events were fixed in place, but the unrecorded details granted room for peculiar maneuvers.","Zu An’s journey to the ancient era of the Celestial Court was an example of that. He had done many things there, and while his actions conformed to what had happened in recorded history, the nuances were completely different.","The Goddess of Wu Mountain sighed. “I wonder if big brother Zu will ever see this recording.”","Zu An’s heart quivered at her sigh. The Goddess of Wu Mountain continued to share events that had happened over the years, as well as her deep yearning for him. He quietly took in her stories and sentiments.","Some time later, the Goddess of Wu Mountain suddenly stood up to look into the distance. Her face reflected both trepidation and determination. “It’s about time. May reincarnation truly exist in this world, so our bond can continue in the future.”","A teardrop flowed down her beautiful cheek. She flew to Wu Mountain’s peak and stood there, gazing in the direction where Zu An had disappeared back then. Her body slowly transformed into the elegant Goddess Peak, fixing itself to the mountain.","Zu An’s heart became heavy. He knew that she often transformed into a mountain peak while gazing at the scenery, but he could tell that something was different this time. She couldn’t transform back anymore.","He dashed out of the cave and headed to Wu Mountain’s peak. Amid the fog, an elegant peak stood out like a graceful, dignified lady. A gentle breeze blew, tugging on the red maple leaves on the mountain. For a moment, he thought he saw the Goddess of Wu Mountain standing there, smiling at him.","“Yaoji...” Zu An subconsciously walked forward, only for her silhouette to vanish. It was only him and the mountain peak.","He turned into a giant as he walked up to the mountain peak and gently embraced the Goddess Peak. He couldn’t stop his tears anymore. “Yaoji, I’m sorry for coming late.”","He didn’t dare to exert any force, fearing that it would hurt the mountain. His tears fell on the Goddess Peak.","As if sensing his sorrow, it began to drizzle on Wu Mountain. A wind blew, and the clouds billowed. It was as if the world was manifesting his remembrance of the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","Zu An spent ten days on Wu Mountain just like that. He even constructed several defensive formations around the Goddess Peak, lest it be damaged by external forces. There were many formidable cultivators in this world capable of destroying mountains, after all.","Even though the Goddess Peak was located in the middle of a remote mountain range, he didn’t dare to take any risks. Worried that the formations would run out of energy over time, he designed a mechanism based on his previous world’s solar panels to tap into the sun and the moon’s essences.","Ten days later, however, Zu An had no choice but to leave. Be it the monsters, the Fiend races, or the Ocean races, there was a huge list of things that he needed to deal with. He kissed the Goddess Peak before departing via Rainbow Morph.","Wu Mountain’s maple leaves swayed as if bidding him goodbye.","...","Zu An descended upon the Fiend races’ new Imperial Court.","The Fiend races tensed up as if a terrifying monster had sprung out of nowhere. It was only when their Saintess leaped into his arms in delight that they remembered his identity.","Many in the Fiend races had previously harbored hostility toward Zu An because their Saintess had threatened to break ties with them to be with him. However, they recently learned that Zu An had single-handedly driven off the monsters from this world. Given his massive accomplishment and his astounding strength, who would dare continue to harbor dissatisfaction toward him?","All the race leaders expressed goodwill toward him, hoping to get into his good books. It was just that Zu An was too tired to deal with all that.","Fortunately, Xie Daoyun took care of it on his behalf. She scattered the crowd and brought him back to her residence. “Big brother Zu, did you find the Mermaid Queen and the Goddess of Wu Mountain?”","Zu An shook his head before explaining what had happened.","The ladies could tell that things hadn’t gone well from his expression, but his story still left them feeling melancholic. Even the most sincere promise couldn’t overcome the relentless passage of time.","“Big brother Zu, there is someone you'll be happy to meet.” Xie Daoyun revealed a rare mischievous smile.","Zu An widened his eyes. He already had a guess who it was.","The ladies escorted him to the entrance of a residence before urging him to enter alone.","Zu An took a deep breath before pushing the door with trembling hands. A woman wearing a red top and a black skirt was applying makeup by the window. Perhaps to conserve her energy, she rested her breasts on the table.","“Ling’er, you have to help me stall him...” The woman reflexively glanced over when she heard the door opening, only to freeze up when she saw Zu An. Her face swiftly reddened. She felt embarrassed to have him see her earnestly doing her makeup.","“Manman...” Zu An was dazed for an instant. It was only moments since he'd returned from Wu Mountain. He thus briefly thought the woman before him was the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","However, they had spent so much time together that he could tell the difference right away. Her air of seductiveness was at odds with the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s lofty disposition.","Pei Mianman had paid Yumen Beiqing a visit back when Xihe was still occupying her body. Afraid that her disguise would be exposed, Xihe had subdued her, but for some reason, she'd opted to imprison Pei Mianman in a formation instead of killing her.","Xihe had already told Zu An the location and the method to unravel the formation. Knowing that she was safe, Zu An had entrusted the task of rescuing her to Xie Daoyun instead.","“They're making fun of me.” Pei Mianman put down her brush as she stood up with a pout.","Unable to repress his yearning anymore, Zu An pulled Pei Mianman into his arms. The strength in his arms evoked the latter’s smile, and she tightly embraced him back. They had been apart for so long that Pei Mianman had even wondered if they would be separated eternally.","Some time later, Pei Mianman suddenly looked at him with an ambiguous smile. “Who are you thinking about right now... me or that Goddess of Wu Mountain?”"]},{"number":2661,"title":"Chapter 2661: Chapter 2613: Suppression","paragraphs":["“Both,” Zu An admitted frankly as he hugged Pei Mianman’s body tighter.","“Scum!” Pei Mianman feigned anger and struggled. But Zu An continued holding her tightly, not letting her go.","Sensing his low spirits, Pei Mianman stopped struggling and gently said, “I heard you went off to look for Chang’e and the Goddess of Wu Mountain. You didn’t find them?”","“I didn’t...” Zu An finally released her. He grabbed her hand and led her to the table, where the two of them sat down. He told her everything that had happened in the last few days.","“To think tens of thousands of years would pass just like that.” Pei Mianman sat in a daze for a brief moment before abruptly asking, “Does the Goddess of Wu Mountain really look like me?”","Zu An assessed her beautiful face and replied, “You’re identical, but opposite.”","“What nonsense is that? You don’t need to tease me.” Pei Mianman harrumphed.","“I mean it.” Zu An stroked her hand. “The Goddess of Wu Mountain is opposite of you. You’re seductive and passionate, whereas she’s cold and lofty. If not for your identical appearances, I wouldn’t have believed she was your past incarnation.”","“Cold and lofty?” Pei Mianman felt stifled. “I knew it. You like Chuyan’s type more.”","Zu An burst into laughter. “Are you getting jealous of yourself?”","“What do you mean by myself? She is herself, and I am myself. We aren’t the same.” Pei Mianman puffed up her cheeks.","She had been imprisoned for a long time. When she was finally rescued, she abruptly learned that her lover had gotten together with another woman who was identical to her. To make things worse, the other party was likely to be her past incarnation, so she couldn’t even lash out. It felt as if something was seething inside her, but she couldn’t let it out.","“You are indeed different. I have never thought of her as you, and I would never think of you as her either.” Zu An thought it was interesting how two identical people could have such different personalities.","That made Pei Mianman feel better, but when she thought about how she was throwing a tantrum when he was already in a bad mood, she felt apologetic. “I heard the others chatting about the Goddess of Wu Mountain. She sounds like a very impressive woman.”","Zu An looked at her weirdly. “It sounds as if you’re complimenting yourself.”","“I am a beautiful woman. If she looks like me, she deserves to be complimented too.” Pei Mianman harrumphed with mirthful eyes. She hugged his arm and lay her head on his shoulder. “Tell me about your story with her.”","Feeling the pressure on his arm, Zu An was once again reminded about how Pei Mianman was different from Yaoji. “Didn’t the others already tell you?”","“They wouldn’t know as much as you.” Pei Mianman cast a sideward glance at him, her beautiful eyes nearly siphoning his soul away.","Zu An finally recounted his story with the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","At the very end, Pei Mianman was taken aback. “You didn’t bed her?”","Black streaks appeared on Zu An’s face. “Was that the point?”","“Of course it is! That’s completely unlike you.” Pei Mianman looked truly astonished. “I didn’t think you would be capable of a purely platonic relationship!”","Zu An looked away, not wanting to respond to her.","“Fine, fine. I won’t tease you anymore, so don’t be angry, all right?” Pei Mianman coyly pulled his arm. “You want to meet that goddess again, right? That’s not that hard.”","Zu An was stunned. “You have a way?”","He had spent a long time racking his brain for a way he could be together with Yaoji, but it was to no avail. Could Pei Mianman have stumbled upon a fortuitous encounter or something?","Pei Mianman straightened her posture and looked at Zu An with an air of loftiness. “Big brother Zu, it has been a while, but we have finally reunited.”","Zu An was stunned.","He knew it was Pei Mianman’s cosplay, but he had to admit that her demeanor was indeed identical to the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s. He fell into a daze as he asked, “How did you learn to imitate her?”","“What do you mean, big brother Zu? This is how I have always been. It wasn’t easy for us to be reunited. Shall we head to Wu Mountain to reminisce our old days?” Pei Mianman continued speaking in a lofty manner.","Zu An burst into laughter.","That made Pei Mianman break out of character. “What’s with your expression?”","Zu An explained to her how in his previous world, ‘head to Wu Mountain’ referred to the union of a couple.","That made Pei Mianman’s face redden in embarrassment. “Why does your homeland have so many weird sayings? How indecent!” Thinking about the bold words she had said made her so ashamed that she wanted to bury herself in the ground.","Zu An hugged her. “Your acting is on point. Have you seen her before, or inherited any of her memories?”","Pei Mianman rolled her eyes. “Have you forgotten I’m close friends with Chuyan? Not to mention her master is the same type too. I’m more familiar with the cold beauty sort than anyone else. Copying her is a walk in the park for me.”","The mention of Chuyan and her master brought a tinge of tenderness to Zu An’s heart.","Just then, Xie Daoyun knocked on the door and said, “I don’t want to disturb your reunion, but there’s something I need to discuss with big brother Zu.”","Pei Mianman pushed Zu An away and tidied her clothes. She double-checked that everything was in place before replying, “You don’t have to be so polite. Come in!”","Xie Daoyun entered the room wearing shaman robes. She first glanced at the two of them before finally turning to Zu An. “Big brother Zu, we're almost done preparing for the Lord of Slaughter’s sealing. I thought about it, and I think it would be better for you to participate in the sealing ceremony to intimidate the monsters.”","“All right.” Zu An was aware that not all monsters were willing to retreat to the Monster World. There were still some who harbored hopes that he was bluffing.","Thus, he made his way to the sealing ground with Xie Daoyun. Many fiends were already on standby for the ritual.","To maximize the intimidation factor, Zu An let the Lord of Slaughter out and removed the seal placed on the latter.","The freed Lord of Slaughter angrily roared, “How did I get here? You’re courting death!”","Seeing those he deemed as ants encircling him, the Lord of Slaughter had an inexplicable feeling that he had forgotten something extremely important, but no matter how he racked his brain, he couldn’t recall it.","Zu An was impressed by Diyao’s abilities. The latter had only erased the Lord of Slaughter’s memories to prevent his dirty deeds from leaking out, but this worked out in Zu An’s favor too.","The Lord of Slaughter’s roar intimidated even the bravest Fiend race warriors. The immense pressure he emanated made the fiends gathered here tremble in fear. Even so, he couldn’t shake off the uncanny feeling he had. Thus, he suppressed his bloodlust and instead leaped into the sky with his humongous physique, opting to escape from here first before deciding on his next move.","However, a golden palm print suddenly appeared in midair and slapped him down to earth. The Lord of Slaughter struggled in anger, but he couldn’t break free of the palm.","Boom!","He was crushed into the ground, and a massive pit formed around him. He tried to rise back up, but several mountains were already being piled up on top of him.","Knowing he couldn’t hold back anymore, he unleashed his ultimate skills, causing the mountains on top of him to ripple. It looked as if he would break free at any moment.","Xie Daoyun was prepared for this, however. She flew into the air and began channeling the formation she had prepared beforehand. Formation runes glowed on the mountains, and the quakes shaking the mountains gradually calmed down. By the time the final formation rune was completed, the mountains had already fallen completely still.","The Lord of Slaughter had been completely suppressed.","Deafening cheers broke out from the fiends as they sang praises about Yumen Beiqing. To them, it looked as if their Saintess Yumen Beiqing had sealed the terrifying Lord of Slaughter.","However, the monster experts secretly observing this scene fell into despair. They could tell the truly terrifying one wasn’t the woman, but the man behind her. The Lord of Slaughter had displayed strength comparable to his peak earlier, but he was still suppressed with ease. What hope did they have against an entity like that?","The remaining hawkish monsters unhesitatingly turned dovish. They hurriedly opened their teleportation formations to escape from this terrifying world as fast as they could."]},{"number":2662,"title":"Chapter 2662: Chapter 2614: Going Into the Ocean","paragraphs":["Upon sensing the Monster Lord’s and other powerful entities’ auras leaving this world, Zu An flew into the air, took out the scepter he had obtained from the Monster Lord, and channeled a secret art to activate this world’s barrier. Due to his experience controlling the World Law Beacon in his previous life, he was able to do it smoothly.","Golden streaks of light appeared in the sky. All living beings in this world watched with bated breath as they interwove into a golden net. Despite no one explaining what was going on, they felt an inexplicable sense of calm. They looked at the humongous figure in the sky and speculated who it was.","Those with insider knowledge whispered that he was Saintess Yumen Beiqing’s lover. By this point, none of the fiends were jealous of him anymore. All they had were sincere blessings for the two of them.","The Saintess had truly descended from heaven to save the world. Not only had she turned the tides against the monsters, she'd even managed to seal off the powerful Lord of Slaughter. Even her man was powerful enough to unleash such a massive skill.","As he activated the barrier, Zu An couldn’t help but wonder why this world barrier was weaker compared to the future, despite the richer ki here. This world barrier was nowhere strong enough to seal off the entire world. On top of that, it would gradually weaken over time, eventually reaching a point where it could no longer ward off invaders.","But these things were all inscribed in fate. Since the future him would clean up the mess anyway, he wasn’t too worried about it.","Once the world barrier was reactivated, Zu An made his way to the Ocean races. There were many things he needed to settle, be it the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons or the Netherworld.","Pei Mianman accompanied him. They had been separated for so long that she didn’t want to part ways with him just yet. Zu An missed her dearly too. Each time took a look at her, he couldn’t help but think about the Goddess of Wu Mountain.","The other ladies were envious, but they had other matters to attend to.","Yumen Beiqing, as the Saintess, needed to lead the Fiend races to eradicate the remaining monsters in the world. Yun Yuqing and Suolun Shi, as members of the Fiend races, decided to stand with the people of this world and aid the Saintess. Even though the strongest ones were no longer around, the remaining monsters still posed danger. It would be more reassuring if the three of them could cover one another’s backs.","Ji Xiaoxi remained in the imperial court to concoct the medicine to curb her constitution. The ingredients were all in place now; all that was left was for her to work her expertise.","Instead of using Rainbow Morph, Zu An and Pei Mianman rode on a cloud to the Ocean races. After reaching immortality, he'd naturally learned how to maneuver clouds.","On the cloud, Zu An rested on Pei Mianman’s thighs while the latter massaged his temples. His exhaustion and sorrow were apparent to Pei Mianman, and it left her with a heavy heart. From their conversations, she learned about his interactions with the Goddess of Wu Mountain, but somehow, she was no longer jealous. Instead, she became curious about the other party.","If she was truly my past incarnation, why would she have such a personality? How baffling.","Meanwhile, Zu An was feeling a little better thanks to Pei Mianman’s service. It felt as if he had been hurrying around nonstop and was finally able to catch a breather. Ah, such days are the best!","“Ah Zu, why do you think my personality changed so much?” Pei Mianman suddenly asked.","Zu An knew she was asking about the Goddess of Wu Mountain, so he replied, “I don’t know. Could she have subconsciously channeled her personality toward another direction because I told her about you?”","Pei Mianman shook her head. “It’s possible for a person’s character to change, but not to that extent. I do have a thought in mind though...”","“What is it?” Zu An’s curiosity was piqued.","“Forget it. You’ll laugh at me,” Pei Mianman replied after some thought.","“So what is it?” Her refusal to speak only further stoked Zu An’s desire to know.","“When you first talked about the Goddess of Wu Mountain, I thought she resembled Chuyan more than me,” Pei Mianman spoke in a much softer voice than before. “Is there a chance that she reincarnated not as me, but as... Chuyan?”","Zu An was startled. Her conjecture sounded credible. Putting their appearances aside, Yaoji’s personality is identical to Chuyan’s.","He was reminded of the suffering Chuyan had suffered under the Bridge of Helplessness, and it made his heart clench up. He couldn’t bring himself to continue lying on Pei Mianman’s thigh anymore.","Pei Mianman noticed his expression and immediately regretted mentioning Chuyan, so she tried changing the topic. “I don’t think the possibility is big though, considering how our appearances are identical. It’s more likely that something huge happened to her, resulting in the change to her personality.”","Zu An thought about the projection left by the Goddess of Wu Mountain, but her character seemed the same then.","While discussing this matter, they arrived above the ocean before they knew it. Zu An dove into the ocean with Pei Mianman in his arms. The seawater naturally parted for him, and a flight of stairs even formed to welcome him.","Pei Mianman was awed. Which woman can withstand such a romantic scene? No wonder Ah Zu has so many beautiful women chasing after him no matter where he goes!","She thought about how she had even gotten jealous of herself, and that evoked her laughter.","The commotion on the ocean surface soon caught the Dragon Palace’s attention. The Four Dragon Kings led their men out to investigate the situation. They were initially tense, but upon seeing Zu An, they revealed relieved smiles.","“Lord Necropolis, have you accomplished your mission?” the Dragon Kings asked as they bowed to Zu An, though they couldn’t help but notice that Zu An was accompanied by another beautiful woman on par with the Mermaid Queen.","Pei Mianman was surprised by how the Ocean races addressed Zu An, but she didn’t expose him.","“I’m done with most of it. I’ll be making a trip to the Mermaid race,” Zu An said grimly.","The Four Dragon Kings exchanged looks, and they could see the worry in one another’s eyes. Could something bad have happened to the Mermaid Queen for him to return without her?","The Mermaid Queen was the Ocean races’ dream lover. Even the Four Dragon Kings harbored tremendous goodwill for her. How could they not grieve if something happened to her?","Soon, they arrived at the Mermaid race’s territory. The elders of the Mermaid race rushed out upon hearing the news.","“Lord Necropolis, where is my queen? Why didn’t she return with you?” A maid rushed out from the crowd and grabbed Zu An’s sleeves. Her eyes reflected her trepidation. She was afraid that she would receive bad news.","She was the Mermaid Queen’s maid, Peach. She had been awaiting both their return, only for one to return alone. How could she not be horrified?","Zu An grimly replied, “I’m here to talk about that. Something has happened to the Mermaid Queen...”","A huge uproar broke out before he could finish speaking his piece.","“Is our queen dead?”","“How can that be? How can she be dead?”","...","Most present were loyal fans of the Mermaid Queen. There were also women who were jealous of her, and they rejoiced at the news despite feigning sorrow.","“Suyin isn’t dead yet, but she’s currently stuck in a palace and won’t be able to return for the time being,” Zu An explained.","“What do you mean by that?” Peach anxiously asked.","Zu An roughly explained the Mermaid Queen’s plight to the crowd, which prompted the crowd to raise their heads to look at the moon. The Mermaid Queen is on the moon?","Some thought to themselves that if she couldn’t return here ever again, the Mermaid Queen was as good as dead to them.","Only Peach rejoiced at the news. There’s hope as long as my queen is alive!","Zu An continued, “It won’t do for the Mermaid race to be without a ruler. The Mermaid Queen has tasked me to relay her intention to pass down her position to the Shang clan.”","The Mermaid race didn’t question his words, especially since they already had the tradition of alternating the ruler position among their five major clans of Gong, Shang, Jiao, Zhi, and Yu. Gong Suyin had no offspring, and there was no one suitable in the Gong clan to take her position. It made sense for her to pass the throne on to the Shang clan.","Her edict made the succession more legitimate.","Zu An felt dazed.","They could have placed another member of the Gong clan on the throne, but Gong Suyin had still decided to pass the position on to the Shang clan while they were chatting in the Frost Palace. She appeared to have made that decision after learning that Shang Hongyu and Shang Liuyu were descendants of the future Mermaid Queen.","Did the past determine the future, or did the future determine the past?","After settling the Mermaid race’s affairs, Zu An proceeded to share what had happened in the dungeon with the Four Dragon Kings. He also told them that most of the monsters had left the world, and thus, the world was finally at peace now.","The Ocean races cheered at the news. They even declared that they would build a divine temple in the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons to commemorate his accomplishment.","Zu An tried to dissuade them, but the Ocean races were adamant. They even said that they would work with the Asuras and the Shamans to build the most majestic palace ever.","That left Zu An in a daze. Hold on, that palace I saw in the future was built for me?","After dealing with the Ocean races, Zu An made his way to the Netherworld. There were many questions in his mind that he needed someone to answer."]},{"number":2663,"title":"Chapter 2663: Chapter 2615: Confrontation","paragraphs":["Pei Mianman requested to accompany him.","Zu An wanted to turn her down, since the death energy was extremely dangerous to the living, but on second thought, he decided to bring her along. He brought her to the Eye of the Ocean, where they were faced with the bleak abyss. Even Pei Mianman shuddered at the sight.","“Don’t worry. I’m here.” Zu An wrapped his arm around her slender waist before leaping into the abyss.","His words calmed Pei Mianman’s anxious heart. Indeed, as long as he’s by my side, I wouldn’t fear a mountain of blades or a sea of fire.","Grayish-white energy lingered in their surroundings as they descended the abyss. Zu An wrapped Pei Mianman with a brilliant light that shielded her from the energy. His cultivation was now strong enough to thoroughly protect his companion from harm.","As soon as they entered the Netherworld, a massive army mounted on elephants rushed over to confront them. The men were hideous, but the women were gorgeous.","“Who dares...” As soon as they recognized Zu An, the soldiers’ hostile faces lit up in delight.","The beautiful woman at the army’s forefront leaped off her elephant and landed before Zu An. “Big brother Necropolis, you’re finally here! Hm? Who is she?”","She was the Asura race’s Princess Ni Huang. She had been anticipating Zu An’s return for quite some time now, only for the other party to return with another woman. She instinctively glanced at Pei Mianman’s chest, and her breath caught in her throat for several seconds.","What a pair of lewd boobs! Hmph! She’s no fighter. I bet she’s baggage in battle!","While Princess Ni Huang was sizing up Pei Mianman, the latter did the same too. Princess Ni Huang was truly beautiful, especially when contrasted against the hideous Asura men standing around her. Her copper skin tone made her look vibrant, as if she was radiating energy itself.","“Ah Zu, is it just me, or does she resemble Qinghe...” Pei Mianman discreetly asked Zu An via telepathy. Their facial features are identical, though compared to the youthful Murong Qinghe, this woman feels more mature. She also resembles Mo Xi a little...","She could tell that the latter fancied Zu An from Princess Ni Huang’s hostile gaze.","Ah Zu is too much! Why is he drawing in bees everywhere? First Chang’e, then the Goddess of Wu Mountain, and now some Princess Ni Huang too?","Zu An stood in a daze. His encounter with the Goddess of Wu Mountain had convinced him about the concept of reincarnation in this world. Murong Qinghe might be Princess Ni Huang’s future incarnation, and Mo Xi might be Princess Ni Huang’s past incarnation.","He had left Mo Xi in the Frost Palace, hoping that one day, she could grow strong enough to sever Gong Suyin’s contract with the Frost Palace. If Mo Xi has reincarnated, could it mean that something bad happened at the Frost Palace that resulted in her death? If so, something might have happened to Gong Suyin too.","Princess Ni Huang was initially angry, but her anger dissipated when she noticed Zu An staring at her in a daze. Sweetness tinged her heart. I knew he liked me more! Ahh, but there’s so many people looking at us. How embarrassing!","There was a cough, and the Asura King descended to their side. “Brother Necropolis, did everything go well?” I know my little sister is beautiful, but isn’t it too much for you to gawk at her when you already have a gorgeous babe with you? You’re putting me in a tight spot here!","Zu An finally snapped out of his daze. “Ah, it went fine.”","Loud rumbling echoed in the distance. Ox Head and Horse Face had rushed over upon hearing the commotion.","When they saw Zu An, they quickly shrank their gigantic physiques and gave him a tight hug. “My brother, you’re incredible!”","They had already heard about the monsters’ eviction from this world, and they were awed by his prowess.","Zu An smiled in response. “I hope you've been fine.”","“Peeps like us remain the same for centuries. It’s all fine,” Ox Head said with a laugh. He suddenly noticed Pei Mianman and exclaimed in bewilderment, “Hm? Why did the lady with you suddenly change? What happened to the Mermaid Queen you were previously with?”","Horse Face quietly kicked Ox Head. Can’t you tell that our Necropolis bro is a player? You shouldn’t be talking about his other lovers right now!","Ox Head quickly realized that and scratched his head awkwardly. He struggled to find the words to alleviate the atmosphere.","Zu An held Pei Mianman’s hand and gently said, “She is Pei Mianman, my wife...”","Pei Mianman hadn’t expected him to introduce her as such in public. The word ‘wife’ filled her with indescribable bliss.","She noticed Princess Ni Huang’s face turning pale and her eyes becoming glazed. Sighing softly, she put on a smile before grabbing the latter’s hand, saying, “You must be Princess Ni Huang. He often mentions you. You resemble a little sister of mine a lot.”","“Little sister?” A rush of curiosity dampened Princess Ni Huang’s sorrow. “I heard him mention something like that before. Who is it?”","Pei Mianman patiently told her about Murong Qinghe and Mo Xi, though she did reserve some information too.","To others, it looked as if Pei Mianman accepted her husband’s philandering ways and even magnanimously extended her goodwill to Princess Ni Huang. This made them extremely awed by Zu An. Not only does he have a lot of lovers, but they're all so caring too.","Zu An proceeded to tell them about what had happened to the Mermaid Queen too. The others were at a loss for words.","Naturally, he didn’t forget about his goal here either. After a quick explanation, he went off to look for Lady Houtu.","Soon, he arrived at the Reincarnation Platform. Ox Head and Horse Face kneeled and kowtowed. “Milady, Brother Necropolis has accomplished his mission and returned.”","A female silhouette soon appeared on the Reincarnation Platform, and a powerful aura rippled outward.","Startled, Pei Mianman looked at Zu An with worried eyes. Why is there such a powerful expert here?","Zu An patted her hand to calm her down.","“Have you found the six races' power insignias?” The female silhouette nodded at Zu An.","“You could say that.” Zu An suddenly changed his tone. “But there are a few things I’d like to ask you.”","The female silhouette gestured to the crowd. “I need to talk to him in private. You may leave first.”","Ox Head and Horse Face respectfully took their leave.","The Asura King and Princess Ni Huang frowned. “Houtu, we aren’t your subordinates.”","The female silhouette wasn’t angered by their refusal to obey. “Asura King, you should know how dangerous some secrets are. There’s no benefit in knowing too much.”","A thought came to the Asura King’s mind, and he narrowed his eyes. With a harrumph, he grabbed his little sister’s hand and left the place. Before he walked out, he turned to Zu An and said, “Necropolis, just call for us if you need our help. We’ll rush in right away.”","“Thanks!” Zu An was thankful for the sentiment. The Asuras were fierce, but they were loyal.","After the others were gone, the female silhouette finally turned to Zu An and asked, “What do you want to know?”","“Were you the one who sent the Mermaid Queen and the others to that Celestial Court world?” Zu An asked coldly."]},{"number":2664,"title":"Chapter 2664: Chapter 2616: Negotiation","paragraphs":["“It sounds as if you’re interrogating me,” Houtu replied with a voice so impassive that it no longer sounded human.","“Should I not be angry? She wouldn’t have been trapped in that world if you hadn’t sent her there,” Zu An replied in a severe tone. The Mermaid Queen had been faring perfectly well here, but Houtu’s intervention had caused her to be trapped in the Frost Palace as Chang’e.","“I was indeed the one who sent her back in time. It wasn't just her, but your other lovers too,” Houtu replied unhurriedly.","“Why did you do that?” Zu An was both perplexed and infuriated.","“You can think of it as their fate.” Houtu’s voice carried a mystical air. “These events are all inscribed in their fate.”","“But all this wouldn’t have happened if not for your intervention!” Zu An retorted. Even Jiang Luofu had gone missing in the Celestial Court world as well.","“How do you know it’s not their fate?” Houtu returned the question.","Zu An was taken aback. Many thoughts flashed through his mind. A long time later, he slowly asked, “Can you see fate?”","Houtu slowly replied, “As the governor of reincarnation, I can vaguely see the trajectory of fate, but I’m not all-knowing. Often, it comes as a brief impulse, guiding me as to how I can achieve a certain goal.”","“I heard something similar from Zhuanxu. He said that time is an inconsequential concept to beings like him. He gave the ‘future’ me the Sun Slaying Bow so that the ‘past’ me could use it to shoot down the suns,” Zu An said as he tried to make sense of the situation. “I also met a Houtu in the Celestial Court world. She bestowed unto me a droplet of the Shaman races’ blood essence. Would it be right to say that you two are the same entity? That Houtu knows about me and the mission you entrusted me with.”","“Your understanding is too simple and riddled with errors, but given your current conceptualization of the world, you can indeed think of it that way.” Houtu was surprised that he could figure out this much.","“Emperor Jun sought to attain Sainthood by vanquishing the Shaman races. Emperor Yao sought to attain Sainthood through the prosperity of the human race. All powerhouses aim to reach Sainthood in their own way. Now that I think about it, it’s probably the same for you.” Zu An looked at the powerful silhouette before him. “The only difference is that they failed, whereas you succeeded.”","Pei Mianman blinked. Ever since her child days, she had always been complimented for her wits, so why was it that she couldn’t follow the conversation before her? I feel like a dimwit.","“You’re half right. I did this to attain Sainthood, but I have yet to reach it,” Houtu candidly replied.","Zu An looked unfazed. “You still need the things in my hand to forge the Six Paths of Reincarnation in order to attain Sainthood.”","Houtu’s way of attaining Sainthood was through the Six Paths of Reincarnation. This system allowed wandering ghosts to reincarnate, and it also encouraged individuals to do more good and commit less evil so that they could reincarnate into better lives. It went without saying that this was a vast contribution to the world.","“You’re right. My Sainthood is founded on the Six Paths of Reincarnation.” Houtu eyed Zu An. “Are you thinking of blackmailing me through this?”","Zu An chuckled. “That is indeed what I have in mind. You need the Six Worlds’ power insignias to attain Sainthood. You can try taking them from me by force, but since you haven’t attained Sainthood yet, I have the power to resist.”","Pei Mianman tensed up. They sounded like friends earlier. Why does it sound as if they're going to come to blows?","She was determined to stand with Zu An, so she secretly channeled her cultivation, ready to make a move at any moment. But this time, our enemy is an enigmatic silhouette. I wonder how I can hurt something like that.","“You forgot. You said it yourself. Time is inconsequential to beings such as us. The past me, the present me, and the future me are one entity. The future me has attained Sainthood. You don’t have the means to deal with the present me,” Houtu replied impassively, as if she was talking about something unrelated to her.","Zu An’s heart sank. He knew she was right, but he couldn’t give up. “You can’t forge the Six Paths of Reincarnation without the power insignias I've collected. That will hinder your path to Sainthood.”","“It looks as if you still have yet to understand the mechanisms of time and history. My attainment of Sainthood in the future is a fact, which means that it will happen with or without you. Someone may aid me in this task in the future. The trajectory of fate is beyond an individual’s means to alter,” Houtu replied.","Zu An thought about how Xihe had done everything she could to change the conclusion of the Ten Suns’ downfall, only for her attempts to end in vain.","Mi Li had also once told him that important points in history, once determined, could no longer be changed. Houtu’s forging of the Six Paths of Reincarnation and attainment of Sainthood was one such important event that couldn’t change.","But Zu An didn’t give up because of that. “Your Sainthood is inevitable, but you still aren’t a Saint yet. Someone else might help you collect the six power insignias if I refuse to cooperate with you here, but you risk losing a lot of time. Who knows how many more years it will take you to get there?”","Houtu shook her head. “You don’t understand beings such as us. What appears to be a long time to you humans is nothing more than a nap to us.”","“Perhaps I didn’t phrase it well enough. Let me put it in another way. If I don’t help you now, you may face many more variables in your path to Sainthood. Existences like you fear nothing more than variables, no?” Zu An asked calmly. “A Houtu will attain Sainthood in the future, but are you certain you will be that Houtu?”","He was using the knowledge he'd learned from the Ten Suns’ incident. Important points in history couldn’t be changed, but a slight change in the process could make a world of difference in the nuances, such as him becoming Yi in the past.","Houtu showed a rare emotional fluctuation. “I have to say that you’re an intelligent human. You have convinced me. Speak, what do you want?” Human politics had little meaning to beings like her. She knew what Zu An was after.","“Help me save the Mermaid Queen and Jiang Luofu,” Zu An said. He could have simply requested her help, but he'd been worried that Houtu wouldn't give it her all since it didn’t concern her.","Houtu frowned. “Ask for something else. What you’re asking for is beyond my means.”","Zu An grabbed Pei Mianman and turned around to leave. “You can find someone else to collect your six power insignias then.”"]},{"number":2665,"title":"Chapter 2665: Chapter 2617: Predetermined Fate","paragraphs":["“Wait!” Unsurprisingly, Houtu quickly called for him. “You would be helping yourself by helping me too.”","“What do you mean by that?” Zu An asked.","“Too much time has passed since that era, not to mention the Mermaid Queen is imprisoned in the Frost Palace. I couldn’t help you right now even if I wanted to,” Houtu patiently explained.","“What about Jiang Luofu? You were the one who sent her into the past. Don’t tell me you can’t do anything about that either.” Zu An suppressed his anger as he negotiated.","“Jiang Luofu’s strong emotions caught the attention of an exalted entity. That’s her fate, as well as her fortuitous encounter. You don’t need to worry about her.” Houtu’s voice quivered when she mentioned the words ‘exalted entity’.","Zu An recalled hearing similar words from Zhuanxu. Looks like she isn’t in any danger for now. Still, he asked, “Who is that entity?”","“You should already be aware that secrets are dangerous. You aren’t strong enough yet. Learning about that entity right now will only result in your destruction.”","Zu An fell silent. He knew about that rule, and he wasn’t a reckless brute either, so he didn’t continue harping on this matter. Instead, he changed the topic and asked, “Is that entity stronger than you and the Celestial Emperors?”","Houtu nodded. “His strength not only surpasses ours, but Saints too. This is our first time learning about beings stronger than Saints.”","Zu An was speechless. Sainthood was usually the peak for most myths and webnovels. He hadn’t expected there to be an even higher level than that.","He suddenly thought about the Time Scribe and the information he'd received from Mi Li, and a thought popped into his mind.","There must be countless worlds in the universe.","Entities like Houtu, even after attaining Sainthood, only command influence within the Six Worlds. Other worlds don’t necessarily recognize her, or there could be other deities in the same position as her.","The stronger entities could be some kind of conceptual god that exists across all worlds in the universe.","This thought sparked the fighting spirit in Zu An. Now that he had a goal in mind, his thoughts suddenly felt clearer than ever. He then asked, “Why bother stopping me when you can’t do anything to help me?”","“To help me is to help yourself.” Houtu got straight to the point. “If you help me in the forging of the Six Paths of Reincarnation, I can use its power to help the Mermaid Queen...”","She paused a second and glanced at Pei Mianman. “...As well as the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s incarnation.","“Reincarnation has to be impartial; it is bound to the laws of the world. What I can do here undermines the system. My main body will suffer a severe backlash because of it, but considering how much you have helped me, I am willing to pay this price.”","Pei Mianman’s heart skipped a beat. She had been wondering if the Goddess of Wu Mountain was truly her previous incarnation, and whether it could have been a coincidence that they resembled each other. Their personalities were vastly different, after all.","But Houtu’s glance appeared to suggest otherwise.","Zu An said grimly, “But they're different people to me. What you’re offering means nothing to the Goddess of Wu Mountain of that era.”","“You need to widen your perspective. Once you’re on a higher level, you’ll come to realize that a person’s appearance, personality, and experiences may change when reincarnated, but their core remains the same. They are still the same person.”","Zu An frowned. He didn’t agree with Houtu’s perception, which conflated two different people into a single entity.","Sensing his indignation, Houtu added, “You need to think it through. What will become of your current lovers if you refuse to let them reincarnate? Do you wish for them to cease to exist?”","“What?!” Zu An was taken aback to hear that. He instinctively glanced at Pei Mianman, only to see her usual reddened face looking a little pale.","“You don’t have to feel so conflicted. A few things happened in that era afterward. Their only option was to reincarnate,” Houtu added.","“What happened?” Judging from the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s projection, Zu An had realized that a major incident had to have happened in that era, but the latter refused to elaborate on it. Houtu would no doubt know more about the matter.","Houtu shook his head. “Very coincidentally, I lost a portion of my memories and don’t remember what happened there. I only vaguely recall there being a major disaster.”","Zu An was startled. Even an entity like Houtu can suffer from memory loss? Did she suffer an injury in that disaster?","He thought about how the Mermaid Queen and the Goddess of Wu Mountain had waited for countless years in vain for him, and eventually faced such a terrifying disaster by themselves. That made his heart ache. He asked, “Was it caused by the war between the Shamans and the Fiends?”","“I don’t think so. The war between the Shamans and the Fiends was a huge calamity, but it ended in mutual destruction for both sides, and they retreated from the front lines together. The human race began to prosper afterward. The two events should be unrelated,” Houtu deduced.","Zu An also remembered the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s projection mentioning that she had waited over tens of thousands of years, during which there hadn’t seemed to be any major disaster.","“I have offered you a solution, and this is the most I can do as well. Now, it’s just a question of whether you want to accept the deal or not. In the worst case, I’ll just take another nap and wait for the next person who is willing to help me. You should know that I succeeded in forging the Six Paths of Reincarnation in history,” Houtu calmly pointed out.","Time indeed had little meaning to an entity like her.","Zu An pondered hard, and he was forced to concede that her words made sense. He had no idea what disaster had happened in that era, but the only thing he could do for the Mermaid Queen and the Goddess of Wu Mountain was to prepare a way out for them. Thus, he took out the power insignias.","Houtu’s expression turned serious. She moved her hands around, creating a swirling vortex. This vortex was much smaller than the Eye of the Ocean, but it looked far darker and deeper. Intense death energy could be felt from it, but it carried hints of overflowing life energy too.","Houtu flicked her sleeves, and the six power insignias floated toward six different directions. They extended a ray of light toward the vortex, filling it with six different colors.","Zu An and Pei Mianman saw flickers of countless worlds in each of the colors. This was a sign that the Six Paths of Reincarnation was establishing its connection with the countless worlds in the Six Paths.","Houtu said, “I am about to be assimilated into the Six Paths of Reincarnation. You have accrued tremendous karma in aiding me in the construction of the Six Paths of Reincarnation. The will of the world will remember this. After the Six Paths of Reincarnation are formed, the Netherworld will be required for their functioning. You are fated to be the master of the Netherworld. Are you willing to take on this role, Necropolis Emperor?”"]},{"number":2666,"title":"Chapter 2666: Chapter 2618: Vow","paragraphs":["The mention of the words ‘Necropolis Emperor’ left Zu An in a daze. For a moment there, he felt as if he was fulfilling his destiny.","In the future, he'd stepped into the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons, entered the Netherworld, and obtained the Necropolis Emperor’s legacy. But now, he had returned to the past. In order to not influence the timeline, he'd decided on a whim to use ‘Necropolis’ as his alias. Little had he expected to become the Necropolis Emperor in history.","In other words, I'm my own successor?","Even the most dimwitted person could feel the inexplicable pull of fate here.","“I never expected myself to become the Necropolis Emperor. I wonder what happens to the Necropolis Emperor in the future,” Zu An remarked. By the time he inherited the other party’s legacy, the Necropolis Emperor had already gone missing. That mystery made him hesitant to take on this position.","But rejection wasn't an option. The world needed the Netherworld and the Necropolis Emperor to ensure the functioning of the Six Paths of Reincarnation. There was no better candidate than him right now.","Sensing his thoughts, Houtu said, “Don’t worry about being bound to the identity of the Necropolis Emperor. You are the Necropolis Emperor, but the Necropolis Emperor doesn’t have to be you.”","Zu An narrowed his eyes. “What do you mean?”","“I can’t reveal the secrets of the future.” Houtu didn’t elaborate. Her silhouette began to thin as specks of light flew out of her and into the Six Paths of Reincarnation. The Six Paths radiated a sacred glow—that was the amalgamation of life and death. It slowly began to spin. Despite its smaller size, it felt vast and enigmatic like the stars in the sky.","A peculiar resonance rippled outward, and the Netherworld began to change. The tangible, grayish-white death energy greatly thinned, revealing the previously concealed Oblivion River and Yin Mountain. The terrain also began to terraform, collapsing and rebuilding itself. Everything soon began to resemble the Netherworld Zu An remembered in his memories.","Upon noticing the commotion, Ox Head, Horse Face, and the Asuras rushed in. With terrified faces, they asked, “What happened?”","“Lady Houtu has become one with the cycle of reincarnation.” Zu An summarized what had happened earlier, and that caused the Shaman race to burst into tears.","Since their defeat in the war between the Shamans and the Fiends, they had been hiding in this dark place. Ancestral Shaman Houtu was their final pillar of support. Now that even Houtu was gone, how could they not suffer a mental breakdown?","Zu An consoled them, “You need not grieve. Lady Houtu isn’t dead yet. She’s merely living in another form. She has already attained Sainthood and became one with the world. You should be happy for her.”","Despite his words, he didn’t know whether it was an evolution or a death for a living being to turn into the unfeeling Six Paths of Reincarnation. He dispelled those thoughts from his mind and continued, “Lady Houtu has planned a way out for you. I’ll be establishing the Netherworld here to govern ghosts from different worlds and facilitate the Six Paths of Reincarnation. You'll become deities of the Netherworld and enjoy the worship of the mortal world.”","The knowledge that they could become deities assuaged the Shamans’ sorrow. Ox Head and Horse Face bowed to Zu An. “Lord Necropolis, Lady Houtu has also told us about this matter. We’re under your command now!”","“You’re being too polite.” Zu An supported them upright before turning to the Asuras. “Asura King, Princess Ni Huang, once the Netherworld is established, I’ll be able to use the Six Paths of Reincarnation to open a path back to the Asura World for you.”","The Asura King voiced his doubts. “Won’t we be reincarnated if we travel through the Six Paths of Reincarnation?”","Zu An explained, “I don’t mean for you to reincarnate through the Six Paths of Reincarnation. Rather, I plan to use the Six Paths of Reincarnation’s power to open a corresponding world. Given how you have the complete Asura World’s power insignia, it shouldn’t be too hard.”","A thought suddenly popped into his mind. Can’t I use this power to open the Celestial Court world and look for the Mermaid Queen and the Goddess of Wu Mountain?","He quickly gave up on that thought, however.","The Asura King had the complete Asura World’s power insignia. It remained mostly intact even after Houtu used it in the forging of the Six Paths of Reincarnation. That was why Zu An could use the Six Paths of Reincarnation’s power, with the Asura World’s power insignia as a medium, to open up a passageway to the Asura World.","In contrast, he had only received a fragment of the Celestial World’s power insignia from Zhuanxu, and it had been completely consumed for the forging of the Six Paths of Reincarnation. Without the Celestial World’s power insignia, he wouldn’t be able to open a passageway to the Celestial World.","That filled him with regret. I should have stolen the complete power insignia from Zhuanxu!","Of course, that could only remain a thought. Zhuanxu, as a Celestial Emperor, could easily crush him just by the sheer disparity in their cultivation. Attempting to steal the Celestial World’s power insignia from Zhuanxu would have been tantamount to suicide.","The Asuras cheered in delight. Only Princess Ni Huang appeared to be brooding.","For the next few days, Zu An drafted up the Netherworld’s blueprints based on his memories. Fortunately, he didn’t need to draft it out comprehensively on paper the way architects had in his previous life. All he needed to do was to create a projection to show the buildings.","The Shaman races enthusiastically commenced construction. Their superior strength allowed them to build with exceptional efficiency.","The Asura race also lent a helping hand for the construction. They worked with the Shaman races to erect a massive sculpture at the entrance of the Netherworld.","Even the Ocean races cooperated with them to construct a complementary palace for the sculpture in the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons.","Zu An was embarrassed, but the Asura King, Ox Head, and Horse Face insisted he needed a sculpture to emphasize his exalted standing. Besides, the sculpture had the pragmatic effect of encouraging faith and intimidating troublemakers. Knowing that the sculpture existed in history, he reluctantly accepted it.","Later, however, it suddenly struck him that he'd forgotten to instruct them on the sculpture’s design. By the time he checked on the sculpture, he realized that it didn’t have distinctive facial features, the same way he remembered it in history.","He asked the Asura King about it, and the latter replied with a chuckle, “It was my little sister’s idea. She said a deity’s appearance shouldn’t be casually revealed, and we thought her explanation made sense. She was the one who designed this sculpture.”","After explaining the sculpture, the Asura King took his leave to give Zu An some private time with Princess Ni Huang,","“Thank you, princess.” Zu An could tell that much thought had been put into the majestic sculpture.","“You’re still being so polite with me,” Princess Ni Huang remarked with conflicted eyes. She sighed softly before continuing on, “Big brother Necropolis, I wanted to stay here with you, but I’m a member of the Asura royal family. I enjoyed a privileged life, growing up with luxuries and the best cultivation resources. I can’t abandon my clan when its fate is uncertain. I have to aid my royal brother in settling the new world. Do you blame me for that?”","“No, I only respect you more. A woman who doesn’t lose herself to emotions will only charm more men,” Zu An replied.","Princess Ni Huang was delighted to hear that. She patted his shoulder and said, “As expected of the man I've set my eyes on. Once things in the new world settle down, I’ll return to look for you.”","Zu An briefly hesitated before revealing his true background. “Actually, I'm not from this world.”","“I guessed as much.” Princess Ni Huang wasn’t disappointed to hear that. “Can you tell me your true identity?”","Looking into her sincere eyes, Zu An chose to divulge his identity to her.","Princess Ni Huang murmured his name to etch it into her mind. All of a sudden, she leaned in and kissed his lips before fleeing. “Big brother Zu, I’ll definitely find you in the future!”","Shortly after she left, Pei Mianman popped out of nowhere and remarked, “You can keep her with you if you can’t bear to part ways with her.”","Zu An shook his head as he looked at Princess Ni Huang’s departing figure. “She has her own mission to fulfill.”","Pei Mianman sighed. “I used to think that you’re a horrible philanderer who went around seducing women, but your life seems pretty tough too.”","“Manman, I’m glad you finally understand my struggles!”","“Don’t push your luck!”"]},{"number":2667,"title":"Chapter 2667: Chapter 2619: Asura’s Tear","paragraphs":["Strong people weren't lacking among the Shamans, the Asuras, and the Ocean races. They built structures even more quickly than the modern world's technology could manage. What they struggled with was formation designs.","Fortunately, the three races had a strong foundation, and Zu An was adept in formations. It took time, but they gradually perfected each of the formations.","As their work approached completion, however, Princess Ni Huang seemed to smile less.","Soon, it was time for them to part ways. Zu An used a secret art to channel the Six Paths of Reincarnation’s power to open a passageway to the Asura World, allowing all the Asuras to return home.","Princess Ni Huang was the last to leave. The Asura King sighed from the passageway and urged her, “Ni Huang, we should get going.”","Princess Ni Huang lowered her head and replied with a “Mm”. All of a sudden, she rushed toward Zu An and gave him a tight hug. Feeling a wet sensation on his shoulder, Zu An’s body stiffened up a little. In the end, he raised his hands to gently embrace her back.","Pei Mianman displayed no jealousy at that sight. If anything, she only felt wistful. After what had happened with the Mermaid Queen and the Goddess of Wu Mountain, she realized that there was no point getting jealous of lovers who were separated across spacetime.","“Ni Huang, the passageway is about to close,” the Asura King anxiously urged. Opening a passageway between worlds was bound to require a tremendous amount of resources. It had taken a lot of time for the other Asuras to cross the passageway; the chances were that Zu An was already reaching his limit.","“Don’t forget me!” Princess Ni Huang said as she wiped off her tears and ran after her brother. Shortly after she entered the passageway, its entrance closed.","Ox Head and Horse Face walked up to Zu An’s side and said, “The Asuras pride themselves on being a warrior race. They see courage and strength as a virtue. Tears are a symbol of weakness for the Asuras, which is why they never cry except in one scenario.”","“What scenario?” Zu An asked worriedly as he recalled Princess Ni Huang’s earlier tears.","“An Asura woman crying for her lover. They only cry if their feelings for their lover have reached an extreme, to the point of causing them great anguish.” Ox Head and Horse Face were awed. Zu An and Ni Huang had only known each other for a short time, but he had already charmed the Asura race’s princess to this degree.","Zu An’s heart clenched. He fell silent for a long time before Pei Mianman walked to his side and gently grasped his hand. Her consolation brought some warmth back to his icy-cold body.","Following that, Zu An selected the Ten Yamas[1] and established all kinds of roles for the Shamans to take on. He couldn’t stay here for long, so he needed to make sure everything was in place to ensure that the Netherworld could run on its own.","At the same time, he wondered why all the ghost guards were missing when the future him arrived at the Netherworld. What happened to them, and where did they go? The more he learned, the more insignificant he felt. There were simply too many things that he was utterly helpless about.","Nevertheless, he still had to try his best. He looked for Ox Head and Horse Face and subtly reminded them to leave a message in the vicinity of the Six Paths of Reincarnation if something huge happened to the Netherworld in the future. In the Netherworld, other than the Oblivion River and Yin Mountain, the Six Paths of Reincarnation were likely the most resistant to the erosion of time.","Ox Head and Horse Face were confused, but they still thumped their chests and gave their word. Zu An made a mental note to check the Six Paths of Reincarnation for information once he returned to his timeline.","Last but not least, he slipped the new World Law Beacon into the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons' palace. He looked at the Mermaid Queen sculpture that was based off Gong Suyin and solemnly bade her farewell.","Everything was finally in place. He turned down the Shamans' and Ocean races' offer to stay and began making his way back to the Fiend races’ imperial court.","While riding on a cloud, Zu An asked the accompanying beauty, “Manman, you seem much quieter in recent days. Is there something on your mind?”","“Too much has happened recently. I’m feeling wistful.” Pei mianman leaned on Zu An’s shoulder while hugging his arm. “After seeing what happened to the others, I can’t help but wonder if we’ll face such a separation in the future too.”","“Let’s cherish every day.” The past Zu An would have promised to protect her well, but after everything he had been through, he'd learned that there were too many things in the world that were beyond his ability to change.","Pei Mianman nodded. Without any warning, she leaned in and kissed him.","There had been too many eyes on them in the past few days, be it in the Netherworld or the Dragon Palace, and it didn’t help that they'd had their hands full with work too. The two of them had hardly enjoyed any private time together. The two of them had too many pent-up emotions that they urgently needed to vent.","There was no need for words; they were too familiar with each other. It didn’t take long for them to be glued together.","“It’s broad daylight. Will anyone see us?”","“Don’t worry. We’re in the sky.”","“What if some powerful cultivators pass by or look toward the sky?”","“No wonder you’re more sensitive than usual. So that’s what you’re worried about!”","“Hey! Don’t talk nonsense!”","...","A cloud in the sky shook intensely for a while. Pei Mianman exclaimed worriedly, “Will this cloud break apart? You need to be gentler!”","“Don’t worry, it won’t break apart.”","...","Looking at the red spider lily tattoo that had appeared on Pei Mianman's lower back due to a rush of blood, Zu An asked, “You often went into a daze whenever we traveled through the Yellow Spring. Were you looking at the red spider lilies?”","Zu An had been busy putting the Netherworld into order, and Pei Mianman had been serving as his secretary. However, in her free time, she had sat by the Yellow Spring and stare dazedly at the red spider lilies.","“Why are you saying this now... I just found the red spider lilies familiar, and it sparked some inspiration.”","“Oh? What kind of inspiration?”","“It’s hard to put it in words. The Paramita Butterfly I acquired seems intricately linked to the Netherworld’s red spider lilies, but I still don’t know what that black butterfly is...”","Pei Mianman suddenly let out an exclamation—Zu An had interrupted her reply. It quickly dawned on her that Zu An wasn’t sincere about those questions either. She felt so frustrated that she clawed him like a little kitten.","...","Xie Daoyun and the others had already gotten anxious from waiting by the time they returned to the Fiend races’ imperial court. Upon seeing the two of them, they breathed a sigh of relief.","“We received news that you were returning, but you were nowhere to be seen even after waiting a while. We thought you encountered danger along the way.”","“I told you. There’s nothing in this world that can threaten big brother Zu now.”","“Hm? Are you sick, Manman? Why is your face so red? Xiaoxi, you should take a look at her.”","...","Pei Mianman was horrified. She would die of shame if Ji Xiaoxi saw through her.","At the most crucial moment, however, Zu An stepped forward and rescued her. “Now that our business here is settled, it’s about time for us to return to our world.”","1. The ten great kings of hell. ☜"]},{"number":2668,"title":"Chapter 2668: Chapter 2620: Reunion","paragraphs":["The other ladies reined in their teasing smiles and solemnly replied, “All right.”","They had first arrived in this ancient spacetime fragment before being transported into the even older Celestial Court world. So many things had happened that it felt as if they had already lived a lifetime.","Only Ji Xiaoxi was hesitant. “What about my little aunt?”","Zu An patted her head and consoled her, “Don’t worry, I checked with Houtu. Big sister principal isn’t in danger. This is a fortuitous encounter for her.”","That lessened Ji Xiaoxi’s worry.","The others asked Zu An about how his trip to the ocean had gone, so Zu An shared the story with them. In the meantime, the other ladies dragged Pei Mianman aside and asked her if Zu An had encountered any other beauties in the ocean.","Pei Mianman immediately thought of Princess Ni Huang, but she decided against revealing that. “No, his heart is too hurt to romance anyone else.”","She figured it wasn’t a lie. For instance, the Peacock Princess had visited the Dragon Palace several times in search of Zu An, but the latter had avoided her by seeking refuge in the Netherworld. He probably doesn’t want her to become fixated on him.","The Peacock Princess had figured out his intentions after missing him several times and spent days crying in the Dragon Palace. She'd looked so pitiful that some from the Ocean races secretly tried to speak up on her behalf. However, Zu An had still refused to meet her. In the end, the Peacock Princess could only leave with a broken heart.","Pei Mianman had tried persuading Zu An to meet the Peacock Princess, but he was too hurt to consider the Peacock Princess, and the last thing he'd wanted to do was to hinder her happiness.","...","Zu An asked Xie Daoyun, “Are you done settling things on the Fiend races’ side?”","Xie Daoyun nodded. “We cleared out the remaining monsters. The Fiend races have reclaimed their previous territories.”","She even meticulously left a projection in the Sealed Land for the future Zu An to find so as to close the time loop.","“Will there be any problem if you, the Saintess, suddenly disappear?” Zu An was worried.","“Don’t worry, the Fiend races have their imperial family. Previously, we had no choice but to band together to deal with the monsters, but now that the external threat has been eliminated, my prestige as Yumen Beiqing would only stoke the imperial family’s wariness. That could lead to a series of complications.” Xie Daoyun, as the wise Saintess of this era, could tell as much.","Yun Yuqing harrumphed. “What use do we have for the imperial family? The Fiends only survived this crisis thanks to yours and Ah Zu’s efforts. I’d say you’re far more qualified to become their empress! Most people in the Fiend races would support you. You can take big brother Zu as your consort afterward...”","The furiously blushing Xie Daoyun clasped Yun Yuqing’s mouth and said, “Shush! That wouldn’t do. I would be changing history if I did that!”","Yun Yuqing’s eyes rolled mischievously. “Oh~ So you’re only worried about changing history. That means you do harbor such thoughts in mind too. Ahh, stop tickling me!”","The pleasant sight of two beauties bantering brought a smile to Zu An’s face. His gloomy mood lifted a little.","While Xie Daoyun made her last preparations, Zu An took the chance to visit the Firecloud Cave. He'd recently remembered the Firecloud Cave, and he had this uncanny feeling that the mysterious person residing there had been luring him to the ancient Celestial Court world. He wanted to get to the bottom of the matter, as well as figure out the other party’s relationship with the Human Emperor.","But when he reached the Purple Ganoderma Cliff, he didn’t see anyone. The Firecloud Cave had also disappeared into thin air.","As he wondered who he had met back then, Zu An allowed the furious winds to batter him. Somehow, it felt as if an invisible hand was controlling him, as if he was a piece on a chessboard.","He tried tapping into the influence of the Fiend races, the Ocean races, and the Netherworld, but he was unable to gather any intelligence about the Firecloud Cave. It was also then that the Nature Jade Plate began to pulsate. Their time here was finally coming to an end.","The Nature Jade Plate should have lost its divine power and turned into a normal stone when they entered this spacetime fragment. However, perhaps due to the special ki in the ancient Celestial Court world, it had amazingly recovered its energy. There had been sufficient energy to not only transport them back, but even to activate again afterward. For a moment, Zu An An even wondered if the Nature Jade Plate was planning to send them to the Celestial Court world once again.","The Nature Jade Plate shone, and Zu An’s group was transported away from the spacetime fragment into another world. Feeling the thinner ki in the surroundings and the connection with the World Law Beacon, Zu An immediately realized that they had returned to their original Cultivation World.","The light in the Nature Jade receded, and it turned back into an ordinary stone container.","Zu An couldn’t help but wonder when the Nature Jade Plate had recharged in the Celestial Court world. If I can find a way to recharge the Nature Jade Plate, can I return to the Celestial Court world again?","“We’re finally back!” Yun Yuqing could tell that they were in the vicinity of the Demon race’s altar.","The other ladies were also overjoyed to see the familiar scenery. This was, after all, their home world.","Zu An could feel everything reverting to normal. He had already re-established his connection with this world’s power insignia. The artifacts he had given away, such as the Oblivion River Water and the Treasure Sinking Coin, returned to his hands. His Human Emperor Seal also regained its powers as the Human Path's power insignia.","He was awed by the effects of a closed time loop. If he could get to the bottom of this phenomenon, wouldn’t he be able to control time? After what had happened to the Mermaid Queen and the Goddess of Wu Mountain, that was the power he desired the most now.","Someone had been guarding the Demon race’s altar, so it didn’t take long for the different clans of the Demon race to rush over. “Welcome back, regent!”","Zu An wasn’t in the mood to deal with this, so he left Yun Yuqing and the others to answer the Demon race’s questions and headed elsewhere himself.","Pei Mianman had an idea of his destination. “You go ahead. We’ll return by ourselves.”","After Zu An left, the other ladies curiously asked Pei Mianman, “Where is he heading to?”","“The Dragon Palace, of course,” Pei Mianman replied with a sigh.","The other ladies nodded in realization.","On a small rocky island, a red and blue mermaid played the zither while fooling around. Their slender fish tails gently flicked the water, producing ripples reminiscent of pearls.","“Little sister, what’s with that glum face? Are you still worried about that fellow?”","“He is strong and cunning. I’m sure he can resolve any crisis that comes his way.”","“Why do you look so glum then?”","“I don’t know either. I have been dreaming a lot recently, but when I wake up, I can never remember what happened in the dream. All I remember is a feeling of coldness and loneliness.”","The red mermaid was startled. She quickly swam to the blue mermaid’s side and placed her hand on the latter’s forehead. “Are you ill? Or did someone hex you? That shouldn’t be. The Dragon Palace’s defense formations are thorough.”","“Don’t worry, I haven’t been hexed. It’s just a dream.” Shang Liuyu clutched her chest. Even though she couldn’t remember the dream anymore, the thought of it left her with an inexplicable heartache.","Shang Hongyu exhaled in relief. “Your worries in the day must have manifested in your dreams. Haa, I wonder when that heartless guy is coming back. But again, even if he returns, he has so many lovers that I doubt he’d look for us right away.”","Shang Liuyu turned around. The familiar figure before her eyes made her stiffen up.","Looking at Shang Liuyu’s familiar face, Zu An could no longer suppress the raging emotions within him. He rushed forward and embraced her tightly. “It’s so good to meet you again!”"]},{"number":2669,"title":"Chapter 2669: Chapter 2621: What to Do When Your Lover Is Sad","paragraphs":["Shang Liuyu initially tensed up in response to Zu An's tight embrace, but his familiar scent caused her to relax quickly. She had been feeling inexplicably melancholic and lonely in recent days, but for some reason, when he embraced her, those emotions dissipated into thin air. She raised her arms and returned the embrace.","A long time later, sloshing sounds suddenly echoed from the side. Shang Hongyu was slapping the waves out of boredom.","“Oi, are you done hugging yet?” Shang Hongyu had initially been overjoyed to see Zu An’s return, but the latter rushed to hug her little sister right away.","She'd initially consoled herself by inwardly saying that those two knew each other first, and she would be next once they were done hugging. To her frustration, those two had refused to let go of each other. Zu An showed no inclination to hug her at all, stoking her jealousy. We’re supposed to be the closer ones!","Startled, Shang Liuyu pushed Zu An away. Her face was so red that it resembled the evening afterglow. Even though she had feelings for Zu An, they had yet to reach that point yet, not to mention there was someone else around. She felt embarrassed.","Zu An looked at Shang Hongyu and recalled that she was likely to be Xihe’s reincarnation. Unable to hold back his feelings, he rushed over and hugged her too.","“Hey hey hey! You only remember me now. I don’t want this kind of charity.” Shang Hongyu pouted in dissatisfaction.","“It’s so good to meet you again,” Zu An said.","“Using the same line twice. How insincere.” Despite her grumbling, Shang Hongyu could still feel Zu An’s overflowing emotions from his embrace. Her expression slowly became gentler.","A while later, it became Shang Liuyu’s turn to feel uncomfortable. She couldn’t help but remember how Zu An and Shang Hongyu had already gotten intimate before, whereas she felt like an outsider here.","Thus, she stood up and said, “You two chat. I’ll be heading off first.”","“Ey, why are you leaving?” Shang Hongyu anxiously stopped her. It feels as if I’m chasing her away. This is so weird.","Zu An also reached out to grab Shang Liuyuu's waist and pulled her toward his body. “Don’t go. We've already been apart for far too long.”","He hugged her tightly. Just remembering the parting they had in the Celestial Court world was enough to fill his heart with pain.","The two sisters exchanged looks. They could sense each other’s awkwardness. They were close sisters, and they were both in love with Zu An. However, it still felt terribly awkward for their lover to embrace the two of them at the same time. They thought of struggling free, but they saw the pain on their lover’s face and their hearts shuddered.","Both of them asked in unison, “Ah Zu, what happened?”","“It’s nothing. Let me hug you a while longer. Just a while is enough...” It hurt Zu An each time he had to recount what happened at the Celestial Court world. His heart was already filled with holes.","Shang Hongyu looked at her little sister worriedly. She had never seen him like that before. Shang Liuyu was worried as well, and asked her older sister what they should do with her gaze.","Shang Hongyu didn’t say a word. She gently wrapped Zu An’s body with her beautiful red tail and rested her body on his. “Ah Zu, we’ll be with you no matter what happens.”","Shang Liuyu felt terribly embarrassed, but she also embraced Zu An and said, “Yes, we’ll always be with you.”","Zu An sighed. The Mermaid Queen and Xihe had wanted to be with him too, but there were far too many things that weren’t within their control.","Sensing his low spirits, the two sisters became even more worried. Something must have happened in the spacetime fragment for him to act like that, but what could it be?","Shang Hongyu suddenly blinked as a smile formed on her lips. “Ah Zu, let’s make a bet. You’ll have to tell me what happened if I can lift your spirits.”","Zu An chuckled. “Just seeing the two of you is enough to raise my spirits.”","“Tsk, how insincere!” Shang Hongyu noticed her little sister’s confused gaze. “Little sister, let me teach you a trick to raise your lover’s spirits.”","Shang Liuyu immediately perked up like a diligent student. She watched as Shang Hongyu straightened her posture and pinned up her wavy hair. Much to her confusion, the latter suddenly dove into the water.","What she witnessed next shocked her. She quickly averted her gaze with a reddened face.","Zu An gasped. He gadn’t expected Shang Hongyu to be so bold as to do it in front of Shang Liuyu, though he had to admit that it was extremely effective. It was hard for him to remain in low spirits in such a situation.","Shang Liuyu tried to leave out of embarrassment, but her hand and waist were being firmly held by Shang Hongyu and Zu An respectively. She bit her lips as her face heated up. These two are really a match made in heaven!","Shang Hongyu, as a mermaid, was capable of breathing in water. The way her beautiful tail fin moved in the water was truly mesmerizing.","“ Wuuuu! ” Shang Hongyu pinched her little sister as she whispered something to the latter.","Shang Liuyu pretended not to understand her words. I’m not going to join my big sister in this madness!","To conceal her awkwardness, Shang Liuyu hurriedly changed the topic. “Ah Zu, can you tell us what happened now?”","Zu An was conflicted. It wasn't a problem for him to share the story, but doing it under such circumstances felt weird. However, considering how the two sisters had already gone this far to console him, he felt that it wouldn’t be right for him to not speak up. Thus, he told them what had happened in the spacetime fragment.","The two sisters had weathered countless storms with Zu An, but they were still shocked when they heard about what happened in the spacetime fragment and the Celestial Court world. In particular, they were left with complex feelings when they learned about Xihe and the Mermaid Queen.","Just as they were reaching an entertaining part of the story, Shang Hongyu suddenly stood up with a red tinge on her face. She rubbed her cheeks as she directed a begrudging look at Zu An. “My cheeks are getting numb...”","She nudged Shang Liuyu. “You do it. I’m totally exhausted.”","“Ah? Me?” Shang Liuyu was flabbergasted. This sort of thing...","Even though Zu An didn’t think that the usually poised Shang Liuyu would agree, he'd gotten so riled up by Shang Hongyu that he couldn’t help but look at her with hopeful eyes.","Shang Liuyu’s heart beat furiously as her mind went blank. However, Shang Hongyu went ahead to pull her over, not giving her time to think.","Shang Liuyu ultimately still couldn’t bring herself to do what Shang Hongyu had done. Instead, she raised her slender hand and said, “I... I’ll help you like that...”","Shang Hongyu knew better than to push Shang Liuyu too far. She first guided Shang Liuyu’s hand to its destination before she settled down beside Zu An and smiled. “Tell me, Ah Zu. Does the Sun Goddess really resemble me? Which of us do you think looks better?”"]},{"number":2670,"title":"Chapter 2670: Chapter 2622: The Method to a Reunion","paragraphs":["“You two resemble each other greatly, but you’re more beautiful.” Zu An conceded that Shang Hongyu’s ‘healing method’ was very effective. The nearby water was as clear as glass, and he was in the company of two beautiful mermaids who gently stirred the water with their fins. It was a truly pleasant scene.","No man could have remained in low spirits under these two women’s ‘consolation’.","Shang Hongyu harrumphed. “Lies. I bet you’d say something different in front of that Xihe.”","Zu An took a sharp breath of air. Shang Liuyu had never done anything like this before, so her movements were still very rigid. Fortunately, her hands were very soft and beautiful, making it a different kind of experience. “Hongyu, you misunderstand me. Xihe was the Sun Goddess and the Celestial Empress. She was beautiful, but she was also fierce and domineering. She was nowhere as gentle and caring as you.”","“That’s more like it.” Shang Hongyu’s beautiful eyes twinkled with glee, but she quickly put on a stern look once more. “Even so, you just said that Xihe is my previous incarnation. Aren’t you saying bad things about my past self then? I feel like I ought to get angry.”","Zu An was speechless for a moment. He pulled her in and began punishing her with his hands. Shang Hongyu’s vibrant yet playful personality was extremely likable.","Shang Hongyu trembled as she pleaded for mercy. The two played around for a little while before Shang Hongyu suddenly turned to her little sister and asked, “Why are you so quiet? Aren’t you curious about your previous incarnation?”","Shang Liuyu rolled her eyes. Don’t you see what I’m doing? I’m not as thick-skinned as you, to be able to chat while doing such stuff.","Shang Hongyu laughed. She could see through her little sister’s thoughts, so she quickly reached out to help the latter. “That’s not the right way to do it. Come, let me teach you.”","Shang Liuyu’s face reddened further. It was even more embarrassing to have someone teach her something like that. She instinctively withdrew her hand, but Shang Hongyu anticipated her movement and firmly grabbed her hand.","“You need to do it like that. It won’t do to be so stiff...”","Shang Liuyu felt as if she was experiencing an entire lifetime’s worth of shame. Shang Hongyu is a lunatic! Why does she have to drag me down with her?!","Even so, thanks to Shang Hongyu’s guidance, she was being far bolder than she usually was. She couldn’t help but be astonished by her big sister’s teachings. I didn’t know there’s so much wisdom behind such things!","She also couldn’t help notice how small her hands were. To think that even mine and big sister’s hands combined wouldn’t be enough!","Shang Hongyu knew how shy her little sister was, so she asked on the latter’s behalf, “Ah Zu, tell us more about Liuyu’s previous incarnation.”","“You can say that she’s the founder of your Mermaid race...” As he reminisced about Gong Suyin, Zu An’s gaze turned gentle.","“I have always been curious as to why there were so few records about the Gong clan. Their lineage has always had few offspring too. That explains it,” Shang Liuyu finally spoke up.","“You’re usually such a philanderer. Shouldn’t you be more proactive about such stuff? It’s because of your inaction that the Gong clan’s main lineage’s bloodline wasn’t passed down.” Halfway through Shang Hongyu’s words, her face suddenly turned red. “No, it’s a good thing you didn’t have any offspring with her, or else the two of us could be your descendants. That would be a huge mess.”","Zu An was speechless. “What nonsense are you spouting? She was a Gong and you’re Shangs. How can you be blood-related?”","“That’s hard to say. Intermarriages often occur within our five major clans.” Shang Hongyu harrumphed. She looked relieved.","“What happened next?” Shang Liuyu was more interested in what had happened between Zu An and her previous incarnation than these details.","“Well...” Zu An sighed. “It ended im tragedy.”","He told them about how Gong Suyin had been cornered and eaten the immortal medicine, which resulted in her ascending to the Frost Palace and how she was trapped there for the rest of her life. The two of them had bade each other farewell and never met again.","By then, Shang Hongyu was already sobbing. “Ahh, that Miss Gong is too pitiful! How can you seduce her and not take responsibility? You’re terrible!”","Zu An didn’t explain himself. Despite being limited by his circumstances, the fact that he had failed to find Gong Suyin was the truth.","Shang Liuyu shook her head. “I disagree. Your feelings with Miss Gong were mutual, and the two of you were lawfully married as well. She loved you even when you were forced to part ways, and she was holding hope in her heart for an eventual reunion. I think the worst thing that can happen to a person is to lose all hope. I think she was only able to hold on because of the hope you gave her.”","Zu An sighed. “Even hope can't stand the test of time. She waited far too long for me, but I never showed up. I can’t imagine how deep her despair must have been.”","Shang Hongyu shook her head. “She might have thought that your feelings for her had changed and harbored a grudge against you for that.”","Shang Liuyu glanced at her big sister. She’s using this chance to unravel the knots in Ah Zu’s heart for good. She played along with Shang Hongyu and continued, “Two people truly in love wouldn’t blame each other. I have never met Miss Gong before, but she sounds like a wise and sentimental woman. I don’t think her love for you would change even if she felt that you would never meet again.”","Seeing someone with the Mermaid Queen’s face say such words shook Zu An’s heart. He felt as if he was meeting the Mermaid Queen once more, and the latter was sharing her countless years of sentiment. Unable to take it anymore, he pulled her into his embrace. At that moment, the Mermaid Queen and Shang Liuyu overlapped for him.","Shang Liuyu gently hugged him back without saying a word.","Only Shang Hongyu was left feeling frustrated. She had to do it alone after Shang Liuyu abruptly retracted her hand. What am I doing here while they're enjoying their pure romance?","“Hey, don’t you think my previous incarnation is pitiful too? She was also alone for tens of thousands of years.”","Zu An burst into laughter and gently embraced her too.","This scene would have felt heartwarming to both sisters... if not for a certain pole pressing against them.","“Ah! Now that I think about it, Liuyu, could your recent dreams be related to that Gong Suyin?” In the end, Shang Hongyu still couldn’t bear to give up halfway through and leave Little An like that.","Shang Liuyu hesitated. She didn’t think it was right to let Shang Hongyu do all the work, so she went back to helping her. “I’m not sure either, but my recent dreams did leave me feeling alone and melancholic. But is it possible to retain past memories after reincarnation?”","Zu An shook his head. “It shouldn’t be possible under normal circumstances. Granny Meng’s soup washes away past memories.”","A thought suddenly struck him. Hold on, I'm the the Necropolis Emperor. I could have made an exception for her. I thought of reuniting with the Mermaid Queen at the Frost Palace, but if she reincarnated, she would have passed through the Netherworld and the Six Paths of Reincarnation.","Shang Liuyu spoke up, “Ah Zu, you need not be so depressed. You might have failed to meet Miss Gong thus far, but it doesn’t mean you’ll never meet her again. You've returned to the past once; I’m sure you can do it again once you find a way to do so.”"]},{"number":2671,"title":"Chapter 2671: Chapter 2623: Betrayal","paragraphs":["Zu An widened his eyes. That’s right. Somehow, I kept thinking of reuniting with them in my timeline, but that would be extremely difficult in any case. I should be thinking of ways to return to their timeline instead.","Time travel was no easy feat, but it wasn't impossible either. Some dungeons and artifacts were capable of time travel, such as the Nature Jade Plate. That artifact had turned back into stone, but there could be other ways to do it.","The thought of that lifted his morale and dissipated his gloominess, though that immediately evoked exclamations from the two sisters...","The following day, Zu An made his way to the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons with Shang Hongyu accompanying him.","Shang Liuyu had been swept away by the atmosphere yesterday and didn’t think much into it, but once the deed was done, she felt so embarrassed that she wanted to bury herself. She refused to meet Zu An no matter what he said.","“Under her carefree exterior is an innocent heart. Don’t mind it too much. She’ll get over her awkwardness in a few days’ time,” Shang Hongyu replied with a gleeful smile. She was happy that she had succeeded in teasing her little sister yesterday.","Zu An also smiled gently when he thought about Shang Liuyu’s clumsiness yesterday. It felt as if the veil dividing them had finally been ripped apart then, but their progress was so fast that it seemed to have scared her off.","“How do you intend to thank...” Shang Hongyu cried out before she could finish her sentence. Zu An had swept her into his arms to kiss her.","Her body quickly relaxed, and her enchanting eyes glimmered as if dabbed with water. “You bullied me a lot yesterday. Is that not enough?”","Shang Liuyu had been the one stroking the zither yesterday, but as the melody played to its climax, her inexperienced self had failed to dodge in time. In the end, she'd run off out of embarrassment to clean herself up and never returned.","Shang Hongyu had needed to clean up the situation. Thinking about what happened afterward made her heart beat quickly.","This temptress, Zu An thought. She cosplayed Xihe and switched between characters yesterday. How am I supposed to endure that?","Unfortunately, they were in the Ocean races’ most sacred Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons. Some of the Mermaid race’s ancestors were buried here. It wouldn’t be right for them to fool around here.","While advancing, Zu An went up to the statue of the founding Mermaid Queen. He had always wondered why the latter resembled Shang Liuyu so much, but he now had the answer—the statue was sculpted in her likeness. Not to mention he was the one who had supervised this project in the ancient era.","He gently stroked the Mermaid Queen statue. It had been battered by time, but she still looked as beautiful as ever.","Shang Hongyu got jealous. “Oh hoh! You sculpted a statue for my little sister’s previous incarnation to remember her by. Why didn’t you do the same for my previous incarnation?”","Zu An sweated profusely. He awkwardly replied, “You were the Sun Goddess and the Celestial Empress in that era. It wouldn’t have been good if our relationship became known.”","“Isn’t it just a human spouse? My sister and I are descendants of the Ocean races, but I don’t see you having any reservations about that.” Shang Hongyu was just joking at the start, but she got emotional halfway through.","It’s a story of three people, but only I am unworthy of being commemorated.","Zu An also realized how inappropriate his actions were, so he pulled her into his arms to console her.","“Forget it. You can walk by yourself. I won’t be accompanying you.” Shang Hongyu gently pushed him away and headed off. A trail of gleaming pearls were left in the dark palace.","Zu An wanted to stop her, but he didn’t know what to say. She seemed truly upset.","Even though he and Xihe had shared an intimate relationship, they'd been more like enemies instead of lovers. He'd been nowhere as close to her as Shang Hongyu in this life. But speaking those thoughts aloud would likely only upset her further. He would rather she blame him instead.","Zu An sighed before advancing deeper into the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons. The time loop had been closed, and the World Law Beacon had returned to his hands. However, he had come here today to verify something. When he sensed the aura of the Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine lingering in the atmosphere, he frowned.","He had entrusted the Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine’s seed to the Mermaid Queen in the Celestial Court world. However, she'd eaten it to prevent Feng Meng from gaining possession of it, which resulted in her ascending to the Frost Palace.","When he constructed the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons with the Ocean races, there had been no substitute for the immortal medicine there. Back then, he'd even worried that the disappearance of the Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine would affect history.","But somehow, he'd still managed to obtain the Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine in this timeline.","There can only be two possibilities. One, there are two Divine Dragon Immortal Medicines. However, immortal medicines are primordial substances, and each of them is unique.","That leaves only the second possibility. Gong Suyin was here. She probably remembered me talking about that, so she intentionally planted the Divine Dragon Immortal Medicine’s seed here to close the time loop.","The thought that Gong Suyin had visited this place and seen her statue excited Zu An. Does this mean that she broke free of the Frost Palace’s restraints? Did Mo Xi grow strong enough to use ‘Farewell, Nanchao’ on her contract?","Zu An’s excitement heightened. He began searching the area, but in the end, he didn’t find anything. This confused him. If the Mermaid Queen was here, why didn’t she leave anything behind? Was she unable to leave anything here?","He continued advancing with a heavy heart. Soon, he passed through the abyss and entered the Netherworld. He first made his way under the Oblivion Bridge and saw Chu Chuyan still in her cultivation. He briefly hesitated, but decided against disturbing her.","The Oblivion River was highly damaging to souls. Even with him, the Netherworld’s master, making a special exception for her, Chuyan still needed to remain in a state of hibernation to endure the relentless flow of time. If she woke up, she would experience the real world’s flow of time, and that would only put her in greater pain.","Zu An quickly made his way to the Reincarnation Platform. He had instructed the Ox Head and Horse Face in the spacetime fragment to leave a message here if anything happened to the Netherworld in the future.","They should have at least left something behind, right?","Zu An nervously made his way to the discreet corner on the Reincarnation Platform that he had pointed out to them. A second later, his body trembled.","There was an extremely small word written in the Shaman language. It was inscribed messily, as if it had been done in a hurry.","‘Betrayal’."]},{"number":2672,"title":"Chapter 2672: Chapter 2624: An Enigmatic Intruder","paragraphs":["Zu An looked at the messily scribbled word and fell into deep thought. Betrayal? Who was the traitor, and who did they betray?","There were far too many possibilities with that single word that Zu An couldn’t make sense of the situation with his limited information.","Why did Ox Head and Horse Face leave this single word behind? Did they have no time to leave more information? Did the enemy discover them while they were inscribing this word? Or did some rule or individual prevent them from leaving behind more detailed information?","In any case, the death of the Netherworld’s other deities likely has something to do with this matter.","“Lady Houtu?” Zu An tried calling out, but the Six Paths of Reincarnation continued operating without answering.","Houtu had initially preserved a sliver of her sentience due to her strength after transforming into the Six Paths of Reincarnation, but after many years of operation, her sentience was bound to erode, leaving behind a pure heavenly law.","Zu An spent a long time pondering things by the Reincarnation Platform. Following that, he went under the Oblivion Bridge once more to visit Chu Chuyan. He spent a while chatting with her despite knowing she was unconscious, but it did calm his heart.","The next day, he went to the Dragon Palace. To his surprise, Shang Liuyu was waiting in the vicinity for him.","“Big sister Shang!” Zu An was overjoyed. He'd thought that she would continue avoiding him due to what happened the last time.","Shang Liuyu’s face reddened as she thought of the same matter. She rolled her eyes and said, “Don’t misunderstand, I’m not here for you. My big sister came back yesterday and kept crying nonstop. I asked her what was wrong, but she refused to speak. She was in a good mood when she accompanied you to the Tomb of Ten Thousand Dragons. What happened?”","Zu An was startled. “I’ll talk to her.”","“I’ve relayed the message. The rest is up to you,” Shang Liuyu said before leaving in a hurry.","Zu An shook his head bitterly, knowing that Liuyu hadn’t recovered from her embarrassment. However, the priority at hand was to talk to Shang Hongyu.","Following Shang Liuyu’s tip, he went to an island near the Dragon Palace and found Shang Hongyu at a beach. She was resting against a boulder, staring at the sky in a daze. Golden rays shone on the emerald ocean water, and the reflected light made her graceful figure glow.","Zu An felt as if he was looking at a beautiful portrait. As he walked over, he said sincerely, “You’re beautiful.\"","“But I have no weight in your heart,” Shang Hongyu lamented.","That sharp response made Zu An sweat profusely. He sat down next to her and grabbed her hand. He was about to speak when Shang Hongyu suddenly interjected, “Do you think I’m jealous of my little sister?”","“Of course not.” Zu An thought he would get angry if he was faced with the same situation too.","Shang Hongyu lowered her head. “I’m not angry at you or my little sister. I’m angry at myself.”","Zu An didn’t know what to say.","Shang Hongyu looked at him with a miserable smile. “It’s not a tantrum. I’m angry at myself for always meeting you later than others. Not only did I meet you later than my little sister in this world, but I also met you later than the Mermaid Queen in that world. It feels as if I’m always one step behind.”","Zu An suddenly laughed as he pulled her into his embrace. “You’re wrong about that. I met Xihe much earlier than Suyin.”","“Really?” Shang Hongyu narrowed her eyes in suspicion.","“Of course. I met Xihe a long time ago in a dungeon...” Zu An told her about his first meeting with Xihe in that dungeon, including how she'd cornered him.","Shang Hongyu was thoroughly entertained by that story. “You’re terrible! Using your Golden Phoenix’s ability on your first meeting, making her fall in love with you.”","Zu An was apologetic about that. “I had no choice. She was going to kill me. That was my only way out.”","“Did you secretly use that ability on us too?” Shang Hongyu eyed him in suspicion.","Black streaks flashed across Zu An’s face. “Of course not! I told you I had no choice then.”","Shang Hongyu breathed a sigh of relief. “I guess you met my past incarnation much earlier than that Gong Suyin. You might have seen Xihe as an enemy because she was after your life the first time you met, so your feelings for her weren’t as pure as compared to Gong Suyin.”","“Yeah, I can’t deny that,” Zu An replied frankly. “Your previous incarnation was formidable. The first time I met her, I was utterly helpless against her. She even prepared an elaborate scheme the second time we met. I would have been sold out by her without knowing!”","Shang Hongyu suddenly remarked, “I think Xihe ended up selling herself out instead.”","“What do you mean?”","“Do you think a woman would willingly sleep with you if she didn’t like you?”","Zu An fell into deep thought. He had considered that matter too.","Shang Hongyu quickly added, “Do you think she did that under the influence of your Golden Phoenix’s ability?”","Without waiting for his answer, she shook her head and said, “The Golden Phoenix’s ability is formidable, but it could only make her fall in love with you; she still retained her rational judgment. There were ways for her to avoid intimate contact with you while she was disguised as Yumen Beiqing, but she still allowed it. She might have initially allowed it due to the Golden Phoenix’s ability, but over time, you should have been able to tell whether her feelings for you were true or not.”","Zu An nodded. “You’re right. She had many chances to kill me, but she didn’t do it.”","He recalled how the Goddess of Wu Mountain, in the projection she had left behind, said that she, Xihe, and the Mermaid Queen had become close friends. That, in itself, spoke volumes.","“I don’t know how it was for my past incarnation, but at least in this lifetime, I sincerely love you.” Shang Hongyu raised her head to look at her lover with gentle but determined eyes.","Zu An leaned in and kissed her.","The two of them cuddled as they thought about their time together. Their hearts felt closer to each other than ever.","Suddenly, Zu An pushed Shang Hongyu aside and coldly glared in a direction. “Why don’t you show yourself when you’re already here?”","Shang Hongyu was initially confused, but she immediately tensed up when she learned that someone else was here, and she hadn’t noticed the other party’s presence at all.","“Hm? You sensed me? How is that possible?” a voice echoed.","A figure slowly revealed itself not too far away. It was a person wearing a bizarre mask and scholar's robes."]},{"number":2673,"title":"Chapter 2673: Chapter 2625: Frog in the Well","paragraphs":["Shang Hongyu immediately put up her guard. Her earlier failure to detect the intruder could be attributed to her putting down her vigilance because she was with Zu An, but despite the other party revealing himself, she was still unable to sense his aura.","She was the Mermaid Queen, a renowned expert of the Ocean races. It was utterly astounding that she couldn’t sense a person despite the other party appearing before her.","Zu An frowned. “Hm? You aren’t from this world. How did you get in?”","The Cultivation World was a rare Wonderpoint World in the universe. With him activating the world barrier through the World Law Beacon to guard against the monsters’ invasion, it shouldn’t have been possible for beings from other worlds to slip in.","Did something happen to the barrier? Zu An narrowed his eyes.","Hearing Zu An’s words and sensing his unique aura, the masked man nodded in realization. “Ah, you are the master of this world. Pardon me for intruding. I am a unique entity, which allows me to enter any world. You need not worry about your world barrier. There are only a handful of people in the universe who possess this ability.”","Zu An examined the other party. As the master of this world, he could utilize resources unthinkable to mortals while he was in this world. Looking through his own eyes, he saw that the other party had no physical body. Beneath the scholar's robe was empty air.","And yet, the other party was a living entity, existing in a way that was incomprehensible to him.","“What are you doing in our world?” Zu An asked vigilantly.","“I chanced upon this place while investigating the death of a comrade.” The other party’s attitude was exceptionally respectful upon learning that Zu An was the world’s master.","“Death of a comrade? What’s your comrade’s name? Let me see if I have an impression of him.” Zu An wondered if one of the experts he had killed was the other party’s comrade.","“You need not worry. This has nothing to do with you,” the masked figure replied with a smile.","Zu An frowned. What are you doing here if it has nothing to do with me? He suddenly thought of something and turned to Shang Hongyu.","Shang Hongyu also realized what was going on and asked, “Me?”","The masked figure nodded. “Yes, my comrade died at that lady’s hand.”","“Are you mistaken?” Shang Hongyu was baffled. She couldn’t think of anyone related to this mysterious entity.","The Mermaid race wasn't fond of slaughter, and there was no way she wouldn’t have an impression of such an enigmatic being.","Zu An subtly pulled her behind him as he said, “She couldn’t have killed your comrade.”","But the masked figure confidently replied, “Our race has very few people, so each of our brethren is very important to us. Our bodies have a unique way of imprinting people who kill us, and there’s no way to remove the imprint. I sensed the imprint while passing by this world, so I came in to take a look. I hadn’t expected the murderer to be such a beautiful lady.”","Zu An frowned. There really are all sorts of mysterious skills in the universe. I have to be more careful in the future. “You said a lot, but there’s no way she could have killed your comrade.”","The masked figure assessed Shang Hongyu before nodding. “Indeed, she’s too weak. It doesn’t seem likely that she could have killed my comrade.”","Shang Hongyu was perplexed. She had heard all kinds of evaluations about her—some said she was pretty, others said she lacked decorum, and yet others said she was fierce. This was the first time someone had said she was weak.","But what was even more maddening was that she couldn’t refute those words. The other party was so unfathomably powerful that she was no match for him.","“It’s good that we have cleared the misunderstanding.” Zu An knew next to nothing about the other party, and his race had a unique way of imprinting people. If things went wrong, it could escalate into a full-blown war. He didn’t want to make such troublesome enemies for no reason. “Since you have come from afar, allow me to welcome you as a host.”","He was hoping to gather more information about the other worlds. He had been to quite a few worlds, but they'd been accessed through dungeons. The only other world he had physically been to was the Monster World, but the Monster World was already on the verge of destruction.","Just the thought of the terrifying Annihilation Beast made him tense up. There were too many powerful entities in the universe, and he was lacking information about them.","“You have misunderstood. I said that the current her is weak, but that doesn’t mean the past her was weak too.” The masked figure shook his finger.","Zu An’s face darkened. “Are you joking with me?”","“Our racial culture is inclined toward solemnity. We don’t joke around,” the masked figure earnestly replied. “Let me see. Using your world’s words, you can say that her past incarnation was the one who killed my comrade.”","Zu An’s heart skipped a beat. Shang Hongyu’s past incarnation was Sun Goddess Xihe. Could it be...","Shang Hongyu came to the same conclusion too. She glanced at Zu An with worried eyes.","Zu An squeezed her hand to reassure her before smiling at the masked figure. “Don’t you think it’s too ridiculous to be talking about past incarnations? It’s too far-fetched to use such excuses to accuse her of a crime.”","The masked figure fell silent, as if weighing the risks of confronting Zu An. A while later, he still chose to patiently explain, “Our race’s imprint is a special one. It remains even after the soul has undergone reincarnation, as long as vengeance is not served.”","“Impossible,” Zu An interjected. “Our world observes the law of the Six Paths of Reincarnation. Anyone who has undergone reincarnation has their memories wiped, making them a different person from before. How can you still sense your imprint?”","“It is baffling. I can also sense the unique nature of your world. Indeed, I shouldn’t have been able to sense the imprint after an individual entered the Six Paths of Reincarnation.” Even through the mask, Zu An and Shang Hongyu could still sense the other party’s confusion. “If I have to fathom a guess, it must be because she’s someone special. Either she used a secret art or a special exception was made in the Six Paths of Reincarnation, allowing her to retain something from her previous life. It is because of that connection that I can sense that imprint. Yes, that must be the case!” He started uncertain, but his voice grew increasingly certain.","“The Six Paths of Reincarnation is impartial. It is a fundamental law of this world. How can anyone retain anything from their previous life after undergoing the Six Paths of Reincarnation? Aren’t you going too far by pinning a crime on my friend based solely on your conjecture?” Zu An exclaimed, startled.","However, the other party’s conjecture made sense. Xihe, as the Sun Goddess and the Celestial Empress, could have used a special artifact to determine her future reincarnation, not to mention her close ties with him. It was possible for the Six Paths of Reincarnation to have made a special exception for her.","The masked figure scratched his head. “You’re putting me in a tough spot.”","“She’s my woman, which makes her this world’s mistress. You’re welcomed here as a guest, but if you’re looking for a fight, we’ll entertain you too.” Zu An coldly eyed the masked figure as he wondered if he should apprehend the other party to gather more information. However, the other party’s ability to imprint on others was indeed troublesome to deal with.","The masked figure straightened his posture as his disposition turned cold. “You must have had a smooth-sailing life to become this world’s master, but you’re nothing but a minor border world in the universe. You’re a frog in the well if you think you’re invincible.”[1]","1. A frog in the well refers to someone who is stuck in their little world and doesn’t know how big the world outside is. ☜"]},{"number":2674,"title":"Chapter 2674: Chapter 2626: Nemesis","paragraphs":["The masked figure exuded a formidable aura, and his words were sharp. He thought that this could be an opportunity to let this border world bumpkin know how huge the universe was. Little did he expect to be faced with a sharp blade of sword ki.","Shang Hongyu was awed by the blinding sword. Ah Zu’s swordsmanship proficiency has advanced considerably. I could still barely understand his swordsmanship before, but now, he has already surpassed this world’s limits.","She knew that if she were in the masked figure’s place, she would have been sliced in two before she could make sense of what was happening.","However, her smile soon froze. The masked figure casually tilted his body, and the sword ki simply passed by him.","Zu An frowned too, but his sword ki didn’t stop there. It abruptly changed its trajectory to move upward.","But once again, the masked figure casually stepped back and avoided the attack.","Zu An unleashed several more attacks, but the other party could always avoid his attacks using the subtlest movements.","Shang Hongyu was stunned. The first time could have been a coincidence, but the other party pulled it off every time. It showed how sharp the masked figure’s judgment was. She didn’t want to admit it, but the other party’s swordsmanship proficiency likely far surpassed Zu An’s. The difference could even be at a fundamental level.","Zu An was shaken up too. Could the power levels in the universe be so drastically different?","When he saw Zu An stop his aggression, the masked figure smiled. “Do you see now that my words are no lie...”","“What you lookin’ at?”","“I’m looking at you, shithead!”","The masked figure was interrupted by the ‘What you lookin’ at’ ability before he could finish his sentence. Zu An didn’t hesitate to use this opportunity to strike. He drew the Tai’e Sword and created countless afterimages to attack the masked figure from all directions.","Initially, the masked figure could still dodge his attacks with casual steps, but over time, his dodging stances became increasingly flustered. He was no longer as relaxed as before.","Shang Hongyu also began singing, layering debuffs on the masked man. She knew that with her current cultivation, engaging the masked figure close up would only result in her being one-shot, so she wisely focused on supporting Zu An instead. Fortunately, the Mermaid race was skilled in support.","The masked figure was already flustered from Zu An’s attack. Shang Hongyu’s intervention placed him in a dangerous position. He immediately retaliated by drawing a brush to deflect Zu An’s sword. At the same time, he flipped open a book and chanted aloud, “Fear arrogance and shackle yourself with humility. Fear narrow-mindedness and be all-embracing like the ocean...”","His forceful words evoked a harrumph from Shang Hongyu as fresh blood seeped from her lips. She had suffered a backlash from the other party’s soulspeak.","“What you lookin’ at?”","“I’m looking at you, shithead!”","...","Zu An hurriedly interrupted the other party’s soulspeak before rushing to Shang Hongyu’s side to examine her condition. Upon confirming that she hadn’t hurt her cultivation base, he exhaled in relief.","The masked figure secretly wiped off his sweat. He didn’t use this opportunity to attack Zu An. “How did you know I couldn’t dodge the subsequent attacks?”","His earlier trick had never failed him. He had used it countless times and shattered many dao hearts, leaving his enemies with no fighting spirit.","Zu An laughed. “I have met and fought many powerful entities, and I don’t believe you’re stronger than them. You probably have an ability to foresee the future, allowing you to predict my attacks, but such abilities either have restrictions or come at a cost. That’s why I sped up my attacks to test your limit. Clearly, I have overestimated you.”","The masked figure fell silent for a moment before replying, “You’re right. I have such an ability. It’s called ‘Constellation Reading’. It allows me to foresee the enemy’s next move. You have an unwavering heart and sharp wits. Such traits are rare in the world. I am in awe.”","He hadn’t revealed the downsides of the ability, but Zu An had hit the nail on the head.","Zu An calmly replied, “The pleasantries are belated.”","The masked figure held a brush in one hand and a book in the other, looking as relaxed as ever. “You might have seen through one of my abilities, but surely you don’t think you can apprehend me with just this much.”","“How would I know if I don’t give it a try?” Zu An took out a formation plate and moved his hands so quickly that they formed afterimages. In the blink of an eye, he constructed a formation channeling the energies of the nearby islands, mountains, and ocean to trap the masked figure.","As the world’s master, he already wielded the ability to control the laws of the world. With the support of his formation, he could intertwine the formation’s laws with the laws of physics.","The masked figure suddenly couldn’t sustain his flight anymore and plummeted into the raging ocean.","“Let history be the mirror that pierces through the veil!” a calm voice echoed.","A light shone amid the waves. The light slowly intensified, which revealed the masked figure’s silhouette in the water. He was upside down like a hanged man, but he remained calm. He flipped open his book as he casually walked on the waves.","The scenery suddenly distorted. A second later, he suddenly emerged from the formation, regaining his previous stance.","Zu An suddenly realized something. “You’re a Time Scribe?”","The other party’s clothes and skills resembled that of the Time Scribe he'd met in the Monster World. With this realization, he finally understood why the other party was after Shang Hongyu. Sun Goddess Xihe had killed that Time Scribe in the Celestial Court world, and Shang Hongyu was Xihe’s incarnation. No wonder the masked figure had come looking for Shang Hongyu!","“Time Scribe?” Those words appeared to agitate the masked figure. He vehemently shook his head as he shouted, “No no no, I’m nothing like those hateful things! I am a Mirror Scribe!”","Zu An was startled by the masked figure's intense disgust. “Is there a difference?” Why are you coming after us if you aren’t on the same side?","“Of course there’s a difference!” the masked figure shrieked. “We, the Mirror Scribes, record true history, whereas the Time Scribes alter history at their whim. They are our nemeses, so how can we be the same?”","“Alter history?” Zu An was perplexed. Is what I did in the other spacetimes considered altering history?","“Hold on, how do you know about the Time Scribes?” The masked figure eyed the duo with suspicion.","“We crossed paths with one recently. You said you wanted to avenge your comrade, so I wondered if it was him.” Zu An and Shang Hongyu exchanged looks.","The masked figure widened his eyes. “Could that fellow be a spy?!”"]},{"number":2675,"title":"Chapter 2675: Chapter 2627: Deity Names","paragraphs":["Zu An was speechless. Hold on, so you really aren’t on the same side?","“Can you tell me more about your encounter with that fellow?” the masked figure urged.","Zu An huffed, “You came here yapping about avenging your comrade. You’re the one who picked a fight, and now you’re also the one who wants to stop the fight. Why should I answer your question?”","The masked figure bowed to Zu An. “I apologize to you for my earlier disrespect and seek your forgiveness. I’ll present you with a satisfactory gift afterward as compensation.”","“What’s the gift?” Shang Hongyu asked. She didn’t want her lover to be fooled by vague terms.","“I guarantee your satisfaction. I swear on my position as a Mirror Scribe,” the masked figure replied.","Since the other party had already made such a vow, the duo didn’t dwell on the matter.","Zu An began recounting his encounter with the Time Scribe in the Monster World. The masked figure raised a few questions along the way, and Zu An answered them all.","After hearing the full story, the masked figure remarked, “Based on what you have told me, that fellow might really have been a Time Scribe. He wielded the Spring and Autumn Brush, the tool used by Time Scribes. But I’m curious to know how you became aware of his identity. He shouldn’t have told an outsider that he was a Time Scribe.”","“I have my ways of finding out.” There was no way Zu An would tell the other party about Mi Li’s existence. “Can you tell me more about the grudge between Mirror Scribes and Time Scribes?”","The masked figure knew someone who had become a world’s master was bound to have many fortuitous encounters. The latter could indeed have encountered a Time Scribe somehow. Since Zu An was unwilling to speak, he chose not to continue probing either. “We might be fellow scribes, but we worship different philosophies and deities. We, the Mirror Scribes, view history as a mirror, and we seek to record objective truths.","“The Time Scribes, on the other hand, have lost their basic principles as scribes and seek to toy with history. Events they pen with their Spring and Autumn Brushes depict a twisted version of the truth, misleading others into forming a false impression.","“That’s why we are absolute nemeses. That fellow was hiding among us for a long time now; there’s no doubt he harbored malicious intent. It’s a relief that you eliminated him, even if unintentionally, or else it could have spelled a disaster for us.”","The revelation that an old comrade had secretly been a Time Scribe made him shudder. To have infiltrated us, he must have been up to something terrible.","Zu An took this chance to probe further. “You mentioned that you worship different deities. What’s the deity you worship?”","He had a feeling that the deity worshiped by the other party wasn't just a minor deity, but a universal deity.","The masked figure frowned. “If you learn their names, you will be dragged into the war among deities. Are you certain that you’re prepared for that?”","Shang Hongyu grabbed Zu An’s hands and looked at him worriedly. Despite knowing the height she had reached in her previous life, she was happy with her current one. Ah Zu is carefree and happy in this world; there’s nothing bad about this. If he gets tied up in other matters, there's a good chance he might have to leave this world. That’s the last thing I want to happen.","Zu An hesitated too. Being this world’s master was a carefree job for him. He wasn’t certain whether he wanted to brave unknown risks. However, this was also his only chance to learn about the deities’ names. Mi Li would never tell him about those beings. But if he confirmed that he wanted to know, this masked figure would tell him.","He thought about how Jiang Luofu had been summoned by an enigmatic entity, as well as Gong Suyin and the Goddess of Wu Mountain’s unknown plights... There were too many mysteries that he needed to unravel, and he needed greater power to do so.","“I’m ready, but I have a question. Someone once told me that it’s a taboo to reveal a deity’s name. Obliteration may ensue if one catches the deity’s gaze. If so, why is it that you are able to tell me your deity’s name?” Zu An asked.","“Your friend was trying to protect you. It’ll only bring destruction upon yourself if you learn about a deity’s name when you are incapable of shouldering the burden. I can reveal it because I am a Mirror Scribe. I am responsible for recording the universe’s objective history,” the masked figure replied proudly. “As a world’s master, you are qualified to learn about the universe’s secrets. That being said, given your limited strength, I can only tell you the names of two deities. You are already implicated in this karma, so with the protection of that karma and my unique identity, you should be able to avoid being destroyed by the deities’ overwhelming power.”","Zu An’s face turned serious. Mi Li wasn’t lying to me. Even the preconditions are harsh.","The masked figure spoke in a tone resembling documentary narrators in Zu An’s previous life, “We, the Mirror Scribes, worship the Deity of Memory, Meng. We record past, future, and erased events. Be it from memories from a person or a world, we record everything that happens in the universe, including life, death, and the destruction of worlds. As long as our records persist, they will not be truly dead.”","Zu An was taken aback. He had imagined the name of a universal god to be majestic, but it was surprisingly simple. Hold on, would having such a thought be considered blasphemy?","He got nervous for a while there, but fortunately, there was no divine retribution.","“You have a noble goal,” Zu An sincerely said. Judging from the other party’s passionate tone, he could tell that the latter believed in his cause.","Their records would no doubt have helped many as well, since the recorded beings and worlds were, in a way, eternal as long as their records remained.","The masked figure was delighted to receive Zu An’s acknowledgment. “Why don’t you join us in worshiping the great Deity Meng and become a Mirror Scribe too?”","“I know too little about the deities. It’d be insincere of me to worship a deity on a whim,” Zu An subtly declined the offer. You must be joking. I don’t even know what’s going on with those universal deities, so how can I haphazardly join a side? Besides, I am at least a minor deity who governs this world’s cycle of reincarnation.","“You’re right. I have gotten ahead of myself.” The masked figure didn’t insist on it. “Next, I will share with you the deity worshiped by the Time Scribes. They believe in chaos and enigma, and their deity’s name is ‘Mi Li’.”","“What did you say their deity’s name was?” Zu An felt as if a hammer had struck his heart."]},{"number":2676,"title":"Chapter 2676: Chapter 2628: Tree and Beehive","paragraphs":["How could Zu An not be shocked when that name sounded just like big sis empress? He'd initially thought that Mi Li was Qin Shihuang’s empress, but it later became apparent to him that that wasn’t the case. She had always been enigmatic to him.","Mi Li seemed to know a lot, but getting information from her was tougher than squeezing out toothpaste. She spoke in riddles, which matched the traits of a Deity of Chaos and Enigma.","While others have grandpas as their cheat, my cheat is one of the most powerful entities in the myriad worlds? The thought shocked Zu An.","“What nonsense are you thinking?” Mi Li’s sneering voice suddenly echoed in his ears. “Do you think I’d babysit you like a nanny if I were truly that Deity of Enigma?”","Zu An thought those words made sense. When he first met her, she'd been sealed in the tomb of Qin Shihuang’s empress and didn’t even have a body. She had to rely on him to find materials to forge a new body for her. It didn’t seem possible for an unparalleled deity to end up in such a plight...","The masked figure was horrified to hear Zu An’s question. He reflexively looked at the sky before replying with a suppressed voice, “Even as a scribe blessed with the great Deity of Memory’s protection, I can’t keep calling the name of that exalted entity. It’ll be terrible if I draw the deity’s attention. But judging from your reaction, have you heard that name before?”","Zu An replied with a strained smile, “No, I must have remembered wrongly.”","The masked figure sternly warned him, “Remember this. You should avoid listening to any universal deities' names unless their envoys personally reveal it to you.”","Zu An was intrigued. “What would happen otherwise?”","“You might draw the deity’s attention and disintegrate on the spot,” the masked figure replied.","“Will it always draw the deity’s attention?” Zu An asked.","“I don’t know. I doubt anyone in the world would dare put their life on the line to test that theory,” the masked figure replied hesitantly.","Zu An thought made sense. It would be better to err on the side of caution.","The masked figure took out a black-gold card and passed it to Zu An. “I promised you a gift. This is an invitation letter to Dreamland. With it, you can access Dreamland, a place countless people across the myriad worlds wish to visit.”","“Dreamland?” Zu An was perplexed.","“As the name suggests, it is a land of dreams. There is no war there; only happiness. It is said that no matter who you are, you can always find the items you need to fulfill your dreams there. Of course, the more precious the item you require, the greater the price you have to pay,” the masked figure explained.","Zu An’s breathing quickened. Whether it was the spacetime divide with the Mermaid Queen and the Goddess of Wu Mountain, the materials needed to reforge Mi Li’s body, or Chuyan, who was trapped under the Oblivion Bridge... He had far too many wishes that couldn’t be fulfilled with this world’s power. If Dreamland was truly that incredible, he would absolutely have to make a trip there.","“Dreamland only opens once every thousand years, and access is based on the invitation letters they distribute. Only those with an invitation letter can enter. There has been bloodshed over the invitation letters all throughout history. Some world emperors even offered to trade a planet for an invitation letter, but there were no takers.”","Sensing Zu An’s astonishment, the masked figure smiled. He was certain that this gift would satisfy Zu An, and his guess was on the mark.","“How can the invitation letters be snatched if Dreamland specifically sent them to certain individuals?” Zu An was perplexed.","“There are no names on the invitation letter. Dreamland only recognizes the invitation letter, not the individual. That’s why I can give this to you,” the masked figure explained.","“It feels as if Dreamland intentionally adopted such a system to stir conflict.” Zu An frowned. He wasn’t fond of such maneuvers.","The masked figure thought nothing of it. “Think of it as a trial. Someone who gets their invitation letter stolen isn’t worthy of entering Dreamland. Dreamland doesn’t want to waste time on the weak either. Experts are capable of offering more valuable things to it.”","Zu An fell silent. It's the survival of the fittest after all. He glanced at the masked figure and asked, “Based on what you've said, the invitation letter is incredibly valuable. Why do you want to give it to me?”","The masked figure sighed. “I obtained this invitation letter because of my position as a scribe. There are many major events in the myriad worlds waiting to be recorded, and I have another mission on hand. On top of that, I must rush back to inform my comrades that a Time Scribe infiltrated our ranks. My hands are full. It just so happens you did us a huge favor, so it feels right to thank you with this invitation letter.”","Zu An took the invitation letter. It was unlike any material he had ever seen before, resembling a fusion between gold and jade.","The masked figure addressed his confusion, saying, “The letters are made from Dreamland’s specially produced amber. They cannot be forged by anyone else, which is why the invitation letters are so highly sought after.”","“Thank you. I just realized that I don’t know your name yet,” Zu An said as he stowed away the invitation letter. The other party looked to be a decent person, and it just so happened that he knew next to nothing about the myriad worlds. It would be good for him to make a friend here.","The masked figure was overjoyed. Scribes like him were obsessed with the notion of making a name for themselves in history. A world's master asking for his name meant that his name could be recorded in the annals, too. He replied, “I am Unblind Zuoqiu.”","“That is a rather scholarly name.” Zu An was perplexed by the name.","Unblind Zuoqiu was overjoyed to hear the remark. “I like this name too. We, Mirror Scribes, usually pick names from people we revere in history as testament to our mission.”","Zu An felt a headache settling in as Unblind Zuoqiu began talking about the elders in his industry. It was a while later before he found a chance to slip in a question. “Brother Zuoqiu, what major powers are there in the myriad worlds? We don’t get much information here.”","Unblind Zuoqiu replied, “The 'myriad worlds' is a term referring to the collection of all universes. Some barriers are nigh impossible to cross between universes and prevent them from interacting with each other. It is tough to travel to other universes unless your universe has reached a certain level of civilization.","“Your universe used to have a fair number of civilizations, but they were all conquered by the Monster World. With the destruction of the Monster World, your world is now the only one left in your universe.”","“There are many theories about the form of the myriad worlds. One of the more mainstream ideas is the Tree Conjecture. It is said that the Creation Tree has countless leaves on it, and each leaf is a universe. Each universe has many galaxies and civilizations, but it is difficult for one leaf to interact with another leaf.","“I am personally more inclined to see the myriad worlds as a beehive. Each honeycomb is a universe, but there are walls between each honeycomb that make it nigh impossible for two universes to interact.”","This greatly clarified Zu An’s thoughts. “The people who destroyed the Monster World—which deity’s worshipers are they?”"]},{"number":2677,"title":"Chapter 2677: Chapter 2629: The Deity’s Gaze","paragraphs":["Unblind Zuoqiu was taken aback by Zu An’s question. He hesitantly lowered his voice and replied, “They worship the Deity of Annihilation. I don’t dare to utter his name, and I don’t advise you to seek it either. You’ll only bring annihilation upon your world if you draw his gaze...” Fearing that his words had offended the Deity of Annihilation, he anxiously took out a book and began chanting as if to tap into his deity’s protection.","Zu An was disappointed by the other party’s frightened reaction. He'd been hoping to gather more information about the Deity of Annihilation. The Monster World had nearly destroyed the Cultivation World, but all it took to destroy the Monster World was a subordinate from the Deity of Annihilation. It was hard not to be wary of such a being.","Zu An wanted to ask more about the myriad worlds, but Unblind Zuoqiu said, “The other civilizations of your universe have been destroyed, so there is nothing else for you to learn about. There is also little point in learning about the other universes’ civilizations in advance. You can take a look yourself if there is an opportunity for you to cross universes.”","He took on a solemn tone as he continued, “Brother Zu, you must remember one thing when you travel to other worlds. Learning about secrets comes with risks. Knowing things you shouldn’t know will bring you danger. It’s the same when you leak secrets too.”","“Thank you for your warning, Brother Zuoqiu. I've gotten ahead of myself.” This wasn't the first time Zu An had heard such words. Secrets must be truly dangerous.","“All right, Brother Zu An. I need to take my leave now. May we meet again.” Unblind Zuoqiu clasped his fist as he bade Zu An farewell.","Zu An panicked. “Brother Zuoqiu, shouldn’t you at least tell me where Dreamland is? Didn’t you mention earlier that there are barriers that cannot be crossed between universes?”","Unblind Zuoqiu smacked his head. “Ah, I nearly forgot that you lack common knowledge of the myriad worlds. The barriers between universes are indeed nigh impossible to cross, but there are plenty of adventurers in the myriad worlds who make it their goal to explore the unknown. They have developed a way to cross universe barriers, but I shan’t elaborate on the details.","“The invitation letter you have isn’t for show. Once Dreamland opens, the invitation letters will sense it. All you have to do is to infuse your spiritual energy, immortal ki, chakra... Well, different worlds have different terms for their energy, but they are all fundamentally the same. You just have to use your ki to activate the invitation letter, and a spaceship will come to fetch you.”","“Spaceship? Is it from Dreamland?” Zu An was taken aback.","“No, it’s from a universal commercial organization. Dreamland hires them to fetch their guests. This ensures that anyone with the invitation letter can reach Dreamland without a hitch,” Unblind Zuoqiu explained. He suddenly widened his eyes as he murmured, “Ah! I unknowingly divulged more secrets to you again. No, I can’t stay here any longer, or else I’ll be taking a huge loss!”","Despite Zu An’s attempts to keep him, Unblind Zuoqiu’s figure slowly turned transparent before vanishing into thin air. Zu An was stunned.","Unblind Zuoqiu's hurried departure invited Shang Hongyu to remark, “He seems more like a worshiper of the Deity of Commerce than the Deity of Memories.”","Zu An chuckled. “Perhaps there are rules for exchange in the myriad worlds. Secrets are probably very valuable commodities.”","“Ah Zu, do you truly intend to head there?” Shang Hongyu asked worriedly.","“Yeah. There are far too many people I have to save, and I've already done everything I can in this world. My only option is to seek solutions elsewhere,” Zu An replied.","“But it’ll be dangerous.” Shang Hongyu bit her lip. She was in no mood to get jealous.","“The greater the risks, the greater the rewards.” Zu An grabbed her hand. “Don’t worry, Hongyu. Danger has accompanied me for many years now, but...”","Shang Hongyu placed her finger on his lips as she looked at him with worried eyes. “Never lose your fear of danger.”","Zu An’s heart warmed. He knew she was telling him not to raise any death flags here.","“It’s still too early to say for sure. I don’t know when Dreamland is going to open yet,” he said. The invitation letter had a date, but it followed a different format from that of the Cultivation World.","“How can that Mirror Scribe be so unreliable? He left without properly explaining things,” Shang Hongyu huffed. “The other civilizations likely use a different language, right? How are you going to communicate with them?”","Zu An’s smile stiffened. He had failed to consider this problem earlier. Hm? Hold on. Isn’t it weird I was able to communicate with others in the other worlds I've gone to? Is it because these worlds all fall under the Six Paths? If so, it might not work in other universes.","“Don’t worry. A spaceship is coming to fetch me, so there must be a solution.” Zu An knew that cultivators of a certain level could communicate through certain laws or telepathy, though it wouldn't be as convenient.","“I hope so. Let’s discuss this with my little sister.” Shang Hongyu grabbed his arm. Her little sister was still feeling embarrassed over what had happened two days ago, but this wasn’t the time for her to be feeling awkward.","Zu An nodded as the two of them made their way to the Dragon Palace. On the way, he began chatting with Mi Li, “Big sister empress, are you truly not that Deity of Chaos and Enigma?”","“Are you hoping for it to be me or not?” The red-dressed Mi Li appeared beside him with an unreadable smile. She was a unique being; unless she chose to reveal herself, only Zu An could see her soul.","“Of course I’m hoping it’s you. With such a thick thigh to latch onto in the myriad worlds, I would have nothing to fear!” Zu An laughed.","Mi Li rolled her eyes. “I also hope it’s me, so I can discipline you for that blasphemous thought.”","All of a sudden, however, her expression warped in shock, and she vanished.","While Zu An was wondering what had happened, white lights suddenly lit up around him. Suddenly, he was no longer surrounded by emerald seawater, and Shang Hongyu was nowhere to be seen either. He now seemed to be floating in the middle of space.","What’s going on? I'm this world’s master. How can something ridiculous like this happen when I've already activated the world barrier?","The surrounding white lights converged to form a peculiar pattern, then unprecedentedly tremendous pressure suddenly weighed down on Zu An. He was horrified. He felt as if he was on the verge of being torn apart.","“You want to latch onto my thick thigh?” an impassive voice boomed."]},{"number":2678,"title":"Chapter 2678: Chapter 2630: Conversing With a Deity","paragraphs":["A mini explosion seemed to happen in Zu An’s mindd, warning him about the danger he was in. He felt as if he could disintegrate at the other party’s mere thought. He had never felt so shaken before, even when he was standing against a Celestial Emperor. Never had he felt so overpowered that he couldn’t even summon the willpower to retaliate.","This entity was even stronger than the mysterious being Qiu Honglei had summoned through the Dance Offering to the Universe. Judging from the other party’s strength and tone, they must be the Deity of Chaos and Enigma, Mi Li.","He finally understood why so many people had warned him not to carelessly mention a deity’s name. He hadn’t expected that a mere joke he cracked would catch the other party’s attention.","He quickly snapped out of his daze and replied, “I just heard what the Mirror Scribe said, and I have to say that I strongly disagree with his view of chaos and enigma. The world is born amid chaos and enigma, and that is bound to be its ultimate state as well. There is no need for events to be recorded so clearly. An overly defined history will only make everything boring. Only vague information shrouded in mystery can bring endless entertaining possibilities.”","His brain was furiously churning to rake up all of the knowledge he had accrued over his several lifetimes to bootlick the other party. He knew that he only had one shot, and if he failed to secure enough goodwill, destruction would be his plight.","“You seem to believe that I am the Deity of Chaos and Enigma, Mi Li?” The other party’s ethereal voice was tinged with mischief. It sounded feminine, but Zu An didn’t know if it would be right to gender stereotype a deity. She didn’t speak in the Cultivation World’s tongue, but Zu An could still comprehend her, as her voice seemed to directly reach his soul.","Her words left Zu An with goosebumps. Hold on, did I bootlick the wrong person?","If the other party was the Deity of Memories, Meng, his earlier words would have been incredibly disrespectful. The entire Cultivation World could be destroyed because of what he'd just said!","“Your heartbeat and your profuse sweat show that you’re very nervous, but why don’t you try explaining yourself? Is Mi Li the only one worth fawning over?” the voice spoke coldly.","“My mortal wits are nothing in the face of a true deity. I’m sure that, with your divine splendor, you can sense the utmost respect I have for you,” Zu An respectfully replied.","“I only feel your cunning.” She had no corporeal body. All Zu An saw were white lights reminiscent of starlight, moving around and pulsating with different degrees of brightness. That seemed to represent her expression.","Sweat rained down Zu An’s face. He didn’t dare to think too much, fearing that the other party could peer into his mind.","“Forget it. You’re in luck. I am Mi Li,” the voice replied.","I would be luckier if I hadn't caught your attention. Zu An shuddered as soon as the thought popped into his head, and he quickly dispelled it. “I am honored to be in the presence of a revered entity like yourself. May I know if there is anything I can do for you?”","The starlight flickered, as if angered by his disrespectful thought. “Can’t I look for you if I have nothing else to do?”","Zu An sensed that the other party wasn’t as inflexible as he had thought. Rather, she seems a bit...","Not daring to dwell too much on that, he quickly replied, “Revered deities like you must be extremely busy. It is beneath a mortal like me to take up your time for no reason.”","“Don’t use your shallowness to comprehend beings like us.” That voice harrumphed. “In this world, you are a deity, but don’t you still frolic around with those females?”","Zu An was horrified. It felt like the other party had been observing him for a long time. “With my minor accomplishments in my narrow domain, compared to your exalted self, I am no deity.”","He was being so subservient that it even disgusted himself, but the omnipresent terrifying aura vanquished such thoughts right away.","“At least you still have some self-awareness.” The voice chuckled. “I'm here to settle the score with you. That Time Scribe was my worshiper. Tell me, how should I deal with this?”","Zu An trembled. “That Time Scribe’s death has nothing to do with...”","He bit his tongue before he could finish speaking. What if the other party goes after Xihe and Shang Hongyu if I shirk responsibility here?","So, he quickly changed his tune, saying, “It’s a misunderstanding. We didn’t know he was your worshiper.”","“You’re a loyal one. It’s good that you’re willing to bear this karma.” The starlight shimmered dazzlingly. “I don’t want any excuses. You killed my worshiper. If I don’t avenge him today, anyone would dare to hurt my worshipers.”","Beneath the beautiful starlight lurked nearly tangible murderous intent. Zu An racked his brain and replied, “That Time Scribe was one of your countless worshipers. You are the master, whereas he’s your servant. It doesn’t make sense for the master to avenge the servant’s death. It should be the servant avenging the master’s...”","“Hm?”","Zu An nearly choked. “What I’m saying is that this goes against the way of things. Others will wonder who is the master and who is the servant.”","“Are you teaching me how to do things now?” It was impossible to read Mi Li’s emotions from her words.","“I don’t dare to, but I have an idea in mind.” Zu An’s mind had never churned that quickly before.","“Speak!”","“It’s just a Time Scribe. You can find someone to fill his place.”","“It sounds as if you want to be a Time Scribe. It’s not that easy.”","“What I previously did, in a way, fulfills the essence of a Time Scribe,” Zu An hesitantly replied. He chose not to fully divulge what had happened in the spacetime fragment and the Celestial Court world to see if the other party was truly omniscient.","The starlight flickered. A while later, she said, “Indeed, you are a talent in this field. You made a mess of history without changing major events. You’re more outstanding than that buffoon.”","Zu An slowly regained his nerves. His willpower had been sharpened from the countless dangerous encounters he had. By now, he'd already made sense of the situation. She wouldn’t have wasted her breath on me if she was truly here to punish me. This might have been her intention from the start.","“You think I was laying a trap for you?” the voice coldly asked.","Cold sweat rained from Zu An."]},{"number":2679,"title":"Chapter 2679: Chapter 2631: Taking a Gamble to Become an Envoy","paragraphs":["She can read my thoughts!","Zu An quickly stifled that thought. He didn’t dare to carelessly harbor any more thoughts lest he blaspheme the deity before him. “I am in awe of the exalted deity’s omniscience!”","He didn't try to explain himself, instead opting to shrug it off with bootlicking.","As he expected, Mi Li didn’t pursue this matter. “Not only are you a world's master, but you know how to read and navigate the situation, too. You have the talent to become a Time Scribe. Very well, from this day onward, you shall be a new Time Scribe.”","An old book and a disheveled brush appeared in front of Zu An. These two items looked extremely normal; no one would have taken a second look at them in a bookstore. But as a world's master, he could tell that something was special about them. They exuded a faint, ancient, desolate intent.","He took the book and flipped through it. The river of history seemed to flow through the book; different images flashed before his eyes, only to recede into the book the next second.","Zu An stared at the blank page before him in a daze. He couldn’t help but wonder if he had been hallucinating.","It was then that he received a series of messages from his Keyboard System.","Item: Time Annal","Ability: ???","Learnable: No.","Zu An was taken aback. After obtaining the Netherworld Book of Life and Death, he'd gained the ability to consume Rage points to learn abilities from items he came into contact with. The only reason he hadn’t used it more often was because of the astronomical Rage points required to invoke that ability, but never before had an item been unlearnable to him. It’s no wonder she’s an exalted deity of the myriad worlds.","All of a sudden, he trembled in shock. Ah, she can read my mind.","“You seem to have something interesting with you.” The starlight flickered with interest.","Zu An suppressed the thoughts in his mind and replied, “Nothing I have is worth a mention before an omniscient deity like yourself.”","The starlight formed two curved eyes. “That’s true.”","Zu An resisted the urge to retort about the other party’s little girl-like nature and hurriedly changed the topic. “I remember that the Time Scribe could alter everyone’s memories. Why don’t I have any ability at all?”","He had never considered rejecting Mi Li at all. You must be kidding me. I would be out of my mind to reject an entity as powerful as her. Besides, if I can obtain a universal deity’s protection as a Time Scribe, I might be able to march anywhere in the universe with my chest puffed out.","“Would you like to swap what you have for that ability if you like it that much?” The starlight flickered once more as she spoke with a teasing voice.","Zu An anxiously changed his tune and replied, “I’ll treasure whatever you bestowed upon me as a treasure, regardless of whether it is good or not.”","The starlight harrumphed. “You aren’t that good at fawning. How can something I bestow upon my worshiper be terrible? Hold the Spring Autumn Brush and the Time Annal at the same time.”","Zu An did as he was told, holding the brush in one hand and the book in the other. Enlightenment immediately came to him.","Spring Autumn Brush and Time Annal Combination Ability: Exists","As long as it is plausible and reasonable, whatever is written with the Spring Autumn Brush in the Time Annal will become reality.","Note: The content written must be reasonable. If it is too far-fetched or the narrative is too easily unraveled, the ability will be rendered ineffective.","Zu An’s breathing quickened. Isn’t this ability overpowered?","It was similar to his Keyboard Come ability, but the latter required too high a price. Each time he used that ability, he would be left on the verge of death. In comparison, this ability didn’t require him to pay a price. All he needed to do was ensure that the content he penned down was reasonable.","He couldn’t resist asking, “O great Deity of Chaos and Enigma, could I become a revered deity like you by writing it down in this book?”","“What do you think?” the starlight asked. Rather than being angry, she was amused by his boldness.","“Probably not,” Zu An replied sheepishly. “Will anything I write be realized as long as it is reasonable?”","“You can understand it that way, but you need to be careful when writing about certain entities. The stronger the target, the lower the chances of success. Know that you’ll suffer a backlash if you fail; it could range from severe injuries to instant disintegration. You need to be very prudent with what you write in the Time Annal,” the voice echoed.","Zu An nodded. If there were no restrictions to their abilities, Time Scribes would have ruled the world by now. The other deities’ worshipers had to have their overpowered abilities too.","A thought came to his mind and he said, “Let me give it a try.” He picked up the Spring Autumn Brush and quickly wrote a few words.","“You’re already using it now?” Mi Li, despite being a deity, was curious as to what he would write.","Zu An soon finished writing what he wanted.","“On a certain day of a certain month of a certain year, Zu An was summoned by the exalted Deity of Chaos and Enigma and earned Her approval. She bestowed him with a standing and power unlike ordinary Time Scribes and conferred him as an Envoy of Chaos and Enigma.”","Other than their worshipers, deities also had envoys representing them, similar to how diplomats represented their respective nations. Needless to say, envoys wielded power and authority far superior to ordinary worshipers.","He was taking a gamble here. He sensed that the other party harbored some goodwill for him, so he pushed his luck a little. Most of what was written here was true anyway, and the fabricated portions, as long as she didn’t object to it, could become reality too. She had her pride to uphold, after all. It wouldn’t look good on her if the ability she had just bestowed failed on the first try... right?","Mi Li exclaimed, “...You sure are brazen!”","The starlight shook. For a moment there, it resembled a CPU burning out.","Zu An put on his most sincere smile and said, “O great Deity of Chaos and Enigma, I can feel your magnanimity and the favor you have shown me. Am I mistaken in my words?”","“You are much more interesting than those boring, inflexible fellows, but don’t you think you’re too bold to scheme against me?”","Starlight abruptly fell on the Time Annal, altering its contents. Zu An lowered his head and saw an additional ‘provisional’ word—'provisional envoy.'","Mi Li continued speaking, “How can becoming my envoy be that easy? But given the good work you have done in those worlds, I’ll let you enjoy being my provisional envoy for now. Don’t worry, you’ll have a chance to become a true envoy as long as you continue doing a good job.”","Zu An felt as if a rock had been lifted from his chest. “Thank you, exalted Deity of Chaos and Enigma!”"]},{"number":2680,"title":"Chapter 2680: Chapter 2632: How Can I Repay Them For Their Sentiments?","paragraphs":["“If you truly wish to thank me, show me more interesting work. It’d be best if you could make a complete mess of history.” The starlight flickered in anticipation of the future.","Zu An was perplexed. Are you the Deity of Chaos and Enigma or the Deity of Entertainment?","Worried that the other party could read his mind, he quickly halted his train of thought and instead tried to gather some information about Jiang Luofu. “O great deity, I have a companion who seems to have been summoned by a true deity. May I ask who that deity is?”","“Oh? Someone from a border world like yours caught the eye of those fellows?” Mi Li was surprised.","Zu An recounted Jiang Luofu’s mysterious circumstances before her disappearance.","The starlight shimmered as if checking on something. A while later, the voice said, “I get it.”","Zu An was overjoyed. “May I know who summoned my friend?”","“You’ll know when the time comes,” Mi Li replied.","Zu An nearly choked on his saliva. Ugh, another riddler! “May I know when the right time will be?”","“You said something that I deeply agree with. We shouldn’t confuse the position of the master and the servant. I granted you power and bestowed you artifacts, and here you are, demanding that I find someone for you. Are you the master here, or am I?” The voice turned chilly.","“Of course you are!” Zu An secretly wiped away cold sweat. These deities are unpredictable!","“It’s good that you know. Go alter more entertaining history and satisfy me, and I'll consider telling you,” Mi Li said nonchalantly.","“Yes!” Zu An tried his luck. “Do you have artifacts that can travel through time? That would make it much easier for me to alter history.”","With such a tool, I could return to the past and reunite with the Mermaid Queen and the Goddess of Wu Mountain. He recalled Shang Hongyu’s anger and added another name to the list. And Xihe too.","“Hmph! Trying to use official work to fulfill your private agenda? I don’t care which women you copulate with. As long as you offer me enough entertaining stories, I can let you copulate with all the beautiful women in the myriad worlds.” Mi Li coldly harrumphed.","Cold sweat rained down Zu An. I nearly forgot she can read my thoughts. How am I supposed to guard against this? He had an overactive brain. More often than not, random thoughts would pop uncontrollably into his mind. And the way she phrased it is bizarre too. It’s almost as if she’s rearing a pet.","“Time-traveling tools fall under a special category. Unlike Time... Hmph, there is much you can’t know about yet. All you need to know is that you don’t need to travel back in time to change history. Everything you do has the possibility to change history. Your trip to Dreamland is a good opportunity. You have to go, and you'd better make it a big event for me. Otherwise, I have no use for you.” The voice gradually faded as if it was leaving.","Zu An barely blinked before the starlight around him disappeared without a trace. He had returned to the ocean, and Shang Hongyu was worriedly tugging his arm. “Ah Zu? Ah Zu?”","“What’s wrong?” Zu An snapped out of his daze.","“I should be asking you that. You suddenly stopped moving,” Shang Hongyu huffed.","Zu An widened his eyes. “How long was I gone for?”","“Not long. Around two to three breaths. But that would have been long enough for an enemy to take you down,” Shang Hongyu replied.","“I was summoned by a deity.” Zu An realized that only his consciousness had been summoned, but he wondered why time hadn’t halted. Won’t I be in danger if the deity abruptly summons me while I'm fighting a life-and-death battle with an enemy? I should ask how she handles such a situation.","“Ah?” Shang Hongyu was stunned. She hadn’t expected to receive such a shocking answer. “What happened?”","“Let’s find Liuyu first, then we’ll talk together.”","Shang Liuyu was still feeling embarrassed and didn’t want to face them, but upon hearing about the otherworldly intruder and Zu An’s meeting with a deity, she hurriedly opened her doors.","Zu An proceeded to share the story of their encounter with the Mirror Scribe and his subsequent audience with a true deity.","The two women were horrified. “We mustn’t carelessly speak of the deities in the future.”","Zu An chuckled as he took out the Spring Autumn Brush and Time Annal. “It turned out to be a blessing in disguise.”","The two women were stunned when they learned about his new ability. It transcended the possibilities of their current world.","Zu An wondered whether to take this chance to write about a steamy night with the two sisters... but he quickly stifled that thought. It was only a matter of time before that came to be, so there was no need to rely on such cheats. Besides, he didn’t know whether writing such nonsense in the Time Annal was considered blasphemy. It would be terrible if he angered Mi Li with that.","“While becoming a deity’s envoy comes with huge merits, it also means that you’ll be embroiled in the conflicts between true deities. That could potentially put you in more danger in the future,” Shang Liuyu reminded him. “Ah Zu, I know you’re determined to head to Dreamland to save the others, but you'll need to avoid flaunting your position. We know too little about the other worlds; we don’t even know what enemies the Deity of Chaos and Enigma has.”","Zu An finally calmed down from his excitement. “Thank you for your reminder, big sister Shang. I was too optimistic earlier.”","They also discussed the potential dangers in Dreamland, but they had too little information to work with. In the end, they could only equip him with a couple of artifacts and pills from the Dragon Palace. Zu An left a few days later. He didn’t know when Dreamland would open, so he needed to make arrangements for his absence.","Before he left, Shang Liuyu gave him a suit of scale mail, saying, “Ah Zu, my big sister and I wove this armor out of our Mermaid race’s most valuable Heart Guarding Scales. We already intended to do so when you headed to the Monster World back then, but it’s only recently that we finally finished working on it.”","Zu An took the scale mail. Iridescent light flowed through its scales; it looked gorgeous. Despite being made out of scales, it was as smooth and flexible as thin silk, and it didn’t weigh much either.","“How fragrant.” He lifted the scale mail to his nose to take a whiff, an action that caused the two sisters to blush.","Shang Hongyu gently smacked him. “What are you doing? This scale mail is made not just from our Heart Guarding Scales but the ones left behind by generations of Mermaid Queens. You’re blaspheming our ancestors.”","Zu An quickly reined in his smile and apologized to the two ladies. He had once received a scale from a certain Mermaid Queen that allowed him to withstand a fatal attack once. This chainmail, on the other hand, was made out of the most important scales from many generations of Mermaid Queens. Its defensive prowess had to be at a ridiculous level.","The two sisters had practically emptied the Mermaid race’s treasury for him. He was moved. How can I repay their sentiments?","But there were too many things he needed to do, so their time together was destined to be limited. He held the two ladies tightly in his embrace. The two also knew that it could be a long time before they met again, so they tightly embraced him back."]},{"number":2681,"title":"Chapter 2681: Chapter 2633: Impetus","paragraphs":["A while later, Shang Hongyu suddenly stood up and said, “Ah Zu, my little sister has something she wishes to say. I shan’t disturb the two of you.” Following that, she left with a bizarre smile. She even shot her little sister a look before closing the door behind her.","Zu An looked at Shang Liuyu in surprise. “Big sister Shang, what do you want to tell me?”","Shang Liuyu’s cheeks immediately reddened. Her previously relaxed expression suddenly looked incredibly awkward. It was a moment later before she spoke up. “My big sister said that since we have already progressed to this point, we should become a proper couple before you leave, lest...”","“Lest what?” The other party’s shy appearance made her look indescribably delectable to Zu An, so he couldn’t resist teasing her further.","Shang Liuyu raised her head to look him in the eye. She gently touched his cheeks with her fair hands. “Lest something were to happen to you. I’d live out the rest of my life in regret.”","Those words moved Zu An, and he grabbed her hand. They are truly concerned about me. I’m heading to other universes that we know nothing about; even I don’t know what will happen.","He pulled her into his arms and said, “I’ll be careful. I have the backing of a true deity now, so the trip won’t be as dangerous as you think it to be.”","“Mm.” Shang Liuyu rested her cheek against his chest and felt his heartbeat. Her heart slowly calmed down.","“You only mentioned what your big sister thought. How about you?” Zu An asked.","“I...” Shang Liuyu looked conflicted. A while later, she shook her head and replied, “I don’t know.”","“Do you feel as if something is missing?” Zu An asked with a smile.","Shang Liuyu instinctively nodded. “Indeed, especially after hearing your story with the ancient Mermaid Queen. She might be my past incarnation, but we're still two different people. I envy the deep bond you two shared.”","Her words were vague, but Zu An understood what she was getting at. He and Shang Liuyu had already maxed out their feelings for each other, but they were lacking an impetus to advance their relationship. Were it not for his encounter with the ancient Mermaid Queen, this parting could have served that purpose.","However, women were sentimental creatures. Zu An already had a grasp of Shang Liuyu’s personality from the first time he met her. Beneath her carefree exterior was an innocent girl who harbored fantasies about love. She didn’t want to be outdone by her previous incarnation.","“You don’t need to feel burdened. We don’t have to rush things and regret it in the future. Wait for my return. We’ll find an auspicious timing and get married...” Zu An’s expression suddenly stiffened halfway through his words.","Pui pui pui! How can I raise such a massive death flag?! Movie characters who promise to marry their lover after returning from a dangerous trip are almost guaranteed to die. How could I make such a low-level mistake?","Shang Liuyu’s face also warped in horror as the same thought occurred to her. “You mentioned before that such words are incredibly inauspicious.”","“Then you should accompany me tonight to console my wounded soul. Don’t worry, I won’t do anything other than hug you.”","Shang Liuyu nodded. It looked as if her cheeks had been applied with the world’s finest rouge. With their parting imminent, she wanted to spend as much time with her lover as possible. They embraced in bed as they shared their yearning for each other.","All of a sudden, Shang Liuyu shuddered. “Y-You... Why are you touching my foot?”","“How beautiful.” Zu An fiddled with the foot in his hand. He finally understood why there were so many people who were into feet. “Big sister Shang, you don’t know how much I hoped to have such a day with you from the first time we met.”","Shang Liuyu recalled the first time they'd met in a gazebo and smiled gently. “So back then, you were already a scheming pervert.”","“It’s called appreciation for beauty.” Zu An missed the old days. “I wouldn’t have dared to overstep the line back then.”","“But now you dare?” Shang Liuyu regretted it as soon as she blurted those words out.","“Well, I’d obey if big sister Shang tells me to stop right now,” Zu An said as he leaned in.","Shang Liuyu immediately exclaimed, “Stop!”","Zu An was rendered speechless. “I haven’t even started yet!”","“But you’re... You’re still holding it.” Shang Liuyu could feel the heat from Zu An’s palm against her foot, and that made her heartbeat quicken.","Zu An was amused by how tense she was. “Does the Mermaid race have sensitive feet?”","Shang Liuyu turned away as she grumbled, “I’m sure you know given how often you play with my big sister.”","Zu An relished in her pleasant, quivering voice. He reflexively gripped her foot even tighter.","Shang Liuyu trembled. She shouted in alarm, “Stop!”","“See, I keep my promises, don’t I?” Zu An chuckled at her flustered response.","“Remove your hand.” The furiously blushing Shang Liuyu tried to withdraw her leg, but Zu An held it so firmly that she couldn’t pull it out.","“I only promised to stop when you asked me to. I didn’t say that I would release your leg.”","“You liar! Ahh, don’t... Stop!”","Zu An was amused. “Are you asking me to stop or not?”","“You’re taking advantage of me!” Shang Liuyu gritted her teeth. She lurched forward and bit his shoulder.","The two of them began bickering. At some point, the room abruptly fell silent. They found themselves so close that they could feel each other’s breaths.","Shang Liuyu’s beautiful eyebrows fluttered. She suddenly found herself at a loss.","Zu An leaned in. Shang Liuyu’s breathing quickened, but she didn’t avoid him.","The two lovers kissed.","Some time later, Shang Liuyu suddenly exclaimed with a quivering voice, “Why are you taking off your clothes?”","“It’s too hot.”","“But you’re taking off my clothes too!”","“Aren’t you hot too?”","“But we’re in the underwater Dragon Palace!”","“How weird. The Dragon Palace feels oddly hot today.”","“No... Stop!”","“Don’t worry, I’ll just cuddle a little.”","“...”","A while later, Shang Liuyu bit her lips. Her eyes glimmered as she murmured, “If you really wish to... I can do it too.”","Her concession left Zu An feeling as if his mind was going to explode, but he shook his head. Perhaps she sounded willing now, but it would leave her with regrets. He didn’t want to leave her with a lifelong regret over a moment of recklessness.","Shang Liuyu felt his concern, and that tinged her heart with sweetness. But when she lowered her head, she couldn’t help but worry. “But your current condition...”","“You can help me.”","“Ah... It was big sister who did it the last time. Should I call her over?”","“You don’t necessarily have to use...” Zu An leaned in and whispered to her.","Shang Liuyu was stunned. Her face reddened in embarrassment. “Where do you learn this nonsense from?”","Worried he would get his way, she morphed her legs back into a tail to cut his thoughts short.","...","The following day, Shang Hongyu and Shang Liuyu escorted Zu An out of the Dragon Palace for thousands of kilometers before reluctantly bidding him farewell.","Shang Liuyu sighed. “Big sister, do you think I’m useless?”","“Ah? You didn’t give it to him even though it was such a good opportunity yesterday?” Shang Hongyu was taken aback.","Shang Liuyu blushed furiously. “That’s not what I’m talking about! I’m lamenting that I can’t be of any help to him even though he’s venturing into an unknown world.”","“So did you give it to him yesterday or not?” Shang Hongyu was more concerned about that."]},{"number":2682,"title":"Chapter 2682: Chapter 2634: Nervousness As Home Draws Close","paragraphs":["“You ruffian!” Unable to take her big sister’s bold remarks, Shang Liuyu turned her reddened face away and fled.","“What’s there to be shy about between sisters? Tell me more!” Shang Hongyu chased her, determined to fulfill her desire for gossip.","Shang Liuyu recalled what had happened last night.","After she morphed into her mermaid tail, Zu An had suddenly shared a fairy tale called ‘The Little Mermaid’ with her. In the story, a mermaid princess had saved a prince and fell in love with him. To be with him, she'd approached a witch to morph her mermaid tail into legs, only to learn that she had to trade her melodious voice for it...","It was such a sad story that it had made her tear up, but Zu An went on to say that the mermaid princess had paid such a heavy price for her legs; it was a huge pity for her not to show hers when she had them.","His argument had stumped Shang Liuyu. In the end, she'd turned her tail back into legs, and somehow, she'd ended up helping him the way he told her to... She could still feel the heat on her feet, and it made her face go red. How can I share something like that with big sister?","“Nothing happened!”","Upon hearing her little sister’s answer, Shang Hongyu got agitated. “How could nothing have happened? What did I tell you before? You should listen to me. You’ll regret it for life if something happens to him out there.”","Shang Liuyu chuckled. “There’s nothing to regret. Our souls are connected. I understand him, and he understands me too.”","“Sure, sure, your love is noble and pure. Only mine is dirty and lustful,” Shang Hongyu huffed.","“Big sister, that’s not what I mean.” Shang Liuyu grabbed her big sister’s hand to placate her. “Rather than satisfying him on the spot, I thought it would be better to give him something to look forward to. He’d have to stay calm when taking risks so that he can come back safely and claim the prize. Who knows? It might give him a boost of power in his time of need.”","Shang Hongyu suddenly felt jealous. “Sure, you’re the more charming one. He thinks about coming back to you to claim his prize even when he’s struggling outside. Hmph! You know how many women that philanderer has outside? He might meet a beautiful foreign woman in Dreamland and melt in her warm embrace. Do you think he w'd still think about you then?”","“Ah Zu isn't that kind of person. I trust him,” Shang Liuyu replied with a smile. “I might not be charming enough alone, but I’m not alone. I have you too.”","“What do you mean?” Shang Hongyu looked at her with confused eyes.","“I promised him that if he returns safe and sound, we could...” Shang Liuyu reflexively lowered her head as her heart beat furiously. I must have been out of my mind to make such a promise to him last night.","Shang Hongyu was stunned. Has my elegant little sister always been this bold? She soon remarked with a pout, “Why are you dragging me into your promise?”","“Are you willing or not?” Shang Liuyu grabbed her big sister’s arm and shook it around.","“Pui! I’m not a casual woman.” Images surfaced in Shang Hongyu’s mind and tinged her cheeks red. “Unless you properly beg me then.”","“I’ll have Ah Zu properly beg you.” Shang Liuyu lowered her head in embarrassment.","“No way. I want you to beg me instead. Who asked you to put on a lofty appearance? That just makes me look cheap in contrast. I never thought you would be this bold...”","“Aiyo, my big sister...”","“You aren’t going to change my mind. Be prepared to beg me!”","...","Meanwhile, Zu An was traveling to the human capital via Rainbow Morph. Along the way, he asked Mi Li about what happened. “Master empress, you’re more incredible than I thought. You sensed a universal deity’s descent and hid in advance.”","“You were so busy playing with the two sisters that you only remembered me now?” Mi Li teased. “I’m nowhere as incredible as you are. You were able to convince that reserved little mermaid beauty to do such things for you.”","That made Zu An remember Shang Liuyu’s delicate feet, which looked like sculpted masterpieces. He let out a cough and hurriedly changed the topic. “Master empress, do you think... that person noticed you?”","“She didn’t,” Mi Li replied without hesitation.","Zu An was taken aback. “Even an existence of that caliber failed to notice your presence?”","“The contract between us is a unique one. No entity aside from you can see me unless I reveal myself on my own accord,” Mi Li declared proudly.","“Then why did you hide?” Zu An expressed his doubt at her words.","“Your lousy brain could have thought about me at a whim and given me away,” Mi Li huffed.","Zu An smiled sheepishly. The universal deities' ability to read minds was a fearsome one. “Can they really read our minds? That makes it impossible to conceal any secrets from them, and no scheme can escape their notice!”","“You're a bold one to think about scheming against them!” Mi Li looked at Zu An with eyes of approval. “They are entities standing above the myriad worlds. It won’t be that easy to deal with them. You don’t have to be worried about their mind-reading ability. They won’t constantly read your mind. It’s similar to how you wouldn’t be concerned about what a roadside ant thinks.”","Zu An nodded in realization. So that mind-reading isn’t a passive ability. It needs to be activated. At least the other party isn’t reading my mind all the time. That’s a relief.","“Have you heard about Dreamland?” he asked.","“I’ve never heard of it,” Mi Li replied without hesitation.","Zu An asked, “...Unblind Zuoqiu said that Dreamland is famous across the myriad worlds, but you've never heard about it?”","“I told you I lost most of my memories. There are two possibilities. Either I used to know about Dreamland but lost that portion of my memories, or Dreamland didn’t exist back in my era.” The red-dressed Mi Li looked into space in a daze. It was hard to tell what she was thinking.","Zu An looked conflicted. “Master empress, you’re finally admitting you’re from another world.”","“Haven’t you already guessed as much?” Mi Li chuckled, not denying it. “But my world is intricately linked to yours.”","“Do you really have no connection with those entities?” Zu An asked.","“I don’t know.” Mi Li shook her head. “I’m not lying to you. I don’t know what memories I've lost.”","Looking at her downcast expression, Zu An consoled her. “Don’t worry, master empress. I've heard Dreamland can fulfill any wish. I’ll find the materials required to reforge your body there. You might regain your memories once you regain your body.”","“At least you have a conscience. Your mind isn’t just filled with thoughts of those women.” Mi Li smiled.","“Aren’t you one of them too?” Zu An murmured.","Mi Li’s eyebrows shot up. “What did you say?”","“Nothing.”","“Are you planning an uprising against your master now?”","“...”","“Hold on! What do you mean by riding your master? What the heck is in your mind?!”","“See, you can read my mind too. And you still say you aren’t related to that Mi Li.”","“You must be tired of living! What are you going to do if she really comes?!”","...","Amid merry chatter, Zu An soon arrived at the human capital. Now that he was about to return home, he suddenly felt nervous."]},{"number":2683,"title":"Chapter 2683: Chapter 2635: Rebellion","paragraphs":["Zu An’s journey to the spacetime fragment and the ancient Celestial Court world hadn't felt long to him, but he'd come back to find that three years had passed in this world. Many things were bound to have changed within three years.","His infant daughter would have already grown up.","He took a deep breath and entered the city gate. He didn’t fly in, as the capital was the stronghold of the human race; it was protected by many formations and experts. He would cause too huge of a commotion by flying in. He wouldn’t be able to quietly do what he wanted once someone recognized him.","But as he passed by the city gates, he couldn’t help but notice that the soldiers’ inspections were much stricter than usual. That brought a frown to his face. Has Linglong not eradicated the monster remnants yet?","However, the capital was as bustling as usual. The populace didn’t seem fazed, so he didn’t think too much about it.","He made his way to the Sang manor. It looked the same as ever. Bi Linglong had intended to bestow Sang Hong with a larger manor, but the latter had rejected it. The Sang clan had few family members, so a larger manor would have only felt cold. It wouldn’t be as warm as their current manor.","Zu An headed straight to the backyard instead of entering via the main entrance—he wanted to give them a surprise. To his surprise, however, there was no one in Zheng Dan and Sang Qien’s rooms.","“Did they go out for a walk?” Zu An was disappointed.","Suddenly, he spotted a fair-skinned girl sitting on the steps, eating something that resembled a black lump. The fragrance of a sweet potato wafted in the air. He walked over and saw the girl wiping her mouth every now and then while munching the sweet potato. This resulted in her chubby cheeks being smeared black like a spotted kitten.","The girl leaped in shock when she realized that someone else was here, and she instinctively hid the sweet potato behind her. But when she saw it was Zu An, she breathed a sigh of relief and said, “I thought it was mother.” She took out the sweet potato and continued munching on it.","“Who’s your mother?” Seeing the girl’s familiar big eyes, Zu An could already fathom a guess about her identity.","“Mother is mother,” the girl mumbled through her full mouth. She thought that this uncle had asked a weird question.","Zu An took a deep breath before sitting down beside her. “Are you Sisi?”","“How do you know?” The girl finally turned away from her sweet potato to look at Zu An, her clear eyes filled with confusion.","Zu An chuckled. “Is the sweet potato delicious?”","“It’s delicious.” The little girl’s eyes lit up as she bragged in glee, “I secretly roasted this in the kitchen. Mother wouldn’t let me roast it.”","“Your mother is just worried that you’ll get hurt.” Zu An leaned closer. “The sweet potato smells good. Can you share some with me?”","The girl warily scooched away. “No way!” No wonder this weird uncle keeps talking to me. He wants my sweet potato!","She quickly stuffed the remaining sweet potato into her mouth, as if frightened that Zu An would steal it from her. It was so scalding that she kept huffing out hot air.","Zu An found this sight funny, yet worrying. He wiped off the black stains from her cheeks as he said, “Eat slower. It’s hot.”","He took out the candied hawthorn he had just bought from the street. “Do you want it? I’ll give it to you.”","When she saw the delectable candied hawthorn, the girl gulped down her saliva. She instinctively reached out to take it, only to retract it right after. “I can’t. My mother said I mustn’t take food from strangers. The stranger could be a human trafficker.”","That made her look at Zu An with even more vigilant eyes. “Who are you? Why have I never seen you before?”","The word ‘stranger’ caused Zu An’s heart to clench up. I’m a bad father. It 's been so many years that my daughter doesn’t recognize me anymore.","“Sisi, I heard you secretly ran off to roast sweet potatoes again?” An angry voice filled the air as a beautiful figure rushed over from afar. But when she saw Zu An, she froze on the spot.","The girl was horrified. She'd been racking her brain for an explanation when she noticed her mother abruptly falling silent.","“Qien’er!” Zu An cried out. It had been several years, but Sang Qien was still as beautiful as ever, although she exuded a much more mature aura now.","“Ah Zu!” Unable to curb her gushing feelings, Sang Qien rushed into Zu An’s embrace with tearful eyes, hugging him tightly as if worried that this was an illusion and he would disappear when she blinked.","Feeling her intense emotions, Zu An also hugged her tightly.","The girl was shocked. A moment later, she became so agitated that she burst into tears. “Mother, why aren’t you hugging Sisi? Sisi won’t secretly eat roasted sweet potatoed anymore. You baddie! Let go of my mother!”","Seeing how her daughter was trying to pull Zu An away, Sang Qien bent down and lifted her up. “Sisi, you often ask me about your father. He ' finally back. Here, call him ‘Father’.”","“You're my father?” The girl shyly looked at Zu An. She couldn’t imagine that the man who'd tried to dupe her out of her sweet potato was the great hero father that her mother told her about.","Unable to hold himself back anymore, Zu An embraced Sisi. The latter felt like a meat dumpling; she was soft and fragrant in his arms. He could feel their shared bloodline.","Sang Qien took out a handkerchief to wipe her daughter’s cheeks. “Look at you. You got so dirty eating a sweet potato again...” She felt a bit frustrated. She hadn’t expected her daughter to look so unkempt during their long-awaited reunion; it made it look as if she hadn’t taken good care of her.","Zu An chuckled. He took the handkerchief from Sang Qien’s hand to help wipe his daughter’s face. “She’s adorable.”","The tenderness in his eyes brought a warm smile to Sang Qien.","The girl suddenly stared intently at Zu An’s candied hawthorn. She licked her lips as she asked, “Mother, I can take food from father, right?”","“Eat, eat, eat! Haven’t I told you to be more demure?” Sang Qien was at a loss for words. Clearly, Sisi had brought her many headaches over the years.","Zu An laughed as he passed the candied hawthorn over. “Of course.”","Seeing that her mother didn’t object to it, the girl’s eyes lit up as she took the candied hawthorn. “Thank you, father!”","Seeing her daughter forgetting about her father once she had food in her hand, Sang Qien looked at Zu An apologetically and said, “Ah Zu, this lass is fond of eating. It may take a while for her to warm up to you.”","Zu An laughed. “I think she’s adorable as she is. Kids are all like that...”","Sang Qien also looked at her daughter with warm eyes. “Indeed. She’s adorable.”","Warmth lingered between them as they chatted about recent affairs. A while later, Zu An asked out of curiosity, “Hm? Why don’t I see Zheng Dan around?”","Sang Qien replied, “Dandan has followed the army to aid the empress in quelling the rebellion.”","“Rebellion?” Zu An was startled.","Sang Qien explained, “The Zhao clan’s kings are dissatisfied that a woman has taken the throne, and it's been years since we last heard from you. So, King Yan and the other kings staged a rebellion in the name of the imperial grandson to force Linglong to abdicate.”"]},{"number":2684,"title":"Chapter 2684: Chapter 2636: Irrepressible Thought","paragraphs":["“Imperial grandson? Who?” Zu An was confused.","“It’s Concubine Bai’s son,” Sang Qien explained. “That’s the crown prince’s only child, so he commands legitimacy. On top of that, the crown prince became the emperor later, giving his child more rallying power within the Zhao clan.”","Zu An frowned. Concubine Bai, huh...","During their trip to Violet Mountain, Zhao Han had sensed his impending death and chosen to prematurely sentence Concubine Bai, a spy of the demonic cult, to death. He'd even instructed Zu An to make the move. It had taken a lot of effort for Zu An to save Concubine Bai by swapping her for someone else.","Later, Concubine Bai had been worried about her son, so she'd snuck back into the capital before going missing.","Zu An's first thought was that Concubine Bai wouldn’t be the ungrateful type, but on second thought, she cherished her son so much that it wouldn’t be surprising for her to do anything to pave the path for him.","“Those Zhao clan kings dare to rebel! I must have been too kind back then.” Zu An’s expression turned cold. He had purged Bi Qi and a few other kings from the capital, but he'd chosen to placate the others. From the looks of it, his soft approach had left behind an underlying threat.","Sang Qien let her daughter enjoy her candied hawthorn while discussing with Zu An, “You’d have incited chaos in advance if you killed those Zhao clan kings back then. We wouldn’t have been able to unite against the monsters. But after we curbed the monsters, the Zhao clan’s kings began to covet power. Furthermore, you've been gone for years, and there were rumors that you'd died in the other world. The ambitious ones couldn’t stay still anymore.”","Zu An was apologetic. “It must have been tough. I’m sorry for worrying you.”","Sang Qien smiled sweetly. “We didn't fall for those rumors. We trust that you can overcome any challenge and return safely.”","Zu An’s heart warmed up. He embraced her and relished in the family warmth. No matter the dangers he faced outside, there was someone here waiting for him.","“Why did Dandan join the battlefield too?” he asked out of curiosity.","“It’s all because you went against conventions and placed an empress in place.” Sang Qien rolled her eyes. “Your presence back then was too strong, to the point that no one dared say anything, but the moment you were gone, the frustrations immediately came bubbling up.","“Linglong is indeed highly competent, but even she can’t do anything about her sex. Unlike the Fiend races, we don’t have a history of empresses. There was great discontentment among the powers, so much so that they rebelled as soon as the chance arose.","“Even within the imperial court, many officials have been secretly defying her. We couldn't turn a blind eye to her predicament, so we went to help her. Thanks to our connection to you, she didn’t doubt us. Dandan led the sect she created in her earlier years to ensure the smooth flow of supplies to the frontlines. I stayed in the capital to deal with the backend logistics because I was worried about Sisi.”","Zu An fell silent after hearing her story. He could imagine how tough it had been for Bi Linglong. He was too irresponsible, to have dumped everything on her.","“What about the empress dowager?” he continued probing about the situation.","“The empress dowager and Linglong are tackling the inside and the outside, respectively. Linglong marched onto the battlefield, while the empress dowager stands guard in the capital. If not for the empress dowager, chaos would have broken out in the capital as soon as Linglong left.” Judging by how she addressed the latter by name, Sang Qien had to be on decent terms with Linglong.","Zu An nodded. Other than the stricter inspections at the city gates, there was nothing different about the capital and the populace. Liu Ning is indeed adept at governance.","“I need to make a trip to the palace,” he said. Only the empress has a bird’s eye view of the situation.","Sang Qien’s expression sank. We’re already parting ways when we've only just reunited. However, she knew that this matter took precedence, so she said, “All right. I’ll wait for you to return.”","Zu An smiled. He grabbed her hand and asked, “Why don’t you come with me?”","His warm hands and gentle eyes dispelled Sang Qien's gloomy mood, and she replied, “Sure!”","But she thought of a dilemma right away. “But there’s no one to take care of Sisi here...”","Zu An lifted Sisi up and said, “She can come with us.”","“But...” Sang Qien wanted to say that this was inappropriate, but on second thought, there should be no place in this world that his daughter couldn’t go. In the end, she only said, “All right.”","So, Zu An carried his daughter with his right hand while holding Sang Qien with his left hand as they made their way to the imperial palace’s main entrance. He didn’t bypass the guards to fly in, but instead strutted in so that more people could see that he had returned.","Sang Qien felt uncomfortable having her hand held in public, especially in a place like the imperial palace, as their relationship had been secret thus far. She tried to withdraw her hand, but Zu An held her tightly and refused to let go. With her wits, it wasn't too difficult to figure that Zu An was bringing her and their daughter to light through this.","She lowered her head and bit her lips, trying not to let her tears fall. She had already resigned herself to be Zu An’s underground lover for the rest of her life, but which woman wouldn’t want to openly appear before others with her lover?","A commotion broke out from the palace doors. “It’s the regent! The regent is back!”","Zu An responded with a smile. He was soon escorted into the palace.","The news spread like wildfire, swiftly reaching the capital’s every nook and cranny.","Liu Ning, who had been busy discussing state matters with the officials, put down her work and rushed out to welcome him.","Someone secretly reminded her, “Your Majesty, this isn’t appropriate...”","The regent was still a subject. Even the emperor had to pay respects to the empress dowager; it was beneath the empress dowager to head out and greet a subject.","Liu Ning smiled. “The regent isn’t just any subject. He’s worthy of it.”","The crowd in the Imperial Library was taken aback. The empress dowager had had a permanent frown on her face for a while now; this was their first time seeing her smiling so happily.","She looked ravishing. The sight reminded the crowd that the empress dowager wasn’t old; she was still in her prime and was exuding feminine charms.","Could the empress dowager and the regent...","The officials stifled that thought as soon as it arose, knowing it was taboo. It should be fine as long as the regent doesn’t openly marry the empress dowager. It’s not uncommon for empress dowagers in history to rear lovers anyway.","Liu Ning lifted her skirt and rushed out of the Imperial Library. There was only a single thought left in her mind, and that was to leap into Zu An’s embrace. Years of separation had simmered her yearning to a boiling point. The rebellion of the feudal kings had also repressed her emotions to an extreme degree. Now, she just wanted to let everything loose. To hell with that empress dowager title, the imperial court, and rumors. I wouldn’t want this damned position at all if not for him...","But when she saw Zu An holding Sang Qien’s hand and carrying a girl, her raging emotions finally calmed down a little. As she regained her rationality, she understood that it wasn't the right time for her to let her emotions run wild.","Even so, a thought did surface in her mind: I’m going to have his baby too!"]},{"number":2685,"title":"Chapter 2685: Chapter 2637: The Regent and the Empress","paragraphs":["Seeing the empress dowager rush out excitedly, only to regain her majestic poise upon seeing their family of three, Sang Qien instinctively released Zu An’s hand. Her womanly instincts told her that Ah Zu and the empress dowager had to have something between them.","She and Dandan had shared their guesses, but because of how sensitive the empress dowager’s identity was, they hadn’t dared to investigate. Even so, at that instant, she confirmed their relationship—there was no need for concrete proof.","She had spent many years living in the capital and understood how powerful the empress dowager was. She didn’t want to get on the empress dowager’s bad side, lest she implicate her daughter.","Zu An could never have known that Sang Qien would have thought this far in an instant. Upon seeing Liu Ning, he smiled and said, “Paying respects to the empress dowager.”","He greeted her like a friend, showing no inclination to bow. The surrounding officials didn’t think that there was anything inappropriate about his behavior either.","“You’re finally back.” Upon seeing Zu An’s warm smile, Liu Ning’s spirits lifted a little.","“The recent situation must have tired you out.” Zu An thought about the kings’ uprising and figured that Liu Ning and Bi Linglong had to have their hands full dealing with the situation.","The empress dowager’s eyes flickered. “Indeed, but now that you’re back, I’m sure my fatigue will be dispelled.”","It had been three years. She felt as if there was a flame inside her that urgently needed to be vented. Most empress dowagers who were widowed in their prime reared boy toys and lovers. She was no maiden herself, but the two men in her life had been truly top tier. After the time she'd spent with Zu An, no one else could catch her fancy anymore.","She'd thought that she would go insane in the last three years. It was almost a relief that the kings’ rebellion had distracted her, or else she wouldn’t have known how to spend the long days without him.","The officials frowned. Is it just me or does her tone sound off? We must be thinking too much of it, right? There’s no way the empress dowager is flirting in broad daylight.","Only Zu An knew that was indeed what she meant. His heart quivered. What a temptress.","But he could only feign ignorance, as there were too many people around. He coughed lightly and asked, “Your Majesty, what’s the current situation?”","“Let’s talk in the Imperial Library.” The empress dowager beckoned the officials to follow her.","Zu An noticed that the officials present looked unfamiliar and young. The empress dowager explained through telepathy, “The imperial court has been in turmoil in recent years. The old foxes have already lined their pockets. They feign submission, only to act against me in the shadows. Linglong and I had no choice but to nurture the younger officials.”","Zu An nodded. He had been in a high position as well, and that had given him a glimpse into the power struggles in politics.","No matter how ingenious and beneficial a policy was, whether it worked out or not ultimately depended on the executor. Should the wrong person be entrusted with a policy’s execution, they could either execute the policy poorly, or warp its intent to cause outrage toward the ruler. The officials who were currently in power had been nurtured by Zhao Han, so it wouldn’t be easy for the empress dowager and Bi Linglong to bring them over to their side.","There was a massive sandbox in the middle of the room. Zu An could tell it was a map of several provinces at a glance. Liu Ning must have been discussing curbing the rebellion with the officials earlier.","The officials quickly explained the situation to Zu An.","In the period shortly after his departure, the imperial court had remained stable due to his intimidation. But when two years passed and he showed no signs of returning, rumors had begun spreading. The empress dowager and Bi Linglong tried to suppress them, but it was to no avail.","King Yan and King Guangling had been the first to gather their armies and rebel. They'd quickly gained the support of other grandmaster kings, and the movement had eventually grown into eighteen kings marching toward the capital to demand Bi Linglong’s abdication.","“They even compiled a list of the empress dowager, the empress, and the regent’s crimes...” The officials’ voices trailed off at this point.","Zu An was stunned. Huh? Did I receive Dong Zhuo’s script?","The officials passed Zu An a scroll submitted by the rebels. He glanced at it—most crimes listed on it were generic, but there was a jarring one accusing him of tainting the imperial harem and having a questionable relationship with the empress and the empress dowager.","He noticed a couple of yellow booklets that appeared to be storybooks circulating in the streets. He picked one up, and the booklet’s title made his eyelids twitch.","‘The Philandering Regent’","‘The Regent’s Romances’","‘The Regent and the Empress’","‘The Regent and My Mom’","...","The booklets were so bold and ridiculous that even the thick-skinned Zu An blushed upon reading them. Did they install cameras in the imperial palace? How do they know so much?!","The other officials also had weird looks on their faces. They'd thought that the rebels had fabricated these stories to besmirch the regent, the empress, and the empress dowager, and that no one should take them seriously. But now... They couldn’t help but wonder if they were real.","Zu An coughed lightly to change the topic. He probed further about the rebellion and learned that the rebels had built incredible momentum. Zhao Han’s imposing reputation had left a strong impression on the masses, whereas the regent’s power was only known within the capital. Furthermore, it hadn’t been long since the regent came to power, so most people were still inclined to side with the Zhao clan.","The central army had initially suffered consecutive losses. Seeing that everything was going to crumble, Bi Linglong had joined the frontline to personally lead the campaign. She'd been accompanied by the Qin clan’s two masters, the Murong clan’s father and daughter, Pei You, Gao Ying... Even Xiao Jianren had brought the Embroidered Envoys there to provide intelligence.","The situation had stabilized, and the central army and the rebel army had come to a standstill at Phoenix Pass outside the capital. The central army couldn’t defeat the rebel army, but the rebel army couldn’t breach Phoenix Pass either. This standstill had lasted for months now.","Bi Linglong had already done a good job, but the sharper ones could all tell that the imperial court was at a disadvantage. Many neutral parties were keeping an eye on the situation, and if they concluded that the imperial court didn’t have the means to quell the rebellion, they could either join the rebel army or declare their independence. That would pose a lot of trouble.","The empress dowager said, “Someone proposed bringing the Fiends in to quell the rebellion. The Fiend Empress dispatched an envoy over to ask Linglong if she needed help, but Linglong turned her down. The rebels have accused us of colluding with the Fiends, so bringing them in would only reinforce that position. Besides, there is enmity between humankind and the Fiend races. If we let the fiend army in, their soldiers could take the opportunity to harm the populace.”","Zu An nodded. “Linglong made the right call.”","Even though he was the Fiend races’ regent, and the Fiend Empress and the upper echelons on that side were his close friends, he understood that if a war broke out, it would be hard to restrain the bloodthirsty fiend soldiers.","“I’ll have to personally make a trip to Phoenix Pass,” Zu An said calmly, as if the army of the eighteen kings wasn't worth a second thought.","And yet, none of those present found anything wrong with that. Their previously gloomy faces lit up with smiles, as they were confident that the regent could quell the rebels given his influence and strength.","The empress dowager coughed. “The rest of you are dismissed. I need to discuss confidential matters with the regent.”","She turned to her lady-in-waiting and instructed her, “Show Miss Sang and little Sisi around the imperial garden. Have the imperial kitchen prepare some snacks for little Sisi.”","Sang Qien was perplexed. What confidential matters do they have to discuss? It feels like she's just evicting us from here. Look at her eyes—she’s on the verge of gobbling Ah Zu up!","Pui! She’s using this as a pretext to fulfill her personal needs.","Despite having guessed the truth, Sang Qien couldn’t fight the empress dowager over Zu An in public. If that were to happen, they would become a laughingstock. Besides, as an official’s daughter, she didn’t stand a chance against the empress dowager.","Forget it, I’ll turn a blind eye to this on the account that she’s treating Sisi well."]},{"number":2686,"title":"Chapter 2686: Chapter 2638: Confident","paragraphs":["After sending away the officials, Sang Qien, and Sisi, the empress dowager dismissed the maids and eunuchs in the room with a wave of her hand. This should have been highly inappropriate, but no one questioned her order. The empress dowager had gained absolute control over the people around her, and her closest eunuchs and maids were aware of her affair with the regent. Sometimes, they'd even had to cover for her.","Once the maids closed the door behind them, the empress dowager rushed into Zu An’s arms.","Zu An embraced her mature body as he asked with a smile, “Ning’er, what do you need to discuss with me?”","The empress dowager raised her head, resting her lower jaw on his chest as she said with a pout, “You only call me that in private. Why didn’t you call me Ning’er earlier?”","Zu An burst into laughter. “You’re the empress dowager. We need to pay heed to your reputation in public.”","“What about Sang Qien and Sisi? You held their hands in public,” the empress dowager complained.","Zu An realized that she was jealous. Instead of explaining himself, he leaned in and kissed her. Only a fool would debate about right and wrong at a time like this. What she needs is emotional affirmation.","The empress dowager moaned. Her lover’s sweet nothings quelled the anger bubbling inside her, and her body gradually relaxed.","Some time later, the two of them began talking about the kings’ rebellion and the imperial court’s initial defeat.","“A skilled housewife can’t prepare a meal without rice.” The empress dowager explained the circumstances then. “Rumors of your death in the other world caused hearts to waver. With those under us thinking about who to side with, it’s no wonder our army suffered defeat after defeat. Linglong and I may be capable, but we've reliant on our subordinates to execute our orders. The situation only stabilized when Linglong joined the frontlines while I held fort in the capital.”","“You've worked hard,” Zu An said, grabbing her hand.","The empress dowager burst into laughter, lighting up the solemn imperial library. “Regent, do you want to know what happened in this time?”","“Of course.” Zu An figured that it wouldn’t hurt to know more about his enemies. With the rebellion having built up so much momentum, it was important for him to draw a clear line between friends and foes.","“Regent, please have a seat. Allow me to slowly explain things to you.” The empress dowager pushed Zu An toward the throne.","Zu An was initially perplexed as to why he had to sit on the throne for them to talk. Where’s Liu Ning going to sit then?","The empress dowager chuckled. She tied her hair up before ducking under the table. Everything immediately made sense to Zu An then.","The empress dowager had a skilled mouth. She shared the details slowly, but in detail.","Zu An could finally make sense of the major events that had happened while he was gone. Some time later, the empress dowager leaned toward Zu An’s ear and whispered, “Ah Zu, I want a child.”","“But you’re the empress dowager.” Zu An was put in a tight spot.","“I don’t care. I want to have your child.” The empress dowager also felt as if something had come over her. She had been the empress for many years, but she'd never been concerned about her lack of offspring. And yet, seeing Zu An carry a girl into the palace struck something deep in her.","Her repressed emotions suddenly burst out at that instant. She realized that she was fond of children all along too; it was just that she hadn’t been willing to bear Zhao Han’s babies.","Besides, Zhao Han wouldn’t have let it happen either. The Liu clan had two empresses. If both were to give birth to sons, the Liu clan’s influence would have grown to an extent where it would be hard to keep them in check. Thus, she'd had no choice but to live with it.","However, her desire to become a mother suddenly became ridiculously intense.","Zu An fell silent.","Liu Ning’s identity was simply too special. The empress dowager bearing a child would be a massive scandal, even when taking humankind’s long history into consideration. It would be impossible to predict what would happen.","The empress dowager’s expression sank, but she soon revealed a seductive smile and said, “I’m joking with you. I am still young and haven’t had enough fun yet. Children are a hassle to deal with.”","Zu An could tell she didn’t mean those words, and that she was merely finding an excuse to end the topic. All he had to do was to play along with her.","And yet, he gently caressed her cheeks and nodded solemnly. “All right.”","“All right?” The empress dowager’s voice quivered in disbelief.","“Let’s have a child,” Zu An said with a smile.","The empress dowager was stunned. She never expected him to accept her request. For a moment there, she felt that she hadn’t lived in vain.","Back when they first started, she had still been the lofty empress, whereas he was a lowly Embroidered Envoy. Taking that first step had left her incredibly nervous and conflicted. She had also wondered if he merely coveted her wealth and standing, or maybe just her beauty.","As she grew closer to him, she'd discarded the first possibility. But as for the second possibility, while Zu An had many young, beautiful lovers, she was the only more mature lover she had, even though she could hardly be considered old at all.","Sometimes, in the dead of the night, she'd wondered if Zu An truly loved her. But she swiftly extinguished this thought whenever it surfaced, as she dared not think deeply into it. She was a mature woman. Her rational mind told her that there was no need to get to the bottom of that; it was enough that they had fun whenever they were together.","But at this moment, she realized that she had a place in his heart. He cared about her feelings and would think on her behalf. This was enough for her.","Her mind suddenly cleared up, and she said, “Ah Zu, my identity is sensitive. It’ll bring too much trouble if I have a child. I’m already satisfied enough to hear you say those words. Thank you.”","Zu An pulled her into his embrace. “Don’t worry. I’ll deal with whatever trouble that arises.”","The empress dowager wanted to say more, but he was too domineering. There was also no way she would reject him after three years of separation. She glanced at the throne, and her face turned bright red. This fellow seems to get more excited whenever he sits on this chair. And for some reason, he doesn’t allow me to take off my phoenix gown...","...","In the rebel army’s commander tent at the distant Phoenix Pass, King Yan looked at the tightly guarded wall and remarked, “Bi Linglong is a capable one. If she had come a day later, I would have already breached Phoenix Pass. The world would have belonged to our Zhao clan.”","Zhao Yuan replied, “No matter how capable she is, she is but a woman. Many in the imperial court refuse to submit to her. You need not worry, King Yan. This standstill is to our advantage. More people will be swayed toward our side. Even those guarding Phoenix Pass aren’t united as one; quite a few people have secretly reached out to us. It’s only a matter of time before we breach the pass.”","King Yan frowned. “A mere Bi Linglong doesn’t worry me. But the longer we stall, the more uneasy I feel. Is it possible that Zu An is still alive?”","That name made Zhao Yuan frown, but he replied, “There’s nothing to worry about, King Yan. Years have passed. He would have long since returned if he was alive. Besides, we've rallied over a million soldiers to our cause. He can’t stop us single-handedly.”","King Yan was still worried. “But that fellow wields terrifying prowess. He might not be no match for our million-troop-strong army in a direct confrontation, but what if he chooses to act against us in the shadows?”","“Don’t worry. I have the means to deal with him even if he returns,” Zhao Yuan replied with a mysterious smile."]},{"number":2687,"title":"Chapter 2687: Chapter 2639: The City Is Breached","paragraphs":["King Yan’s eyes lit up. “Really?”","Zhao Yuan looked at him with deep eyes. “Do I look like the type to joke around?”","“That’s true...” King Yan figured that Zhao Yuan was a highly reliable and calculating individual. “How do you intend to deal with him?”","“It won’t do to reveal the answer beforehand. You’ll naturally know what it is if we ever reach that point.” Zhao Yuan stood up and left.","After Zhao Yuan was gone, King Yan’s aide walked over and said, “Your Highness, Zhao Yuan is keeping many things from you. He doesn’t seem to respect you.”","King Yan narrowed his eyes. “He must be guarded against.”","The world believed he was leading the rebellion, but the true mastermind was Zhao Yuan. Granted that he had contributed by reaching out to several kings, it was insincere and dishonest from Zhao Yuan’s side to withhold intelligence from him. Who’s the boss here?","Unfortunately, Zhao Yuan had served the imperial guards a few years back and knew the imperial court’s secrets better. On top of that, he had close ties with the other kings and key officials. For the time being, King Yan couldn’t cut off Zhao Yuan yet.","Hmph, I’ll first use him to take down the capital before slowly settling the scores afterward.","He wasn’t worried, as he had the largest army among the eighteen rebelling kings. He had always wanted the throne and had been secretly making preparations for it. The other kings, who had decided to participate in the rebellion on a whim, couldn’t hope to match him.","...","In the capital, the empress dowager was still explaining the details of the rebellion to Zu An. She lay in Zu An’s arms like a kitten, her face flushed. Her usual solemnity was nowhere to be seen. Even her voice felt much gentler and sweeter than usual.","Zu An recalled what had just happened, and he had to concede that the empress dowager was indeed in her prime. He could always go all out with her.","“Shall I call Miss Sang to join us?” The empress dowager drew circles on her lover’s chest, her eyes reflecting a hint of fear. It has only been a few years, but Ah Zu’s body has become much stronger than before. Can he still be considered a human now?","Zu An huffed. “Don’t change the subject. Let’s continue talking about the rebels. Have they not tried anything else after being stuck at a standstill at Phoenix Pass for several months?”","“Indeed. Linglong and I were worried that they were merely tying down our troops while ravaging the other provinces, spreading chaos everywhere. But they didn’t do so. Perhaps the eighteen kings aren’t as united as we thought,” the empress dowager replied.","“The rebel army must have smart people in their ranks for their movement to even grow to such a scale. They would have considered doing that, and there must be a reason they aren’t doing so.” Zu An spent a moment in thought before suddenly murmuring, “Could they be confident in taking down Phoenix Pass?”","The empress dowager was startled. “That can’t be. We've already overcome the most dangerous phase, and Linglong is holding the fort at the frontlines. The situation has already stabilized. With Linglong’s ability, the rebel army shouldn’t be able to breach Phoenix Pass.”","“Let’s hope so.” Zu An still felt unnerved despite saying so. “This won’t do. I should quickly make my way to Phoenix Pass.” There were too many people he cared about there. He was worried they would face danger.","As Zu An hurriedly put his clothes on, the empress dowager harrumphed. “What a heartless man. Wiping your hands and leaving right after the deed is done.” Despite her grumbling, she still got up to tidy her lover’s clothes.","Zu An kissed her. “I’ll come back to accompany you once I quell the rebellion.”","The empress dowager walked him to the entrance. She couldn’t leave in her current state, or else anyone who saw her would immediately understand what had just happened.","She watched as Zu An’s figure disappeared before returning. Barely after taking a few steps, she suddenly realized something and quickly flitted to the bed by the side. She lay down flat and raised her legs against the wall. She couldn’t let any of it go to waste.","She thought about the earlier warmth and bit her lip. I hope I can have his child this time.","...","After leaving the imperial library, Zu An found Sang Qien and Sisi playing in the imperial garden.","Rather than playing, however, perhaps it was more apt to say that they were dining. A magnificent spread had been laid out in a gazebo. Sisi held a chicken thigh in one hand and a sweet beverage in the other while still chewing on a cake.","Sang Qien sighed as she wiped Sisi’s mouth. “Slow down. No one is going to steal your food.”","Glancing at the nearby maids, who were smiling warmly at them, Sang Qien felt so embarrassed that she wanted to hide in a pit. She felt as if she would die of shame if the empress dowager and Linglong learned about this.","“It’s good to be able to eat well. It shows that she’s healthy,” Zu An said with a chuckle as he walked over and lifted Sisi up.","“Father, the food is yummy. Do you want some too?” Sisi asked as she offered him an oily chicken drumstick.","“Look at how dirty your hands are!” Sang Qien anxiously wiped the grease off Zu An’s robe.","The maids were startled. This girl calls the regent her father! And looking at how Miss Sang doesn’t hesitate to wipe the regent’s clothes, there's no question that they are a family.","They had guessed that the girl was from a distinguished background, but they'd thought that the regent was only doting on her because of Sang Qien. They hadn’t expected her to be the regent’s blood daughter. They patted their chests, relieved that they hadn’t been perfunctory when serving the mother and daughter duo.","Sang Qien noticed the maids’ expressions and realized what was going on. She wanted to teach her daughter not to recklessly call Zu An ‘father’ in public, but she didn't know how to say it in front of so many people.","Zu An gestured that it was fine with a shake of his head before munching down on Sisi’s chicken drumstick with a smile. “Mm, Sisi’s chicken drumstick is the best!”","He took such a huge bite that Sisi was startled. Her mouth quivered, and she looked as if she was about to burst into tears. “How can you eat it all? Bad father!”","Her adorable demeanor made Zu An burst into laughter. “Yes, it’s father’s fault. I’ll get ten more drumsticks for you.”","The heartwarming interaction between the father and daughter brought a tender smile to Sang Qien’s face. Hearing Zu An affirm Sisi’s identity lifted a boulder that had been weighing on her heart for many years.","The maids, however, were on the verge of tears. Are we allowed to know this? Will we be silenced for knowing too much?","The regent had a righteous reputation, but having worked in the imperial palace for many years, they understood that knowing too much could spell one’s death.","Looking at the nervous maids, Zu An chuckled. “You may leave first. I’d like to talk to Miss Sang privately.”","“Yes!” The maids exhaled in relief and quickly took their leave.","Zu An placed his daughter down before the table, allowing her to gorge herself, before heading to the lakeside with Sang Qien.","“Thank you.” There had been much to say at the back of Sang Qien’s throat, but it eventually came out as those two simple words.","Zu An embraced her. “I won’t let the two of you suffer any grievances.”","Sang Qien smiled sweetly as she nuzzled her cheek against his chest. All of a sudden, she raised her head and stared at him. “You’re covered in the empress dowager’s scent.”","Zu An sweated profusely. I got careless!","“Did you satisfy the empress dowager?” Sang Qien had initially felt stifled when the empress dowager sent her away, but the earlier interaction lifted her spirits. She was now in the mood to tease Zu An.","“It should be the empress dowager satisfying me.” Zu An harrumphed.","“Ah?” Sang Qien was initially surprised to hear those words, but on second thought, it made perfect sense. Her face reddened. “You always defy conventions. I wonder what the empress dowager is like when she’s satisfying you...”","“I can call you along if you want to know. The empress dowager was thinking of it earlier.”","“Pui. I’m not going to go crazy with the two of you.”","After some joking around, Zu An finally revealed his purpose.","Sang Qien was saddened to hear that he was going to leave again, but she replied, “Your worry isn’t unfounded. Dandan and the Crown Prince Consort are there. It’ll be disastrous if something happens. You should hurry there.”","After exchanging farewells, Zu An rose into the sky and made a beeline toward Phoenix Pass.","The capital had rules against flight. A formation swiftly whirred into action as experts rushed out from all directions to stop the lawbreaker, but when they saw that it was Zu An, they froze up.","Zu An exchanged pleasantries with them before he morphed into a rainbow and disappeared into the distance. He was intentionally revealing his face to let the entire capital know that he had returned safely. This should make those who are wavering settle down.","...","Night descended upon Phoenix Pass.","Shortly after Bi Linglong completed her military duties and went to sleep, she was awakened by an uproar. She immediately sat upward. An ominous feeling gripped her heart. It was abnormal to hear such a commotion on a silent night.","Soon after, a golden-armored Murong Qinghe marched into her tent and reported, “Bad news, Your Majesty. The rebels have breached the city!”"]},{"number":2688,"title":"Chapter 2688: Chapter 2640: A Desperate Fight","paragraphs":["As soon as she heard the commotion outside, Bi Linglong swiftly put on her clothes. Naturally, her dress here was nowhere as elaborate as when she was in the palace. What she heard shocked her.","“Come in!”","The guard opened the door, and Murong Qinghe entered anxiously. Her tall stature and her golden armor gave her an air of valiance, but she looked flustered. She quickly repeated what she had just said.","Bi Linglong’s face darkened. “General Murong, don’t talk nonsense!” Were it not Murong Qinghe reporting this matter, she would have had the other party punished to stabilize the army’s morale.","Unsurprisingly, the nearby guards and maids began whispering under their breath in panic.","“It’s true, Your Majesty. Chaos suddenly broke out in the city. I was patrolling the streets when I chanced upon it. The rebel army was in the city. I ordered the troops to stall them before rushing here,” Murong Qinghe said anxiously. “The rebels seem to be after Your Majesty. Your Majesty, you have to retreat somewhere safe!”","“That’s impossible. Phoenix Pass is tightly guarded. How could the rebel army slip in without any notice?”","Even though Bi Linglong had always trusted Murong Qinghe, at this very moment, she was secretly hoping that the latter had betrayed her and was relaying fake news. She pushed Murong Qinghe aside and walked out of the room. She was staying at a higher elevation, which allowed her to have a bird’s eye view of the situation in the city.","Flames blazed furiously in the pass. Screams and cries filled the air everywhere. Soldiers were slaughtering the civilians one-sidedly.","Bi Linglong’s heart sank. Under her leadership, Phoenix Pass had become heavily reinforced. It was inconceivable to her how it could be breached just like that.","There must be traitors!","That was the only explanation. The rebel army couldn’t have breached their defenses otherwise.","“Relay my orders. General Gao and General Pei are to lead the troops to stall the enemy soldiers, while the others are to gather at the inner city right away.”","Bi Linglong knew the troops she had in the city were no weaker than the rebel army’s. The problem was that most of her troops were asleep, whereas the enemy had come prepared. In their current state, they were no match for the rebel army. Her only shot at turning the tables was to rally her troops together.","“Your Majesty, we won’t make it in time.” Murong Qinghe was awed by Bi Linglong’s composure, but as a military veteran, she had to offer her judgment.","“We have to give it a try nevertheless.” Bi Linglong clutched a pillar so tightly that her fingers turned pale. She understood that there was nothing more fearsome to an army than a night raid.","Panic was infectious. It was hard to gauge how strong an enemy force was when facing a night raid. Without any intelligence, one could easily exaggerate the threat. Once an army succumbed to panic, they were doomed to be obliterated.","But Bi Linglong had no choice. If the rebel army were to breach Phoenix Pass, the capital would be in danger. At this rate, she could lose the throne. While she had no desire to cling to her position as empress, Zu An had entrusted this country to her. How could she face him if she lost the country in just a few years?","Despite the rumors that Zu An had died in the other world, she believed that the man who had created so many miracles would return alive.","Just then, a guard rushed over and reported, “Your Majesty, the messenger was killed by a rebel soldier shortly after he was dispatched. We have no way to get in touch with the two generals.”","Bi Linglong felt as if her heart hda bene plunged into cold water. The worst situation had happened.","“Where are the formation masters? Can’t you send the message directly?!” she roared with gritted teeth. Teleportation formations consumed a huge amount of resources, but this was an emergency. While refining Phoenix Pass’ defensive system in the last few days, she'd set up teleportation formations in several crucial spots so that they could communicate even in such situations.","“I’ve checked it. Someone tampered with the formations. They wouldn’t activate!” the fully armored Zhang Zitong rushed in and reported. As the commander of the imperial guards, she had to accompany the empress wherever she went.","Bi Linglong was enraged. “Every formation is heavily guarded, yet someone still managed to tamper with them? Where are the Embroidered Envoys? What are they doing?!”","Zhang Zitong’s eyelids twitched. It was a major slip up from the Embroidered Envoys to not send a heads up when something this huge had happened. But she couldn’t help but speak up for her former colleague, saying, “Lord Xiao says that there must be traitors among the upper echelons in the city. He has personally set out to contact the generals, and he warns Your Majesty to think carefully about who to trust.”","Bi Linglong’s face turned ice-cold. For the rebel army to slip into the city and quietly tamper with so many important formations, there had to be several high-ranking defectors.","The clashing sounds grew closer. Zhang Zitong grew anxious. “Your Majesty, the rebel army is on its way here. We need to retreat right now!”","“Retreat? Where can I retreat to?” Bi Linglong looked bitter. Beyond Phoenix Pass was a plain, so the rebel army could make a beeline for the capital. The imperial court would have no way to stop them anymore.","Zhang Zitong understood that, but she still advised, “Your Majesty, the regent has entrusted me with your safety. As long as you survive this ordeal, we can always come up with something.”","The mention of Ah Zu raised Bi Linglong’s low morale. She took a deep breath and commanded, “Relay my order. Hoist up my personal banner and the White Tiger Banner. Have the soldiers rally toward me.”","The White Tiger Banner could only be used by the emperor. It represented a strong offensive, which meant that she was determined to put up one last fight.","Zhang Zitong was horrified. “You mustn’t! It will be too conspicuous in the middle of the night. Not only will our soldiers see it, but the rebel army will also know where you are! If they encircle this area, we won’t be able to get away.”","Zhang Zitong was confident she could escort Bi Linglong out of the city if they did it secretly, but the same couldn’t be said if they made a huge fuss about it.","“Escape? There are still many soldiers fighting in the city. How can I flee on my own?” Bi Linglong’s expression turned cold. “Execute my order!”","Zhang Zitong still wanted to dissuade her, but Murong Qinghe interjected, “I’m willing to put my life on the line with Your Majesty!”","Murong Qinghe grabbed the war horn and blew it. A majestic call echoed through Phoenix Pass. A brilliant yellow banner and the solemn White Tiger Banner were raised at a vantage point in the city.","The morale of the fleeing imperial soldiers lifted when they saw the banners. “Our empress is still fighting with us!”"]},{"number":2689,"title":"Chapter 2689: Chapter 2641: Reinforcement","paragraphs":["Most of the imperial soldiers had woken up in the middle of the night, hearing that the rebel army had infiltrated the city. They were surrounded by enemies. The commanders couldn’t find their soldiers, and the soldiers couldn’t get to their commanders. Under such circumstances, they could only obey their primal instincts and flee, thus leading to a one-sided slaughter.","Some had tried to rally the soldiers together to resist, but there were too few of them, so the enemies overran them swiftly. Their defeat further lowered the morale of their comrades, leading them to dare not fight back. The only thought left in their minds had been to flee.","But when they saw the two magnificent banners flying high, and someone shouting that the empress was still fighting, they suddenly felt as if they had found their backbone.","“Everyone, head to the White Tiger Banner!”","“For the empress!”","...","The squads that had been wandering around like aimless flies finally found their center and regained their morale. They began rallying around Bi Linglong.","King Yan, who had been spectating the battle from afar, saw the imperial army slowly regaining their footing and remarked, “Bi Linglong is indeed a talent. Despite being a woman, she shows tremendous courage in a crisis.”","King Guangling, Zhao Yuan, nodded. “She handled administrative tasks well while she was still the crown prince’s consort. Many in the imperial court respect her.”","Everyone had known the crown prince as a fool. Bi Linglong had been the one propping up the Eastern Palace.","“It’s a pity she betrayed the imperial family’s trust. She sided with an outsider instead of our Zhao clan.” King Yan harrumphed.","“You wouldn’t have had a chance if not for that,” King Guangling remarked with a chuckle.","Glee flickered across King Yan’s face, but he quickly restrained himself and said, “I am doing this for the sake of our Great Zhou.”","King Guangling played along. “Your Highness’ loyalty to the country is an example that we should follow.” I wonder who was preparing for a rebellion all this time. Don’t you think it’s a bit thick-skinned to play the good person here?","King Yan knew the other party was retorting in his heart, but he didn’t mind it. He had the highest seniority and commanded the most prestige among the kings, making him the de facto leader of this alliance.","I ought to thank Zu An. Zhao Han’s bloodline is mostly gone. Once we arrive at the capital, no one can compete with me for the throne. I only need to defeat the imperial army here and kill Bi Linglong...","The thought of that suddenly made him worried. “Is there any chance of her turning the tables?”","Zhao Yuan replied, “You’re thinking too much. The imperial court has lost its momentum. She’s merely making a desperate struggle. We should be more worried about her escaping amid the chaos. Someone of her ability could make a comeback. We should be glad that she’s insisting on fighting to her death for some cheap sentimentality. This gives us a chance to take her down for good.”","King Yan’s eyes lit up. “Indeed. Everything will be settled if we kill her here!”","He summoned his aide and deployed his elite troops to capture Bi Linglong, promising that the one who accomplished the feat would be conferred a hereditary marquis position.","The handsome reward made the rebel soldiers’ eyes turn red. They roared in enthusiasm as they charged toward the White Tiger Banner.","The fighting intensified. The imperial army desperately rallied around the White Tiger Banner, but the rebel army was also making its way over.","At the city lord’s residence, Zhang Zitong anxiously urged Bi Linglong, “Your Majesty, the rebel army is a mere three hundred steps away from here. If we don’t leave now, it’ll be too late!”","Her body was soaked in blood. She'd been caught in a battle in the brief moment she had left to scout the frontlines.","Bi Linglong coldly eyed Zhang Zitong as she drew her sword. “Captain Tong, if you continue uttering words that shake our army’s morale, I’m going to punish you under military law.”","Zhang Zitong’s heart shuddered. Bi Linglong had commanded an air of majesty even when she was the Crown Prince’s consort; after she became the empress, her disposition had only gotten even stronger. She did not doubt that Bi Linglong would kill her on the spot if she continued trying to persuade her.","Bi Linglong retracted her gaze and said, “I don’t need you to protect me. Take the imperial guards to the frontlines to fight the rebels. We have to give it our all for a chance to turn the tables around.”","She had been observing the battlefield. Raising the White Tiger Banner had greatly raised the morale of their imperial army, but the rebel army had also come prepared. It also didn’t help that the imperial soldiers were rushing here haphazardly from all directions. Murong Qinghe had led her soldiers to receive the incoming imperial soldiers, but the rebel army was so strong that they quickly fell into a disadvantageous position.","Bi Linglong keenly knew that their defense line was on the verge of crumbling, and she needed to devote all her soldiers to hold their ground.","Zhang Zitong wanted to warn the empress that she wouldn’t have guards with her, but she quickly remembered the latter’s earlier warning. She held her tongue and said, “Understood. Imperial guards, Embroidered Envoys, follow me!”","She led her subordinates down to the frontlines. With their efforts, the situation at the defense line stabilized a little.","Murong Qinghe was astonished to see Zhang Zitong. “You’re here too? What about Her Majesty?”","Zhang Zitong replied with a bitter smile, “Her Majesty sent me here.”","Murong Qinghe fell silent. She knew that given the current situation, there was no other option, and she had to concede that Bi Linglong was a decisive leader.","Someone in the rebel army bellowed, “Even the imperial guards have been mobilized. They're cornered. Once we breach this defense line, victory will be ours!”","Cheers broke out in the rebel army as they fearlessly charged forth. This was their opportunity to earn a hereditary marquis position; it could turn their fates around for good.","The pressure on Murong Qinghe and Zhang Zitong increased. Their comrades collapsed one after another, and even they were sustaining injuries. In a battle of this scale, unless they were at the regent’s level, an individual’s valiance was inconsequentia; not to mention that the rebel army was filled with experts too. The two women exchanged looks of despair.","“Who says we don’t have people?”","Another army suddenly arrived at the scene. It was led by a silver-haired old man—it was Qin Zheng from the Qin clan. He was accompanied by Qin Yongde and Qin Guangyuan. Qin Zheng commanded great prestige in the army, so his arrival greatly lifted the imperial army’s morale.","A king from the rebel army shouted, “What’s there to fear? That old fart has one foot in the grave! Besides, they don’t have many troops left!”","Qin Zheng had brought his personal elite troops, but they were indeed nothing much compared to the scale of this battle.","“Don’t forget about us!” Pei You and Gao Ying joined the fray with their troops too. Cheers broke out among the imperial soldiers.","The rebel army’s morale took a hit, but a king quickly yelled that they still had the numerical advantage. They continued their advancement, but with fresh blood joining the imperial army, their momentum was slowed.","As the situation on the battlefield stabilized, Bi Linglong exhaled in relief. She had overcome the danger for the time being. As more imperial soldiers gathered in the area, they would have a chance to turn the tables around.","Just then, a figure descended from the sky. “Duke, I’ll be entrusting this place to you. I’ll protect Her Majesty!”","It was Du Jian, one of the Eight Dukes. His son had been the empress’ aide in the Eastern Palace. Qin Zheng exhaled in relief and said, “I’ll be leaving Her Majesty to you, Du Jian.”","He gestured for his subordinates to open a path for Du Jian.","Bi Linglong frowned. “Lord Du, I don’t need any protection. Go and aid General Qin instead.”","Du Jian smiled. “Your Majesty, please leave the battlefield to the soldiers. I’ll take you somewhere safer.”"]},{"number":2690,"title":"Chapter 2690: Chapter 2642: Two Walnuts to Kill Three Officials","paragraphs":["Bi Linglong rejected the offer without hesitation. “How can I leave when my soldiers are fighting with their lives on the line? Now that Lord Du is here, I should have nothing to worry about. If we lose the battle here, I won’t be safe even if I return to the capital.”","Du Jian tried to persuade her, “Your Majesty is right, but you didn’t consider how the rebel army slipped into the reinforced Phoenix Pass in the first place. There must be a traitor among us, and that traitor is likely to be a high-ranking person. I’m not confident I can protect you against the traitors.”","“Are you saying that there’s a traitor among the other Eight Dukes?” Bi Linglong asked with a frown. Given their high standing and great prestige, she had brought the Eight Dukes with her to the battlefield, as they could stir up problems in the capital otherwise. Their high cultivation could be an asset on the battlefield, too. That being said, she'd remained guarded against them.","Du Jian’s son had once been an advisor in the crown prince’s Eastern Palace, and she'd been the one in charge of managing the Eastern Palace, so there were some ties between them. Similarly, Imperial Preceptor Yu Rui was from the Yu clan; Zu An was close to Yu Yanluo, and Yu Yanluo trusted Yu Rui.","Thus, Bi Linglong had tasked Du Jian and Yu Rui to keep an eye on Great General Cheng Yuan and Imperial Tutor Zhuang He. There were only four of the Eight Dukes here, but that was because Zu An had already dealt with the other four.","Are Cheng Yuan and Zhuang He the traitors here?","“They are indeed suspicious. Despite the ongoing crisis, neither of them is stepping forward to hold the fort,” Du Jian replied.","“Old Du, it’s not good to speak behind others’ backs.” A cold harrumph came as a figure descended from the sky—it was Imperial Tutor Zhuang He.","“Indeed. I rushed here as soon as I was done organizing the soldiers. Rather, I find it perplexing how Lord Du rushed here so quickly without doing anything,” another old man said as he walked over from another direction. It was Great General Cheng Yuan.","Du Jian was unfazed. “I am merely speaking the truth. Phoenix Pass was suddenly breached, and none of the formations in the city are working. There must be a traitor among us. To tamper with the formations and quietly open the city gates; the traitor must be a high-ranking, influential individual.”","Zhuang He’s expression turned cold. “Are you implying we’re the traitors?”","Cheng Yuan also coldly glared at Du Jian with narrowed eyes.","“I’m merely pointing out the most reasonable conjecture.” Du Jian shielded Bi Linglong behind him. “As far as I know, Brother Zhuang had a conflict with the regent a while back and has been harboring a grudge against the latter. I wouldn’t be surprised if you were dissatisfied with Her Majesty too.”","Bi Linglong also remembered that incident. Zhuang He had publicly opposed Zu An, but the latter’s decisiveness in killing the Zhao clan’s Eight Dukes forced him to lower his head.","Zhuang He’s face reddened in shame. “I did what I did for the sake of the country; it has nothing to do with the regent! Don’t you utter falsehoods to mislead others now!”","“I am being objective here,” Du Jian replied.","Great General Cheng Yuan spoke up too, “Brother Du Jian, how can you say you’re being objective when you’re attacking Brother Zhuang? You are suspicious as well. How did someone tamper with the formations under your watch?”","“The traitors came prepared. I was caught off guard,” Du Jian refuted him. “Besides, you were in charge of guarding the city gates. Who knows whether you let the rebels in?”","“Enough!” Bi Linglong’s face turned frosty. She didn’t trust any of these people fully, but she needed all the manpower she could get right now, especially experts of the Eight Dukes’ caliber.","People of their stature wouldn’t be tasked with grunt work like guarding the formations and the city gates. They had merely been assigned as the reinforcements if anything went wrong with those areas.","“We shouldn’t be fighting among ourselves when our survival is at stake! We’ll only become laughingstocks!”","Du Jian interjected, “Your Majesty, we have to root out the traitor, or else they could turn against us at a critical moment later on, rendering our efforts futile.”","Zhuang He berated him, \"You keep talking about catching the traitor, but who knows if you are the traitor here?”","“What are you saying, you old fool?!” Du Jian roared. The tension between them heightened, and it looked as if they were going to duel each other to the death.","“Enough!” Their argument made Bi Linglong’s head hurt. Their words made sense, and none was clear of suspicion. With her sharp wits, she quickly came up with a plan. “There’s an easy way to determine who’s the traitor. You three head to the frontlines, and the one who kills the most rebel soldiers is the least likely to be a spy.”","The three old men fell silent. They were awed by Bi Linglong’s wits. The rebel army was already close to victory. Going on a massacre right now was bound to draw the eighteen kings’ ire. The true traitor wouldn’t do something like that.","Great General Cheng Yuan said, “Your Majesty is wise, but I’m worried that the true spy will hold Your Majesty hostage after I leave. That would be disastrous.”","Du Jian huffed, “Old Cheng, why are you looking at me?”","Zhuang He sneered, “You should know the reason best.”","“You must be tired of living!” Du Jian roared. The two of them began bickering.","Looking at the three bickering old men chilled Bi Linglong’s heart. Her straightforward ploy should have revealed the traitor. Even if the traitor played along and fought on the frontlines, it would still be to her benefit. And yet, these three were bickering here. Despite their righteous words, they were refusing to execute her order.","This could only mean one thing—they were all traitors! That thought plunged her into despair. Of the trio, she'd trusted Du Jian the most because of his ties with the Eastern Palace. She hadn't expect the other party to betray her.","But this wasn’t the time to pursue the issue. Her only leverage in this situation was that the trio didn’t seem to know one another’s identities. It could be because they were serving different kings, or that the rebel army hdn’t revealed their presence to the other traitors due to their sensitive identities...","Regardless, she had to find a way to turn the trio against one another so she would have a chance to take them down.","So, she declared, “Lord Du, General Cheng, apprehend Imperial Tutor Zhuang first.”","Zhuang He was horrified. “Your Majesty, are you suspecting me now?”","“Lord Du is right. You have harbored dissatisfaction against me and the regent, and that makes you the likeliest suspect. You need not worry. I’ll investigate this matter, and I’ll personally apologize to you if you have been framed.” Bi Linglong eyed Du Jian and Cheng Yuan. “What are you waiting for?”","Du Jian and Cheng Yuan were overjoyed. They had been worried about exposing their identities, leading to a two-against-one situation. If they could eliminate Zhuang He first, it would boil down to a one-on-one, thus increasing their chances of victory. Thus, the two of them charged at Zhuang He.","Zhuang He fended against their attacks while shouting, “Your Majesty, you fail to identify who is loyal to you! You’re bringing the empire to ruin!”","Soon, however, he no longer had the energy to continue shouting. Du Jian and Cheng Yuan’s relentless attacks quickly cornered him, to the point that he could lose his life at any moment.","Bi Linglong calmly watched as Du Jian and Cheng Yuan dished out killing blow after killing blow. Just as I thought.","Just then, a sigh filled the air. “You fools. How can you let a mere lass take you for a ride?”"]},{"number":2691,"title":"Chapter 2691: Chapter 2643: Cornered","paragraphs":["An old man dressed in a fluttering white robe flew over. He had a smooth complexion. It wouldn’t have been surprising if he had charmed many women in his younger days.","“Brother Yu!” The fighting trio stopped upon seeing him. They dared not continue fighting, as they didn’t know the old man’s stance and were worried that he would stab them in the back.","The man who had just arrived was one of the Eight Dukes, Imperial Preceptor Yu Rui.","Bi Linglong should have been overjoyed by Yu Rui’s arrival, since considering Yu Yanluo and Zu An’s relationship, the latter should have been an ally. But what Yu Rui had just said revealed too much about his stance.","The other three looked at Yu Rui with confused eyes as they asked, “Brother Yu, what did you mean by that?”","“Exactly as you heard,” Yu Rui huffed. “The three of you are comrades, and yet you let her manipulate you into fighting among yourselves. You must have lived all these years in vain.”","Usually, they would have lost their tempers right away if anyone dared reprimand them like that, but at this moment, they were more concerned about what Yu Rui had just said. They exchanged looks as they wondered... Could it be...","Yu Rui was worried that these fools would continue fighting, so he clearly spelled it out for them. “King Guangling told me that you secretly pledged your allegiance to different kings, which means we are in the same faction. If we continue fighting amongst ourselves, we’ll only become a laughingstock.”","“What?!” All of them were astounded. Their first thought was to wonder whether Yu Rui had intentionally said those words to bait them into revealing themselves.","However, they had been the Eight Dukes for many years now, such that they could converse just by exchanging looks.","“I didn’t expect you, thick-brows, to defect to the rebels too.”","Zhuang He scoffed, “Old Du, your earlier pretense of righteousness nearly scared me.”","Du Jian’s face reddened. “I was worried you two would gang up on me.”","Cheng Yuan laughed. “To be honest, Brother Du, I didn’t expect you to side with King Yan. Otherwise, we wouldn’t have fallen for your deception.”","In Bi Linglong and their eyes, Du Jian had no reason to join the rebels.","“A hero knows how to read the tides.” Du Jian felt awkward, as his act of betraying his liege was dishonorable. “But I hadn’t expected Brother Yu to side with the rebels.”","Bi Linglong shared the same doubt too. She coldly asked, “Why, Imperial Preceptor Yu?”","Yu Rui fell momentarily silent before replying, “Crown Prince Consort, it’s all over. It’s time for you to surrender. I can guarantee your safety in my name.”","He had chosen to address Bi Linglong as ‘Crown Prince Consort’ instead of ‘Your Majesty’, which showed that he didn’t acknowledge her position.","Bi Linglong held her blade in front of her as she coldly retorted, “How can I surrender when my soldiers are still fighting?”","Zhuang He laughed. “Do you think you can defeat us single-handedly?”","The others smiled too. Before Zu An appeared out of nowhere, the Eight Dukes had been the strongest experts in the world. They were legendary figures to mortals, and there were four of them gathered here.","“Someone once told me to not give up, no matter the difficulty faced. If I persist, a day will come when the sky clears.” Bi Linglong’s stern face turned gentle, making her look so beautiful for an instant that it mesmerized the four old men.","“That’s just meaningless consolation. What can you do even if you persevere now?”","A laugh suddenly echoed from afar as a group of people galloped over from an alley. This group was led by none other than King Yan.","Bi Linglong laughed. “You're too sly, King Yan. It took so much to lure you out. Imperial Preceptor Yu and Lord Du, you have done well.”","King Yan was horrified. He quickly halted his charge and ordered his aides to protect him well.","Zhuang He and Cheng Yuan were enraged as well. “Yu Rui, Du Jian, I knew you two were up to something!”","In truth, they'd doubted that Yu Rui and Du Jian would betray Yu Yanluo, and King Yan’s reaction enlightened them to the truth. To win the favor of their new master, they immediately made their move.","Yu Rui and Du Jian were stunned. They guarded themselves while explaining, “Don’t listen to that woman’s nonsense!”","Bi Linglong suddenly changed her tune. “Indeed, I was uttering nonsense.”","Zhuang He and Cheng Yuan had initially been doubtful about Bi Linglong’s claim, but the latter’s abrupt change in attitude made them wonder if she was protecting Yu Rui and Du Jian so that they could find an opportunity to strike. It also didn’t help that Yu Rui and Du Jian were formidable rivals. This was a good opportunity to get rid of them, lest there will be two thorns in their back in the future.","So, they intensified their offense, unleashing killing blow after killing blow.","Yu Rui and Du Jian realized their words were futile, and that made their anger surge. They decided to fight back. The nearby houses crumbled under the shockwaves from their clashes, and nearby trees were reduced to dust.","Fortunately, King Yan’s aides stepped forward to suppress the shockwaves, allowing King Yan and Bi Linglong to remain safe.","King Yan clapped his hands. “Impressive. You are full of schemes. You turned them against one another with just a few simple words... but you remain cornered.”","Bi Linglong fell silent. She had dealt with the four dukes for now, but King Yan had many experts on his side, whereas she only had a couple of guards left.","Her stalwart guards drew their weapons and stood in front of her, saying, “We’ll guard Your Majesty to our dying breath!”","Murong Qinghe and Zhang Zitong noticed the twist in the situation and wanted to lead their forces back to rescue Bi Linglong, but the rebel army had already received orders to stall them at all costs.","Bi Linglong understood the situation she was in and sighed softly. Ah Zu, I've done everything I can, but I still don’t see a ray of hope.","She turned to King Yan and said, “King Yan, I have one last question to ask. How did you convince them to betray me?”","Given the situation in the city, the traitors clearly weren’t just limited to these four.","King Yan sneered, “Demoness, do you think I would let you stall for time? I’ll give you a chance to preserve your dignity and end your own life now. Otherwise, don’t blame me for what happens next.”","Bi Linglong was indeed beautiful—it was a waste to let her die like that. However, it was too dangerous to keep her alive. He was aiming for the throne, and she outranked him. He could potentially sully his reputation if he didn’t deal with this well. The ideal situation was to have her end her own life. Once the others learned about her death, the imperial army would lose its fighting spirit.","Bi Linglong quietly raised her blade. As the empress, she couldn’t let anyone sully her.","“I’m sorry, Ah Zu.” As she was about to slit her throat, a single teardrop fell from her eyes.","At her moment of death, however,she seemed to have seen a beautiful rainbow. How gorgeous. If only Ah Zu were here with me to witness this sight... but why is there a rainbow in the middle of the night?","“Didn’t I tell you to never give up?” a gentle voice echoed. It was reproachful, yet sympathetic."]},{"number":2692,"title":"Chapter 2692: Chapter 2644: A Frog In the Well","paragraphs":["Bi Linglong was startled. Did something happen to Ah Zu? Is that why I'm seeing him now that I’m dead?","But the warm embrace and familiar aura snapped her out of her daze. She murmured incredulously, “Ah Zu, is it really you?”","“It’s me. I came late.” Zu An hugged her trembling body with a fearful heart. He had felt unnerved while he was in the capital, which was why he rushed here right away. Had he been a second later, he would have lost her.","“Regent!” The imperial guards were moved.","When they saw the empress preparing to slit her own throat, they'd felt so indignant that they had followed suit, only for their blades to be knocked away. By the time they recovered, the regent was already standing in front of them.","On the other hand, King Yan and the others turned ghastly pale. Didn’t they say that this accursed man died in the other world? How did he return?","“It's been a while, King Yan. Why are you leaving without greeting me?” After consoling Bi Linglong, Zu An turned to the old man who was planning to slip away.","King Yan’s body stiffened up. He awkwardly turned around and said, “You have become more spirited over the last few years.”","Zu An laughed. “You must be wondering why I didn’t die in the other world.”","King Yan laughed sheepishly. “Regent, you are as humorous as ever.”","Zu An’s expression suddenly darkened. “I’m not in the mood to joke with you.”","He wasn’t planning to waste his breath arguing with King Yan here. Countless soldiers were dying due to the ongoing war below. So, he flew into the air and roared, “STOP!”","His thunderous voice could be heard clearly by every soldier despite the chaotic battlefield.","“It’s the regent! The regent is back!”","Many in the imperial army cheered in delight when they saw Zu An. In contrast, the rebel soldiers exchanged frightened looks. The meat grinder that was the battlefield abruptly stalled to a halt.","Zhang Xitong wiped off the blood on her face as she looked at the glowing figure in the sky, who resembled a deity descending to the mortal world. Ah, the regent is so dashing.","Even Murong Qinghe’s eyes twinkled as well. Soldiers respected the strong, and her brother-in-law was the strongest expert out there. However, she soon remembered something that made her face redden, and her expression became conflicted.","Bi Linglong lost her usual air of majesty, displaying the pure joy of a woman in love. Whenever Zu An was with her, all problems faded away.","After stopping the battle, Zu An turned his attention back to the four members of the Eight Dukes. “As the foundation of the empire, why didn’t you aid the empress earlier?”","The four of them opened their mouths, but they didn’t know what to say.","Bi Linglong was worried that the others would take advantage of his ignorance, since he had just arrived and was oblivious to the situation, so she said, “Ah Zu, they have defected to the rebel army.”","Zu An nodded. “I see. How perplexing. You have already reached the pinnacle of wealth and power within the empire, so how did King Yan convince you to join his side?”","He didn’t look at Zhuang He and Cheng Yuan, as it wasn’t surprising for those two to rebel. Rather, he was baffled that Du Jian and Yu Rui had betrayed Bi Linglong as well.","Yu Rui and Du Jian fell silent.","It was Zhuang He who spoke up. He knew that given their past history and this incident, Zu An wouldn’t let him off, so he said, “What other reason could I have? You disappeared for so many years that everyone thought you were dead. I have a huge clan behind me. It’s only normal for me to find another way out.”","“Is that all?” Zu An frowned. He looked at Yu Rui in disappointment. He had always treated the Yu clan well because of his relationship with Yu Yanluo. He hadn’t expected Yu Rui to backstab him at a time like this.","Yu Rui took a deep breath and said, “It’s too late for words.” His aura suddenly surged.","Bi Linglong was startled. She sensed Yu Rui’s cultivation rising beyond the might he had displayed thus far. His aura was even more intense than Zhao Han’s.","The other members of the Eight Dukes were startled before chuckling. “So you made a breakthrough too.”","Their auras also surged, rising all the way up to the pinnacle of Earth Immortal as they spread out to encircle Zu An. They had hidden their cultivation earlier to use it as a trump card to catch their opponent off guard, but now that Yu Rui had shown his hand, there was no reason for them to continue concealing their strength.","King Yan was overjoyed. He hadn’t expected there to be such a twist in the situation, though he couldn’t help but wonder how these fellows had grown so fast as to even surpass his cultivation. The Eight Dukes had always been formidable, but times had changed. As a feudal king, King Yan had access to far more cultivation resources and cultivation manuals. He'd thought that he had become the most influential figure, beneath only Zu An.","The rebel soldiers cheered in delight. In contrast, the imperial soldiers looked grim. Can the regent overcome this crisis?","Zu An’s eyebrows shot up as he assessed the four people. “Is this the basis of your confidence? I must say that your growth has been abnormally fast.”","Fusing the worlds together had greatly enriched this world’s ki, but the resources these four had were nowhere on par with Zhao Han's. It didn’t make sense for them to have surpassed Zhao Han.","Zhuang He gleefully replied, “Regent, you might have easily crushed the Earth Immortal Imperial Tutor Zhao back then, but times have changed. Within the last three years, our cultivation has grown by leaps and bounds. We have surpassed not just Zhao Chen but the former emperor too. It’s no longer your world!”","Clearly, no one recognized that fool, Zhao Ruizhi, as a legitimate emperor. By former emperor, they meant Zhao Han.","Cheng Yuan warned, “Don’t let your guard down. The strength he displayed when he quelled the Doomsday Spirit and the Plague Monarch is not to be underestimated.”","Despite their vigilance, they weren’t worried. Zu An was formidable, but the four of them had already surpassed Zhao Han. On top of that, they had the massive armies of the eighteen rebel kings backing them. Losing this battle was unthinkable to them.","Du Jian finally spoke up. “Regent, the empire belongs to the Zhao clan. You have gone overboard with your actions. Why don’t I propose a deal? If you leave right now, we will ensure your safety and not pursue your crimes. On top of that, you can retain your king title too. This way, we can avoid meaningless casualties. Won’t that be for the best?”","He figured it would still be ideal to avoid a fight, or else they would have to pay a hefty price. Considering how he had betrayed Zu An, there was a chance that Zu An, when cornered, could choose to drag him down to hell with him.","King Yan didn’t like that suggestion. He wanted to overturn it, but he was worried that if he pushed too far, Zu An would go after him first. It’s better to concede for now and slowly erode his influence over time. I can use the strength of the entire empire to settle the scores with him later on.","“The empire belongs to the Zhao clan?” Zu An acted as if he had heard the most hilarious thing in the world. His expression turned cold as he scoffed, “The world belongs to me.”","Cheng Yuan harrumphed. “Aren’t you being too arrogant, regent?”","Zu An suddenly sighed. “Your world is too small. You’re frogs in a well, gazing upon the moon. Your ignorance is what gave you the courage to oppose me. If you had further advanced your cultivation, you would have understood the vast difference between us.”","He gently waved his hand. A massive golden palm suddenly appeared in the sky and instantly crushed the four dukes into dust."]},{"number":2693,"title":"Chapter 2693: Chapter 2645: Shadow Group Revealed","paragraphs":["Loud exclamations rippled through the battlefield. The abrupt twist in the situation had shocked everyone. Ordinary soldiers wouldn't understand the difference in the cultivation levels of both sides, but they could still feel the immense pressure the four dukes had exerted in that instant. Even the strongest expert in their respective armies wouldn’t stand a chance against entities of that level. It would take an army on an open field to subdue such an opponent.","And yet, the regent had crushed all four of them at once?","The imperial soldiers weren't too surprised, as they had previously witnessed Zu An’s prowess in the capital. They cheered in delight at his feat.","The rebel soldiers, however, were mostly from other provinces. They had heard rumors, but they'd thought they were exaggerated, especially with the kings downplaying Zu An’s strength. This sight crushed their morale. How were they supposed to fight someone so unbelievably powerful?","Even Bi Linglong was dumbstruck. She'd been worried when the four dukes emanated auras surpassing even Zhao Han’s. While she had always known her lover was formidable, the latter appeared to have gotten far stronger in the past few years.","But Yu Rui is from the Yu clan. Won’t this put Madam Yu in a tough spot?","King Yan was flabbergasted. When he saw how strong the four dukes were, he felt both envy and relief. He'd thought that if they combined their prowess, the four would perhaps able to take down Zu An. He hadn’t expected such an outcome.","At that instant, he doubted the decades he had spent cultivating. What’s the point of cultivating when people like Zu An can just crush us at a whim?","But when he recalled how he had ruled with unquestioned authority in his fief, he realized he wasn't the incompetent one. It was this Zu fellow who was inhuman!","Zhao Han had been the dominant power of his era, but now, Zu An was proving to be far stronger than that.","“It’s a misunderstanding, regent.” King Yan, with his high stature, was accustomed to others fawning over him. He hadn’t expected a day would come when he would be fawning over others, let alone that he would be such a natural at it too.","“Misunderstanding? Your rebellion has cost the lives of countless civilians and soldiers, but you’re shrugging it off as a misunderstanding?” Zu An didn’t even raise his hand, but King Yan floated up from his tight encirclement of guards. He kicked his legs frantically while clawing at his neck, as if an invisible hand was strangling him.","King Yan finally experienced the terror the four dukes had experienced earlier. The other party gave off such intense pressure that despite his cultivation, he felt like an infant. A warm stream flowed from his crotch, and an awful stench wafted. Yet due to the overwhelming terror paralyzing his head, he didn’t feel the slightest shame.","He frantically racked his brain for an excuse. Fortunately, his brain seemed to function better when his life was at stake, and he found a scapegoat to blame everything on. “Zhao Yuan instigated me!”","“Oh?” Zu An loosened the restraint on King Yan. “Where is he?”","King Yan gasped for air like a drowning person who had just been brought to shore. “He stayed outside the city, to receive incoming troops. He told me to join the battle here to build my name.”","He secretly cursed Zhao Yuan and his ancestors as he spoke. That fellow is a schemer! Now that I think about it, he was digging a pit for me!","Worried that this wouldn’t be enough to convince Zu An to spare him, he added, “Regent, I thought you met with a mishap in the other world, which was why I foolishly fell for Zhao Yuan’s tricks. I have always been worried... No, I have always thought that you would overcome the hurdles in your way and return safely! But Zhao Yuan said that he had ways to deal with you even if you returned alive.”","The more King Yan spoke, the angrier he felt. That fellow said he had a way to deal with Zu An, but I don’t see him doing anything at all. Why did I foolishly fall for his nonsense?","A sigh suddenly echoed and a voice said, “King Yan, that’s behavior unworthy of a ruler.”","A figure slowly walked over from the distance. It was King Guangling, Zhao Yuan.","King Yan retorted, “Talk is cheap. Why don’t you go deal with him?” He had just witnessed the deaths of four powerful dukes before being lifted like a little chick. Only someone who had been in the same position would understand the despair he felt.","Zhao Yuan looked at Zu An with conflicted eyes. “Regent, you have grown more imposing over the last few years.”","Zu An was surprised by Zhao Yuan’s composed attitude. “You don’t seem flustered.”","“Why did you think I would be flustered?” Zhao Yuan calmly replied with a smile.","“I was wondering how the four dukes could have grown so quickly. I can now see it's due to your credit,” Zu An replied. When he saw the calm Zhao Yuan, the doubt he had been harboring was answered.","“The regent is as sharp as ever.” Zhao Yuan smiled.","King Yan was horrified. This fellow helped the four dukes surpass Zhao Han? Why didn’t he help me too? Hold on... If he could help others make a breakthrough, he must be even stronger himself!","He thought back about the times he had put on airs before Zhao Yuan, and the latter had played along with him. He suddenly felt incredibly embarrassed. Damn it! I must have looked like a clown to him!","Suddenly, a shadow on the side wall came to life and attacked Zhao Yuan. Even its sword was dyed black, reflecting not the slightest light.","This sight shocked many. Zhao Yuan was currently alone without his guards. This assassin had truly found the best opportunity to take him down. It was a wonder how the assassin had known Zhao Yuan would appear here in the first place.","Could the regent have arranged for this? No, there’s no reason for someone as powerful as the regent to resort to such tactics.","While the crowd was making sense of the situation, a dull thud echoed. The assassin had been sent flying, with fresh blood spurting from his mouth.","Many of the experts present rubbed their eyes in bewilderment. They didn’t even see how Zhao Yuan made a move. But what they were more concerned about was the assassin—who would dare assassinate Zhao Yuan under such a setting?","The black cloth veiling the assassin’s appearance had been knocked off, revealing a pale face mired in regret and indignation. It was an unfamiliar youth, but he commanded the disposition of a top-notch assassin.","But Zu An recognized the youth. It was the person he had spared at the Lake of Hatred during the Devil Sect’s infighting—Jing Li, the son of the Skysplitting School’s sect master. What is he doing here? Could it be...","“You’re courting death!” Infuriated, Zhao Yuan thrust his palm at the other party.","As if knowing he wouldn’t survive this ordeal, Jing Li turned to Zu An and shouted, “Zhao Yuan is the Shadow Group Master!”"]},{"number":2694,"title":"Chapter 2694: Chapter 2646: Trump Card","paragraphs":["Zu An didn’t want to see someone he knew dying just like that, so he casually raised his hand and pulled Jing Li to his side, thus saving the latter from Zhao Yuan’s fatal attack. He was astonished to hear Jing Li’s words, repeating, “He’s the Shadow Group Master?”","The Shadow Group was the most elusive assassin organization in the world. Even the Embroided Envoys could only find their branches, but not the identity of its master. While there had been clues suggesting the Shadow Group Master was in the imperial palace, that conjecture had never been verified.","Thinking about it, Zhao Yuan was an imperial relative and a commander of the imperial army. He should have wielded considerable influence, yet he had always maintained a low profile and had hardly any presence. This had benefited him. He alone had remained standing when all the renowned figures in the imperial palace had met with mishaps. Were it not for the previous rebellion, the imperial army would still have been under his control.","Many things would suddenly make sense if he was the Shadow Group Master.","The others also stared at Zhao Yuan in astonishment. None of them had expected him to be the most secretive person in the world.","Zhao Yuan broke his composure and glared at Jing Li with vicious eyes. “I should have never spared a bastard like you.” There was no point refuting it now, after all.","His admission caused a huge commotion. The Shadow Group had held a resounding reputation before Zu An’s rapid ascent in the capital. Many influential figures in the imperial court had feared that their throat would one day be slit by a Shadow Group assassin.","King Yan looked at Zhao Yuan with fearful eyes. He hadn’t expected the person he had recently spent so much time with to be such a terrifying individual. And I kept bragging in front of him!","“You seem confident.” Zu An was surprised by Zhao Yuan’s frank admission. It seemed the latter had something to fall back on.","“This world would have been mine if not for your sudden emergence.” Zhao Yuan shook his head regrettably.","A thought surfaced in Zu An’s mind. “You don’t seem to just be referring to this rebellion.”","“Of course not. Your appearance foiled my careful arrangements.” Zhao Yuan had bottled these thoughts up for a long time, and he could finally vent them. “I was a distant imperial relative. The throne wouldn’t have been mine even if a thousand emperors came and went. But were it not for your intervention, with the previous emperor’s passing, the crown prince’s weakness, and the conflict between the Crown Prince Consort and the empress, they would have fought each other to the death without any outsider meddling.","“The distinguished King Qi’s lineage always coveted the throne. There were also many ambitious ones among the other kings, be it the previous King Wu or the current King Yan. Chaos should have befallen this world a long time ago!”","Zu An sneered, “Only then would you stand a chance.”","“Your intervention resulted in King Qi’s faction’s premature retirement. The Crown Prince Consort and the empress, despite their long-standing feud, made peace and became allies. I would have never expected you to conquer those two tigresses...”","Zu An’s face reddened. “Don’t talk nonsense!” He had to be careful, since they were in public.","Bi Linglong noticed many gazes falling on her. She tried her best to maintain her composure, but she wouldn’t hesitate to dive into a hole if she could.","Zhao Yuan continued, “You suppressed King Wu and dealt with the previous emperor’s sons. You unraveled many of the conflicts among major clans in the capital. My many years of effort went down the drain because of you.”","“You sought to turn the major clans and princes against one another, so you could swoop in and reap all the benefits afterward. The main imperial lineage had to suffer a hit before a distant imperial relative like you could stand a chance.” Zu An could guess the other party’s plan.","“Indeed. Your appearance changed it all.” Hatred flickered through Zhao Yuan’s eyes. “But heaven isn't blind. I finally found an opportunity to incite Bi Qi to make a move against the Liu clan, thus finally putting my plan into action. I never expected you to foil it yet again.”","Bi Linglong widened her eyes. The previous chaos in the capital had resulted in the decimation of the Bi clan and the Liu clan. So this fellow was the one behind it!","Zu An frowned. “Weren’t the monsters behind that? You defected to the monsters?”","“The monsters? The likes of them aren’t worthy of my loyalty.” Zhao Yuan placed his hands behind his back as he spoke arrogantly.","“Let me see the basis of your confidence.” Zu An unleashed a blade of golden sword ki at Zhao Yuan. The attack was only intended to sever Zhao Yuan’s arm. There were too many things that he needed to question the latter about.","A black aura suddenly manifested around Zhao Yuan and neutralized the golden sword ki.","The rebel soldiers cheered in delight. Their leaders were mostly Zhao clansmen, and they understood that their defeat spelled death. Even though Zhao Yuan was the Shadow Group Master, he was still an imperial relative. His victory was more advantageous to them than Zu An’s. After witnessing Zu An’s overwhelming strength, they had given up hope, but the way Zhao Yuan had easily neutralized Zu An’s attack brought them renewed hope.","King Yan further lowered his head in shame.","On the other hand, Zu An remarked in astonishment, “Annihilation power?”","This power wasn't foreign to him. The Monster World had been destroyed by a terrifying Annihilation Beast, an expert in the path of annihilation. Those walking the path of annihilation believed in the annihilation of the universe itself, and they were feared in the myriad worlds. Zu An hadn’t expected Zhao Yuan to wield annihilation power!","Zhao Yuan was surprised. “I never expected you to have heard of my master. If you’re willing to join us, I can speak to my master on your behalf and have him accept you as a disciple.”","Spatial tears opened in the vicinity. Black-clothed assassins emerged from the tears and surrounded Zu An. They were shrouded in black auras suffused with annihilation power.","Most spectators were astounded. They didn’t know what annihilation power was, but they recognized the black-clothed assassins as elites of the Shadow Group. Each elite assassin in the Shadow Group was a legendary figure who wielded the power to kill a king.","Despite their fearsome reputation, most people didn’t think they posed a threat to the regent. However, the auras they were currently emanating surpassed even those of the four dukes.","This sent everyone into a frenzy. Is the Shadow Group that powerful?"]},{"number":2695,"title":"Chapter 2695: Chapter 2647: Mark of Annihilation","paragraphs":["The battlefield had no lack of outstanding cultivators who had trained for many years, yet they paled far in comparison to these nameless assassins who'd popped out of nowhere. They couldn’t help but wonder if they had cultivated in vain.","Only Zu An could tell these assassins from the Shadow Group hadn't truly reached their present level. Their cultivation had been forcefully raised by annihilation power. It would be impossible for them to further advance their cultivation. That said, he didn’t know if there was a growth system for universal deities’ disciples. If the Path of Annihilation’s deity bestowed them with more divine power, they could potentially grow faster than him.","These elite assassins stood in a formation that suppressed him.","Zhao Yuan revealed a victorious smile. “Regent, I do admire you despite our being enemies. In just a few years, you rose from a nobody in a distant city to this. It wouldn’t be far-fetched to say that your talent is unmatched in human history.”","“You know too little about human history to say that.” Zu An thought about the astounding figures he had met in his travels through spacetime. “You don’t need to flatter me. I have no compliments for you.”","Zhao Yuan’s smile stiffened, and his expression turned cold. “Do you think you are invincible? Indeed, you might be so by human standards, but that’s because you have never witnessed the glory of true deities.”","His gleeful attitude left Zu An speechless. I wonder how he’ll react if he learns that a universal deity has ‘visited’ me.","But there was no reason for him to share that with Zhao Yuan. Instead, he said, “I heard you staged this rebellion in the name of the imperial grandson. Are you holding Concubine Bai and her son hostage?”","“Hostage?” Zhao Yuan was perplexed. “I have long heard about your lustful nature, but I didn’t expect you to be thinking about Concubine Bai when you’re already at death’s door.”","The crowd frowned. Some were perplexed, as it had been a long time since they had heard from Concubine Bai. Those privy to insider knowledge wondered if she had been sentenced to death. But the majority was just astonished to hear the news.","There’s something between the regent and Concubine Bai too? The novels on the market are still too conservative!","Bi Linglong frowned. Back then, that woman was the crown prince’s concubine. To think that she’d compete with me over Ah Zu now. I guess we’re fated to be enemies.","Zhang Zitong felt indignant. These people keep slandering the regent. I would know best whether he’s lecherous or not! I dropped hints toward him so many times, but he showed no inclination to take advantage of me. He’s obviously a gentleman!","Hold on... Could it be that he’s just not attracted to me?","Her expression suddenly collapsed at that realization.","Murong Qinghe looked at the figure in the sky and shook her head. My brother-in-law would have been perfect if not for his philandering ways. Big brother Chu is more devoted, but...","“Death’s door? You’re very confident that victory is in your grasp.” Zu An chuckled.","“Does the regent not sense the anomaly in your body? This is disappointing.” Zhao Yuan shook his head in contempt.","Bi Linglong anxiously looked at Zu An, wondering if something had happened to him.","“Are you referring to the weakening in my defense, agility, and divine sense?” Zu An calmly replied. That was the effect of the formation constructed by the elite assassins.","He was in no rush to make his move. He was about to head to Dreamland, where he would encounter experts from other worlds and disciples of other universal deities. He could deal with experts from the Path of Annihilation better if he could learn more about them here.","“You seem to be probing our abilities?” Zhao Yuan saw through his thoughts and sneered. “Regent, you are bold, but you made a miscalculation. You have been afflicted with the Mark of Annihilation, which is widely feared in the myriad worlds. While you were stalling for time, we stacked the marks to the maximum, weakening you by half. Surely you don’t think you can deal with us with just half your strength?”","“The regent is weakened by half?” The crowd was stunned.","The military also had formations that could amplify ally damage and weaken enemy defense, but often, both sides would possess similar methods, so the eventual buff was usually no more than 20%. Furthermore, these formations rarely worked on experts. Military formations took time to construct, and no expert would be so dumb as to wait on the spot for the formation’s completion.","It hadn’t been long since the elite assassins encircled the regent. There shouldn’t have been enough time for them to even complete the formation!","Do they have a secret art that allows them to directly apply the effect to the regent?","“Mark of Annihilation? What an interesting ability.” Zu An merely found the inexplicable power influencing his physical state interesting.","His abnormal composure stoked Zhao Yuan’s unease. Not daring to wait anymore, he ordered, “Attack!”","The ten elite assassins abruptly vanished.","“Careful! That’s the specialty of the Shadow Group’s assassins, Void Weaving!” a few people in the crowd exclaimed.","A few of the ladies exchanged looks, as they could sense one another’s concern for Zu An, but this was no time for them to be distracted. Their attention swiftly returned to the battle in the sky.","Zu An frowned. This wasn't his first time dealing with such methods; the dark elves specialized in this too. Given his cultivation and grasp of the world’s will, he should have been able to track their movements even when he was weakened by the Mark of Annihilation and they were hiding in the void.","And yet, he couldn’t sense the elite assassins at all.","Is the annihilation power concealing their presence?","Zu An wasn’t worried. He was capable of slipping into the void too. He also vanished on the spot, entering the void’s chaotic flow. He was about to search for the elite assassins when a slender sword suddenly emerged from his blind spot to strike his vitals, almost like a venomous serpent.","But Zu An merely laughed. Hmph, I was only afraid that you’d continue hiding. Swordsmanship had little meaning to his current self.","That elite assassin suddenly found his lethal thrust reversing direction to slit his neck. It was abrupt, and he had no idea how it even happened!","But Zu An frowned right after. For some reason, his life force was dissipating.","Just then, Zhao Yuan sneered from the void, “Ah, I forgot to warn you. When they kill a person who inflicted the mark on them, someone afflicted with the Mark of Annihilation will lose a tenth of their life force. I dare you to kill them all.”"]},{"number":2696,"title":"Chapter 2696: Chapter 2648: Tribute","paragraphs":["Zu An was startled. I’ll lose a tenth of my life force if I kill an assassin, and ten assassins placed the Mark of Annihilation on me earlier. Won’t I be dead if I kill all of them?","The abilities of the path of annihilation were downright underhanded. It was fortunate he was learning about them here, or else it would have been worse if he had been caught off guard by a stronger enemy in Dreamland.","Two black figures suddenly flanked him and attacked his vitals. These people were the most elite assassins of this world—they understood their craft and knew how to efficiently kill or incapacitate their target.","Zu An’s expression darkened. He raised his hand and struck the two assassins. The two assassins didn’t have time to react before they collapsed to the ground, dead.","He wasn’t so dumb as to blindly trust the enemy’s words; it would be wiser for him to verify the facts himself.","Soon, however, he felt two-tenths of his life force seeping away. Zhao Yuan wasn’t lying about the Mark of Annihilation’s ability.","The way Zu An effortlessly dispatched the three elite assassins sent a shiver down the spines of the rest. There was a vast disparity in their fighting prowess. Even when buffed by annihilation power, they were still no match for him.","So, they opted for long-range attacks instead, but these tools couldn’t hope to hurt Zu An. He neutralized them with ease, too.","“How can you be so powerful despite having lost half your strength?” Zhao Yuan roared angrily.","He couldn’t make sense of the situation. He'd thought that their annihilation power buff, their numerical superiority, and the Mark of Annihilation debuff were enough for them to rival Zu An. It should have been an easy victory for them. So why is he still making quick work of us?","Zu An didn’t bother answering Zhao Yuan’s question. They could have stood a better chance against him had they been in another world, but in this world, he was god.","Meanwhile, he'd figured out another function of the Mark of Annihilation—it allowed the caster to locate the target. He was traversing the void, yet the assassins could locate and launch a coordinated attack against him. It was as if they had planted a tracker on him.","He decided not to hold back anymore. He raised his hand and declared, “Void traversal is forbidden in this land.”","This wasn't soulspeak—he was rewriting the world laws with his authority as the world's master.","Zhao Yuan and the other seven assassins reappeared in midair. Their bodies were weirdly distorted, likely because they had been squeezed into small spatial cracks. They hadn’t expected to be revealed at Zu An’s command.","Initially, the crowd in Phoenix Pass had been worried when all of them suddenly disappeared. The rebels were worried about Zhao Yuan, whereas the imperial court was worried about Zu An. The Shadow Group’s elite assassins were notorious, and they wielded the fearsome annihilation power. How could they not be worried?","When they saw Zu An reappearing safe and sound, whereas the elite assassins had lost three of their comrades, the imperial forces breathed a sigh of relief.","Zu An flitted to Zhao Yuan’s side and struck his head, not giving the latter a chance to react. He couldn’t be bothered to spare Zhao Yuan’s life, knowing that the latter would remain relatively intact under the annihilation power’s protection. It would be easier to question him with his authority as the netherworld’s master.","But his body soon stiffened. He realized that the person he had just struck wasn't Zhao Yuan, but a nearby elite assassin.","The elite assassin’s eyes were popping out. He had no idea how he had suddenly gotten here when he should have been some distance away.","Zu An frowned. He glanced at Zhao Yuan. That fellow must have used a secret art to swap places with his subordinate, turning the latter into his scapegoat.","“You are truly...” Before he could finish speaking, his eyes suddenly narrowed, and he anxiously dodged to the side.","The elite assassin he had just smacked to death abruptly exploded, and the terrifying shockwaves that ensued distorted even the surrounding space.","Zu An could have easily avoided the explosion, but he could sense how powerful the shockwaves were. If he left the explosion be, the entirety of Phoenix Pass would be destroyed, and many would lose their lives. He raised his hand and sealed off the surrounding space to limit the explosion radius, but the more he tried to restrain it, the greater the backlash he felt. It also didn’t help that the explosion was imbued with annihilation power. Evidently, this body explosion was also an ability from the path of annihilation.","Even with Zu An’s strength, the tremendous shockwave still tore through his finger webbing, and blood seeped from the corner of his lips.","Zhao Yuan’s eyes lit up. “I see the regent has much that he cares about. That simplifies things.” As the Shadow Group Master, he knew that assassins excelled not in their physical prowess, but in exploiting all factors to create the ideal conditions to assassinate their target.","Zu An’s expression turned cold. “You don’t even hesitate to sacrifice your subordinates. Many of your brethren are in the rebel army. They would have been caught in that explosion too.”","“Don’t try to drive a wedge between us. Those who pursue the path of annihilation should be prepared to die at any time. To us, death is not an end, but rather glory.” Zhao Yuan gazed down on Phoenix Pass. “It’s their fate if they get caught in our battle and die. All beings eventually have to die anyway.”","Many rebels cursed him for being so heartless as to leave them in the lurch, but Zhao Yuan was unfazed by their remarks.","Zu An sighed. “If you truly believed that death is an honor, you wouldn’t have used your subordinate as a scapegoat earlier. You don’t seem to be a devout believer of annihilation.”","Zhao Yuan looked flustered. “Don’t you dare insult me! You have no right to doubt my faith in my master!”","He took out a dagger and plunged it into his chest. “Master, I offer you my fresh blood. Please grant me power.”","The remaining elite assassins also plunged their daggers into their chests and murmured some obscure chant.","The crowd in Phoenix Pass was taken aback. They wondered if Zhao Yuan and his elite assassins were out of their mind.","But Zu An frowned. He suspected that this was a skill to offer their blood essence in exchange for a temporary burst of power.","Flames enveloped Zhao Yuan and the seven elite assassins, and their auras grew two times stronger. Black runes appeared on Zhao Yuan’s face, making him look even more creepy and deranged than before. “Regent, you may be strong, but you are ultimately mortal. The likes of you can’t hope to withstand my master’s might!”"]},{"number":2697,"title":"Chapter 2697: Chapter 2649: Frog in a Well","paragraphs":["Zu An observed the assassins’ transformation. It’s similar to the Devil Sect’s blood ignition, where they ignite their blood essence to temporarily raise their fighting prowess, but it's much more advanced. They've grown two times stronger.","Those from the path of annihilation are troublesome to deal with.","At Zhao Yuan’s order, the assassins formed a sword formation and attacked Zu An. Each of their blades ignited with a peculiar flame that was suffused with violent energy.","Zu An was starting to find the situation a little tricky.","The others in Phoenix Pass could only see shadows flashing across the sky to attack Zu An; the elite assassins had attained a speed beyond what the spectators could follow.","Bi Linglong’s hand was soaked in sweat. She had already reorganized the imperial army by now, and she turned to the Qin clan’s two dukes and asked, “Can the formation masters in our army support the regent?”","The two dukes exchanged looks. Qin Zheng said, “Their strength is beyond our understanding. It’ll be hard for our formation masters to intervene in a duel of this caliber. If we carelessly make a move, we might distract the regent instead.”","Bi Linglong frowned. She thought hard and ordered, “Evacuate our men from Phoenix Pass. Get them away as far as possible.”","“But that would mean leaving brother-in... the regent alone with the rebel army!” Murong Qinghe was worried.","Zhang Zitong said, “General Murong, Her Majesty is right. We aren’t of any help to the regent here, and it’s probably the same for the rebel army. If anything, our presence here might only hinder the regent, as he'd have to protect us.”","Murong Qinghe was no fool. She recalled what Zhao Yuan had said and knew it wasn’t wise to linger here.","Soon, Bi Linglong began arranging for the imperial army to leave the battlefield, while she and a few other commanders scaled a faraway mountain to watch the battle.","The rebel kings wanted to pursue them, but after witnessing what had happened earlier, none of their men were willing to move, except for a few die-hard loyalists. A couple of silver taels per month wasn’t enough for them to lay down their lives.","Even the loyalists realized that the others weren’t going to join the pursuit, and challenging the imperial army with their meager strength would be tantamount to suicide. Thus, they had no choice but to let the imperial army retreat. When the imperial army retreated from Phoenix Pass, they were initially perplexed, but since the goal of this battle was to claim Phoenix Pass, they thought it was a good thing anyway.","Several kings excitedly ordered their subordinates to occupy Phoenix Pass’ vital chokepoints in case the imperial army regretted their decision and returned. They had tasted despair when the regent returned earlier. They were relieved to see Zhao Yuan and his team of assassins turning the tables on the regent.","They weren’t bothered about Zhao Yuan’s identity as the Shadow Group Master, since he was also a member of the Zhao clan. They didn’t think he would mistreat them. In contrast, Zu An would claim their lives if he won! This prompted them to cheer Zhao Yuan on.","In the sky, Zu An defended against the elite assassins’ sword formation as he said, “The people below are cheering hard for you.”","When he saw how light-hearted Zu An was, Zhao Yuan’s expression turned grim—the latter was still in the mood for idle chatter. “How are you still fine despite having so many Marks of Annihilation layered on you?”","He had been confident in his chances of winning this battle after his blood tribute greatly raised his strength. Initially, the battle unfolded the way he'd expected. He and his assassins’ sword formation suppressed Zu An, forcing the latter into a defensive stance.","But he soon noticed something amiss. They had the upper hand, but somehow, it wasn’t translating to victory. Zu An could always find ways to neutralize their offense. Chances were that he was using this as an opportunity to decipher their abilities.","How is this possible? I layered five Marks of Annihilation on him, weakening him by half! On top of that, he killed three of my assassins—that should have cost him 30% of his life force. He was also injured by the earlier explosion. He should be at his limit now!","What’s going on here?","He recalled what Zu An had said when he killed the four dukes: ’ Your world is too small. You’re frogs in a well, gazing upon the moon. Your ignorance is what gave you the courage to oppose me. If you had advanced your cultivation further, you would have understood the vast difference between us. ’","Zhao Yuan shuddered. He suddenly had a feeling that Zu An was as unfathomable as the sky.","No, that can’t be. I've obtained the power of a true deity. How can a mortal compete with that? He must be blowing his horn. He’s feigning infallibility to erode our fighting spirit.","Thus, he howled, “He’s already at his limit! We just need one last push to bring him down!”","Elite assassins like them had been honed to be unwavering, and Zhao Yuan’s words further raised their morale. They charged at Zu An like shooting stars.","An inferno gushed outward each time Zu An deflected their attacks with his Tai’e Sword, and sparks of flame fell from the sky and landed in the rebel army. These sparks unleashed destructive waves of flames as soon as they touched the ground. Soldiers afflicted with the flames, including experts, tried to put them out, but they couldn’t be extinguished. It didn’t take long for the troops to be reduced to ashes.","Soon, the falling sparks engulfed the entirety of Phoenix Pass in flames.","The imperial army was horrified. Fortunately, Her Majesty ordered our retreat, or else the consequences could have been dire.","Zu An frowned. “At this rate, your people are going to suffer heavy losses.”","Except for the higher-ups, most soldiers in the rebel army were here because they had no choice but to obey orders.","Zhao Yuan sneered, “You should surrender if you feel sorry for them. Otherwise, there will only be more casualties.” We might be on the same front now, but in the future, the other kings will become my rivals. If I weaken their armies now, no one will be able to defy me in the future.","The conversation in the sky shocked and horrified the rebel army. Some cursed Zhao Yuan for his heartlessness, while the others begged the regent to save them.","Zhao Yuan laughed even harder. “You hear that? They're begging you to save them. Are you going to leave them in the lurch?” It’ll be in our favor if Zu An gets distracted trying to save them.","Zu An harrumphed. “I can do that easily.”","The sky suddenly turned dark. A thunderous crackle boomed, and torrential rain fell right away. The flames engulfing Phoenix Pass were swiftly extinguished.","Deafening cheers broke out in across Phoenix Pass. Even several high-ranking officials in the rebel army shouted \"Long live the regent!\"","Zhao Yuan was dumbstruck. He knew this was no ordinary rainwater—ordinary water couldn’t hope to put out their annihilation flame. More than that, this rainwater didn’t just extinguish the flames in Phoenix Pass; it also put out the ones blazing from them.","The spectating imperial army breathed a sigh of relief.","Zhang Zitong squealed, “The regent is the strongest!”","Bi Linglong nodded in agreement as a blissful smile formed on her lips.","Murong Qinghe watched the imposing figure and suddenly blushed.","...","“You... can control this world’s weather?” The drenched Zhao Yuan stared at Zu An in disbelief. He sensed inexplicable law power emanating from the rainwater.","“In this world, I am god.” Zu An stood towering in the sky with lightning crackling behind him, outlining his cold expression.","It was at this moment that Zhao Yuan finally understood that he truly was a frog in a well."]},{"number":2698,"title":"Chapter 2698: Chapter 2650: Double Agent","paragraphs":["Zu An knew that now that they had acquired annihilation power, Zhao Yuan and the others couldn’t be underestimated. They would have made troublesome foes anywhere else. But he held the World Law Beacon of this world, making him the true god here. He could even alter the laws of this world.","He could have altered the world laws anytime to cancel the Marks of Annihilation’s weakening effect. Similarly, the elite assassins’ deaths siphoning away his life force didn’t pose a problem to him either. He could easily regenerate it with his Primordial Origin Sutra.","He'd only been entertaining Zhao Yuan and his subordinates to gather more information about the path of annihilation. Now that he had gotten what he wanted out of them, it was time to draw the curtains on this farce.","Sensing Zu An’s aura swiftly recovering, Zhao Yuan and the others descended into despair.","He was toying with us all this time!","As the Shadow Group Master, Zhao Yuan had never tasted despair no matter how strong his opponent was. He knew an assassin’s true strength didn’t lie in direct confrontation; he simply had to engineer the most advantageous circumstances to eliminate his target.","Even so, this time, he collapsed into true despair.","After acquiring annihilation power, he'd thought he was strong enough to dominate the world, not to mention that he had the aid of the Shadow Group’s top ten elite assassins. They had also grown by leaps and bounds after acquiring annihilation power. He'd thought, Surely we can bring down a mortal with the power of a true deity?","He hadn’t expected the world to be so cruel. Is a true god’s power inferior to that of a mortal?","With his elite assassins losing their fighting spirit, he knew it was pointless to continue this fight. So, he gritted his teeth and said, “Concubine Bai and the imperial grandson are in my hands. Are you going to abandon them?”","Zhang Zitong glanced at Bi Linglong. Her Majesty and Concubine Bai used to be sisters in the Eastern Palace. Is history going to repeat itself?","Many in the imperial army’s upper echelons looked at Bi Linglong too. They knew the two women weren’t on good terms.","The gazes on her made Bi Linglong frustrated. She wanted to say something but couldn’t find the words, so she decided to wait for Zu An’s decision first.","Zu An frowned. “The previous emperor secretly sentenced Concubine Bai to death. How did you find her?”","“There’s nothing in the world the Shadow Group can’t find. When it comes to gathering intelligence, we’re far superior to the Embroidered Envoys.”","Zhao Yuan’s words angered Xiao Jianren and Zhang Zitong, but they had to concede that the Shadow Group was indeed not inferior to the Embroided Envoys when it came to intelligence, and they were even a notch higher when it came to confidentiality.","“Where’s Concubine Bai?” Zu An asked.","“Let us go, and you’ll see her.” Deep down, Zhao Yuan knew that he was only inferior to Zu An; he was strong enough to tower over everyone else. As long as he avoided Zu An, he could still live a carefree life. And if he continued praying to the Deity of Annihilation, perhaps he could just gain new powers to turn the tables on Zu An.","Zu An shook his head. “Your rebellion has caused the deaths of many innocent civilians and soldiers. I can’t let you go.”","“If I die here, those two won’t live either!” Zhao Yuan anxiously exclaimed.","“I doubt that.” Zu An figured he could sieve through the memories of Zhao Yuan’s soul after killing him. He could figure Concubine Bai’s whereabouts by doing that.","Zhao Yuan suddenly laughed maniacally. “Concubine Bai, it looks like your regent doesn’t care about you. You can come out now.”","His words shocked both the rebel army and the imperial army. Is Concubine Bai not being held hostage?","A woman dressed in white slowly walked out from a house in Phoenix Pass. She looked frail. Her beautiful face contrasted with the surrounding blood and flame remnants, which made her look even more pitiful.","“Concubine Bai!” Many recognized the beautiful woman. The dimwitted crown prince was lucky to have such a beautiful concubine!","Unlike the authoritative Crown Prince Consort, her frail stature evoked a man’s desire to protect.","“It has been a while, regent.” Concubine Bai looked at the man in the sky with conflicted eyes.","“Concubine Bai, if you convince the regent to let us go, I’ll ensure your son’s safety.” Zhao Yuan said.","Many soldiers in the rebel army cursed Zhao Yuan. We’re fighting against the empress in the imperial grandson’s name, yet you’re holding the imperial grandson hostage? This is ridiculous!","Zu An descended to Concubine Bai’s side. “Who could have thought we would meet again under such circumstances?”","Hesitation flickered across Concubine Bai’s face as she secretly sent him a telepathic message, “Be careful, regent. Zhao Yuan intends for me to find an opportunity to assassinate you.”","“I know.” Zu An smiled. “Why else would I come here?”","“You already know?” Concubine Bai was taken aback.","“He wouldn’t have let you move independently if you were truly a hostage.” Zu An sighed. “You’re also from the Shadow Group, aren’t you?”","Concubine Bai looked at him with a bitter smile. “Indeed. I am the Shadow Group’s Holy Maiden, as well as its eleventh elite assassin. It’s quite a coincidence. Back then, you were the eleventh Embroidered Envoy, and I was the eleventh assassin.”","Despite having figured out her identity, Zu An still had questions. “But you're Yun Jianyue’s junior. How did you get involved with the Shadow Group?” I always thought she was a spy planted by the Devil Sect in the imperial palace. Is she a double agent?","“The Shadow Group has its roots in the Devil Sect’s Skysplitting School.”","Concubine Bai didn’t explain in detail, but that was all Zu An needed. There had been infighting in the Devil Sect when he was at the Lake of Hatred. There, he'd learned about the relationship between the Shadow Group and the Skysplitting School and released the son of the Skysplitting School’s master, Jing Li.","Jing Li had been investigating the Shadow Group Master all this while. Due to this link, he was probably the only one in the world who could have uncovered Zhao Yuan’s true identity.","Seeing the hushed conversation between Concubine Bai and Zu An, Zhao Yuan began losing his patience. He shouted, “What are you waiting for?”","Concubine Bai suddenly dropped to the ground. Zu An reflexively reached out to support her, but she suddenly whipped out a blue, glowing dagger and stabbed it into his chest."]},{"number":2699,"title":"Chapter 2699: Chapter 2651: The King of Assassins Becomes a Joke","paragraphs":["This shocked everyone present, especially Bi Linglong and the other ladies. They had been jealous when they saw Concubine Bai and Zu An acting friendly with each other. Who could have thought Concubine Bai would suddenly turn against him like that? They were so nervous that they thought their hearts would beat out of their chests. They had never worried about Zu An losing to a man, but he was so philandering that it felt inevitable that he would lose to a woman.","Zhao Yuan smiled in glee. This was the trump card he had prepared just in case. As the Shadow Group Master, he knew an assassin’s ability couldn’t be evaluated by their cultivation. More often than not, a frail beauty could be more useful than a powerful cultivator.","Concubine Bai was the card he had reserved to deal with Zu An. He had spent years investigating Zu An’s weakness. The latter was indeed a formidable foe, both in cultivation and wits, but he had a fatal weakness—his lustfulness.","Zhao Han had secretly sentenced Concubine Bai to death, but Zu An had taken on a huge risk to save her. That suggested he had special feelings for her. Thus, Zhao Yuan had begun formulating this plan. The dagger was smeared with the most formidable poison developed by the Shadow Group.","But his smile soon stiffened up. Concubine Bai had thrust the dagger toward Zu An, but the latter stood up casually as if nothing had happened. Zhao Yuan's gaze moved downward, only to realize that the dagger hadn’t pierced Zu An’s skin.","Concubine Bai was baffled too. His body is even harder than metal!","While she hadn’t exerted her full strength, it should have been enough to cut his skin. Of course, she hadn’t smeared the lethal poison on the dagger either. The dagger’s blue glow was a gimmick.","Zu An smiled. “You don’t have to go through so much trouble. I can help you rescue your son.”","Concubine Bai had just requested for him to put on an act with her. Zhao Yuan was holding her son hostage, forcing her to carry out this assassination. But Zu An hadn’t played along with her script.","Zhao Yuan’s face darkened. He exclaimed angrily, “You bitch! You’ll never see your son again!”","He uttered something to the elite assassins, and their eyes suddenly reddened with madness. They let loose loud screeches as they abruptly charged at Zu An.","“Careful! They're going to detonate themselves to bring you down with them!” Concubine Bai anxiously warned him.","Zu An also sensed the threat they posed. By the time he held Concubine Bai closer to him, the assassins were already in their vicinity.","Unlike before, they weren’t planning to fight. Their bodies swiftly swelled up and exploded. The simultaneous explosions of the remaining elite assassins triggered a chain reaction, culminating in a humongous explosion far stronger than the one before. A black hole suffused with destructive energy appeared in the sky. It exerted an incredible suction force that pulled the houses and trees into it.","The rebel kings and their aides had been the closest to Zu An—they'd remained on standby in case an extra hand was needed to take Zu An down. The turn of events scared them out of their wits. They desperately fled for their lives, but they couldn’t outrun the suction force. Despite their best attempts to run forward, their bodies were dragged backward.","As the black hole got bigger, even the experts in their ranks succumbed and flew into the sky too. Out of despair, some of them begged Zu An to save them.","But Zu An didn’t have the energy to entertain them. His mind was focused on altering the surrounding world laws. If he couldn’t stop the black hole in time, Phoenix Pass and the hundreds of thousands of soldiers in the vicinity would be annihilated here.","A massive hand suddenly manifested in the sky. It grabbed the black hole, and the two vanished into the void together.","Even though Zu An had transported the black hole into the void in the shortest time possible, Phoenix Pass was still destroyed. The rebel army also suffered heavy losses.","“Hahaha! Bastard Zu, look who I have in my hands!” A frenzied laugh echoed. Zhao Yuan held Bi Linglong before him, with a sword pressed against her neck.","As the Shadow Group Master, he needed to be resourceful. Concubine Bai was merely one of the hands he had prepared; the other was Bi Linglong. He knew Bi Linglong was on close terms with Zu An, so much so that there were novels about them on the streets. While his subordinates were exploding, he'd charged into the imperial army’s ranks and grabbed Bi Linglong. After what happened earlier, he'd had little confidence that the explosions would work.","Many people had been guarding Bi Linglong, but none were powerful enough to stop Zhao Yuan. In the blink of an eye, he already had Bi Linglong in his grasp. He immediately turned to Zu An, only to see the latter easily neutralizing the explosion. That filled him with fear and relief. Good thing I had a backup plan.","“Your Majesty!” Shocked and horrified, Zhang Zitong, Murong Qinghe, and the others quickly surrounded Zhao Yuan. They wanted to attack him, but they were worried that he would hurt Bi Linglong.","Zhao Yuan didn’t spare a glance at Bi Linglong’s guards. He cleared his throat and addressed Zu An, “Let me go and promise not to pursue me. I’ll let her go once I’m somewhere safe.”","He thought of forcing Zu An to break his arms, but he was worried that the other party would give up on Bi Linglong if he forced him too far. He had heard about Zu An’s many lovers, and while Bi Linglong was beautiful, she was merely one out of many in his massive harem.","Zhao Yuan didn’t want the crown anymore. After the consecutive blows he had received, his ambition had been quelled. He just wanted to survive and find somewhere peaceful to live out his life. Being the Shadow Group Master or the emperor was no longer important to him.","Of course, he wouldn’t release Bi Linglong even after reaching somewhere safe. He never believed his enemy’s promises. Only with the hostage in hand would his safety be guaranteed.","Concubine Bai looked at Zu An apologetically. Even though she wasn't the culprit here, he wouldn’t have been distracted if not for her. She secretly warned Zu An, “Big brother Zu, Zhao Yuan doesn’t believe in anyone. It is unlikely he will release big sister Linglong after getting to safety. It’ll be more dangerous if you allow him to take big sister Linglong away.” But she couldn’t think of any solution at hand.","In contrast, Zu An remained perfectly calm. One step at a time, he slowly made his way toward Zhao Yuan.","“Stay away! I won’t show mercy.” Zhao Yuan panicked. He tightened his grip on his sword, causing a blood slit to appear on Bi Linglong’s fair neck.","The chilling touch of the blade sent goosebumps all over Bi Linglong’s body, but she still calmly shouted to Zu An. “Don’t worry about me, regent. This man is the source of all this chaos. We have to kill him for the peace of the world!”","“I didn’t expect a woman like you to be so brave. What a pity he’s a sentimental man. I doubt he’ll bear to lose a beauty like you.” Zhao Yuan laughed, but he was uncertain. He was worried that Zu An would forsake his lover and attack him.","Bi Linglong wanted to say more, but Zu An stopped her with his gentle eyes. He turned to Zhao Yuan and said, “I don’t think you understand what it means to be god.”","Zhao Yuan felt uneasy. He tightened his blade further, holding Bi Linglong firmly in place.","All of a sudden, however, he sensed something amiss. He lowered his head and found that instead of Bi Linglong, he was holding a broken pillar.","Bi Linglong was standing next to Zu An!"]},{"number":2700,"title":"Chapter 2700: Chapter 2652: Clearing All Threats","paragraphs":["“How’s this possible?” Zhao Yuan panicked, his eyes brimming with confusion.","As the king of assassins, he had absolute control over his body. He was confident that he could dictate the life or death of anyone within a one-meter radius of him. Even when Zu An appeared, he'd still been confident he could kill Zu An if the latter got within a thirty-centimeter radius.","If someone had told him that an enemy could easily rescue a person he was holding hostage, he would have never believed it. What did it mean to be the king of assassins? It meant no one could rescue a person under his control!","That was the basis of his confidence, which was why he'd dared to negotiate with Zu An after holding Bi Linglong hostage.","What's going on? Was it all my delusion? Reluctant to believe this was real, he even tried stabbing the pillar in his grasp. It was indeed no illusion. What he was holding was a rotten pillar.","It wasn't just him; the crowd was also flabbergasted.","Murong Qinghe and Zhang Zitong rubbed their eyes before exchanging confused looks. They had seen Zhao Yuan holding Bi Linglong hostage. It was one thing for Zhao Yuan to hallucinate, but how could all of them be hallucinating together?","Bi Linglong felt as if she was dreaming. It was just a second ago that Zhao Yuan had his blade pressed against her neck, and she had already resigned herself to death. She'd even considered slitting her neck against the blade so that she wouldn’t be a liability to her lover. But then, the next second, she suddenly appeared by his side.","She reflexively touched her neck and felt the thin cut on it. That confirmed she wasn’t hallucinating. What’s going on?","Everyone present was full of questions.","Zu An sighed. “I told you, I call the shots in this world.”","After obtaining the World Law Beacon and the acknowledgment of the world’s will, he'd been granted the equivalent of a superuser privilege. He could freely alter the world laws, though only to a certain degree—it couldn’t threaten the functioning of the world.","To be exact, it was the equivalent of having access to a game’s backend engine, allowing him to freely alter data. Even moving mountains and seas wasn’t beyond him, let alone substituting Bi Linglong with a pillar.","In this world, he was no longer at the level of a simple cultivator anymore. Other cultivators had to rely on fighting to obtain what they wanted, but he could solve problems with a simple thought.","He'd still struggled to use these privileges before, but after his encounter with the deities in the ancient Celestial Court and the Deity of Enigma and Chaos, Mi Li, his grasp on power and laws had risen to another level. It helped him decipher his privileges in this world.","But he could only access these godlike abilities because he was this world’s master, which meant that he couldn’t use them anywhere else. Had he bumped into Zhao Yuan in another world, it wouldn’t have been such an easy fight.","That said, even the experience of being a god in a little world was meaningful. It deepened his understanding of power and laws, allowing him to deduce the abilities of the mythological and universal deities.","“So this is the power of a god...” Zhao Yuan looked crushed. He knew he was cornered, and there was no way Zu An would spare him after everything he had done.","“How tragic it is to be mortal!” He slit his throat with his blade. He looked at Zu An and Concubine Bai with a mocking gaze as life seeped from his body. “I won’t let you interrogate me. Concubine Bai, you'll never see your son again!” Thanks to the annihilation power's enhancement, he could still speak so much despite having slit his throat.","Concubine Bai exclaimed in horror. Her face turned ghastly pale.","Zu An stared at Zhao Yuan with an enigmatic smile. “Do you think death is the end for a god?”","Now that death was drawing close, Zhao Yuan had been fearless, but Zu An’s words made him panic. Could it be...","The truth soon became apparent. Zu An casually waved his hand, and a transparent soul emerged from Zhao Yuan's body. The latter looked back at his corpse, followed by his current transparent form that no one else could see. He was shocked and frightened. “This is... my soul?”","Zu An smiled. “I should have told you that I’m also the netherworld’s master. Deceased beings fall under my jurisdiction.”","Zhao Yuan was horrified. “NOOOOOO!”","Zu An turned to Concubine Bai and said, “Don’t worry. He hid your child in a small town not too far away from Phoenix Pass. I’ll send someone to rescue him.” He called Zhang Zitong over and relayed the instructions to her.","Zhang Zitong excitedly replied, “Consider it done!”","I’m the first one the regent thinks of when he needs something done! He's given me the location and the defense layout. With the imperial guards and the Embroidered Envoys under my command, I should just buy a slab of tofu and bang my head on it if I can’t rescue the hostage despite that.","Zu An turned back to Concubine Bai and said, “The Shadow Group fed him a poison to keep him under their control, but you don’t need to worry. I already know the antidote’s concoction method. I’ll hand it to someone from the academy later.”","Concubine Bai was overjoyed. She kneeled to him and said, “Thank you, Zu... Regent!”","Bi Linglong frowned. She wanted to say something, but she held her tongue.","Zu An supported Concubine Bai to her feet. Then, he turned to address the rebel soldiers in Phoenix Pass. “You have brought chaos to the empire by aiding the rebellious kings, but they have been purged now. I’ll give you a chance. Lay down your weapons, and I’ll spare your lives as long as you haven’t hurt any innocent civilians.”","“Thank you, regent. Long live the regent!”","Now that Zhao Yuan was dead and Concubine Bai had submitted, who would dare to continue the rebellion, especially after what they had just witnessed? Right now, they only felt thankful to the regent for his magnanimity.","Listening to the cheers from the crowd, some imperial officials secretly glanced at Bi Linglong. When they saw her looking at her lover with adoring eyes, they burst into laughter. In history, officials who were so celebrated by the people drew their liege’s suspicion and would eventually be purged, but no one thought anything was wrong with what had just happened.","Zu An entrusted the two dukes from the Qin clan with the important responsibility of processing the rebel army’s surrender, while he greeted the officials and caught up with old friends like Gao Ying and Pei You. It had been years since they had met, so there was a lot to chat about.","It took a while before Bi Linglong got some private time with Zu An. “Ah Zu, I don’t think we should spare Concubine Bai’s son.” Fearing that he would misunderstand, she quickly added, “I’m not on good terms with Concubine Bai, but I’m not saying this out of a personal vendetta. That child is Zhao Han’s descendant. Others might seek to use him when he’s still young, and if he learns that you killed his father later when he grows older, he might turn against you. It wouldn’t be wise to keep him around.”"]}]);
